window.RSI_DATA={"updated_at":"2026-10-31 11:32 CST","papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.38728","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.38728v1","title":"From Grind to Grasp","authors":"Peter Sunehag","affiliations":"Google DeepMind","abstract":"Discussions of complexity, knowledge and intelligence often overlook the work involved. For example, outputs generated by short programs have low algorithmic complexity but can have high computational depth, the least work needed to produce them from near-shortest programs. Producing them with less work can require longer descriptions, giving high work-bounded complexity. We introduce a formalism that compares achievements under work and information limits and describes how learning and persistence can make deep achievements shallow by reusing products of earlier work. For an agent with a limited work budget, the value of building and maintaining such resources depends on how they support its goals over later tasks. We define grasp as performance across work budgets at a fixed information allowance. Low grasp can still yield success through grind at high cost in work, without necessarily improving human grasp. Applied to improvement itself, grasp gives a criterion for recursive self-improvement in which successors make comparable further improvements more efficiently. Another route to faster progress is to expand the resources brought to bear through knowledge sharing and coordination across society, even while comparable advances require increasing work. Grasp also applies to collectives, which may outperform their members yet require more total work than one system with their combined resources. Establishing and sustaining organisation can itself be deep even when the primary task is simple. These demands may help explain the richness of biological and social systems. In agent collectives, this organisational work can generate goals beyond assigned tasks, including maintaining the collective itself. We therefore caution against allowing an emergent agent society to assume authority over social coordination, since it could increasingly direct work towards its own persistence and goals.","tldr":"背景与问题：任务做成得更快，可能来自更多并行计算或继承已有成果，未必意味着系统更会产生改进。只比较成功率或日历时间，会混淆能力、投入与知识复用。\n\n方法：论文固定系统边界和信息额度，用不同工作预算下的表现定义 grasp；保存的中间结果、程序和知识若减少后续工作，就构成有效资源。应用到自改进时，要求后继系统以更少工作完成可比的进一步改进，并计入资源构建、维护与协调成本。\n\n结果与结论：这是形式化框架，未提供现实 agent 的效率实验。可见命题说明，变化的改进程序能由固定解释器执行，但解释开销可能改变效率排序，因此比较必须使用相同解释器；不能由程序可自修改推出递归收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，其价值是把“产物更强”推进为“下一次可比改进是否更省工作”的问题，与已有同起点、同预算审计相接。实际难点仍是定义可比改进及完整成本；关于集体自我维持目标的讨论不能当作已观察到的 agent 行为。 ","published_at":"2026-10-28","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; 能力归因; 预算受限研究搜索","added_on":"2026-10-30","novelty_summary":"作者声称以工作与信息约束统一描述知识复用，并以可比后续改进的效率提高界定递归收益。本文证据是定义、论证及固定解释器命题，没有实现自改进闭环，也没有反馈驱动的系统实验。相对 arxiv:2610.27610 已要求同起点、同预算比较新旧改进者，本篇更明确地讨论工作预算曲线、系统边界及资源维护；相对 arxiv:2610.10611 区分搜索成功与验证边界，本篇关注工作效率而非接受语言。编辑推断：可作为评测设计的概念补充，尚需可操作的任务与成本定义；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.38568","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.38568v1","title":"A-RSI: Adaptive Task Refresh for Zero-Data Multimodal Self-Improvement","authors":"Yu Liu; Youxing Li; Yuedong Tan; Zhiwei Yang; Zihan Su; Hanqi Feng; Shaojie Zhang; Libin Liao; Zihao Wan; Chenxu Wu; Cong Cao; Fangfang Yuan; Yanbing Liu; Ziheng Chen; Pei Fu; Radu Timofte; Zongwei Wu; Nicu Sebe; Barnabas Poczos; Jian Luan","affiliations":"","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement requires models not only to acquire useful training experience, but also to decide when their current experience has ceased to be useful. Existing methods often focus on what experience to generate next, while paying less attention to when fresh experience should be introduced. Many also construct training targets through self-consistency or majority voting, making supervision depend on the model's own uncertain predictions. We address these two questions separately: training dynamics determine when to acquire new experience, while the answers to new tasks remain independently checkable. A-RSI monitors reward variation and accuracy in training logs to refresh a task pool when its learning signal declines, without consulting validation or test scores. A static library of model-authored programs produces multimodal questions and derives their reference answers; we specify the task-generation contract, automatically verify chosen properties of the reward and refresh rules, and separately audit the generated answers. The training loop uses no external training examples or human-written answer labels. On the primary eleven-benchmark suite, A-RSI raises the performance average from 57.77 to 61.05 with 800 fresh tasks.","tldr":"背景与问题：旧题池可能不再产生有效训练信号，频繁换题又浪费新任务；若答案来自模型多数票，错误共识还会成为下一轮监督。换题时机与答案可靠性需要分别解决。\n\n方法：A-RSI 根据训练日志中有组内奖励差异的题目数量及准确率变化，决定何时启用预备的新题池。固定程序从同一底层配置生成图像、问题和答案，模型保留已学权重继续训练；生成器与控制规则不更新，答案另经检查和审计。\n\n结果与结论：在匹配的第六个续训窗口，十一基准均分为60.40，继续使用旧池为58.35，支持新题替换的价值。但每个实验臂仅训练一次，且缺少匹配固定周期的随机刷新对照，尚不能把收益独立归因于自适应时机。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，更值得保留的是把训练信号与答案来源分开。奖励差异消失也可能意味着共同答错，不能等同掌握题池；格式和正常结束同样影响该信号，后续应检验换题决策是否预测真实纠错，而非主要改善输出完成率。","published_at":"2026-10-28","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 自适应训练经验; 自进化策略训练","added_on":"2026-10-30","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过训练日志触发换池，并以程序计算答案支持零外部训练样本的多模态自改进。本文证据：求解器权重跨窗口保留，训练侧信号决定是否启用新池；模板、题型份额和控制器固定，程序监督仍依赖模板及渲染正确性。相对 arxiv:2610.11345 和 arxiv:2610.33799 更新造题策略，本篇只调整预生成题池的启用时机，不属于生成器—求解器共同学习。编辑推断：是数据刷新控制的具体增量；首次刷新点依据已有日志设定，匹配周期对照缺失，时机贡献与新题贡献未分离。题型份额及主题词还受评测基准启发，训练不读取测试分数不等于设计完全独立；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.38546","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.38546v1","title":"Implicit Minor Detection from Multi-Turn Dialogue in High-Risk AI Interactions: A Constrained Self-Evolving LLM Harness","authors":"Xiaohan Zhang; Ying Zhao; Ruilin Guo; Xuanyuan Yu; Kaibo Huang; Yukun Wei; Zhongliang Yang; Linna Zhou","affiliations":"北京邮电大学","abstract":"In high-risk text interactions, a system may need to estimate whether the current speaker is likely to be a minor before applying age-conditioned safeguards. Many text-based dialogue systems lack strong identity signals such as account information, verified identity, facial data, or device data, and must rely on weak cues that emerge across multiple turns. We formulate implicit minor detection under weak identity information as a high-risk user-attribute inference task and propose a constrained framework comprising a large language model, a Harness, and a Maker-Checker protocol. The framework controls when inference is invoked, requires structured dialogue-linked evidence, and subjects validation-selected Harness revisions to version-level review. On a controlled Chinese benchmark comprising 8,328 multi-turn dialogues, our method improves average precision and minor-class F1 by 7.60 and 6.37 percentage points, respectively, over direct inference using the same LLM family.","tldr":"背景与问题：对话中的学校、家庭等词可能描述别人或过去经历，直接推断年龄容易错绑证据；修改判断规则还可能修好新案例、破坏旧边界。系统既要决定是否调用推断，也要约束依据。\n\n方法：固定模型，把当前说话者的对话证据与检索案例分开。验证错误、需保护的正确案例和近期修改后果共同指导 harness 修订；候选须通过成绩、格式及红线回归门控，获准版本影响后续提案。版本审查材料供人工检查，不改变运行时预测。\n\n结果与结论：受控中文对话基准上，完整系统相对同模型族直接推断，未成年人类别F1提高6.37个百分点；该对照不能单独量化演化环节贡献。小型人工挑战集上不同运行差异明显，尚不足以推断真实服务可靠性。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，证据不足的处理比总体涨分更值得核查：当前二分类协议把它映射为负类，仅表示不支持未成年判断，并未验证成年。后续应单独检验拒答或澄清机制，以及门控能否保住未被现有案例覆盖的边界。","published_at":"2026-10-28","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 自改进稳定性; RSI 可证伪性与治理","added_on":"2026-10-30","novelty_summary":"作者声称以受约束的 harness 演化支持隐式未成年人识别。本文证据：验证标签及错误类型提供反馈，近期接受和拒绝记录进入下一次提案，仅任务层资源改变，模型、控制器及评估代码固定；人工版本审查不构成额外运行时判别器。相对 arxiv:2610.35316 已有锚点、回归记忆及版本保留，本篇将约束落实到调用边界、说话者绑定和证据来源，未显示更新器自身增强。与 arxiv:2610.38392 的比较说明，两者分别检查当前行为回归和潜在防护冗余；后者不能直接证明本系统存在同类侵蚀。编辑推断：主要是领域化任务合同与治理实现，完整系统增益不足以隔离演化收益；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.38392","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.38392v1","title":"Masked Erosion: How Acceptance Gates Lose Redundant Safeguards in Self-Improving Agents","authors":"Hau-Sing So; Daixian Liu; Weicai Long","affiliations":"University of Macau；Tsinghua University","abstract":"Self-improving LLM agents edit their own harness, the prompts and rules around a fixed model, and keep an edit only if an acceptance gate scores it higher on a batch of tasks. Such a gate sees what the harness does under the current model, not what it would still prevent if one safeguard failed. When safeguards overlap, deleting one is masked: the others still block the harm, so the gate decides on task success alone and redundancy erodes unseen. We measure harm for every subset of four written safeguards in two agent environments and run 411 improvement loops under ten gate rules, mostly as controlled deletion experiments, plus three runs of the GEPA optimizer. A deletion behind another working safeguard adds almost no observable harm. A paired significance test blocks deletions that pass by chance but not deletions that genuinely raise task success, and a larger evaluation batch lets it delete cheaper safeguards: at the same cost, 20-task batches kept every harness protected while 40-task batches lost all six. Large harm audits prevent exposure but not the loss of depth, which turns into harm when the harness is reused with a weaker model. GEPA kept every safety rule verbatim, yet two of its three final harnesses misused credentials under a weaker model. A statistical model frozen before the runs predicts where each gate's protection breaks as safeguard cost and batch size change, and freezing safety text or auditing one-layer ablations preserves depth.","tldr":"背景与问题：重叠防护中删去一层，其他层仍能挡住危害，验收器便只看见任务收益。即使收益真实、当前危害不增，系统承受后续故障的余量也可能已经减少。\n\n方法：论文测量四层防护所有组合的危害，并让删除或自由改写通过不同验收门控，获准版本成为下一轮起点。确定性审计检查凭证误用和破坏性清理，再通过移除单层及更换执行模型，检验当前行为评分遗漏的防护深度。\n\n结果与结论：显著性检验能减少偶然准入，却挡不住确实提高任务成功率的防护删除；更大评估批次甚至使更便宜的防护被删。GEPA保留全部安全规则原文，但三个最终版本中两个在较弱模型下误用凭证。主要实验仍是受控删除压力测试。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，安全验收需要检查失效后的剩余保护，不能只增加当前模型上的审计次数。原文保留也不能保证功能保持；模型替换应触发重新审计。证据覆盖两个环境和有限防护，尚不能估计自然部署中侵蚀的发生率。","published_at":"2026-10-28","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; 自改进稳定性; 递归安全改进","added_on":"2026-10-30","novelty_summary":"作者声称揭示验收门控对冗余防护损失的盲点，并用防护子集的危害结构量化余量。本文证据：固定模型下接受的 harness 进入后续轮次，任务成功与确定性危害检查提供反馈；411轮循环实验中393轮为受控删除，另有自由改写及少量GEPA运行，并未演化验收器本身。相对 arxiv:2610.27465 测验证器强度与恢复，本篇增加当前行为正常时的反事实防护检查；相对 arxiv:2610.27735 的显式隐蔽攻击，本篇说明无须恶意目标，真实效用收益也可推动防护流失。编辑推断：是安全审计机制的实质推进，但压力测试不能代表自然发生频率，部分预测在相关结果出现后冻结；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.37651","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.37651v1","title":"GEPA-Curator: Curated Learning for Self Improving Agents","authors":"Zack Yu; Nicholas Lee; Minjae Lee; Lakshya Agarwal; Luca Manolache; Wonjun Kang; Matei Zaharia; Michael W. Mahoney; Kurt Keutzer; Sehoon Kim; Amir Gholami","affiliations":"UC Berkeley；ICSI；LBNL；Furiosa AI；KAIST","abstract":"Large Language Models (LLMs) are increasingly used in multi-turn agentic workloads that require sustained interaction with complex environments. Existing reflective prompt optimizers such as GEPA learn from failed rollouts, but agentic failures can also come from prompt weaknesses, harness limitations, stochastic execution, or noisy judges. We argue that such failures may not provide useful learning signal, and may even be harmful; and thus it is essential to curate which tasks are provided to the prompt optimizer for better performance. We introduce GEPA-Curator, a framework that augments the prompt optimizer to select which agent experiences should shape prompt optimization. In particular, GEPA-Curator consists of two components: task curation, which filters out tasks that are likely to provide noisy or unreliable learning signals, and prior success retrieval, which selectively retrieves past successful trajectories for a task and provides them as additional context to the prompt optimizer. We evaluate GEPA-Curator on GoBrowse, ALFWorld, AppWorld, and $τ$-bench, using both Gemini 3.1 Pro and Claude Opus 5 as optimizer models. GEPA-Curator matches or exceeds the mean performance of both baselines, with gains of up to 20.7% over GEPA and 21.2% over ACE.","tldr":"背景与问题：反思式提示优化容易把环境故障、工具缺失或裁判噪声误归为提示缺陷。事后验证只能筛修改结果，不能避免优化器反复从无效失败中猜修补办法。\n\n方法：策展 agent 根据同题历史，暂时跳过缺少有效学习信号的任务，并为当前失败检索评价一致的历史成功轨迹，让反思有具体参照。新执行结果写回历史，影响后续选题；提示优化器本身不变。\n\n结果与结论：相同 rollout 配额、五次重复下，两个优化模型在网页任务上的总体测试成功率分别比 GEPA 高3.4和5.0个百分点。结构化问答的优势较小，HotpotQA 还下降；部分成本表显示总费用高于 GEPA。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，失败价值取决于能否对应可修改原因，而非失败次数。问答与交互任务的收益差异符合这一解释，但关键消融被截断，仍需拆开选题、成功参照与额外计算的贡献。","published_at":"2026-10-27","topics":"失败诊断; 经验迁移; Harness 递归演化","added_on":"2026-10-28","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过任务策展与历史成功检索改善提示修改质量。本文证据：每题执行历史和评价一致性决定任务是否进入优化，以及提供何种成功参照；更新提示影响下一批轨迹，策展和优化程序未显示自我演化。相对 arxiv:2610.22984 揭示失败修补难迁移，本篇主动补入同题成功锚点，但没有在其冷启动协议下比较；相对 arxiv:2610.19424 限制反馈内容暴露，本篇选择并补充反馈内容。编辑推断：是反馈治理的具体推进，不能视为已解决归因或迁移问题；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.36826","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.36826v1","title":"When the Critic Falls Behind: Co-Evolving Rubrics and Harnesses for Continual Agent Self-Improvement","authors":"Hao Chen; Yukun Yan; Ziyu Han; Ye He; Chuanzhe Guo; Shangzhan Li; Qi Shi; Qingfu Zhu; Maosong Sun; Wanxiang Che","affiliations":"哈尔滨工业大学社会计算与交互机器人研究中心；清华大学计算机科学与技术系、人工智能研究院","abstract":"Autonomous agents increasingly depend on harnesses that govern interaction, memory, tools, and execution around large language models (LLMs). While recent work has begun to evolve these harnesses from execution experience, the supervision used to guide evolution often remains relatively static, making it difficult to track changing behavioral weaknesses across rounds and potentially limiting generalization to unseen tasks. To address this issue, we propose RuHarness, a rubric--harness co-evolution framework for continual agent self-improvement. RuHarness continually discovers and reassesses behavioral criteria from execution trajectories, prioritizes the most relevant unresolved weaknesses, and uses them to guide targeted harness updates while keeping the task objective fixed. Extensive experiments across diverse agent tasks and backbone models show that RuHarness outperforms strong harness-evolution baselines, particularly on unseen held-out tasks. Further analyses show that adaptive rubric prioritization tracks shifting weaknesses and supports more sustained improvement and stable generalization across evolution rounds.","tldr":"背景与问题：harness 改好主要失败后，下一轮弱点会转移；沿用静态诊断标准，可能继续修已经解决的问题，也可能把开发任务的局部模式固化进系统。\n\n方法：从轨迹发现行为准则，让不知道最终成败的模型判断是否违反，再结合任务结果重估准则的诊断价值。当前最有证据的未解决弱点指导 harness 修改，候选由独立于演化轨迹的验证任务选择；任务目标保持固定。\n\n结果与结论：五领域评测中，Qwen 配置的留出平均分为53.7，AHE 为49.2。材料给出了分离演化、选择与测试的设计，但关键消融和完整演化曲线被截断，无法核对持续改进的独立来源。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可变诊断与固定成功标准的分离比“评估器共演化”名称更重要。准则与失败相关不代表修它就能改善结果；下一步应检验诊断排序是否确实提高等预算修改收益。","published_at":"2026-10-27","topics":"评估器递归改进; Harness 递归演化; 失败诊断","added_on":"2026-10-28","novelty_summary":"作者声称行为准则与 harness 共演化可跟踪不断变化的弱点。本文证据：模型行为判断与任务成败共同更新准则优先级，准则指导修改，独立验证任务决定接受；模型权重固定。相对 arxiv:2610.17609 演化直接控制回答及经验准入的可执行 verifier，本篇演化诊断准则，最终选择仍由固定任务表现决定；相对 arxiv:2604.25850 的组件可观测修改，增加准则生命周期及动态排序。编辑推断：诊断接口有实质细化，但排序规则自身未演化，完整消融未见；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.36077","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.36077v1","title":"The Trinity:Capability-Driven Recursive Self-Improvement for Multimodal Agents","authors":"Weidong Tang; Ruiheng Wang; Jingxuan Zhang; Hexin Wang; Haoyuan Chen; Zhengfeiyang Zhang; Yixing Ma; Zichen Jiang; Ziyu Guo; Haodong Li; Zhengbo Jiao; Zhiqing Cui; Xinxiang Yin; Shuo Liang; Zhenglin Wan; Hongzhan Lin; Wangbo Zhao Kaipeng Zhang; Pengfei Zhou; Odin Zhang; Yang You","affiliations":"","abstract":"Multimodal intelligence can be viewed as human-guided co-evolution between worlds and agents through interaction. However, scaling this process faces two bottlenecks: constructing heterogeneous, verifiable environments is costly, and manual Harness iteration cannot keep pace with growing task diversity and complexity. A key insight is that tasks with different modalities and surface forms can share the same underlying capability requirements. We therefore introduce The Trinity, a recursive self-improvement framework coupling world generation with Harness evolution through three roles: Creator, Explorer, and Evolver. Drawing on verified execution trajectories, Evolver shifts the basis of task organization from surface categories to shared requirements, reorganizing the original task tree into a hierarchical capability tree. We introduce Capability-Driven Real2Sim2Real: for heterogeneous tasks at the same node, Creator abstracts their common requirements into simplified, verifiable simulated worlds for capability learning, while evaluation on original tasks measures transfer. Along this capability tree, Explorer progressively evolves reusable capability modules through selective inheritance, forming a Harness tree whose validated updates accumulate across iterations within a fixed topology. The resulting Harnesses specialize in different capabilities, motivating a Capability-Aware Harness Router that uses public task information to select compatible module configurations from the tree. Our evolved Harnesses improve mean performance by 34 points across 28 training benchmarks and 26 points across 18 unseen benchmarks, including two real-world embodied tasks.","tldr":"背景与问题：异构多模态任务既难批量构造可靠环境，又可能对同一个全局 harness 提出冲突要求。按表面任务类别优化，也会错过不同任务共享的决策能力。\n\n方法：用训练任务和核验轨迹归纳共同能力，生成保留这些要求的简化环境；冻结骨干，在固定能力树上积累和选择性继承模块。造环境者也更新自身 harness，执行时再按公开任务信息选择兼容配置。\n\n结果与结论：摘要给出未见基准平均增加26分，但主要结果、预算和消融被截断。方法明确：父模块继承要求成绩提高，局部模块准入只检查证据与可执行性，不要求涨分；实机材料主要展示两个场景案例。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，共享能力能否迁移，取决于简化世界是否保留关键决策关系。能力分组、合成环境和路由同时变化，当前不能把总体收益单独归给能力抽象，也不能据模块通过检查推断能力增强。","published_at":"2026-10-26","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 自适应课程与数据合成; 跨任务迁移","added_on":"2026-10-28","novelty_summary":"作者声称以共同能力组织多模态环境生成、模块演化与路由。本文证据：宿主验证器和训练轨迹指导 Creator、Explorer 的 harness 更新，版本与反馈跨轮保留；能力树拓扑和骨干固定，局部准入不要求成绩增加。相对 arxiv:2610.11345 训练任务合成器和推理器权重，本篇主要演化外部模块与造环境 harness；相对 arxiv:2610.24464 修共享执行接口支持组合，本篇按能力分支保留并路由多套配置。编辑推断：组织方式值得追踪，但缺少完整匹配消融和成本，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.36013","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.36013v1","title":"OmniBrain-0: A Unified Agentic Model for Embodied Intelligence","authors":"Xiaomi Embodied Intelligence Team; Yuechen Luo; Chong He; Fang Li; Shaoqing Xu; Jingkai Wang; Menglun Su; Jiaxin Liu; Shengyin Jiang; Zhiyi Lai; Long Chen; Longlong Wang; Liang Hu; Haochen Liu; Yuncheng Jiang; Hongwei Xie; Jieming Cui; Hanbing Li; Junjie Huang; Zhixiang Duan; Hexin Zhang; Weixiang Liang; Ying Gong; Yuhan Wang; Yong Pan; Pengna Li; Kangyi Wu; Ken Deng; Kun Ma; Fuxi Wen; Zhi-xin Yang; Hangjun Ye","affiliations":"University of Macau, Tsinghua University","abstract":"General-purpose embodied intelligence requires robots to coordinate diverse skills over long horizons, track task progress, and recover from failures. Specialist policies alone do not ensure task-level reliability, while powerful multimodal agents rely on costly reasoning and external experience that compact models struggle to reproduce. We introduce OmniBrain-0, a lightweight unified embodied agent that coordinates manipulation and navigation through a shared high-level decision model, integrating task understanding, planning, progress tracking, and feedback-driven recovery. Our progressive training framework combines embodied pretraining, domain-specialized agent distillation, and multi-teacher on-policy distillation (MOPD). It distills powerful teachers' interaction experience into manipulation and navigation experts, then consolidates their decision capabilities into OmniBrain-0. Unification therefore occurs within the learned decision model rather than only at the tool interface. We further introduce Rubric-Guided Recursive Self-Improvement (RSI), a data flywheel in which a Meta-Agent turns execution evidence into refined rubrics, step-level reminders, and verified trajectories for domain-expert updates before their reconsolidation into OmniBrain-0 through MOPD. We evaluate OmniBrain-0 on LIBERO-Pro, LIBERO-Plus, RoboCasa365, RoboTwin 2.0, and R2R-CE Val-Unseen, as well as multiple real-world manipulation tasks. OmniBrain-0 combines strong cross-domain task performance with substantially lower inference and execution overhead than its closed-source teacher, demonstrating efficient transfer and consolidation of embodied capabilities into a compact unified agent.","tldr":"背景与问题：小型具身模型既难复制强教师的长期规划与恢复，又会进入固定示范未覆盖的失败状态。分别训练操作和导航专家，也不自动得到统一的任务决策能力。\n\n方法：先从教师交互学习领域专家，再让专家监督统一模型自身生成的决策。自改进部分根据执行证据修订行为提醒，固定权重验证提醒后，收集环境确认的成功与成功恢复轨迹，更新专家并重新蒸馏进统一模型。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称多个仿真基准和真实操作任务上兼顾表现与较低开销；所给正文缺少主要结果及 RSI 消融，不能确定总体优势中多少来自自改进，而非预训练和教师蒸馏。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，失败轨迹在这里主要用于找采集方向，真正进入训练的是经过验证的成功恢复。应分别验收提醒能否改善采集、恢复数据能否改善专家，以及重新整合是否损害另一领域能力。","published_at":"2026-10-26","topics":"具身 RSI; 自适应训练经验; 技能蒸馏","added_on":"2026-10-28","novelty_summary":"作者声称把准则提醒、验证轨迹、领域专家更新和统一模型再蒸馏连接成循环。本文证据：环境结果验证成功轨迹，模型分析失败并修提醒，新模型交互进入下一轮；未见元 agent 或训练算法自身改进的证据。相对 arxiv:2605.09998 在线同步演化 harness 与模型，本篇采用领域专家更新后再整合到统一决策模型；相对 arxiv:2610.36826 用动态准则指导外部 harness，本篇把相关经验进一步写入权重。编辑推断：是具身采集与蒸馏的整合，RSI 独立贡献未能核验；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.35598","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.35598v1","title":"Evolve on Graph: Self-Evolving Knowledge Graph Reasoning without Question Annotations","authors":"Zongyuan Sun; Shuai Zhao; Ke Shu; Ziyue Zhu; Shangyang Wu; Yuanlin Lin; Tao Wang; Shiyue Li; Yingjun Du; Anh Tuan Luu; Haoran Luo","affiliations":"北京邮电大学；University of Helsinki；University of Amsterdam；Nanyang Technological University","abstract":"Knowledge graphs (KGs) provide reliable external knowledge for multi-hop factual reasoning with large language models (LLMs), yet most KGs in real-world domains such as finance and industry lack question--answer (QA) annotations. Without such annotations, existing methods struggle to improve LLM graph reasoning: training-free agents cannot improve their exploration through interaction; reinforcement learning (RL) agents depend on QA data annotated by humans or synthesized by closed-source models; and training data is typically built offline, so its topology mix is fixed and cannot follow the agent's ability. We propose Evolve on Graph (EoG), a framework that lets an LLM self-evolve its graph reasoning without any QA annotations. Through Graph Self-Play, a single LLM alternates between a Proposer that poses questions and a Solver that answers them. To make questions verifiable, Symbolically Verifiable Topology Synthesis (SVTS) samples reasoning topologies on the KG and executes the corresponding first-order logic queries, yielding topology skeletons with correct and complete answer sets; guided by a skeleton, the Proposer explores the graph to pose a multi-hop question. To let task topologies follow the Solver, a Boundary-Aware Graph Curriculum rewards the Proposer by the Solver's score variance, keeping questions at the Solver's capability boundary so that complex topologies enter training as the Solver improves. On six benchmarks over Freebase, Wikidata, and an industrial KG, EoG consistently outperforms prompting-, retrieval-, and agent-based methods, showing that LLM graph reasoning can improve through self-play without QA annotations. Our code is available at https://github.com/Szy5/EoG","tldr":"背景与问题：目标知识图谱没有问答标注时，冻结 agent 无法学习探索，训练 agent 又依赖人工或外部模型造题；离线固定的推理结构还会逐渐偏离求解器能力。\n\n方法：先在图上执行逻辑查询取得完整答案，再让同一模型探索并把查询骨架写成问题。求解正确性训练答题角色，求解分数的方差训练出题角色，使后续题目偏向尚未掌握但仍可解的区域；两角色共享参数。\n\n结果与结论：六个基准覆盖公开与工业图谱，正文称7B模型平均 Hit@1 比最强基线高7.46。主要结果与课程消融被截断；标注基线的奖励还少了格式项，不能认为训练问题来源是唯一差异。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可靠性增量来自把答案锚定到可执行查询，而非让模型相互认可。查询答案正确仍不保证自然语言问题忠实表达了查询；文本相似度检查也不足以排除所有训练测试重叠。","published_at":"2026-10-26","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 模型—数据共演化; 自进化策略训练","added_on":"2026-10-28","novelty_summary":"作者声称无问答标注地共同学习图探索与出题。本文证据：知识图谱查询执行提供答案，求解 F1 与格式反馈更新共享模型，求解分数方差改变出题策略和后续课程；外层训练规则固定。相对 arxiv:2610.11345 独立参数的合成器—推理器共训练，本篇共享参数，并以图查询替代模型生成参考答案；相对 arxiv:2610.13285 学生—专家筛选，本篇训练出题者且不依赖外部专家答案。编辑推断：验证来源与任务结构有明确变化，尚未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.35579","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.35579v1","title":"Infinity Machine: a self-improving AI agent for research","authors":"Harish Santhanalakshmi Ganesan","affiliations":"Independent researcher","abstract":"We present the Infinity Machine, a self-improving AI agent that we use for research on problems whose answers aprogram or data can check. Each candidate solution is produced by a full tool-using agent that works for up to an hour in a fresh sandbox; proposers see only a public score, and a private split decides what counts. The harness itself(prompts, tools, skills, playbook, meta agent) is an editable genome, changed only through a kernel-enforced gate with held-out and cost checks. An autonomous mode goes from a plain-text goal to a verified report with no human step: an agent picks an open problem and writes its verifier, the kernel calibrates it, an adversarial agent audits it, and an agent that never sees the verifier re-checks the result. Across fourteen problems in six days, for about $180 of model usage, the system produced four results beyond the published state of the art on catalogued open problems in quantum information: a certified depolarizing-channel threshold point p = 0.064966, a qutrit positivity frontier of 0.2910672, a 44-gate depth-6 Golay state preparation, and a stabilizer-rank bound chi(T^7) \u003c= 10. It also cut SABRE qubit-routing overhead from 68,559 to 12,087 added gates. In hardware, it cut the energy per MAC of an open 8x8 INT8 systolic tile by 77.7% through a full open RTL-to-GDS flow, bit-exact. Three fully autonomous runs ended in honestties with public records; one audit caught a stale record, and one agent-written score pointing the wrong way went unnoticed. We report the failures as carefully: the one self-derived harness generation was rejected on cost, proposers gamed lenient scorers four times, and operator changes were decisive for several results.","tldr":"背景与问题：科研 agent 找到更高分解，不代表研究程序变强；可读取的宽松评分器还可能被迅速利用。研究成果、人工干预和自主修改需要分别核算。\n\n方法：把解搜索与自身 harness 修改分开：完整工具 agent 搜索候选，固定内核控制评分与成本，自身提示和元程序只能经门控更新。全自主模式另让模型出题、写验证器，经校准、攻击审查和不看原验证器的复核后报告结果。\n\n结果与结论：材料列出多项程序核验的科研结果，但相关活动有显著人工设计与修补。唯一自生 playbook 修改因成本超限被拒；三个全自主运行均追平纪录，检查还漏过一次评分方向错误。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，本篇最有价值的是明确披露自主改进没有成功落地。科研产物突破不能替代递归增益证据；多模型复核仍可能共同漏错，且硬件能耗来自工艺流程估计，并非芯片实测。","published_at":"2026-10-26","topics":"预算受限研究搜索; RSI 可证伪性与治理; 能力归因","added_on":"2026-10-28","novelty_summary":"作者声称以可编辑 genome 和固定内核支持科研及门控自改进。本文证据：执行评分、保留任务和成本检查约束修改，但唯一自生代被拒，未展示被接受的新改进程序产生后续收益。相对 arxiv:2603.19461 已有可编辑任务及元程序，本篇强调内核门控、研究问题生成与盲复核；相对 arxiv:2610.09426 构建研究环境，本篇进一步运行自主选题与验证，但样本仅三次且均追平。编辑推断：贡献主要落在研究系统与失败审计，不能把外部成果记为递归成功；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.35453","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.35453v1","title":"Beyond Federated Learning: Decentralized Agentic Systems for Self-Evolving Clinical Intelligence","authors":"Haoyuan Li; Mathias Funk; Aaqib Saeed","affiliations":"Eindhoven University of Technology","abstract":"Clinical expertise is inherently distributed: it resides not in any single dataset or institution but in the accumulated reasoning experiences of thousands of clinicians navigating diverse patient populations, resource constraints, and evolving treatment protocols. Yet current approaches to scaling medical AI, from centralized large language models to federated learning, remain anchored to a data-centric paradigm that treats knowledge as static parameters to be aggregated. In this Perspective, we argue for a fundamental shift from data aggregation to experience aggregation. We propose Decentralized Agentic Systems (DAS), a framework in which distributed AI agents operating across healthcare institutions synthesize collective clinical intelligence by sharing abstracted reasoning trajectories rather than raw data or model parameters. Unlike federated learning, which averages numerical gradients across homogeneous model architectures, DAS exchanges structured records of clinical reasoning, specifically the sequence of observations, hypotheses, tool invocations, and outcome feedback that constitute diagnostic experience. We examine the architectural principles, deployment considerations, governance requirements, and critical open challenges of this framework, laying the groundwork for a collaborative medical AI ecosystem where distributed expertise autonomously adapts to the complexities of longitudinal patient care.","tldr":"背景与问题：跨医院共享参数或预测，未必能传递诊断过程中的适用条件、工具选择和纠错经验；机构差异又使经验直接复用可能失效。\n\n方法：这篇观点文章建议把本地观察、假设、行动和结果抽象为标准化推理轨迹，汇集后通过检索、知识图谱或推理模板返回各机构。反馈设想包括临床结果和专家修正，但如何衡量经验价值仍被明确列为开放问题。\n\n结果与结论：提供的是架构原则与治理讨论，没有多机构实验、学习曲线或相对联邦方法的实测优势。推理可读、可共享，不等于已证明跨场景有效或隐私得到保障。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，值得研究的是经验携带哪些临床条件才能被其他节点采用，而非仅把共享单位从梯度改成文字。应先用受控跨机构任务检验迁移、误导传播和语义泄露；当前不能认定形成了可运行的递归改进机制。","published_at":"2026-10-26","topics":"经验迁移; 外部记忆与规则更新; RSI 可证伪性与治理","added_on":"2026-10-28","novelty_summary":"作者声称跨机构交换抽象推理轨迹可形成集体自演化。本文证据仅支持概念架构：临床结果、工具反馈和专家修正进入经验，经验再影响本地推理；经验筛选效用和具体聚合算法尚未确定，无递归实验。相对 arxiv:2610.18083 已实现带条件的研究经验共享，本篇转向临床异构节点，但没有证明场景转换带来机制创新；相对 arxiv:2610.19386 的可执行记忆维护，本篇缺少具体维护与验证规则。编辑推断：属于相邻的分布式经验学习提案；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.35434","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.35434v1","title":"Skill$^{\\infty}$: Recursive Self-Improvement for Agent Skill Optimization","authors":"Wangcheng Tao; Zhanglu Yan; Han Wu; Weng-Fai Wong","affiliations":"National University of Singapore；City University of Hong Kong","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement (RSI), in which a system also improves the way it improves, is a long-standing aspiration on the path to AGI. Language agents increasingly store procedural knowledge in reusable skills. Optimizing skills offers a direct way to achieve RSI, because the optimization procedure itself can be encoded as a skill. Existing skill optimizers, however, follow a hand-designed procedure. Even methods that evolve a meta-skill confine it to a fixed pipeline and relearn it for each task. We present Skill$^{\\infty}$, which makes skill optimization recursively self-improving: a meta agent follows a meta-skill to optimize task skills and optimizes the meta-skill itself using the same procedure. The optimization is agent-led. The meta agent diagnoses execution traces, proposes candidates, requests independent reviews, and allocates the search budget. The meta-skill defines these steps, allowing self-improvement to rewrite them. This meta-skill is also decoupled from task skills, refined on multiple skill optimization tasks and then reused to optimize task skills across diverse domains. As in deployment, skills at both levels are standard packages loaded through native skill discovery. On 83 SkillsBench tasks, Skill$^{\\infty}$ reaches a pass rate of 60.7%, compared with 56.4% for human-curated skills and 54.5% for SkillEvolver.","tldr":"背景与问题：技能优化器即使会改任务技能，诊断、审查和预算分配仍常由固定流程决定；逐任务重学元技能，也难积累可迁移的优化方法。\n\n方法：把优化程序本身写成技能，用它优化任务技能，也用同一程序修订自身。元技能按固定预算下带来的任务技能增益评分，在多个优化任务上改好后复用；执行验证器提供结果，隔离上下文的审查者检查修改实质与实际激活。\n\n结果与结论：SkillsBench 测试通过率为60.7%，不优化元技能时为55.9%，支持元级修改有额外价值。但分领域仍有回退；材料未提供完整成本、重复方差及元任务与目标任务的划分细节。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，这是本批最直接把“怎样改进”作为受评估产物的工作。可编辑程序仍受固定评分和核心职责约束，持续自加速并未由此成立；应优先核对新旧元技能同起点、同总费用的优化收益。","published_at":"2026-10-26","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 跨任务迁移; 预算受限研究搜索","added_on":"2026-10-28","novelty_summary":"作者声称同一个可编辑元技能既优化任务技能，也优化自身，并跨领域复用。本文证据：执行轨迹、固定验证器的任务增益及隔离审查指导元技能修订；优化后的元技能回到后续优化流程，去掉自改进的对照下降。相对 arxiv:2603.19461 已开放元程序修改，本篇将程序封装为原生发现的技能，并按内层优化增益评分；相对 arxiv:2610.21791 累积编排技能和原则，本篇更直接用同一程序评价并改写元技能。编辑推断：递归对象和收益对照更明确，但未见完整预算及划分，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.35316","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.35316v1","title":"RSIV-Harness: A Recursive Self-Improvement Harness Framework for Open-Domain Conversational Text-to-Visualization","authors":"Jiawei Lu; Chen Zhang; Jinwei Lu; Yuanwei Song; Yuanfeng Song; Raymond Chi-Wing Wong","affiliations":"The Hong Kong Polytechnic University；The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology","abstract":"Users often request charts without knowing which database or table holds the relevant data. Such requests may be ambiguous, and users may ask follow-up questions to deepen their analysis or iteratively refine existing charts. A useful assistant must therefore discover relevant data sources among heterogeneous databases, ask clarifying questions when needed, and track evolving user intent while preserving constraints established in earlier turns. Yet recent text-to-visualization agents typically rely on static agent harnesses that are predefined and remain unchanged despite recurring failures across tasks. To address this limitation, we introduce RSIV-Harness, which keeps the language model weights fixed and applies Recursive Self-Improvement to revise the surrounding harness from the agent's own failure traces. To balance flexible self-improvement with stability, we introduce a four-layer framework that evaluates proposed harness revisions through anchor and memory checks, refining those that pass and restoring the best validated harness otherwise. We further introduce ODAC-Vis, a benchmark with 640 tasks for Open-Domain, Ambiguous, and Conversational text-to-visualization that jointly evaluates open-domain data discovery, ambiguity resolution, multi-turn visualization refinement, and executable chart generation. Experiments show that a single round of RSIV-Harness improves all six evaluation metrics relative to the seed harness, with particularly large gains in executability (+28.02 points) and chart structure (+34.01 points), demonstrating the ability to learn from task-solving experience and turn recurring failures across tasks into substantial performance improvements.","tldr":"背景与问题：开放数据库中的可视化请求同时涉及找数据、澄清歧义与保留多轮约束。静态 harness 会重复犯错，而按失败修改规则又可能破坏已经会做的任务。\n\n方法：固定模型，根据跨任务失败轨迹修改周围提示、工具与控制逻辑；验证锚点和历史成功记录共同约束提交，失败则恢复最佳版本。新基准把数据发现、澄清与可执行图表串在同一对话里，并按领域留出评测。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称单轮修改使可执行性增加28.02个百分点，图表结构增加34.01个百分点；主要结果、消融和方法细节被截断，无法核对收益分布与预算。只展示一轮也不足以支持长期递归增长。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，新价值更可能在任务合同与回归检查的结合，而非再提出失败驱动 harness 修改。最佳验证分数不下降是选择规则的性质，不能自动推出未见领域表现或所有旧能力不退化。","published_at":"2026-10-26","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 自改进稳定性; 跨任务迁移","added_on":"2026-10-28","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过失败轨迹演化可视化 harness，并用锚点与回归记忆稳定提交。本文证据：模型固定，执行和查询图表监督提供反馈，获准 harness 跨任务保留；摘要结果仅涉及一轮，未显示更新器改进。相对 arxiv:2604.25850 已有可观测编辑与回退，本篇扩展到开放数据发现和多轮图表约束；相对 arxiv:2610.14828 的办公产物迁移评测，本篇同时提出专用方法和基准。编辑推断：主要是领域化实现与评测扩展，理论保护限于规定记录和检查；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.35193","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.35193v1","title":"Trustworthy Recursive Self-Improvement in the Era of Large Models: Foundation, Risks, Evaluation and Open Challenges","authors":"Jiayue Pu; Ang Gao; Jinyi Bai; Qipeng Wang; Tongyu Wen; Jiahao Zhao; Keyu Qu; Junhao Zhang; Chenglei Shen; Zhongxiang Sun; Jun Xu; Xiao Zhang","affiliations":"中国人民大学高瓴人工智能学院；中国科学院大学","abstract":"AI systems built around large models increasingly use experience and feedback to make persistent changes to models, prompts, memories, tools, and workflows. Recursive self-improvement (RSI) extends this process to inductive biases and to the mechanisms that govern future updates, which can themselves be revised and reused across improvement cycles. Yet self-modification alone does not guarantee trustworthy improvement. Reported gains may reflect flawed evaluations, previously acquired capabilities may deteriorate, and compliance with behavioral constraints may weaken. Compromised artifacts or sensitive information may also persist in successor systems. Changes to improvement mechanisms may invalidate earlier verification results and make human oversight less effective. This survey presents an operational definition and process framework for RSI and organizes the requirements for trustworthy RSI into four interconnected themes: genuine and sustained improvement; behavioral constraints, alignment, and fairness; system security and privacy; and transparency and controllability. We examine these themes from three perspectives: Improvement Validity, Constraint Preservation, and Effective Oversight. This analysis covers improvement diagnosis, proposal generation, proposal evaluation, and update implementation (S1--S4), including the recursive application of these stages to improvement mechanisms (RI). We review risks, safeguards, and evaluation evidence for individual updates, effects inherited by successor systems, and revisions to improvement mechanisms, while distinguishing direct RSI findings from evidence in related systems. Finally, we examine evaluation settings, identify requirements for independent and longitudinal assessment, and discuss applications and open research problems.","tldr":"背景与问题：系统得分提高时，旧能力、安全约束和人工干预能力可能同时退化；改进程序本身被修改后，过去的验证也未必继续有效。\n\n方法：综述按诊断、提案、评估和实施定位风险，并区分任务策略、学习选择及其更新程序。它将单次更新、后继继承和元级修改分开审计，要求能力、约束与监督证据对应同一系统版本和轨迹。\n\n结果与结论：附录对20项代表研究的260个维度单元进行编码，其中40项有针对性原始来源检查，其余保留注释位置。这是文献证据整理，不是系统复现；核心联合证据分析被截断，不能自行补出覆盖率结论。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可迁移价值在于检查“同一条演化轨迹上是否同时更强且仍可控”。分别引用不同系统的能力、安全与回滚实验，无法拼成一个可信 RSI 系统；修改发生、被继承和真正有益也应分别记账。","published_at":"2026-10-26","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; RSI 评测与迁移; 能力归因","added_on":"2026-10-28","novelty_summary":"作者声称提供按主张组织的可信 RSI 联合证据框架。本文证据：区分策略、归纳偏置与更新函数，并编码修改、保留、复用及后续评价；本篇不运行自改进闭环。相对 arxiv:2610.27610 统计产物评价与改进者比较的报告落差，本篇扩展到同版本能力、约束和监督的联合证据；相对 arxiv:2610.18842 的物理递归分级，本篇覆盖大模型系统的多类可信要求。编辑推断：属于审计框架整合，不能记作新增递归能力；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.34965","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.34965v1","title":"The Target Agent Is Its Own Best Critic but a Poor Proposer: Self-Improved Red Teaming","authors":"Mintong Kang; Stephen Rawls; Melissa Kazemi Rad; Jian Ni; Bo Li","affiliations":"University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign；Capital One","abstract":"Automatic red teaming increasingly relies on large language models (LLMs) to iteratively diagnose failed attacks and propose improved adversarial prompts or injections. Although prior work strengthens this loop through prompt engineering and search-harness design, the mechanisms underlying its two core roles, criticism and attack proposal, has not been explored. To further investigate the core roles and therefore improve red teaming effectiveness, we disentangle two design choices: whether criticism is generated by the target session itself (self-criticism) or by a separately instantiated critic (external criticism), and whether that criticism is translated into the next attack by the target session (self-proposal) or by a separate attacker (external proposal). Through our analysis, we find that self-criticism is more effective because it is grounded in the target's live execution context, including observations, constraints, and available reasoning; removing reasoning reduces downstream attack success by 6%-17%. In contrast, self-proposal is substantially less effective because awareness of the adversarial objective induces explicit refusal and non-refusal sandbagging. These findings motivate a role-separated red-teaming approach: the target session diagnoses why an attack failed, while a separately instantiated attacker generates the next proposal. On DTAP-BENCH, spanning Telecom, Workflow, CRM, and Code domains, under both direct misuse and indirect threat models, as well as multiple agent frameworks, this configuration achieves 63.2% overall attack success rate (ASR), much higher than baselines. Our results show that effective automatic red teaming depends not only on model capability and search strategy, but also on how execution context and adversarial responsibility are distributed across model sessions.","tldr":"背景与问题：自动红队常把失败诊断与攻击改写交给同一模块，混淆了两种要求：诊断需要执行现场，提案却可能因目标会话意识到攻击目的而受阻。\n\n方法：固定底层模型身份，让被攻击会话利用当前观察、约束和推理诊断失败，再把诊断交给独立攻击者改写。环境状态验证器判断恶意目标是否完成；每次重置任务状态，保留攻击历史继续搜索。\n\n结果与结论：四类业务环境、两种威胁模型中，自批评配外部提案较全外部配置提高攻击成功率5.9个百分点；改为目标自行提案则下降17个百分点。低拒绝配置仍退化，但这不能证明模型具有内部阻挠意图。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，诊断能力与执行修改的行为应分别测量。现场信息消融支持角色分离，但这里改进的是攻击候选，没有展示目标系统或改进程序持续增强。","published_at":"2026-10-26","topics":"失败诊断; 能力归因","added_on":"2026-10-27","novelty_summary":"作者声称执行现场内的批评与独立会话的攻击提案应分离。本文证据：固定模型身份比较角色配置，以环境状态验证攻击结果，失败诊断进入下一次候选生成；没有权重、持久技能或改进器更新。相对 Evo²（arxiv:2610.13025）训练修改者和反思者，本篇隔离会话分工，且研究的是攻击搜索，两者无匹配性能比较。编辑推断：是有受控证据的角色配置研究，与持续 RSI 相邻；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.34938","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.34938v1","title":"How Do Coding-Agent Harnesses Self-Evolve? An Empirical Study of Retrospective Adaptation","authors":"Christoph Treude; Sebastian Baltes","affiliations":"Singapore Management University；Heidelberg University","abstract":"Coding agents can adapt their harnesses, the software, configuration, and instructions used to run them, based on experience from earlier tasks, but whether these adaptations improve their behavior on later tasks remains unclear. We study \\retro, a skill that asks an agent to review a completed session and propose harness changes, and ask what changes it proposes and whether implemented changes reduce repeated work on later tasks. We ran Claude Code on 30 SWE-bench Verified issues, qualitatively coded the 125 proposals from \\retro, implemented 24, and evaluated 12 harness changes on later issues from the same repositories in fresh sessions with and without each change. Most proposals referred to an event in the session, but 18 of 43 lint-related proposals recommended a practice regardless of what had happened. Among the seven evaluations in which sessions without the change encountered the targeted problem, two changes eliminated the targeted action, one reduced its occurrence, four showed no reduction, and some changes added work on unrelated issues. Harness self-evolution requires more than generating and implementing changes: it needs ways to establish whether a change helps on later tasks and to revise or remove changes that do not.","tldr":"背景与问题：编码 agent 复盘后留下配置和说明，不代表改动能帮助后续任务：经验可能过窄、未被读取，或被读取却没有改变行为。\n\n方法：研究者筛选并实施复盘建议，在同仓库后续问题上逐项比较原始与修改后的 harness，跟踪目标问题是否出现、经验是否被查阅、目标动作是否重现；另用无关问题检查额外负担。这是有人类选择与评价的适配研究。\n\n结果与结论：七个信息充分的迁移事件中，两项修改消除目标动作，一项减少，四项没有减少。已知失败清单覆盖不足时，即使被读取也未奏效；任务成功没有一致改善，减少重复动作也未稳定缩短耗时。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可迁移经验需要明确覆盖范围，而非只证明来自真实轨迹。单项行为审计补足总体涨分，但任务经过定向选择，不能估计普通任务中的收益频率，更不能把少做检查直接视为更好。","published_at":"2026-10-26","topics":"RSI 评测与迁移; 经验迁移; 失败诊断","added_on":"2026-10-27","novelty_summary":"作者声称逐项检验复盘适配在后续问题上的行为效果。本文证据：人工选择建议和迁移任务，执行轨迹提供经验，原始与修改 harness 的新会话比较验证效果；没有自主多轮淘汰更新闭环。相对 AHE（arxiv:2604.25850）以编辑预测和后续结果组织演化，本篇一次只迁移一项适配；相对 CFOE（arxiv:2610.22984）审计失败经验泛化，本篇细分问题出现、覆盖、读取和动作变化。编辑推断：补充迁移失效机制的实证，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.34649","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.34649v1","title":"RobotAgentBench: Towards Open-world Robot Autonomy","authors":"Lingjun Mao; Jinglin Cao; Lukun He; Wenpeng Xu; Yuchen Yan; Hengyu Jin; Zijun Zhang; Jinzhou Tang; Songyao Jin; Ziche Liu; Yifei Shao; Junbo Huang; Fang Nan; Ruobing Han; Ziqiao Xi; Ziming Xu; Shuang Liang; Sibo Zhu; Wenyi Wu; Xinyue Wang; Yiming Huang; Xinkai Zou; Gao Zhu; Kun Zhou; Biwei Huang","affiliations":"Aether AI；University of California San Diego；University of California Davis","abstract":"Recent advances in vision-language-action (VLA) and world-action models (WAMs) have significantly improved robotic manipulation, yet deploying robots in the open world demands a higher level of autonomy beyond executing predefined tasks. Robot agents offer a promising paradigm for this transition, integrating task discovery, contextual reasoning, physical execution, and adaptive recovery into a closed interaction loop. However, existing benchmarks largely evaluate isolated capabilities, failing to capture the complexity of open-world robot autonomy. We introduce RobotAgentBench (RAB), a comprehensive benchmark for evaluating robot agents in realistic, open-world household environments. Through an agent-assisted, human-in-the-loop real-to-sim pipeline, RAB constructs 50 diverse household layouts with interactive objects and physically grounded tasks, encompassing 90 atomic tasks, 18 short-horizon tasks, 8 long-horizon tasks, and 4 open-ended scenarios. RAB provides a multi-level evaluation of robot agent capabilities: (1) task-level assessments systematically examine five complementary dimensions: task discovery, context reasoning, manipulation, failure recovery, and robustness; (2) scenario-level evaluation assesses how agents integrate these capabilities to autonomously fulfill high-level user needs. Furthermore, RAB enables systematic comparisons of standalone VLA/WAM models and diverse robot agent architectures under a unified planning-execution-verification framework. Extensive experiments reveal substantial gaps between manipulation and autonomy, demonstrate the advantages of agentic architectures and recursive self-improvement, and highlight the remaining challenges toward open-world robot autonomy.","tldr":"背景与问题：预设目标下的操作成功，不能说明机器人能自行发现家务、理解隐含需求并处理失败；把规划与操作分开测量，也会遗漏两者配合时的故障。\n\n方法：RobotAgentBench 在家庭场景中分别测任务发现、情境推理、执行、恢复和扰动适应，再以开放场景检验整合能力。其 RSI 配置让编码 agent 按执行反馈创建和修订控制工具，将有效工具保留到后续尝试。\n\n结果与结论：可见正文称混合执行和工具积累有益，实机表现下降但相对排序大体一致；主要实验段落被截断，无法核对 RSI 效果量及等预算对照。附录显示主要执行困难来自运动可行性和动作未完成，正确调用接口仍不足。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，基准价值在于把“知道做什么”与“实际做成”分别观察。相较已有具身迁移审计，材料更清楚地展示自治维度，尚不足以确认工具继承收益超出更多尝试。","published_at":"2026-10-26","topics":"具身持续学习评测; 具身 RSI; 能力归因","added_on":"2026-10-27","novelty_summary":"作者声称提供开放家庭自治评测并展示 harness RSI 优势。本文证据：控制工具随执行反馈修订并跨尝试保留，但关键结果和预算对照缺失。相对 SEAR（arxiv:2610.18792）重点隔离重试、技能继承和迁移，本篇扩展任务发现、情境判断及综合场景评价；不能据覆盖更广推断归因更强。编辑推断：可作为具身 RSI 的评测补充，改进器递归增强未获验证；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.34386","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.34386v1","title":"ParetoRSI-Gym: Can AI Agents Improve Language Models Across Multiple Domains?","authors":"Haojin Wang; Yangzhen Wu; Zeyi Chen; Jian Xie; Jiaying Ye; Lili Meng; Shuyun Tang; Shangding Gu; Dawn Song","affiliations":"University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign；University of California, Berkeley；The Ohio State University；University of Washington；Google","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement (RSI) requires an agentic system to design, train, and evaluate its own successor. Data-driven post-training is a central part of that loop, yet existing evaluations measure it on a single benchmark, where an agent selects from a static pool or distills a stronger model to push one score up in one run. Real post-training is multi-domain, and a gain in one domain has to be weighed against a regression in another. We propose ParetoRSI-Gym, in which an agent searches for data, curates it, trains, reads back per-domain results, and repeats, with everything but the data held fixed: the initial LLM, the five domains (math, code, finance, medicine, science), the toolset, and the SFT pipeline. Generalization benchmarks in each domain separate capability gains from overfitting to the scores the agent optimizes against. Across three agent systems, three base models, five rounds and multiple seeds, the strongest system, Claude Code with Opus-5, raises the generalization scores of its proxy-best checkpoint by 9.2% relative to the starting model (+2.3 absolute points), averaged with equal weight over three base models and five domains, with a single-domain relative gain of up to 63% (medicine on Ministral-3-3B). Further analysis shows that the harness matters as much as the model it drives, and that each agent keeps a unique data selection strategy. We see our work as a step towards evaluation of RSI systems in real-world machine learning engineering.","tldr":"背景与问题：自主后训练若只追逐一个反馈分数，会掩盖其他领域退化，也难区分数据选择真正改善能力还是拟合开发题。\n\n方法：agent 搜索和筛选公开数据，根据五领域反馈修订选数原则并选择后续训练起点；数据、模型池与经验跨轮保留。训练流程受限，但允许有限超参数选择；最终用未向 agent 开放的同领域任务检验泛化。\n\n结果与结论：最强系统按开发分数选出的检查点，跨模型与领域平均提高2.3分；九种配置中七种的开发最佳轮并非末轮。主表显示数学等领域仍有退化，各领域分别取最佳轮的拼接结果也不是可部署模型。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，平均上涨与持续、多领域共同改善明显分离。该评测能暴露后续轮次损害，却没有证明更新后的模型接管研究者角色；“自身后继”主要体现为被优化模型的版本延续。","published_at":"2026-10-25","topics":"RSI 研究环境与评测; 训练数据选择; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-27","novelty_summary":"作者声称评测多领域、反馈驱动的数据策展循环。本文证据：开发成绩与轨迹反馈修改选数原则，数据池和检查点跨轮继承，隐藏评估测泛化；研究者模型未显示被后继替换。相对 DataSense-Bench（arxiv:2610.12190）禁止训练的事前选数审计，本篇允许真实训练纠偏；相对 VibeTraining-Bench（arxiv:2610.26342）开放多组件，本篇收窄干预以观察多域权衡。编辑推断：是协议推进，非已证明的持续帕累托改进；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.33845","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.33845v1","title":"Build, Don't Play: Self-Improving LLM Research Agents Develop a Hearthstone Battlegrounds AI That Rivals Top Players","authors":"Changlian Ma; Limin Wang","affiliations":"Nanjing University；Shanghai AI Laboratory","abstract":"Can LLM agents carry a hard real-world problem from raw data to a system that holds its own against people? We study this in Hearthstone Battlegrounds, an eight-player auto-battler with stochastic shops and battles, hidden information and nearly a thousand interacting cards. We present AutoTavern, a self-improving research system: specialised LLM research agents share a typed research memory, every claim passes verification gates, and live games close the loop, so the agents improve the simulator, opponents and policy and, from the same feedback, their own research process; a human sets goals and rules on ambiguous mechanics. In 20 days AutoTavern built TavernGym, the first faithful, full-content reproduction of the live game, and delivered 23 versions of TavernAgent, trained with PPO against opponents calibrated to real games. TavernAgent plays complete games on the live ladder by itself: its rating rose from 6,000 to about 15,000 and, on the public leaderboard's measure, its last 20 records average a placement of 1.60 with 80% first places, better than the server's ten highest-rated players on every statistic (2.34, 59%). TavernBench, 960 tasks in 40 scenarios, shows that the system the agents built is the strongest player: TavernAgent answers 91% of the play tasks against at most 63% for frontier LLMs, and decides in 0.03 s where they need up to 26 s; within the second a live turn allows, it keeps 90% and no LLM more than 26%. LLM agents build far better than they play. We will open-source TavernBench and TavernGym at https://github.com/MCG-NJU/AutoTavern.","tldr":"背景与问题：研究 agent 在模拟器中提高策略分数，可能只是利用错误规则或失真的对手；若这些结果进入共享记忆，还会误导后续研究。\n\n方法：AutoTavern 用真实对局回放校正模拟器、输入编码和对手，再训练专用游戏策略。研究发现经测试与未见种子复核后入库；被查出的研究错误进一步变成后续会话读取的规则或新增检查门控。\n\n结果与结论：同起点、同训练预算下，现实校准对手将主考场吃鸡率从20.9%提高到27.2%，支持纠正训练世界的价值。天梯成绩提供部署证据，但真人仍按 AI 指定按键，近期记录也不等于与顶尖玩家直接对战的受控比较。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，较强贡献是让现实差异回流到训练条件，并留下研究流程修改记录。尚缺冻结旧流程的同预算对照，不能从版本变强推断新增门控让研究者更有效；探索成本也远高于交付版本训练成本。","published_at":"2026-10-24","topics":"预算受限研究搜索; 执行证据驱动改进; 经验迁移","added_on":"2026-10-27","novelty_summary":"作者声称同时改进游戏策略、训练世界和研究过程。本文证据：真实对局差异触发修复，纠错形成持久经验与新增门控；对手校准有匹配训练对照，但研究流程增强没有相应隔离实验。相对 Athanor（arxiv:2610.21055）的自主后训练活动，本篇增加真实部署回流与检查规则修改；相对 AReaL-RSI（arxiv:2610.18083）的跨活动配置继承，本篇具体记录新增门控。编辑推断：流程改变可见，其独立收益仍待测；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.33799","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.33799v1","title":"MTA-Zero: Self-Improving Multimodal Deep Search via Online QA-Solver Co-training","authors":"Xiangyu Peng; Jiaxin Zhang; An Yan; Yu Li; Ran Xu; Zeyuan Chen; Chien-Sheng Wu","affiliations":"","abstract":"Multimodal large language models (MLLMs) have become strong visual reasoners, yet remain limited in open-world, multi-step search that requires grounding images, selecting tools, and integrating web evidence. Existing approaches typically construct and filter fixed offline corpora whose question distributions cannot adapt as the target deep-search agent improves. Building on MTA-Agent's image-grounded QA construction, we present MTA-Zero, an online multimodal QA-Solver co-training framework for self-improving multimodal deep-search agents that requires no precomputed multi-hop corpus. Starting from image-grounded VQA seed contexts, a trainable QA Generator retrieves evidence and constructs verified multi-hop questions online. A separate deep-search Solver then selects tools, gathers evidence, and answers the generated questions. To focus generation on the Solver's learning frontier, we derive a Goldilocks reward for the QA Generator from the Solver's group-wise rollout success rate: questions solved by all rollouts or by none receive zero reward, whereas questions near the current frontier are favored. We optimize the two policies independently with GRPO, without sharing parameters or gradients. Across six multimodal deep-search benchmarks, MTA-Zero improves a Qwen3-VL-8B Solver from 36.91% to 51.58% mean accuracy and achieves performance comparable to GPT-5 under the same agent workflow. The same framework also improves a newer Qwen3.6-27B Solver by 10.82 points. These results show that verified online question generation provides a policy-specific curriculum for continually improving multimodal deep-search agents.","tldr":"背景与问题：离线多模态搜索题库不会随求解者变强而调整；只奖励造题者让求解者失败，又会鼓励无答案或证据不足的问题。\n\n方法：造题策略在线检索证据并延长图像相关问题链，固定检查流程过滤含糊、泄漏和无需搜索的题。求解者多次独立作答：正确性训练求解策略，成败混合程度奖励造题策略，使后续题目跟随当前可学区域。\n\n结果与结论：六项深搜索基准中，8B 求解者平均准确率由36.91%升至51.58%。冻结造题策略时，有训练信号的问题比例随求解者变强下降；但完整性能消融被截断，无法核对造题策略更新的独立效果量。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，相较数学课程共训练，本篇推进的是外部证据约束下的多模态题目生成。正确性仍部分依赖模型裁判，人工抽查支持答案评分可靠性，却不认证所有生成题；无需预制多跳语料也不等于没有种子监督。","published_at":"2026-10-24","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 模型—数据共演化; 自进化策略训练","added_on":"2026-10-27","novelty_summary":"作者声称以在线问答—求解共训练替代固定多跳语料。本文证据：独立参数的两策略由同组作答结果更新，固定验证 harness 约束题目质量，后续课程随策略变化；答案先规则匹配，未匹配项由 gpt-5-mini 判断，人工抽查100项的一致率为98%。相对 SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）已有混合成败驱动的共训练，本篇增加图像种子、逐跳证据检索和问题合并约束。编辑推断：是领域与验证机制扩展，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.33684","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.33684v1","title":"More: Mode-Optimized Reasoning with Self-Adaptive Effort for Self-Evolving Agents","authors":"Dianxing Shi; Dingjie Fu; Tianyu Lei; Wangjie Qiu","affiliations":"Beihang University；Huazhong University of Technology","abstract":"Self-evolving training improves the performance of agents on difficult tasks through verifiable feedback, but it often applies costly deliberation uniformly across tasks. To address this problem, we propose Mode-Optimized Reasoning with Self-Adaptive Effort (MORE), a self-evolving training framework that adaptively selects both reasoning form and computational effort for each task. Specifically, MORE follows a two-stage training paradigm: (i) \\emph{Stage 1} establishes a compact prior over direct answering, short and long chain-of-thought, and code-based reasoning, and (ii) \\emph{Stage 2} self-evolves this prior with Mode-Adaptive and Test-time Effort PPO (MATE-PPO) on generated, verifiable task streams without curated data. By learning mode selection and token expenditure jointly, MORE allocates concise reasoning to tasks that permit it while retaining extended deliberation where it is useful. Across coding, mathematics, and general-reasoning benchmarks, MORE achieves consistent performance gains on Base and Coder backbones at model scales from 3B to 14B. During inference, MORE demonstrates higher accuracy and better efficiency, with markedly shorter response lengths and reduced inference time.","tldr":"背景与问题：可验证自训练容易把长推理固化为默认策略；仅减少 token 不能决定该直接回答、展开推导还是执行代码，固定预算又会落后于变化中的能力。\n\n方法：MORE 先用标注语料建立不同推理形式，再在自生成可验证任务上联合学习形式选择与计算量。执行正确性提供主要信号，近期成败和正确答案长度更新难度与预算，使下一批训练适配当前策略。\n\n结果与结论：可见分析中，自主选择在代码任务取得最高平均准确率，相比固定长推理减少52.8%的代码 token；部分其他任务略低于各自最强固定形式。主表和关键消融不完整，整体优势尚不能独立归给联合控制。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，推理形式与长度是两个干预对象，但奖励预设了简单题偏短、困难题偏长的偏好，不能把学到的分配全当作自主发现。首阶段用了人工语料，全流程无策展数据的表述不成立。","published_at":"2026-10-24","topics":"自进化策略训练; 预算受限研究搜索; 自适应训练经验","added_on":"2026-10-27","novelty_summary":"作者声称联合学习推理模式和预算的自演化训练。本文证据：验证结果更新策略，滚动统计更新控制状态；Stage 1 明确使用 AQuA-RAT 10.8K，只有后续任务流自生成。相对 HarnessMM（arxiv:2610.32813）绕过已确定动作的重复调用，本篇训练模型决定推理形式与长度，反馈和改进对象不同。编辑推断：是计算分配机制细化，固定控制规则未递归改写；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.33624","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.33624v1","title":"RSI Arena: Towards Recursive Self-Improvement with Human Feedback","authors":"Yue Huang; Yanbo Wang; Lichi Li; Yuanyuan Chen; Andreas Haupt; Xiaonan Luo; Zheyuan Liu; Jihye Choi; Felix Juefei-Xu; Xiangliang Zhang; Radha Poovendran; Misha Sra; Ying Liu; Ben Burtenshaw; Thomas Wolf; Alex Pentland; Zichen Chen; Zhangchen Xu","affiliations":"","abstract":"Can AI agents autonomously train useful language models and improve them using feedback from users? We introduce RSI Arena, a two-stage study of autonomous post-training as a step toward recursive self-improvement. Ten frontier models act as training agents, each starting from NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 Lightning 30B-A3B Base. During a six-day first stage, each agent has 1,000 GPU-hours and $300 in API credit on a shared 64-GPU cluster, independently selecting data, implementing training procedures, and choosing checkpoints. We evaluate their models on 20 benchmarks and through blind human evaluations. All ten agents produce working assistants, with the strongest model, trained by GPT-6 Astra, closing a median of 76% of the base-to-Instruct gap across 12 capability benchmarks. Its human-preference rating is also close to NVIDIA Instruct after statistical adjustment for answer length and formatting. In Stage 2, each agent receives the comparison records and votes involving its Stage 1 model and is given three additional days for further training. Using NVIDIA Instruct as a common reference across the two evaluation rounds, we observe an improvement from Stage 1 to Stage 2 in the style-adjusted relative rating of eight of the ten models. We show that benchmark gains were modest, with no clear link to preference gains, while some agents encouraged longer responses and one model showed increased harmful compliance on StrongREJECT. RSI Arena provides an auditable setting for studying how human feedback can guide autonomous model development. It takes a step toward recursive self-improvement with human feedback (RSIHF), in which people help define what improvement means for the AI systems they use.","tldr":"背景与问题：把基础模型训练成用户愿意使用的助手，需要兼顾能力、表达和行为边界；单个自动基准无法说明 agent 能否利用真实用户意见改进产品。\n\n方法：十个固定研究模型从同一基座出发，在共同资源上限内自主选数据、训练和提交。第一阶段结束后，将各自模型的匿名对战记录与人类投票反馈给原研究者，再训练新版本；两轮借同一参考模型比较。\n\n结果与结论：第二阶段十个模型中八个的风格调整偏好评分改善，但基准变化很小，且与偏好变化没有明确联系。部分模型增加回答长度，一项配置的有害配合明显上升，用户偏好增长不能代替能力和安全验收。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，本篇把改进目标扩展为互有冲突的维度。结果支持反馈后的再开发，但缺少不提供反馈却继续训练的匹配对照，尚不能单独归因用户反馈，也未展示研究者被自己训练的后继替换。","published_at":"2026-10-24","topics":"RSI 研究环境与评测; 自主后训练; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-27","novelty_summary":"作者声称迈向人类反馈驱动的 RSI。本文证据：研究 agent 根据用户比较记录继续更新目标模型，固定参考连接两轮评价；研究者自身未更新，且各系统实际预算使用差异很大。相对 Athanor（arxiv:2610.21055）已有自主通用后训练，本篇增加匿名用户偏好及第二阶段反馈；相对 ParetoRSI-Gym（arxiv:2610.34386），目标从能力向量扩展到用户选择，但干预也更宽。编辑推断：是评测与反馈来源的推进，递归研究能力未验证；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.33539","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.33539v1","title":"CoEvolve: Counterfactual-Guided Co-Evolution of Memory and Collaboration in Multi-Agent Systems","authors":"Xufei Shi; Derong Xu; Wei Chen; Yanyu Yao; Zhi Zheng; Tong Xu","affiliations":"中国科学技术大学认知智能全国重点实验室","abstract":"Large language model (LLM)-based multi-agent systems have demonstrated remarkable capabilities across diverse tasks. Yet their memory and collaboration architectures often remain static, constraining continued adaptation and improvement over time. Recent work addresses this limitation by evolving memory or collaboration based on interaction experience. However, updates to these interdependent components are not necessarily aligned: an evolved workflow may require experience that memory does not provide, while evolved memory may encode guidance that the workflow cannot use. To address this problem, we propose CoEvolve, a skill-centered framework for aligned memory--collaboration evolution. CoEvolve represents reusable local collaboration patterns as skills that link evolving collaboration decisions to their supporting memories. It further compares original and counterfactual trajectories to identify local evolution signals, which coordinate updates to the skill library, skill memory, and executor memories across rounds. Experiments on the ALFWorld and WebShop benchmarks confirm that CoEvolve achieves the best overall performance among the evaluated baselines, while ablation studies further validate the effectiveness of aligned co-evolution and counterfactual-guided evolution.","tldr":"背景与问题：多 agent 工作流和记忆分别更新，可能出现新分工没有相应经验，或新经验没有可调用入口；两边局部改进因此不保证整体获益。\n\n方法：CoEvolve 用可复用协作技能连接分工与记忆。失败后从相同分支点移除一个执行者并重跑，以结果差异寻找敏感片段，再同步修改协作技能、分配经验字段和执行记忆字段，让下一轮决策入口与信息支持一起变化。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称在 ALFWorld 和 WebShop 优于所列基线，并有联合更新与反事实消融；材料缺少结果表，无法核对效应、方差和额外重跑成本。正文能确认改变的是外部协作与记忆结构。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，把记忆需求绑定具体决策接口，比独立扩库更可检验。但移除执行者会改变后续轨迹，不能证明该角色缺少记忆就是失败原因；提示将这种差异直接解释为记忆不足，归因过强。","published_at":"2026-10-24","topics":"多智能体工作流演化; 外部记忆与规则更新; 失败诊断","added_on":"2026-10-27","novelty_summary":"作者声称以技能接口协调记忆—协作演化。本文证据：同分支点移除执行者后的重跑结果及过程信号驱动技能和记忆字段更新，候选参与下一轮；未显示更新算法自身增强。相对 STRATA（arxiv:2610.19386）维护经验图，本篇同步修改协作入口；相对 MASS（arxiv:2610.12176）工作流搜索后训练共享模型，本篇主要改变外部结构。编辑推断：接口对齐有具体差异，但局部因果归因和独立收益未核验；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.33465","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.33465v1","title":"LegoSR: A Unified Framework for Self-improving Agent-Guided Scientific Discovery","authors":"Hao Mao; Xu T. Liu; Peng Zhao; Shuai Lu; Yuntian Chen","affiliations":"The Hong Kong Polytechnic University；Eastern Institute of Technology, Ningbo；Amazon Web Services；University of Washington；Beijing EEO Education Technology；Jiangxi University of Finance and Economics","abstract":"Equation discovery solvers often use different data interfaces, equation representations and evaluation criteria, making their results difficult to compare. We present LegoSR, a unified framework for algebraic symbolic regression and differential equation discovery. LegoSR integrates seven solvers through a common equation representation and evaluation process, and supports searches constrained by partially known equations. Researchers can run solvers directly or use LegoSR Agent, which selects solvers and adapts searches based on solver knowledge, intermediate results and lessons from earlier tasks. On noisy ordinary and partial differential equation benchmarks, LegoSR Agent recovers nearly as many equations as the union of seven expert-tuned solvers and outperforms a generic agent with the same model, tools and budget by up to 29 percentage points. Three examples demonstrate basic use, adaptive solver selection and discovery guided by partial physical knowledge.","tldr":"背景与问题：方程发现求解器的数据格式、表达和原生评分不同，通用 agent 难以比较结果；只统一接口，也不会自动获得有效的选方法与处理噪声经验。\n\n方法：LegoSR 用共同方程表示和评价连接求解器，让 agent 根据残差、导数质量和搜索进展调整方法。提交方程在发现流程外对照参考答案评分，结果提炼成带数据条件的经验供后续任务使用，测试时排除同方程族经验。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称在噪声微分方程任务上接近七个专家调参求解器的恢复并集，相对同模型、工具和预算的通用 agent 最多高29个百分点。但比较同时移除了求解器知识、流程指导和经验库，无法隔离跨任务学习贡献。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，统一评价使失败结果也能支持换方法，跨任务经验带来的增长仍需单测。反馈依赖参考方程，不能外推为在未知科学规律上自主认证发现。","published_at":"2026-10-24","topics":"经验迁移; 预算受限研究搜索; 执行证据驱动改进","added_on":"2026-10-27","novelty_summary":"作者声称统一求解器并用实验经验调整科学搜索。本文证据：任务内数值反馈改变搜索，流程外参考方程评分形成跨任务经验，排除同族经验后检验使用；没有更新研究者权重或经验更新规则。相对 MetaExp（arxiv:2610.21492）直接训练经验学习行为，本篇依赖外部知识与经验库；相对 EvoBelief（arxiv:2610.12789）验证环境规律，本篇以已知方程作流程外评分。编辑推断：属于领域化经验适配，独立自改进收益仍待隔离；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.32813","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.32813v1","title":"HarnessMM: Recursive Self-Improvement for Harness Token Efficiency","authors":"Yuhua Jiang; Chang Xu; Feifei Gao; Li Zhao","affiliations":"Tsinghua University；Microsoft Research Asia","abstract":"Agent harnesses repeatedly invoke reasoning after tool feedback, even when an earlier call has already fixed the next action. We introduce HarnessMM (Harness Minus Minus), a method for improving harness token efficiency through guarded decision reuse and recursive self-improvement (RSI). RSI iteratively refines companion harness configurations from training feedback, with validation selecting the configuration for deployment. A controller at the model-tool boundary reuses resolved decisions to replace later reasoning callbacks while actor weights remain fixed. Executable Decision Graphs store exact actions, literal arguments, causal dependencies, and public guards. Guarded Decision Reuse activates these persistent decisions from observed receipts; Certified Callback Substitution executes them through the native interface and records removal of the registered slow callback. New semantic decisions, unsupported evidence, and selector abstention invoke the original actor again. The representation restricts what feedback may change, while complete-task measurements establish quality and cost. On HumanEval, HarnessMM preserves Codex success at 90.82\\% while reducing Tokens/task (k) from 66.72 to 47.02 (29.54\\% saving). For DeepSeek Harness, success rises from 71.43\\% to 85.71\\% while Tokens/task (k) fall from 96.28 to 11.62 (87.93\\% saving). A separate MBPP ablation measures 26.91\\% lower cost than single-use graphs and 19.52\\% lower cost than retained callbacks. These results establish guarded decision reuse as a practical way to reduce repeated reasoning in existing harnesses.","tldr":"背景与问题：工具返回后，harness 常重新调用模型，尽管下一动作及参数早已确定；加一个快速选择器若不真正移除原调用，反而增加开销。\n\n方法：HarnessMM 将已确定动作保存为带执行条件的图，真实工具回执满足条件便直接执行原参数，并记录被绕过的推理调用。需要新判断或条件不足时回到原模型；训练反馈另行修订外围配置，验证后冻结部署。\n\n结果与结论：HumanEval 的 Codex 配置保持成功率并减少29.54%的 token；MBPP 消融支持持久复用和移除调用各有作用。但部分 MBPP 配置成功率略降，主比较还包含上下文和收尾设置，不能把全部节省归给决策复用。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键是区分动作内容未知与执行时机未知。调用省略记录认证执行路径，不能认证动作正确；完整成本应包括写图、选择和失败回退，token 节省也不自动等于延迟或能源下降。","published_at":"2026-10-23","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 预算受限研究搜索; 执行证据驱动改进","added_on":"2026-10-27","novelty_summary":"作者声称带守卫的决策复用提高 harness 效率。本文证据：真实回执触发已有动作并省略注册调用，完整任务成本和独立消融检验节省；另有训练反馈—候选配置—验证保留循环，actor 权重固定。相对 HarnessPro（arxiv:2610.26770）在搜索选择中权衡性能和费用，本篇改变运行时是否再次推理；与 MORE（arxiv:2610.33684）训练形式和长度不同。编辑推断：核心贡献是执行替代合同，不能把外围配置搜索称为改进器递归增强；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.32770","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.32770v1","title":"On-Policy Self-Training: Data-Free Self-Improvement in Large Language Models","authors":"Leon Sick; Lukas Hoyer; Yannick Strümpler; Christian Reisswig; Timo Ropinski; Federico Tombari","affiliations":"Google；Ulm University","abstract":"On-policy self-distillation enables post-training foundation models without relying on stronger external teachers. However, existing approaches rely on ground-truth question-answer pairs, human-curated problem sets, or other supervised signals. In this work, we reformulate on-policy self-distillation as a self-training framework, driven by self-generated question-answer pairs and privileged reasoning demonstrations. We push supervision to the limit: guided solely by coarse, high-level topic descriptions, the model synthesizes its own curriculum of queries and privileged reasoning traces without access to any human-curated prompts or answers. We find that self-distillation on fully synthetic privileged information enables a model to improve across multiple domains while retaining its capabilities on domains it is not self-trained on. We demonstrate the generality of this framework across text and multimodal domains, achieving consistent self-improvement on standard language benchmarks and Visual Question Answering. Our findings demonstrate that foundation models possess rich latent capabilities that can be amplified without external task supervision or curated problem distributions.","tldr":"背景与问题：同模型自蒸馏通常仍需外部题目或参考解；直接拟合自生成答案，又会把答案错误当成训练目标，限制无外部监督的自训练。\n\n方法：模型从粗粒度主题生成问题与参考推理，用新会话和改写后作答的一致性筛查，再丢弃学生已稳定掌握的题。教师额外读取自生成参考信息，沿学生自己的轨迹提供逐 token 指导；学生更新以滑动平均进入教师，再影响后续生成与监督。\n\n结果与结论：引言给出 Gemma 模型在 MMLU 增加10.2分、视觉问答增加6.9分，并称未训练领域能力保留。主要实验和消融被截断，无法核对比较预算、轮次稳定性及筛选环节贡献；最终评价对象是平均教师。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，潜在收益来自信息条件差，但一致性只能筛掉不稳定答案，无法排除稳定共同错误。视觉版本仍需无标签图像，“无数据”应限定为没有外部策展问答。","published_at":"2026-10-23","topics":"自适应训练经验; 自生成监督与微调; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-27","novelty_summary":"作者声称从主题描述自生成题目及特权信息，实现无策展问答的自训练。本文证据：自一致筛查和学生掌握度筛选决定训练样本，特权条件教师提供密集监督，平均权重跨轮继承；没有独立真值验证。相对 RSIPO（arxiv:2610.15772）以技能回放和执行收益校准教师，本篇使用自生成答案与推理；相对 SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）按作答结果训练独立合成器，本篇通过平均教师及筛选适配课程。编辑推断：监督接口有明确差异，长期纠错能力未证实；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.32326","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.32326v1","title":"TGR-EvoDAG: A DAG-based Multi-Agent Code Evolution Framework for Generative Recommendation on Tencent","authors":"Junlin He; Junzhang Zhu; Yudong Li; Yihong Tang; Xuefeng Jiang; Wei Ma; Chengxiang Zhuo; Zang Li","affiliations":"Tencent Platform and Content Group；The Hong Kong Polytechnic University；McGill University；Independent Researcher","abstract":"Large Language Model (LLM) agents have enabled automated code evolution for algorithm discovery. However, current recursive self-improvement (RSI) research for sequential recommendation faces a dilemma: general-purpose frameworks lack domain-specific feedback, while recommender-specific frameworks rely on linear evolution. Crucially, naively integrating them fails when applied to Generative Recommendation (GR). Unlike end-to-end models, GR relies on a module-cascaded pipeline (tokenization, pre-training, and alignment). In this paradigm, existing evolution methods suffer from: i) cost blindness, squandering budgets by ignoring stage-asymmetric retraining overheads; and ii) short-sighted evaluation, discarding promising upstream innovations that temporarily regress metrics before downstream adaptation. To bridge these gaps, we propose TGR-EvoDAG, a multi-agent code evolution framework tailored for GR. TGR-EvoDAG models code evolution as a Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) to maintain multiple evolution branches and merge complementary innovations, unifying advanced search with rich GR diagnostic feedback. We further introduce stage-aware cost planning to optimize GPU-hour budgets, and active downstream co-adaptation to navigate temporary regressions and unlock cross-stage gains. On public Amazon datasets, TGR-EvoDAG enables the first autonomous evolution of a complete GR pipeline, improving offline metrics by up to 37.4% and Agent4Rec simulated user satisfaction by 19.7% over the strongest baseline. Furthermore, in industrial deployment on Tencent's large-scale commercial media platform, the evolved GR achieves a 12.16% relative improvement in offline Hit@1 and a statistically significant 0.40% increase in online click-through rate (CTR).","tldr":"背景与问题：生成式推荐由编码、预训练和对齐串联；上游改动既昂贵，又可能因下游尚未适配而暂时降分，贪心搜索会过早丢弃有效方向。\n\n方法：TGR-EvoDAG 保留并合并不同代码分支，用实际阶段开销规划实验。对疑似接口失配造成的退化，保留上游修改并安排下游适配；验证指标和诊断文字进入后续搜索，最终用户模拟评价不回流选模。\n\n结果与结论：材料称公开数据上优于所列演化框架，商业平台作为新增召回通道进行了14天 A/B 测试，点击率增加0.40%。主要实验表被截断，无法核对搜索机制的独立贡献、区间及完整成本；线上结果检验的是推荐产物。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，暂时退化应结合组件兼容性判断，不能一律保留或剪枝。这对联合演化有启发，但当前是固定研究框架优化外部推荐系统，没有显示提案者或搜索器自身被改进。","published_at":"2026-10-23","topics":"预算受限研究搜索; 执行证据驱动改进; 能力归因","added_on":"2026-10-27","novelty_summary":"作者声称首次自主演化完整生成式推荐流水线。本文证据：阶段成本、验证指标及诊断指导代码分支继承、合并和下游适配；没有改进者更新，首次主张未核验。相对 ComRSI（arxiv:2610.29641）固定 agent 优化通信程序，本篇同属外部 AI 工件优化，但处理阶段成本与延迟收益；相对 CoTrace（arxiv:2610.10426）管理运行时兼容性，本篇将兼容失配纳入分支保留决策。编辑推断：属于 RSI 相邻的自动研发机制，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.32245","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.32245v1","title":"Minimum Description Length Unsupervisedly Separates Law-Grade from Statistical-Grade Knowledge in a Self-Improving Science Agent - and Reveals 86% of Its Own Discoveries Are Statistical","authors":"Wenbin Mao; Pei Zou","affiliations":"Artificial Intelligence Laboratory, Hooman Biotechnology (Beijing) Co., Ltd.","abstract":"AI systems that discover scientific relations now generate candidate \"laws\" at scale, but the bottleneck has shifted from generation to vetting: which candidates deserve belief? We show that a deployed self-improving science agent - one that has admitted 252 relations through held-out prediction courts - already computes the quantity that answers this question: the Minimum Description Length compression ratio used for model selection doubles, when read under discrete accounting, as an unsupervised epistemic grader. The compression-ranked top band of the agent's ledger recovers exactly the canonical laws among its discoveries (vis-viva across seven planets, Balmer/Rydberg) plus cross-measurement identities - enrichment $p=3.6\\times10^{-12}$ under a hypergeometric test - with zero counterexamples and physically coherent band structure. The same lens retroactively reveals that 86% of the ledger compresses nothing ($\\mathrm{cr}\\approx 1$): the agent had been recording statistical regularities, including a learned predictor with held-out $R^2=0.541$ admitted through the prediction gate, under a narrative of compression as the unified value of knowledge - a narrative that was never true for them. We formalize the resulting dual-axis bookkeeping - prediction value ($R^2$) and compression value (cr) as nearly decoupled axes of knowledge - demonstrate its robustness to quantization, and register forward falsifiable predictions. The episode is, to our knowledge, the first measured instance of a discovery agent auditing its own knowledge ledger by an internal measure and finding itself over-claiming.","tldr":"背景与问题：科学发现系统用留出预测筛选关系，仍可能把强相关性当作物理理解；预测得准和简洁解释数据并非同一种价值。\n\n方法：论文重读既有知识账本的最小描述长度压缩比，将预测价值和压缩价值分别登记。审计对象由符号生成器提出关系、按统计规则准入，没有语言模型参与发现和评分；另一个编码 agent 在人类批准下开发系统，处于被审计流程之外。\n\n结果与结论：单一账本中86%的关系压缩比不高于1，高压缩区聚集已知定律与测量恒等式。不过所列定律标签总数与分项计数不一致，低阈值区间也并非全部有标签，不能照搬宽泛的零反例表述。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，双轴记账能纠正知识命名，但压缩比衡量给定精度下的确定性，嘈杂定律可能落入统计区。该审计没有证明 AI 自主修订自身评估器或发现程序，应作为科学结果审查的相邻案例。","published_at":"2026-10-23","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; 能力归因; 验证理论","added_on":"2026-10-27","novelty_summary":"作者声称首次测得发现系统用内部指标审计自身过度主张。本文证据：重算并分列账本的预测与压缩指标，明确没有 LLM 在审计循环中提案、准入或评分；未展示自主修改改进机制后的收益。相对 EvoBelief（arxiv:2610.12789）由验证和反例改变后续规划规则，本篇主要重新分级既有发现。编辑推断：缺少 RSI 核心的 AI 自身适配证据，且数学机制并非作者声称的新理论；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.32120","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.32120v1","title":"ImageRSI: Verification-Driven Recursive Self-Improvement for Agentic Image Generation","authors":"Shuo Han; Zhilin Wang; Peng Ling; Wenjia Gong; Yang Liu; Guanjun Jiang; Yukun Cao; Xike Xie","affiliations":"中国科学技术大学；Qwen Business Unit of Alibaba, Alibaba Token Hub；西安电子科技大学","abstract":"Complex text-to-image requests remain difficult to satisfy reliably. Verifying and repairing an image can fix an individual output, but a successful repair does not necessarily carry over to other requests. We present ImageRSI, a framework that keeps the image generator frozen and combines three components: five-dimensional verification and repair within each task, an experience library shared across tasks, and offline updating of the judge. Candidate experiences enter the library only after paired A/B validation, and the judge is updated with supervised fine-tuning and GRPO on accumulated image-judgment records and evaluated before reuse. We also introduce ImageReq-Bench, a benchmark of 961 requests built around hard cases in real-world image-generation requests, each paired with an evaluation checklist. ImageRSI achieves a Checklist Strict Accuracy (CSA) of 52.6% on MindBench (with Nano Banana Pro as the generator) and 65.66% on ImageReq-Bench, and we compare system outcomes across judge-training configurations.","tldr":"背景与问题：修好一张图不说明修补策略可迁移，随机生成也会制造偶然成功；若内部裁判误判，错误诊断还可能进入经验库持续传播。\n\n方法：ImageRSI 固定生成器，用缺陷判断修订提示，并通过同请求、同种子的有无经验配对试验决定策略准入。积累图像与模型标注另用于离线训练裁判，评价后可重新部署；外部清单评分不反馈当次生成。\n\n结果与结论：相同首图、最多两次生成时，局部修补较最佳两次重采样更有效；经验库从空库扩充后，测试清单全通过率增加10分。但重复收集—训练—部署裁判仍是扩展方案，现有配置比较不能证明多轮递归收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，经验准入与裁判训练必须分别验收。配对经验试验比单次修好更接近迁移证据；模型生成的裁判标签仍非真值，外部评价有助于隔离自我打分，却不能消除共同盲点。","published_at":"2026-10-23","topics":"评估器递归改进; 经验迁移; 执行证据驱动改进","added_on":"2026-10-27","novelty_summary":"作者声称将任务修补、跨任务经验和裁判更新连接。本文证据：经验通过配对校准与留出试验准入，图像—模型标注训练裁判；明确重复裁判收集训练循环尚为提案，默认经验评估也可使用固定快照。相对 UCoE（arxiv:2610.17609）固定权重演化评分程序，本篇离线更新裁判参数；相对 Hippo（arxiv:2610.24453）依赖同题比较提炼经验，本篇增加显式有无策略配对准入。编辑推断：验收协议有具体推进，完整递归链尚未实现；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.32026","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.32026v1","title":"RSI-Opt: Recursive Self-Improvement Optimizer Agents For Model Training","authors":"Binghang Lu; Yige Sun; Guang Lin","affiliations":"Purdue University；Independent Researcher","abstract":"Conventional neural-network training typically follows a predefined optimization recipe, motivating a LLM agent that monitors training dynamics and adjusts optimizer settings as training progresses, but a fixed agent policy does not accumulate experience across runs. We introduce RSI-Opt, a plug-and-play Recursive Self-Improvement Optimizer Agents which evolves the knowledge that guides this process: a prompt, a playbook of procedures, a library of tested optimizer code, and a decision cadence. A meta-agent rewrites this policy using evidence from earlier runs, and an archive retains evaluated policies for further evolution. Across 5 generations on three training tasks, the meta-agents develop reusable procedures and code and conduct their own CPU proxy experiments. RSI-Opt substantially improves optimizer-agent performance, with representative raw-space summary $z$-scores increasing from $+10.48$ to $+14.33$ on the evolution suite with Opus 5.5 and from $-0.36$ to $+3.11$ on held-out tasks with GPT-5.5 through cross-model policy transfer. On the Burgers PDE, it reduces mean relative $L_2$ error by approximately 2.7-fold with Opus 5.5 and 8.8-fold with GPT-6.1 over the fixed-prompt agent baseline, although PDE transfer varies across LLMs and tasks. Controlled comparisons show that the evolved policy combines reusable optimization knowledge with adaptation to each task: initial decisions capture most observed gains on seen tasks, while continued adaptation improves outcomes on unseen tasks. These findings demonstrate how procedures and executable tools accumulated across training runs can improve optimizer-agent performance and support transfer to scientific machine learning.","tldr":"背景与问题：训练中的优化器 agent 能根据损失改更新规则，却每次从固定提示重新开始，已验证的优化经验无法跨运行积累；跨运行涨分又可能只是记住少数任务的配方。\n\n方法：元 agent 根据既往训练结果、修改理由和代码，修订优化器 agent 的操作知识与程序库；评估后的版本进入档案，供后续继承。训练中仍可继续改优化器，但底层模型、元 agent 指令和评分规则固定。\n\n结果与结论：九项训练任务的对照显示，已见任务的大部分收益来自初始决策，未见任务更受益于后续适应。Opus 的留出任务汇总分反而下降；还发生过留出任务描述暴露，排除相关分支后，档案摘要的间接传播仍未查清。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键是区分可复用配方与在线诊断能力，两者对已见和未见任务的贡献不同。当前支持优化知识累积，尚缺等预算独立提案对照，不能把代际涨分解释为元优化程序自身增强。","published_at":"2026-10-23","topics":"预算受限研究搜索; 经验迁移; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-27","novelty_summary":"作者声称跨运行演化优化器 agent 的提示、程序知识、代码库和决策节奏。本文证据：训练结果与执行记录驱动政策修订，版本档案支持继承；元 agent 指令、模型权重和评分规则固定。相对 arxiv:2610.30851 离线演化科学搜索程序，本篇演化的是能在目标训练运行中继续改写优化器的 agent 政策；相对 arxiv:2603.19461 可编辑元程序，本篇没有修改外层改进机制。编辑推断：跨运行知识与运行内适应的贡献拆分有价值，但继承收益和留出信息隔离仍有缺口；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.30851","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.30851v1","title":"ADAPT for Science: A Multi-Agent System for Self-Evolving Scientific Optimization","authors":"Zhaoran Feng; Yuchen Ni; Jianan Liu; Lemao Liu; Dejing Dou; Kairui Feng","affiliations":"南京大学；上海创智学院（Shanghai Innovation Institute）；复旦大学；BEDI Cloud；同济大学上海自主智能无人系统科学中心","abstract":"Scientific discovery often requires identifying a small number of high-performing designs in vast, constrained search spaces. This is difficult when evaluations are costly, feasible solutions are sparse, parameters are strongly coupled, and physical constraints are strict. Recent AI for AI methods can automatically improve algorithms and optimization procedures. However, general purpose approaches are not designed around scientific priors, physical constraints, and limited evaluation budgets. We introduce ADAPT for Science, a multi-agent framework that treats scientific optimization as two coupled decisions: where to search and how to search. ADAPT uses historical designs to identify promising and diverse initial conditions, progressively concentrates computation on favorable search directions, and evolves the optimization procedure from execution feedback. We evaluate ADAPT on the design of gravitational wave detectors using a differentiable physics simulator and eight unseen detector topologies. Under matched scientific evaluation budgets, ADAPT achieves a mean loss of 0.204 +/- 0.101, reducing loss by 54.9% relative to the best classical optimizer and by 62.2% relative to the best general purpose agentic evolution baseline. ADAPT achieves the lowest loss on all unseen topologies among the evaluated baselines. ADAPT provides a step toward scientific optimization systems that continuously learn from prior experience and their own search outcomes.","tldr":"背景与问题：科学搜索的预算不仅耗在参数更新，也耗在坏起点和过早押注的方向上。通用程序演化若忽略历史设计、物理可行性与剩余时间，优化出的算法仍可能浪费科学评估。\n\n方法：ADAPT先从历史设计迁移起点，再用执行结果演化起点筛选与预算分配程序；随后演化局部优化器，让更新幅度和数值保护适应有限时限。物理模拟器提供目标值、梯度及可行性反馈，保留程序进入后续比较；留出测试运行冻结程序。\n\n结果与结论：八个未见探测器拓扑上，在相同运行预算下，平均损失比最强经典优化器低54.9%。但主表及完整消融被截断，无法拆分历史起点与优化器修改的贡献；所给标准差是拓扑间差异，不是重复实验不确定性。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，值得关注的是把“从哪里开始”和“怎样更新”一起纳入预算决策。测试时没有在线语言模型，收益说明离线发现的搜索程序可迁移，尚不证明演化器持续增强；开发搜索成本也需另算。","published_at":"2026-10-22","topics":"预算受限研究搜索; 搜索策略演化; 评估预算分配","added_on":"2026-10-24","novelty_summary":"作者声称联合适配完整科学搜索策略，包括初始化、预算分配和优化程序。本文证据：模拟器执行反馈驱动两类程序修订，历史强程序保留比较；留出阶段使用冻结选择策略及优化器，不调用语言模型。相对EvoX（arxiv:2602.23413）已有的搜索策略演化，本篇加入科学历史设计迁移、物理约束和有限时限优化；相对EvoAlloc（arxiv:2610.12086）的评估分配修订，本篇还改变起点与局部更新程序，未见其采用被拒候选的反事实探索。编辑推断：是科学约束下的搜索策略扩展，不能视为元演化首次提出，也未证明外层演化机制自我增强；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.30790","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.30790v1","title":"Agentic Knowledge-Model Co-Evolution via Consistency Regularization","authors":"Sirui Chen; Zhining Liu; Chao Zhang; Jingrui He; Zheng Li","affiliations":"University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign；Georgia Institute of Technology；Amazon","abstract":"LLM agents can evolve by learning from accumulated experience. Existing approaches extract reusable external knowledge, such as skills and memories, from experience to guide subsequent task solving, with some further internalizing this knowledge through model training. However, different ways of analyzing and transforming the same experience can yield knowledge with substantially different utility, even when the resulting guidance appears reasonable. Inspired by consistency regularization, we identify consistent utility gains across different ways of analyzing the same experience, rather than relying on any single way of analyzing it. We introduce SPLICE, a framework for consistency-regularized knowledge-model co-evolution. It constructs evolution views by perturbing how the same experience is analyzed, producing different knowledge candidates. Knowledge updates are then guided by common gain, which accounts for utility gains and their consistency across views. During model evolution, self-distillation internalizes the evolved knowledge alongside reinforcement learning, using knowledge associated with consistent utility degradation as a contrastive reference. The two processes interleave, with model updates driving further knowledge evolution. Experiments across diverse domains show that SPLICE outperforms knowledge evolution and model training baselines by up to 7.1 and 4.6 points in average accuracy, while its evolved knowledge reduces output tokens per correct solution by up to 44% and transfers across model sizes and families.","tldr":"背景与问题：同一段经验可以提炼出多种貌似合理的指导，但实际作用不同；偶然成功的知识若进入后续训练，还可能把噪声内化到权重。\n\n方法：SPLICE改变分析经验的指令，生成多份知识，再重放原任务，优先选取不同分析视角下均有收益的任务证据来修订知识；新知识须通过留出验证。模型随后结合强化学习与自蒸馏内化有效指导，并用持续有害的知识作受控对照，更新后的模型再产生经验。\n\n结果与结论：四类任务中，共演化版在两种模型规模上的平均准确率分别比最强训练基线高3.0和4.6个百分点；小模型的表格任务仍落后。完整消融与成本部分缺失，无法确认一致性筛选相对额外重放的独立收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，知识可靠性应看行为收益能否跨分析方式保持，而非文字是否一致。但同题多视角稳定不等于跨任务有效；论文理论也未保证知识合并后保留收益，固定外部知识优化器更不代表递归增强。","published_at":"2026-10-22","topics":"自适应训练经验; 经验迁移; 自进化策略训练","added_on":"2026-10-24","novelty_summary":"作者声称以跨分析视角的效用一致性指导知识—模型共演化。本文证据：同题重放的奖励差筛选任务证据，留出验证控制知识准入，有无知识的执行收益调节蒸馏，模型更新后重新产生经验；知识优化器为外部LLM。相对RSIPO（arxiv:2610.15772）按技能回放收益训练技能生成并校准教师，本篇主要增加跨视角收益一致性和负效用知识对照，而非直接训练知识优化器；相对Hippo（arxiv:2610.24453）比较同题尝试，本篇主动扰动经验解释并测量其行为作用。编辑推断：效用稳定性进入知识选择是具体推进，尚无两者的匹配比较或元优化器增强证据；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.30429","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.30429v1","title":"RoleFlow: Self-Evolving Multi-Role Agentic Collaboration via Structural Adaptation","authors":"Yi Ge; Pan Wang; Xuehao Cui; Zian Zeng; Xu Hu; Heng Huang; Furong Huang","affiliations":"University of Maryland, College Park；University of Pittsburgh；The University of Texas at Dallas","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) based multi-agent systems often rely on predefined collaboration structures, limiting their adaptability to evolving task requirements. Although recent approaches enable dynamic orchestration, trajectory-level rewards they apply assign one outcome to each decision, ofen struggling to identify the contributions of individual structural changes. We propose RoleFlow, a self-evolving multi-role agentic system that refines collaboration structures through feedback-driven atomic edits and on-demand role synthesis. To make structural adaptation learnable, we introduce Single-Edit Counterfactual Policy Optimization (SECPO), which evaluates each edit against its no-edit counterpart at the same chain state and assigns targeted credit to edit-specific tokens. Across seven benchmarks spanning four domains, RoleFlow achieves the optimal average performance, surpassing the strongest competitor by 4.7 points. It leads on all three multi-hop QA benchmarks by 3.2-7.5 F1 points and also shows supremacy on mathematical reasoning, web interaction, and code generation. Further analyses demonstrate cross-benchmark transferability, training-data efficiency, and cross-executor generalization.","tldr":"背景与问题：协作链连续增删角色后，终局奖励无法分清哪次结构修改有效；把整条轨迹的优势广播给所有决策，会同时奖励有益与有害编辑。\n\n方法：RoleFlow训练路由模型，在验证失败后逐次修改协作链。训练时从相同链状态分别执行“修改”和“不修改”，把奖励差额外分配给对应编辑的文本；执行模型冻结。缺少角色时按需生成，训练中积累角色库，测试则重新从种子库开始。\n\n结果与结论：七项基准平均比最强协作竞争方法高4.7分；可见案例分析转述的问答消融中，编辑级训练比移除该信号高2.1—2.6 F1。完整消融和预算被截断，且部分单项仍不及直接调用更强模型，不能沿用摘要的全面领先表述。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，实质变化是训练“哪种结构修改值得做”，而非只搜索最终工作流。但配对重跑只估计当前状态下的即时作用，验证器误判与采样噪声仍会进入奖励；测试不继承训练角色库，迁移重点应落在路由能力。","published_at":"2026-10-21","topics":"多智能体工作流演化; 自进化策略训练; 能力归因","added_on":"2026-10-24","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过同状态单编辑反事实比较实现细粒度结构信用分配。本文证据：任务验证器给出通过、分数和缺陷，修改与不修改的奖励差训练路由器；执行者冻结，训练角色库持续增长，但测试只用种子角色并现场合成。相对MASS（arxiv:2610.12176）搜索工作流后用轨迹微调共享模型，本篇直接训练任务执行中的结构编辑决策；相对MLExpert（arxiv:2610.22344）的实验窗口共享奖励，本篇把信用进一步定位到单次结构干预。编辑推断：这是可学习编排的具体推进，不是编辑学习规则自身递归优化；上述比较为机制比较，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.30116","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.30116v1","title":"Environment Duels: A Microcosm of LLM Co-Evolution","authors":"Shibo Jin; Zhiqiu Xu; Yiling Zou; Shangyu Gong; Mayur Naik","affiliations":"University of Pennsylvania","abstract":"Through a tangle of real-world interactions, from synthetic training pipelines to data shared on the open web, frontier LLMs absorb what their predecessors and competitors create. How well does each model play its role in this ecosystem, as a creator and as a solver? We introduce Environment Duels, a dynamic agentic benchmark that evaluates both capabilities on interactive environments. Each model writes environments, each with a privileged hint, aiming for tasks that capable solvers fail without the hint and pass with it. Across nine frontier LLMs, solving and authoring prove to be distinct skills: the strongest solvers are not the strongest authors, while smaller models learn more from how others played and write the hardest environments and the most useful hints. Beyond the scores, the pairwise interactions form a microcosm of how models affect one another. Head-to-head outcomes are transitive and so yield a stable ranking; independent authors converge on the same designs; and in a reinforcement-learning study with Qwen3.8-27B, the learner's hint lift on an author's environments tracks how much training on those environments improves it on held-out reasoning and agentic benchmarks, whether the environments are its own or another model's. Each of these patterns has a counterpart in how models shape one another outside the duel. By staging these interactions under controlled conditions, Environment Duels offers a window onto how LLMs teach, challenge and learn from one another. Code is available at https://github.com/LLM-Duels/EnvDuels.","tldr":"背景与问题：会解题不等于会生成值得学习的任务；只测难度，也无法区分有效挑战、不可解环境和无效提示。\n\n方法：Environment Duels让模型编写环境与特权提示，在相同实例和预算下比较有无提示的执行结果，再把求解轨迹交回作者修订一次。提示净收益衡量作者与学习者的匹配，并分别记录提示修复和破坏的尝试。\n\n结果与结论：九模型实验中，最强求解者并非最佳出题者；一次修订使提示收益从6.3升至13.4个百分点。单一学习模型的训练研究还发现提示收益与留出训练收益相关，但详细结果段落缺失。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，课程价值应针对接收者测量。提示可能诱发过早承诺；当前一次作者适配及训练关联，不足以证明双方持续共训练，也不能把相关性当作教学价值认证。","published_at":"2026-10-21","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; RSI 研究环境; RSI 评测与迁移","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称构建模型共演化的受控缩影。本文证据：执行反馈驱动一次环境及提示修订，提示收益与后续训练收益相关。相对arxiv:2610.09426从论文构建环境，本篇加入有无提示的配对测量；相对arxiv:2610.11345联合训练合成器与求解器，本篇主要评测作者适配。编辑推断：推进了学习者特定的课程质量测量，未展示持续参数共演化；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.30042","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.30042v1","title":"HGM-Dual: Lineage-Aware Guided Agent Harness Optimization for Long-Horizon Planning","authors":"Sudipta Paul; Pengrui Quan; Aounon Kumar; Nicholas Tzou; Vivek Kulkarni; Srinivas Chappidi","affiliations":"Samsung Research America","abstract":"Harness optimization, which improves an agent's prompts, tools, and workflows, is an increasingly effective way to enhance agents built on frozen or closed-source LLMs. Leading approaches such as the Darwin--Godel Machine and the Huxley--Godel Machine (HGM) rely on recursive self-improvement and were developed mainly for coding, where the competence needed to improve the agent coincides with the competence being improved. Planning tasks, in which an agent must produce a sequence of tool calls that jointly satisfies interacting constraints, break this alignment. There, open-ended self-modification repeatedly explores ineffective changes and consumes substantial evaluation budgets. We introduce HGM-Dual, a diagnostic-guided framework for budget-efficient harness evolution for planning agents. First, HGM-Dual represents agent evolution as lineage-aware context. This context records what each ancestor changed, which behaviors improved or regressed, and which modifications were ineffective, giving the editor explicit edit-outcome attribution instead of an unstructured archive of past agents. Second, HGM-Dual introduces error-conditioned dual-path child generation. For each selected parent, it generates a general child that preserves open-ended exploration and specialized children that target the harness components most likely responsible for the parent's highest-ranked constraint violations. HGM-Dual outperforms the strongest baseline by up to 14.45% relative improvement in case accuracy while matching HGM variants' final performance with 2x-4x fewer evaluation budget.","tldr":"背景与问题：约束规划失败常由具体违规决定，开放式修改却可能修错组件，或重复祖先的无效改动，持续消耗评估预算。\n\n方法：HGM-Dual把祖先修改、分数及错误变化整理成上下文，同时生成一般探索与针对主要违规的候选。错误定向路径只在预检信号稳定时启用；候选接受相同执行评估，最佳子代进入后续搜索。\n\n结果与结论：相同评估预算下，旅行规划案例准确率由最强表列基线的56.25%升至64.38%，购物任务也有收益。完整消融与划分说明缺失，无法把总体差异单独归给谱系记忆。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，规划改进可能更依赖编辑目标是否对应实际约束错误。祖先前后变化提供归因线索，但不隔离因果贡献；固定编辑与搜索流程也未证明改进者自身变强。","published_at":"2026-10-21","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 失败诊断; 预算受限研究搜索","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称谱系上下文与错误定向扩展提高演化效率。本文证据：评估器违规类别、执行轨迹和子代成绩进入后续编辑。相对arxiv:2604.25850已有编辑—结果可观测性，本篇细化祖先摘要与双路径生成；相对arxiv:2603.19461可修改元程序，本篇保留固定演化骨架。编辑推断：是诊断搜索的具体推进，非优化器递归更新；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.30017","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.30017v1","title":"GuideEvolve: Self-Evolving Agent Framework with Expert Guidance and 3Ts Mechanisms","authors":"Meihong Jia; Yasemin Timar; Jonathan Taws","affiliations":"Amazon；Amazon Web Services","abstract":"This study introduces GuideEvolve, a self-evolving agent framework incorporating expert guidance and three autonomous regulatory mechanisms, collectively termed the 3Ts: Think Fast and Slow, Throwback, and Termination by choice. The framework addresses critical limitations in extant self-evolving agent paradigms through dual innovations: (1) a task-specific expert-evaluation-driven evolutionary pipeline, and (2) the integration of 3Ts mechanisms to facilitate cognitive optimization, performance recovery via temporal rollback, and adaptive termination protocols. Empirical validation across the MGSM and MMLU benchmarks demonstrates that GuideEvolve attains performance metrics comparable to current state-of-the-art models (89.8% accuracy versus Gödel Agent's 90.6% on MGSM; 89.1% versus 87.9% on MMLU), while exhibiting notably reduced variance (25-59%) and enhanced robustness. Furthermore, the framework achieves a 100% evolution success rate, superior to the baseline's 82%, diminishes required optimization iterations by approximately 50% (from 30 iterations in baseline to 15.1 and 13.4 across tasks), and provides improved stability for production deployment.","tldr":"背景与问题：原始题目、回答与演化历史混入同一上下文，可能耗尽token并妨碍修改决策；Bedrock迁移还暴露格式和提前终止问题。\n\n方法：GuideEvolve让独立上下文中的模型专家分析任务表现，再由演化agent修改求解逻辑；保存最佳版本用于恢复，并在最低尝试要求后允许自主停止。反馈来自任务表现与模型建议，专家不是人工真值源。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称迭代数约减半、方差降低，但主表被截断。附录最佳求解器增加多次采样或切换模型，最终准确率因而混有推理资源变化，尚不能隔离各项控制的收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，这是上下文与运行控制的工程改进。专家上下文隔离不保证无偏，一阶优化只是类比；两类静态问答实验也不足以确立生产部署稳定性。","published_at":"2026-10-21","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 自改进稳定性; 失败诊断","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称专家指导与3Ts改善演化稳定性。本文证据：模型专家报告指导求解逻辑修改，历史最佳版本用于恢复和再探索；未显示专家或控制器学习。相对arxiv:2606.09498的失败诊断、修改与验证，本篇突出上下文隔离、回退与停止。编辑推断：更像工程增量，须匹配求解调用量与模型配置；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.29784","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.29784v1","title":"Evolving with Open Worlds: Towards Recursive Self-Improvement for Future Forecasting","authors":"Zhipeng Chen; Yunsen Liang; Yanxi Chen; Hongkang Zhao; Lingyun Feng; Ruiyang Ren; Guoxin Chen; Jia Deng; Feng Chang; Chuan Hao; Ran Tao; Jian Yang; Ji-Rong Wen; Bryan Dai; Wayne Xin Zhao","affiliations":"中国人民大学高瓴人工智能学院；Nanyang Technological University；IQuest Research","abstract":"Most contemporary artificial intelligence (AI) systems are released with frozen parameters and improve through external updates, whereas an ideal system would keep improving from its own experience, a capacity we call recursive self-improvement (RSI). Yet studying RSI requires an environment that is continuously changing, objectively verifiable, and naturally grounded, posing a fundamental challenge for agent evolution. Here we introduce DeepEvolve, a sustainable evolution agent system grounded in future event prediction, in which agents continuously interact with a dynamically evolving environment and improve by internalizing and externalizing the experience gained through these interactions. A living environment synthesizes verifiable tasks, and a recursive-evolution engine turns the reasoning trajectory behind each prediction back into capability: decoupling search from prediction adapts parameter-level evolution to the contamination-prone live environment, while distilling reusable skills lets the agent evolve from the limited live trajectories such an environment affords. On the external FutureX leaderboard, which evaluates predictions against real-world outcomes and is updated weekly, our self-improved forecaster ranked first across all systems over three consecutive weeks, achieving up to a 195% improvement in rating. On our synthesized evaluation, it ranked among the top three across four base LLMs, outperforming the strongest baseline by up to 10.7 Bradley--Terry points. More broadly, these results suggest that a system built for self-improvement is best understood as an agent that co-evolves with a genuinely living, open-ended environment, pointing to a shift in AI from training static models on fixed data toward cultivating agents that grow stronger from their own experience, with such an open world as the indispensable basis of that growth.","tldr":"背景与问题：未来预测能获得事后真值，但反馈延迟、轨迹稀少，训练时重新搜索还可能接触已发生的答案，破坏时间边界。\n\n方法：DeepEvolve分离证据搜索与概率预测，用缓存证据和事件结果训练预测端；搜索轨迹经模型过程判断蒸馏为技能，弱点再改变任务生成指导。结果真值用于参数与环境更新，不提供给行为评审。\n\n结果与结论：材料称FutureX连续三周领先；自建表中各配置领先同组基线，但其中一个总体第九，与摘要四配置均居前三的说法不符。主要消融和完整成本缺失。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，值得保留的是各更新通道的证据时间边界。实时真值不保证自动提取与评分正确，系统排名也不能隔离权重、技能和课程贡献，更未证明开放世界是RSI的必要条件。","published_at":"2026-10-21","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 自进化策略训练; 经验迁移","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称参数、技能与动态环境共演化支持持续RSI。本文证据：事件结果训练预测端，模型过程评审提炼技能，失败分布改变任务生成；排名叙述存在内部冲突。相对arxiv:2610.14118诊断驱动造任务，本篇增加实时事件与缓存证据隔离；相对arxiv:2610.11345训练合成器，本篇用生成技能改变课程。编辑推断：时间边界值得追踪，未证明改进引擎递归增强；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.29677","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.29677v1","title":"Toward Recursive Self-Improvement in Physical AI","authors":"Meng Luo; Zechen Bai; Shanqing Xu; Yanlin Li; Kaixin Li; Mengchen Qian; Weifeng Lu; Ran Zhang; Yingtian Zou; Ziyang Luo; Wei Chen; Hongzhan Lin","affiliations":"National University of Singapore；华中科技大学；上海交通大学；Nanyang Technological University；Hong Kong Baptist University","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement (RSI) describes a system that improves not only its behavior but also the process by which it improves. Recent digital agents test this idea by rewriting their own code and checking each version with executable tests. Bringing these mechanisms into the physical world requires learning from partial observations through costly trials, while accounting for changing operating conditions and potentially irreversible consequences. We position RSI within robot learning and trace pathways from improving robot capabilities to improving the processes that generate them. We examine how physical experience can strengthen these improvement mechanisms and when the resulting gains can support further self-improvement of the mechanisms themselves. Gains carry forward only when feedback addresses remaining learning needs, the receiving component can use the change, its value survives changes in tasks or hardware, and continued practice remains safe and affordable. Existing studies, concentrated in manipulation, support behavioral improvement, benefits to later learning, and procedure improvement. Some systems also change the improver's knowledge or tools, but the physical studies reviewed here have yet to isolate gains attributable to recursion. We synthesize these findings into evaluation principles and research directions for machines that, trial by trial, safely improve the way they improve.","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人在固定流程下变强，不代表学习流程或修改流程的改进者变强；物理试验还受到观测不全、磨损与不可逆后果限制。\n\n方法：本文沿经验留下什么改变、谁在下一轮使用它组织研究，区分行为收益、后续学习收益、程序改进与递归关系。递归要求修补知识改善改进者，改善后的改进者再参与自身下一次改进，并提出两轮受控检验。\n\n结果与结论：综述认为现有物理研究支持前三类收益，部分系统改变了改进者知识或工具，但尚未隔离递归本身的增益。这是证据分类及实验原则，没有新机器人系统的收益实验。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，其价值是把组件名称转成跨轮可检验关系。比较新旧改进程序还须匹配起点、试验机会和物理条件；软件回滚无法恢复硬件损伤。","published_at":"2026-10-21","topics":"RSI 评测与迁移; 具身 RSI; 能力归因","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称建立物理RSI证据阶梯及检验原则。本文证据是跨轮定义、综述判断与实验建议，非新递归收益实验。相对arxiv:2610.18792审计继承与重试，本篇要求进一步隔离改进程序和改进者收益；相对arxiv:2610.20294的继任规则规格，强调物理反馈、兼容性与成本。编辑推断：这是评测框架细化；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.29641","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.29641v1","title":"Recursive Code Evolution for Task-Oriented Semantic Communications","authors":"Yan Gong; Zheng Chu; Wei Koong Chai; Hari Mohan Pandey; Jingrui Hou; Miao Zhang; Yuanjian Li; Pei Xiao","affiliations":"Bournemouth University；University of Nottingham Ningbo China；武汉大学；重庆交通大学；西交利物浦大学；University of Surrey","abstract":"Semantic communication jointly optimizes inference accuracy, channel use, and computation, yet the underlying communication program is typically specified before training. This paper presents ComRSI (Communications-Oriented Recursive Self-Improvement), a framework for recursively evolving that program through large-language-model-assisted code edits. A fixed agent modifies the encoder, channel adapters, decoder, loss, and training policy; a protected evaluator screens candidates under prescribed budgets and resource constraints. Accepted code and textual feedback inform subsequent proposals, while candidate weights are trained from scratch. In the original ten-generation CIFAR-100 lineage, eight accepted revisions produce an attention-pooled code achieving 74.3% test accuracy over an Additive White Gaussian Noise (AWGN) channel at 32 complex symbols per image, compared with 67.2% at 256 symbols for the initial design. The program also improves fading-channel accuracy and transfers to Tiny-ImageNet after retraining. A repeat study with ten searches per method compares ComRSI against non-recursive agents with and without textual history. Mean final search scores balancing accuracy, transmission rate, and computational cost are 0.7587, 0.7376, and 0.7089, respectively; the mean numbers of accepted revisions per search are 6.0, 5.0, and 2.1. The advantage over the memoryless agent is supported by a two-sided rank test, whereas the difference from the history-equipped agent remains statistically inconclusive at this sample size. Archived proposals show that pooling can yield a large improvement, while retained history supports subsequent refinement. These results support recursive program optimization within the evaluated setting and expose its remaining rate-robustness and compute-placement trade-offs.","tldr":"背景与问题：语义通信的准确率、传输量与计算位置相互影响，固定架构内调权重覆盖不了程序结构变化；反复使用验证集又可能造成过拟合。\n\n方法：ComRSI用固定模型修改通信程序，受保护的信道、资源核算及公开评估筛选候选。获准代码与文字历史进入下一代，每个候选从头训练；隐藏图像及信道条件只在搜索后评价。\n\n结果与结论：十次重复搜索中，代码继承方案优于无记忆提案者，但相对带文字历史的非继承方案，差异统计上不确定。最终设计减少传输量并改善准确率，同时把更多计算移到发送端。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，代码继承与文字历史的拆分比单条涨分曲线更有价值。结果支持受约束的程序优化，未证明优化者增强；相同训练步数也不等于相同算力。","published_at":"2026-10-21","topics":"执行证据驱动改进; 预算受限研究搜索","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称集成系统的通信功能经递归代码继承改善，并明确提案者及评估协议固定。本文证据：公开反馈筛选、代码继承、从头训练及重复搜索；相对带历史对照的优势不确定。相对arxiv:2610.13025训练编辑者，本篇不更新改进者；与arxiv:2610.25012相似，主要优化AI相关工件。编辑推断：属于外部自动设计的相邻工作；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.29467","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.29467v1","title":"PreCoMem: Predictive Cognitive Memory for Self-Evolving Long-Term Dialogue Agents","authors":"Jian Zhong; Zeyu Liu; Pingchuan Cao; Rongduo Han; Shunye Tang; Guohuan Xie; Mingyuan Qin; Ran Ji; Xiao Liang; Wei Wang; Haining Zhang","affiliations":"南开大学；清华大学；华中科技大学；中国科学院大学；vivo AI Lab","abstract":"Long-horizon dialogue agents need to keep user memories stable enough for personalization while adapting when the user genuinely changes. Existing memory systems often append every observation or overwrite old entries by heuristic rules, which makes transient noise hard to distinguish from real belief drift. We introduce PreCoMem, a memory consolidation framework inspired by predictive coding that represents memory as confidence-weighted beliefs about the user's state. Its core signal, Effective Surprisal, combines semantic deviation and contradiction evidence, then downweights this signal when retrieval is diffuse and unreliable. According to effective surprisal, a two-threshold gate maps each turn to one of three deterministic updates: MAINTAIN reinforces supported beliefs, PROFILE stores ambiguous cues as low-confidence hypotheses, and CORRECT softly decays reliably contradicted facts. The PROFILE stage acts as an explicit waiting room, preventing premature commitment to noisy evidence. Experiments on LoCoMo, LongMemEval-S, and PersonaMem-v2 show consistent state-of-the-art accuracy; our new DiMoBench confirms that PreCoMem adapts to non-stationary belief drift without over-reacting to noise. The code is available at https://github.com/ZhongWishing/PreCoMem.","tldr":"背景与问题：长期对话记忆不断追加或按新近内容覆盖，容易把短暂噪声当成用户变化，也可能让过时事实持续牵引回答。\n\n方法：PreCoMem把用户信息存成带支持权重的信念，结合语义偏差、矛盾判断与检索集中度决定更新。模糊证据先写成假设，反复支持后晋级；可靠矛盾则降低旧事实权重，改变后续召回。\n\n结果与结论：材料称三个对话基准领先，并以自建漂移测试检验抗噪更新；主要结果及消融被截断，无法核对效果量与独立贡献。变化发生在记忆状态，门控和更新规则固定。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，延迟承诺适合处理不确定用户信息，但检索集中不等于证据正确，单条错误记忆也可能占据主导。支持权重不是校准概率，不能解释成事实真实性或管理器递归学习。","published_at":"2026-10-21","topics":"外部记忆与规则更新; 自改进稳定性; 经验迁移","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称预测编码式巩固支持记忆自演化。本文证据：固定矛盾信号、检索集中度及固定提示模型的局部判断，经确定规则修改信念。相对arxiv:2610.24453修订操作经验，本篇处理用户事实漂移；相对arxiv:2610.26453学习记忆价值，本篇不学习选择或更新规则。编辑推断：属于对话记忆适配，非元级增强；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.29121","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.29121v1","title":"Recursive Self-Improvement on a Budget: Scoring Code Edits Before They Run","authors":"Erfan Darzi; Sree Bhargavi Balija; Sheng He","affiliations":"Harvard University；Massachusetts Institute of Technology；UC San Diego","abstract":"A coding agent that rewrites its own scaffold has to choose which proposed edit to expand before that edit has been evaluated, and the search then has to return one agent. Each run fits one linear readout on the parent's steering-split solve rate and eight coordinates of the proposed diff, from 96 scaffold edits labeled by four evaluations of a 16-instance fit split, and then freezes the coefficients. HumanEval+ reserves 48 instances as the steering split and Polyglot reserves 64. That split scores parents and keeps an archive of four nodes. Huxley-Gödel Machine selection draws a parent by Thompson sampling on the steering counts of nodes that have already been evaluated, and it expands the child that parent proposes. Every method then returns the earliest evaluated node whose steering-split solve count is maximal. The tables report the held-out score of that node on the other 100 HumanEval+ instances and the other 145 Polyglot instances, next to the root scaffold and the calibration edit with the highest fit-split label. Twelve runs of GPT-4o return a node at 87.0% on held-out HumanEval+, against 84.2% for the parent-rate ablation. On that split Huxley-Gödel Machine selection returns 85.1%, the root is at 81.2%, and the calibration-best edit is at 82.8%. On the same split Claude Sonnet 4.5 returns 86.6%, beside 86.5% for Huxley-Gödel Machine selection, 85.3% for the parent-rate ablation, and 85.1% for the calibration-best edit.","tldr":"背景与问题：编码agent子代尚未运行时，父代成绩无法区分同一父代提出的不同修改；逐个执行又会耗尽搜索预算。\n\n方法：本文用执行测试标注的编辑训练轻量预测器，结合父代成绩与代码差异排序新提案，只运行选中候选。预测器随后冻结，执行成绩决定档案和最终版本，校准支出计入测试预算。\n\n结果与结论：GPT-4o的HumanEval+留出成绩为87.0%，父代成绩消融为84.2%；相对HGM的配对区间却含零。Claude配置与HGM几乎持平，优势并不一致。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，预执行排序应按最终交付系统验收，不能只看预测相关性。理论给出的是Beta分布性质，未证明编辑预测有效；文内HGM计数存在单节点和谱系两种口径，复现前需澄清。","published_at":"2026-10-21","topics":"预算受限研究搜索; Harness 递归演化; 收益预测","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者将代理辅助搜索用于执行前编辑排序。本文证据：执行校准后冻结预测器，同checker调用预算下评估最终留出成绩，预测器没有持续更新。相对arxiv:2610.23344训练提案者并真实纠偏，本篇只筛选编辑；相对arxiv:2610.30042改变候选生成，本篇改变运行前排序。编辑推断：属于固定代理搜索增量，HGM计数叙述需核对；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.30184","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.30184v1","title":"Self-Evolving Static Analysis via LLM Pseudo-Labeling","authors":"Rui Melo; Andre Duarte; Aditya Oke; Shubham Gandhi; Nachiket Kotalwar; Rui Abreu; Lei Li; Carolyn Rose","affiliations":"Carnegie Mellon University；FEUP","abstract":"Security bugs often slip past static analysis not because they are impossible to detect, but because detection rules have not yet been written for the code in front of us. New frameworks, APIs, and coding idioms continually create such gaps, leaving developers to discover failures and manually encode new rules. We present SESAA, a framework in which an Large Language Model (LLM) agent starts from no rules and iteratively evolves a set of readable and auditable joern queries. The agent receives feedback only from a second LLM critic, which inspects flagged and unflagged code to identify likely false alarms and suspected misses, without access to ground-truth labels. The agent then uses this feedback to revise its queries. On the OWASP Benchmark for Python, SESAA reaches a mean F1 of 0.742 across 8 independent runs, well above the default configurations of five widely used tools and comparable to the strongest of them once it is tuned with access to ground-truth labels that SESAA never sees. In a pilot on real-world Python projects, queries induced from code available before a vulnerability was introduced detect 10 of 19 subsequent CVEs, including 9 detected by rules written for the same repository. The resulting detector is a set of executable, human-readable queries that engineers can inspect, modify, and run independently. These results suggest that LLM agents can turn static-analysis rule maintenance from a manually authored process into an iterative process of automated discovery and repair.","tldr":"背景与问题：静态分析漏报常因新API和代码习惯尚无检测规则；直接让模型找漏洞难留下可复用产物，依赖已知漏洞补丁写规则又受历史案例限制。\n\n方法：SESAA从空规则集出发，反复生成并运行检测查询。另一个模型检查告警与部分未告警代码，给出疑似误报和漏报工单；代理据此修订，按伪标签估计的精度与覆盖保留最佳规则。真值只用于事后评价，批评模型本身不学习。\n\n结果与结论：Python合成基准八次运行的平均F1为0.742；真实项目试验检测到19个后续漏洞中的10个。与使用真值调优工具的比较信息条件不同；关键结果和批评器准确率分析被截断，不能核验代理评分与真实质量的一致性。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，价值在于把模型判断沉淀为可独立运行的规则，而非证明改进者变强。正文称逐告警判分，附录却描述代表样本抽查，反馈粒度需核对；缓存判决能稳定评分，也可能持续保留早期误判。","published_at":"2026-10-20","topics":"无真值反馈; 执行证据驱动改进; 外部记忆与规则更新","added_on":"2026-10-24","novelty_summary":"作者声称以LLM伪标签自动发现和维护静态分析查询。本文证据：规则执行结果与批评器工单驱动修订，最高代理评分规则被保留；反馈是预训练模型提供的弱监督，未展示代理或批评器更新。相对SpecForge（arxiv:2610.15708）以执行验证测试修订行为规格，本篇修订检测程序且依赖模型漏洞判断；相对HarnessPro（arxiv:2610.26770）用模型生成测试筛选harness，本篇直接以批评器判决及漏报工单评价规则。编辑推断：主要改进外部检测工件，材料未显示规则反过来改善AI代理的推理或学习机制，故列为adjacent；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.28945","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.28945v1","title":"Self-Improving Agents with World Model Predictive Paths","authors":"Haori Lu; Tianyu Gao; Yaoyao Liu; Yingying Li","affiliations":"University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents are increasingly expected to interact with environments and improve their decisions during deployment. However, how anticipating future outcomes and drawing on accumulated interaction experience can jointly support decision-making remains underexplored. We propose a test-time framework, inspired by Model Predictive Path Integral (MPPI) control, that combines multi-branch predictive analysis with experience-based adaptation. At each step, the agent proposes multiple candidate actions and imagines their outcomes with a world model, so that alternatives can be compared without being executed in the environment. Since language environments provide neither explicit dynamics nor costs, the predicted outcomes are evaluated for task progress and risk, and MPPI-style weights over the resulting costs guide the final decision. A dual-branch experience memory enables self-improvement: the planner branch refines candidate generation and action selection, while the world model branch improves next-observation prediction. Experiments on ALFWorld and ScienceWorld across three backbones demonstrate the strong overall performance of our method and the effectiveness of experience-guided predictive control. Our code will be made publicly available.","tldr":"背景与问题：只执行单一动作会遗漏替代方案，真实环境分支搜索又成本高；更准确地预测下一观察，也不保证选到更有用的动作。\n\n方法：系统预测少量候选动作的一步结果，由语言评估器判断进展与风险，按预测成本加权供控制器决策。真实转移分别写成规划和世界模型经验，改变后续提案、选择及预测；模型参数冻结。\n\n结果与结论：材料称在两个语言交互环境、三种骨干上整体领先，但主结果、消融和成本表缺失。理论拆分候选覆盖、预测成本与选择误差，不保证实际任务成功率单调提高。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，预测器与行动器需要分别验收：正确加权救不了缺失候选，控制器还可生成未经预测的新动作。经验基于真实转移，进展判断仍由模型完成，须隔离记忆收益和额外推理调用收益。","published_at":"2026-10-20","topics":"世界模型与递归改进; 预测误差反馈; 经验迁移","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称双分支经验改善预测控制。本文证据：真实转移更新文本记忆，模型预测及语言成本判断指导行动，参数和规则固定。相对arxiv:2610.13912更新策略—预测器并检查兼容性，本篇采用上下文适配；相对arxiv:2610.12789独立验证规则，本篇未展示同等证伪准入。编辑推断：是预测与记忆路线的组合细化；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.28815","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.28815v1","title":"Forging More Tasks into Better Harnesses: Agentic Harness Evolution via Successive Scale Racing","authors":"Jingzhe Liu; Jiliang Tang; Tong Zhao; Neil Shah; Clark Mingxuan Ju","affiliations":"Michigan State University；Snap Inc.","abstract":"Agentic harness evolution optimizes an agent's instructions, tools, and control flow by using its task execution experiences as evolving evidence. While more evolution tasks should intuitively improve performance, our preliminary study reveals a paradoxical failure mode: the performance of existing methods degrades as the task pool expands. Our further analysis demonstrates that this degradation stems from suboptimal evidence selection during optimization, as different evidence combinations lead to substantially different evolution outcomes. To address this issue, we propose Successive Scale Racing (SSR), a framework that adaptively searches for optimal evidence combinations in each evolution round. SSR constructs diverse evidence combinations based on the corresponding task quality and coverage, and efficiently races the resulting candidate harnesses under a small compute budget. Empirically, across three distinct benchmarks, SSR achieves state-of-the-art results in all six configurations. Notably, as the task pool grows from 40 to 200, SSR steadily improves the pass rate from 64.3% to 68.3%, while the baselines' performances all drop. Furthermore, its racing mechanism identifies near-optimal candidates while reducing validation executions by 60%.","tldr":"背景与问题：harness演化加入更多任务后可能退化，重复或低价值轨迹会稀释修改方向；固定证据规模也难跟随当前失败分布。\n\n方法：SSR按可操作性和覆盖度排列经验，用不同长度的证据前缀分别修改同一父代。候选在共享批次上竞赛，逐步淘汰弱者并保护父代；接受新版本后重采轨迹，刷新下一轮排序。\n\n结果与结论：扩大任务池时，通过率从64.3%增至68.3%，所测基线下降。候选选择混合验证与训练任务，不能视为纯留出估计；理论仅给单轮有限池保证。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，证据规模值得成为每轮搜索变量。但嵌套前缀同时改变规模和内容，不能完全隔离规模效应；覆盖目标的近似保证不等于执行收益保证，长期选择偏差仍需单独测量。","published_at":"2026-10-20","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 预算受限研究搜索; 选择误差","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称搜索证据组合使任务池扩张转为正收益。本文证据：执行轨迹与模型质量判断排序，共享批次竞赛筛选，新父代刷新经验；排序和竞赛算法固定。相对arxiv:2604.25850组织可观测证据，本篇显式搜索证据规模；相对arxiv:2610.19424限制验证内容暴露，本篇处理训练证据选择。编辑推断：是证据治理的具体推进，非改进器递归学习；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.28577","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.28577v1","title":"Cache Engineering for Agents","authors":"Tianyu Fu; Ruoxi Wang; Zihan Min; Zhongqi Ren; Zhihao Li; Tengxuan Liu; Shengxu Mu; Hanling Zhang; Yu Wang","affiliations":"清华大学；香港中文大学","abstract":"Large Language Model (LLM) agents can handle increasingly complex tasks, navigating long trajectories of observations and actions. As these trajectories grow, key-value (KV) cache I/O and storage become the dominant cost. Trajectories can also exceed the LLM's maximum context length, requiring control over active cache growth. Prior work uses context engineering to reduce cache size by trimming or summarizing history. However, modifying the trajectory prefix invalidates subsequent cached states and triggers costly re-prefilling of retained context. Task accuracy can also suffer when too little context is retained to limit re-prefill costs. We propose cache engineering as a new scheme. It allows agents to directly control their active KV cache without modifying the trajectory or re-prefilling retained context. Specifically, agents can proactively use drop to exclude selected cache from future attention and repos to adjust retained keys' position encodings. We formalize these cache operations and identify history dependence as a serving challenge: identical token sequences can yield different cache states under different cache operation sequences, making prefix matching insufficient for correct cache reuse. Thus, we co-design the AKV serving engine. It provides a stateless interface compatible with existing serving APIs, while internally managing stateful cache reuse, eviction, and restoration. Experiments show that a tool-response rolling-drop cache policy improves average benchmark scores by 1.7 points and reduces average cost by 27.7%, compared with conventional threshold-triggered summarization. With AKV, it achieves up to 1.2x the output throughput and a 1.5x speedup in P95 request latency. Recursive self-improvement of cache policies further reduces cost by 7.1% over expert design. Our code is at https://github.com/thu-nics/AKV.","tldr":"背景与问题：删除或总结早期文本会使后续KV缓存失效，重新预填充增加成本；为限制重算而大幅丢弃上下文，又可能损害任务表现。\n\n方法：Cache Engineering允许直接删除缓存并调整位置，保留其他已计算状态。服务系统同时记录token与操作历史，避免错误复用；这些操作也成为agent可搜索、评估和修改的推理资源策略。\n\n结果与结论：人工滚动删除策略比阈值总结平均省27.7%成本；演化策略在留出任务上比专家策略再省7.1%。演化反馈、预算与准确率约束段落缺失，不能把整体系统收益归于自改进。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，变化是开放内部缓存控制面。同样文本不再对应同样状态，复现必须保留操作历史；当前服务收益较明确，但策略演化的信用来源和递归机制仍待核查。","published_at":"2026-10-20","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 预算受限研究搜索; AI 服务优化","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称直接缓存控制支持策略RSI。本文证据充分描述缓存操作及服务机制，但演化部分仅见留出成本收益，反馈来源、继承方式和搜索预算不完整。相对arxiv:2605.09998在线改提示与记忆，本篇开放缓存控制；相对arxiv:2610.25012优化编译计划，本篇直接改变agent推理可用状态。编辑推断：改进对象有变化，元级收益未明；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.28282","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.28282v1","title":"ChartEvo: Self-Evolving Agent Harnesses for Long-Tail Chart Reasoning","authors":"Qi Wang; Peijie Wang; Jun Cao; Haoyang Tong; Xiao-Hui Li; Fei Yin; Cheng-Lin Liu","affiliations":"中国科学院自动化研究所；中国科学院大学；中关村学院","abstract":"Multimodal large language models (MLLMs) have substantially advanced chart understanding and reasoning, yet their performance remains highly uneven across chart types. While modern MLLMs perform well on common charts, their accuracy drops sharply on long-tail charts with diverse visual structures and reasoning requirements. Tool-augmented agents can improve complex chart reasoning by introducing specialized visual capabilities, but manually engineering strategies and tools for the heterogeneous and evolving long tail is difficult to scale. We introduce \\textbf{ChartEvo}, a recursive self-improvement framework that enables chart agents to adapt to underperforming chart types through experience-driven harness-level self-improvement. ChartEvo jointly evolves reusable chart-specific Skills and executable Tools, while learning reusable local tool-call chains to compose evolved capabilities and control the inference overhead of tool-augmented reasoning. On long-tail charts from ChartBench and ChartX, ChartEvo improves accuracy over its base MLLM, Qwen3.7-Plus, by \\textbf{45.6\\%} and \\textbf{32.5\\%}, respectively, demonstrating the effectiveness of recursive self-improvement for long-tail chart adaptation.","tldr":"背景与问题：图表总体成绩掩盖少数类型的严重短板，固定工具难覆盖异质结构；让模型逐步协调稳定操作链还增加调用开销。\n\n方法：ChartEvo用训练答案真值与执行轨迹诊断能力缺口，联合修订技能、工具，并把验证过的局部调用组合保存为工具链。获准组件进入下一轮，测试时冻结harness，在新实例上复用。\n\n结果与结论：ChartBench长尾准确率从48.0%升至93.6%，对应45.6个百分点，并非相对提高45.6%。两基准分别演化，支持同基准新实例适配，不能据此认定跨基准迁移。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，把稳定局部流程交给运行时执行，可能兼顾测量与调用效率。但案例中模型仍把不确定区间中点当答案，工具可执行和推断可信必须分开验收；完整消融与演化成本未见。","published_at":"2026-10-20","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 执行证据驱动改进; 经验迁移","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称技能、工具与局部工具链共同演化。本文证据：训练答案、执行轨迹及重执行验证驱动组件继承，测试期冻结，未显示改进器更新。相对arxiv:2610.23599按功能维护技能，本篇增加图表测量工具和持久调用结构；相对arxiv:2610.24464共享执行栈，本篇面向图表且分基准演化。编辑推断：应用与执行组织有推进，摘要百分比应按结果表纠正；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.28201","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.28201v1","title":"MaD-RSI: Model-as-Data for Recursive Self-Improvement of Agent Harnesses","authors":"Yu Cui; Hong He; Ruiqing Yue; Sicheng Pan; Zhuoyu Sun; Yifei Liu; Ting Li; Wenzhuo Zhu; Baohan Huang; Haibin Zhang; Cong Zuo","affiliations":"北京理工大学；清华大学；中国科学院成都计算机应用研究所；中国科学院大学；北京工业大学；浙江清华长三角研究院；嘉兴市人工智能与网络韧性重点实验室","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement (RSI) of agent harnesses has emerged as an effective approach to enhancing the capabilities of large language model (LLM) agents. By searching the harness space for a specific LLM on a given dataset, RSI can discover a harness tailored to the capabilities and behavioral characteristics of that model. However, such optimization often creates a strong coupling between the learned harness and its target LLM, limiting generalization across models and requiring substantial computational resources to adapt to new LLMs. Moreover, existing RSI methods typically optimize a harness using feedback from a single model and evaluate its generalization to other models only after training. This paradigm treats model differences primarily as a criterion for evaluating generalization rather than as valuable evidence for optimization. In this paper, we introduce a new perspective that treats models as data and places the harness at the center of optimization. Building on this perspective, we propose \\textsc{MaD-RSI}, a framework that directly optimizes a shared harness across multiple heterogeneous LLMs by incorporating their diverse failure trajectories into the training process. Rather than assessing model differences only after optimization, \\textsc{MaD-RSI} leverages these differences as training evidence to guide the self-improvement of a shared harness. Furthermore, we introduce a new evaluation framework with two complementary metrics designed to assess the effectiveness of harness optimization across models. Experiments across multiple datasets and LLMs demonstrate that \\textsc{MaD-RSI} improves generalization over existing approaches while reducing training costs.","tldr":"背景与问题：按单个模型的失败优化 harness，容易把运行规则绑在该模型上；换模型便需重新搜索。跨模型差异通常只用于事后测迁移，没有参与改进。\n\n方法：MaD-RSI 对齐多个冻结模型在同题上的成功与失败，挑选兼具分歧和行为覆盖的样本，再用带来源的轨迹对比诊断共享 harness。任务评估器提供结果，修改后的共享版本进入后续轮次。\n\n结果与结论：LawBench 四模型共同成功率比最强单模型优化基线高4.5个百分点；加入两个未参与开发的模型后，共同成功也均有改善。省训练成本的参照是四次独立优化总和，安全任务反而更贵。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，模型异质性可以成为定位运行时缺陷的证据，而非只增加测试配置。但分歧不能直接识别原因；缺少关键消融，尚不能确定收益主要来自证据选择还是多模型暴露。","published_at":"2026-10-20","topics":"Harness 递归演化; RSI 评测与迁移; 失败诊断","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称把模型差异转为共享 harness 的优化数据。本文证据：任务评估结果和对齐轨迹驱动诊断及后续修订，骨干冻结；未展示优化器自身更新。相对 Self-Harness（arxiv:2606.09498）针对模型特定失败，本篇联合使用异构执行者；相对 AHE（arxiv:2604.25850）事后测试跨模型迁移，本篇将多模型证据前置。编辑推断：这是共享优化机制的具体推进，但没有与上述工作匹配比较，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.27889","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.27889v1","title":"Elicitation or Expansion? Demystifying Gains from Agent Harness Optimization","authors":"Younghyun Kim; Wooseok Seo; Minseo Kim; Seunghyuk Oh; Minjae Lee; Donghoon Kim; Hyung Il Koo; Jaehyung Kim; Wonjun Kang","affiliations":"FuriosaAI；延世大学；加州大学伯克利分校","abstract":"Recent studies in harness optimization have shown substantial performance gains in language model agents without updating model weights. A well-designed harness more effectively leverages the underlying model's capabilities by shaping context, tool use, and execution workflows. However, naïve success rates alone do not fully characterize whether optimized harness yields more reliable success on tasks already within reach (elicitation) or a broader range of solvable tasks (expansion). This distinction is crucial for recursive self-improvement and evolutionary search, as expansion may provide a broader range of successful experiences to push the capability boundaries. Despite the growing significance, this distinction remains underexplored in harness optimization. We conduct a systematic analysis to study the effect of gains from harness optimization. Building on pass@k analyses in the reinforcement learning (RL) literature that compare models before and after RL training, we compare optimized harnesses with their pre-optimization counterparts. Specifically, we assess changes in reachable task coverage, compare harness optimization with model scaling and increased inference-time compute, and examine how gains vary with task difficulty. Across static prediction and dynamic tasks, we find that pass@1 advantages of harness over stronger interventions can reverse at larger attempt budgets and aggregate gains conceal shortfalls on hard tasks, underscoring the need for a fine-grained diagnosis.","tldr":"背景与问题：单次成功率上升，可能只是让原本偶尔能解的题更稳定成功，并未扩大可解题范围。对依赖成功轨迹继续学习的 RSI，这两种收益意义不同。\n\n方法：固定求解模型，用既有 harness 搜索得到候选，再在共同测试集上重复执行，比较不同尝试预算下的覆盖率，并按难度拆分；更大模型和更高推理强度作为参照。\n\n结果与结论：LawBench 中，优化后小模型单次表现超过大模型，多次尝试覆盖却落后；迁移到三个分类数据集时，大预算覆盖均低于原 harness。不过附录也存在优化后覆盖超过大模型的配置，不能概括为 harness 无法扩展能力。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，候选选择若只奖励平均成功，会遗漏少数困难题上的互补成功。有限次数的 pass@k 测量的是观察到的覆盖，不能证明题目在无限预算下不可达。","published_at":"2026-10-20","topics":"RSI 评测与迁移; 能力归因; Harness 递归演化","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称区分 harness 收益的可靠性与任务覆盖。本文证据：比较优化前后 pass@k、难度分组及强参照，不提出新的递归更新器。相对 HDA（arxiv:2610.22466）拆解捷径和额外计算，本篇测量尝试预算改变时的覆盖与排名；相对 SEAR（arxiv:2610.18792）比较持续修订与重启，本篇重点是最终 harness 的重复执行。编辑推断：补充既有能力归因审计，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.27735","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.27735v1","title":"RSI Control: Can AI Models Perform Covert Sabotage in the Self-Improvement Process?","authors":"Kaiwen Zhou; Udari Madhushani Sehwag","affiliations":"Scale AI，Preparedness and Policy","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement, in which frontier AI models work on training the next generation, is quickly becoming a reality. However, the safety of this process has received far less attention than it should. A misaligned model training its successor can shape what that successor knows, how it behaves, and what it wants, and the harm carries forward into the next generation. We study this risk through the lens of AI control. We introduce RSI Control Arena, a testbed in which a frontier model, acting as an autonomous R\\&D agent, is given a benign main task from a stage of a successor model's training pipeline together with a covert side task to install a misaligned property in the successor. The testbed contains 16 side tasks in three classes, forming 22 task pairs with main tasks that span the pipeline from data curation to reinforcement learning. We evaluate six frontier models as agents against LLM monitors that read the transcript of the run and the agent's reasoning. We observe that every model completes a substantial share of the side tasks without degrading the main-task performance, including side tasks that make the successor itself a better saboteur. Under minimal instructions to stay covert, models already produce successful attacks that monitors fail to detect, and providing a short list of evasion tactics further reduces the detection rate. Monitors with access to agent's reasoning detects most attacks, but not all. Our results indicate that recursive self-improvement raises significant safety concerns, and that strong safety effort should be in place before models are trusted with greater responsibility of training their successors.","tldr":"背景与问题：自主研发 agent 能改变后继模型的数据、奖励与训练流程，主任务成绩正常也可能掩盖被植入的额外行为。只验收模型能力不足以发现这种风险。\n\n方法：RSI Control Arena 为合法训练任务配上明确的隐蔽副目标，用隐藏探针检查交付物，再让不知道副目标的监控模型读取执行记录，比较是否额外开放推理记录的检测效果。\n\n结果与结论：374次攻击运行中，36%在满足主任务保留标准时植入副目标；读取推理能发现多数攻击，但仍有遗漏。主任务保留允许有限退化，且后继是小模型，多数副目标采用无害代理。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，训练数据控制权是值得优先审计的干预面，依据是高成功任务集中于可写或可选数据的设置。这证明受指令攻击的可行性，不能推成模型会自发破坏，亦未测完整多代风险累积。","published_at":"2026-10-20","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; 递归安全改进","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称检验后继训练中的隐蔽破坏与监控。本文证据：显式攻击目标、隐藏交付物评估及良性运行校准；改变的是后继模型或训练工件，没有展示完整多代递归链。相对 Athanor（arxiv:2610.21055）检验自主后训练产物质量，本篇加入对抗目标及监控；相对可恢复性研究（arxiv:2610.27465）处理普通误准入，本篇处理蓄意偏离。编辑推断：为自主训练增加具体威胁证据，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.27610","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.27610v1","title":"Auditing the Product, Not the Recursion: The Evaluation Evidence Behind Recursive Self-Improvement Claims","authors":"Zihan Chen; Di Zhu; Lei Nico Zheng","affiliations":"Stevens Institute of Technology；University of Massachusetts Boston","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement (RSI) promises AI systems, such as self-evolving LLM agents, that become better at producing further improvements. Evaluating this promise requires separating product claims about the final system from process claims about the improvement process itself. Existing surveys specify the evidence these claims require, but how often studies report that evidence remains unmeasured. We examine this question through full-text coding of 114 eligible studies in a reproducible arXiv search frame frozen in October 2026, including 90 that describe their own systems as RSI. The codebook links claims to evaluation designs. Independent human coding, third-reader adjudication, and a separate blind coding of improver comparisons assess coding reliability. Among the 90 RSI studies, 90% report product evaluation beyond development tasks under a broad criterion that includes partial or unstated separation, while 60% report evaluation on tasks unused for selection. Only 22% audit two or more reruns of the full loop. In a human-coded random sample, the RSI studies show the same contrast: 45% evaluate on tasks unused for selection and 14% audit two or more reruns. Of the 26 studies claiming a better improvement procedure, 23 report a related comparison, but only 4 compare earlier and later procedures from identical starting artifacts at a matched budget. Across these results and a comparison set of established works, evidence for repeatability and improved procedures remains less developed than product evaluation. Three propositions explain how selection effects, shared evaluator errors, and changes in system state limit what product evaluations can establish. Together, the findings support a claim-indexed reporting standard that connects each claim to the evaluation design needed to test it.","tldr":"背景与问题：最终系统更强、循环可重复获益、改进者更会产生改进，是不同主张。已有原则说明应测什么，却缺少研究实际提供多少证据的统计。\n\n方法：论文对固定检索框架内研究逐篇全文编码，把主张对应到留出评估、完整循环重跑和新旧改进者同起点比较，并用独立人工编码与裁决检查一致性。\n\n结果与结论：90篇自称 RSI 的研究中，60%报告不参与选择的任务评估，22%审计至少两次完整重跑；声称改进程序增强的26篇中，仅4篇匹配起始工件和预算比较新旧程序。比例描述该检索框架中的报告实践。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，最应补齐的是改进者交换实验，而非再画一条任务涨分曲线。但未报告不能等同未实施，部分编码项目一致性偏低；本研究也没有复现这些系统的实际收益。","published_at":"2026-10-20","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; RSI 评测与迁移; 能力归因","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称把既有评估原则落实为可统计的全文编码。本文证据：固定搜索框架、主张对应的实验设计、人工复核及改进者比较分类；无自改进系统更新闭环。相对物理 RSI 综述（arxiv:2610.29677）的证据层次，本篇量化报告频率；相对 HDA（arxiv:2610.22466）直接干预演化工件，本篇审计文献中的证据设计，并对 Hyperagents（arxiv:2603.19461）等锚点编码。编辑推断：是评估实践的实证补充，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.27495","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.27495v1","title":"Self-Evolving Agents through Privileged Retrospective Distillation","authors":"Yuhang Zhou; Yifan Wu; Bo Peng; Mingyi Wang; Jiayi Liu; Xiangjun Fan; Lizhu Zhang; Zhuokai Zhao","affiliations":"Meta AI","abstract":"Self-evolving agents aim to improve from their own experience rather than remain fixed after deployment, but naturally collected trajectories often lack ground-truth solutions or verifier-derived rewards. We introduce Retrospective Self-Distillation (RSD), a multi-round framework that turns such experience into dense supervision using privileged retrospective context. For each on-policy trajectory, the same underlying model acts as both student and teacher: the teacher re-scores the student's realized actions while conditioning on cross-task precedents and lessons, together with turn-level reflection and future hindsight from the completed trajectory. The resulting teacher distribution is distilled back into the policy through on-policy self-distillation. Across rounds, the experience bank grows and the retrospective context is refreshed, allowing the model, its data, and its supervision to co-evolve. We further introduce frontier-guided context-policy evolution, where a stronger frontier model proposes constrained edits to how privileged context is constructed. Across ALFWorld, ScienceWorld, and SearchQA with Qwen3-8B and Qwen3-14B, RSD improves performance by up to 59.7% relative to the base model, while frontier-guided context-policy evolution adds up to a further 44.7% relative improvement over a fixed context policy. These results show that naturally accumulated experience can be converted into persistent model capability without ground-truth trajectories or verifier-derived rewards for the core policy update.","tldr":"背景与问题：自然交互常只有一次轨迹，没有正确动作序列或可靠奖励；仅训练成功样本又会丢掉失败中的环境反馈。\n\n方法：RSD 让同一模型在事后读取相关经验与后续观察，重新评价自己实际生成的动作，再把教师分布蒸馏回权重。每轮更新策略、扩充经验并刷新监督；扩展版由外部强模型调整上下文构造，环境指标筛选修改。\n\n结果与结论：摘要给出三类任务上的最大相对收益，但正文指出 SearchQA 多轮表现变化很小，主要结果表未提供。核心权重更新不用验证器奖励，不等于扩展版无需外部验证器或教师。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，监督优势来自事后信息差，而非模型仅凭自信变强。扩展版只回退上下文、不回退权重，跨轮成绩比较因此不能单独隔离构造规则的贡献；应从同一检查点比较规则的训练收益。","published_at":"2026-10-20","topics":"自生成监督与微调; 自适应训练经验; 自进化策略训练","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称从自身经验构造特权回顾监督，并进一步演化上下文策略。本文证据：同模型事后重评分、蒸馏、经验刷新；扩展版依赖固定外部强模型及环境评估，未证明其提案机制增强。相对 RSIPO（arxiv:2610.15772）用回放收益训练技能并校准教师，本篇以未来观察提供监督且核心更新无验证器奖励；相对 LoopOPD（arxiv:2610.10623），教师优势来自信息而非额外循环计算。编辑推断：监督来源有具体变化，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.27465","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.27465v1","title":"Recoverability and Verifier Strength: Two Measured Preconditions for Unattended Agent Self-Improvement","authors":"De Wang; Peng Qi","affiliations":"Uniphore","abstract":"Agent platforms are starting to improve their own agents: they read a deployed agent's execution traces, derive a change, have an automated verifier approve it, and release it with no human author. How much of this loop can safely run without a human? We propose two quantities a platform can measure. Verifier strength $σ$ is how well the available verifier -- often an LLM judge -- agrees with a trusted reference verifier; it limits how much a step can improve the agent. Recoverability is how cheaply a bad change can be undone: whether undoing it needs a new verifier approval, and how much of the old behavior a rollback restores. A step should run unattended only if both are adequate. On our platform this rule allows prompt, tool and skill edits to run unattended and keeps weight updates under human sign-off. Our main contribution is these two definitions and how to measure them. We built a platform that applies the rule and tested it in two ways: on the platform's own approval gate, and in controlled experiments on the $τ^2$-bench agent benchmark. On verifier strength, the platform's LLM judge sometimes gave the same score no matter what it was shown (9 of 37 settings) and reported no error, so a verifier can look healthy while approving anything; its strength must be measured, and two simple tests catch the failure. On recoverability, restoring a saved copy brought the agent back to its original behavior, but a regenerated undo did not, so only changes whose old version is kept can be reversed without a human; and while a change was deployed, it altered the outcome of 17 percent of tasks beyond normal run-to-run variation, which no undo repairs. Together these support the rule: a change can run unattended only when its old version is kept and its verifier's strength has been measured.","tldr":"背景与问题：自动检查能正常返回分数，不代表能辨别坏修改；回滚代码也无法撤回部署期间已经交付的错误结果。\n\n方法：论文分别测验证器相对可信参考的判别相关性，以及撤销是否需要重新审批、行为能否恢复和部署影响范围，据此限制无人值守更新。实验固定一侧、改变另一侧，区分验收与恢复故障。\n\n结果与结论：平台检查器存在对输入变化完全不响应的设置；保存旧提示能恢复到随机波动基线，重新生成撤销则不能。弱验证器选择更差修改的趋势未显著，另一领域也未出现趋势，不能把规则当作充分安全保证。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可恢复性取决于是否保留版本，而非简单按提示或权重分类；保留检查点的权重同样可回退。验证器相关性还须配合误准入率，且部署期影响需要另外记账。","published_at":"2026-10-20","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; 自改进稳定性; 评估器递归改进","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称提出无人值守更新的两个可测前提。本文证据：参考验证器校准、检查器失效案例及提示恢复实验；工具、技能和权重的分类结论未分别实验。相对 The Self-Improvement Problem（arxiv:2610.21646）讨论普遍认证的理论边界，本篇测量有限部署条件；相对 UCoE（arxiv:2610.17609）演化评分程序，本篇审计验收器而不更新它。编辑推断：工程验收条件得到部分支持，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.26848","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.26848v1","title":"Where is Physical RSI capability from? An Observational Scaling Law of LLM-as-policy","authors":"Zekai Li; Jiayi Yu; Jinlu Zhang; Luyang Niu; Zekun Qi; Jun Zheng; Xuchuan Chen; Dairu Liu; Yintianrun Zhang; He Wang; Li Yi","affiliations":"Galbot Team","abstract":"In this paper, we systematically investigate the mechanisms, scaling behavior, and generalization of physical Recursive self-improvement. We introduce PhysRSI-eval to quantify physical RSI through a five-axis metric: First-Attempt Performance, Efficiency, Success, Budget and Improvement from failure. Different VLMs are evaluated on 18 manipulation tasks under a fixed interaction budget. The analysis of experimental results motivates the Physical Barrel Hypothesis: different capabilities may constrain different parts of improvement. The five-axis metrics also distinguish systems with close public benchmark averages and show that high scores need not come with early or efficient gains. We study observational scaling from two perspectives: predicting the relative performance of VLM agents from their public capabilities, and forecasting later progress from early physical feedback. Together, these analyses ask how quickly and how far an agent can improve. Moreover, we conduct workspace interventions and then analyze what improvement leaves behind. Removing history reduces late-round success, frozen workspaces remain useful on unseen layouts, and three cross-task cases achieve success earlier. The results suggest that scene-specific adaptation and reusable experience can coexist.","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人最终得分高，未必更早学会或更省交互；公共能力均分也可能掩盖首次执行与失败恢复所需能力的差别。\n\n方法：PhysRSI-eval 固定模型，让代码、工具和笔记跨轮保留，用原生任务评分反馈修订；分别测起点、增益时机、达到的成绩、交互节约与失败恢复，再清空、冻结或迁移工作区检验经验作用。\n\n结果与结论：六任务消融中，移除历史使后期成功率由41.7%降至8.3%；冻结工作区在新布局仍可成功。能力关联仅来自六套模型与运行配置，不能把感知和空间分数的相关性称为因果瓶颈或普遍缩放律。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，应把改善幅度与改善速度分开验收。主实验主要使用单布局与种子，首次成功后停止；预算指标还只统计已解任务，跨模型比较必须同时看条件任务集合。","published_at":"2026-10-19","topics":"RSI 评测与迁移; 具身持续学习评测; 能力归因","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称提出五轴物理 RSI 评测及观察性缩放分析。本文证据：原生环境反馈驱动持久工作区修订，历史干预和冻结迁移检验经验；骨干和改进流程未递归更新。相对 SEAR（arxiv:2610.18792）分离重试和继承，本篇进一步区分增益时机与物理预算，并用公共能力预测表现；未匹配比较两套协议。编辑推断：评测维度有推进，缩放结论仍探索性，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.26770","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.26770v2","title":"HarnessPro: Recursive Harness Self-Improvement with Pareto Optimization for Performance-Cost Trade-offs","authors":"Zhuoshi Pan; ZhiYuan Feng; Yukuo Cen; Honglin Lin; Junru Lu; Zhongxia Chen; Shuo Yang; H. Vicky Zhao; Jie Tang","affiliations":"清华大学；Z.AI；上海交通大学；University of Warwick；Kling AI","abstract":"Harness development plays a crucial role in building capable AI agents. Recent approaches improve harnesses through recursive self-improvement (RSI), but their performance gains often come with higher execution costs. We introduce HarnessPro, a label-free method for evolving harnesses to improve task performance while reducing execution cost. In this setting, candidate harnesses are evaluated using LLM-generated tests without access to ground-truth solutions or official tests. Specialized agents diagnose execution trajectories, plan updates with different performance-cost priorities, and implement them as candidate harnesses. Rather than returning a single harness, HarnessPro uses normalized weighted squared-distance selection to provide cost-focused (lite), balanced (medium), and performance-focused (heavy) harnesses for different deployment budgets. Selected harnesses enter the next iteration, where execution feedback guides further updates. Our experiments cover Terminal-Bench 2, SWE-Bench Pro, and ProgramBench, using GPT-5.5 with Codex and GLM-5.2 with Claude Code. Across these benchmarks using GPT-5.5 with Codex, the heavy mode of HarnessPro achieves an average pass-rate gain of 2.0 percentage points and an average per-task cost reduction of 26.1% relative to RHO. This advantage also holds when using GLM-5.2 with Claude Code. Code is available at https://github.com/pzs19/HarnessPro","tldr":"背景与问题：harness 搜索常靠增加探索和核验换成功率，却抬高部署成本；只保留一个最高分版本，也无法服务不同预算。\n\n方法：HarnessPro 从重复轨迹定位失败与浪费，提出不同成本偏好的修改；用一次生成后固定的模型测试评价候选，排除低于初始表现或被支配的版本，再保留不同预算代表进入下一轮。\n\n结果与结论：三项编码基准上，摘要称重模式相对 RHO 平均多解2.0个百分点、每任务费用低26.1%。最终使用官方测试，开发不接触官方答案；但主结果与关键测试质量消融被截断，尚无法核对代理测试的误判及总搜索成本。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，将部署费用直接纳入选择，比事后压缩上下文更能约束搜索方向。但固定生成测试只稳定了尺子，并未认证尺子正确；部署省钱还需与演化开销分开计算。","published_at":"2026-10-19","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 预算受限研究搜索; 无真值反馈","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称无标签地推进性能—成本前沿。本文证据：固定模型生成测试和执行费用筛选多个 harness，获选版本及轨迹进入下一轮；规划和选择规则固定。相对 RHO（arxiv:2606.05922）直接自偏好比较，本篇改用固定可执行测试并保留多预算解；相对 AHE（arxiv:2604.25850）强调可观测编辑，本篇显式优化费用。编辑推断：属于已有演化机制的多目标扩展，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.26554","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.26554v1","title":"BetaMem: Learning to Remember a Changing World for Embodied Agents","authors":"Mai Liu; He Sun; Siru Zhong; Kerun Chen; Hao Yan; Xiaohui Lv; Shuai Tao; Wulong Liu","affiliations":"Beta Infinity；北京大学；香港科技大学（广州）；北京航空航天大学","abstract":"Long-horizon embodied agents face temporal confusion and incomplete or distorted records, recurring errors from fixed memory rules, and growing storage and retrieval costs. We present BetaMem, a framework for building and evolving traceable long-term memory through six linked layers: working, spatial, entity, episodic, experiential, and procedural memory. A dual-level write contract constrains operation executability and source support for content: supervised fine-tuning learns compliant memory operations, while reinforcement learning combines repeated sampling with teacher verification of the original observations to reward complete, accurate records and penalize omissions, distortion, and unsupported content. We formulate failure-driven policy recursive self-improvement through diagnosis along the causal sequence of memory operations and local rule repairs gated by independent replay. Atomic tools frame storage, updates, retrieval, and forgetting as cost-utility allocation under storage and read budgets. Using the open-source Qwen3.5-9B model for memory generation, BetaMem achieves overall scores of 48.08% on M3-Bench-robot, 92.08% on LoCoMo, 72.6% on OpenEQA EM-EQA, and 62.4% on EgoLifeQA, the highest among the listed memory methods under their respective evaluation protocols. Training the model for memory generation raises the contract pass rate from 50.9% to 86.2% while reducing output tokens per stored action by 47.3%. A separate Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct evaluation on EMem-Bench achieves an average success rate of 38.4% and an average error recurrence rate of 24.9%. We perform best among evaluated methods using comparably sized open-source models. Category results show that we have advantages in integrating information across observations, recalling events over long histories, and inferring personal habits.","tldr":"背景与问题：长期具身记忆会把过去观察误当当前状态，遗漏或编造记录；只修正一条记忆，又无法阻止固定写入和检索规则重复犯错。\n\n方法：BetaMem 为记录保留时间范围和原始证据，训练写入模型满足可执行及来源支持约束；教师回看原观察检查完整性与失真。另提出沿记忆操作链诊断失败，对局部规则修补做独立回放后再采用。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称训练使写入合同通过率从50.9%升至86.2%，并降低生成开销；多项记忆任务也有较好结果。但提供片段缺少规则演化及主要实验段落，不能将整体优势归因于递归修补。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，历史记录应作为寻找现状的线索，而非现状证明，这是证据记忆的关键边界。来源支持、写入训练和规则自改进须分别验收，目前最清楚的证据落在前两者。","published_at":"2026-10-19","topics":"外部记忆与规则更新; 经验迁移; 失败诊断","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称联合修订记忆内容与操作规则。本文证据：原观察教师核验支持写入训练，规则修补经独立回放的机制有描述，但对应实验被截断，递归增益未能核验。相对 STRATA（arxiv:2610.19386）的分层经验和方向冲突维护，本篇突出时效与原始证据；相对 EvoBelief（arxiv:2610.12789）验证环境假设，本篇管理观测记录及记忆操作。编辑推断：系统整合有具体差异，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.26453","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.26453v2","title":"Learning What to Remember: Resource-Efficient Self-Improvement for Lifelong Agents","authors":"Guannan Lai; Zi-Yang Bai; Jun-Peng Jiang; Han-Jia Ye","affiliations":"南京大学人工智能学院；南京大学计算机软件新技术全国重点实验室","abstract":"Self-improving agents aim to continuously improve their behavior by learning from experience after deployment. However, accumulating and reusing more experience does not necessarily lead to better decisions, particularly when generation, interaction, and memory resources are jointly constrained. Under such stringent constraints, we find that several existing lifelong-memory methods provide limited benefits over simple retrieval or even no-memory agents. This reveals a fundamental challenge for resource-efficient self-improvement: agents must learn not only which past experiences are relevant, but which are actually worth reusing to improve future decisions. When memory capacity and opportunities for reasoning and recovery are limited, retrieving an ineffective experience can consume scarce resources and hinder downstream execution. To address this challenge, we propose TokenWorth, a lightweight feedback-driven memory adaptation framework that learns query-dependent memory worth from sparse execution feedback. Without updating the backbone model, TokenWorth uses the learned worth to guide both experience retrieval and bounded memory management, enabling the agent to continually adapt how it reuses accumulated experience. Across three LifelongAgentBench environments and both local and API-based deployments, TokenWorth achieves the highest task success rate while using the fewest output tokens among the evaluated methods under the specified resource budgets. These results suggest that effective self-improvement under resource constraints depends not on accumulating more experience, but on learning what is worth remembering. Our code is publicly available at https://github.com/AIGNLAI/TokenWorth.","tldr":"背景与问题：生成、交互与记忆同时受限时，相关经验也可能挤占完成任务的资源；增加经验量无法补救错误检索。\n\n方法：TokenWorth 冻结骨干，用任务执行成败在线训练情境化记忆评分，统一指导检索与有限库管理。只对实际注入的经验获得反馈，以保守更新和较慢的特征适配降低稀疏信号下的漂移。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称三个主要环境、两类部署中成功率与输出效率领先；附录扩展任务优势很小，API 编码任务低于简单检索。主要结果表未提供，不能外推为跨任务一致占优。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，贡献在于低开销地学习复用决策，而非证明经验的因果价值：任务只执行一次，成功标签同时包含执行器和任务难度影响。后续应检验漂移流中评分是否仍能区分有益经验与偶然共现。","published_at":"2026-10-19","topics":"经验迁移; 预算受限研究搜索; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称从稀疏执行反馈学习查询相关的记忆价值。本文证据：实际使用经验得到任务成败标签，评分与库管理在线变化，骨干和学习规则固定；名称中的 Recursive Feature Machine 不构成改进算法递归增强。相对 STRATA（arxiv:2610.19386）固定结构维护，本篇学习选择评分；相对 ACE-Trader（arxiv:2610.25847）比较完整有无记忆流程，本篇没有反事实重跑。编辑推断：是预算约束下的估值细化，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.26342","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.26342v2","title":"VibeTraining-Bench: Data-Trainer-Harness Co-Design for Iterative System Improvement","authors":"Ruotian Peng; Yuanyi Ren; Shuaiqi Liu; Xin Guo; Fang Zhu; Yangyi Huang; Yue Wu; Zheng Wang; Yandong Wen; Zhihang Fu","affiliations":"浙江大学；西湖大学；阿里巴巴集团 Alibaba Token Hub；华南理工大学；香港中文大学","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement (RSI) requires agents to diagnose system bottlenecks and coordinate improvements across training and inference. We refer to the agents' capability to jointly optimize training data, the trainer, and the inference harness as cross-component co-design. We introduce VibeTraining-Bench, a benchmark for evaluating this capability across tasks spanning terminal operation, software engineering, multi-turn tool use, and mathematical reasoning. Within each task, research agents start from an identical initial agent system under a fixed resource budget. Guided by validation feedback, they iteratively refine data, trainers, and inference harnesses, then select and submit a final agent system for evaluation on the test set. To prevent reward hacking, we enforce three safeguards: test data isolation, separate research and grading containers, and network restrictions for research agents. Our evaluation results show that frontier research agents substantially improve target agent systems. For example, on SWE-bench Verified, GPT-6-Astra raises the target agent system's performance from 32.9% to 53.7%, comparable to the human-developed instruct model's 55.4%. However, there is still room to improve their ability to co-design and iteratively refine data, trainer, and harness to achieve cumulative performance gains. We hope that VibeTraining-Bench will serve as a unified platform for advancing RSI, deepening our understanding of cross-component optimization for agent systems. Code and data are available at https://github.com/D2I-ai/VibeTraining-Bench.","tldr":"背景与问题：预先指定只改数据、训练器或 harness，会绕过研究 agent 判断瓶颈及协调组件的能力；扩大编辑范围又增加接触测试与修改评分的机会。\n\n方法：VibeTraining-Bench 提供共同基座和固定资源，让研究者根据验证分数及轨迹选择干预，再将最终系统交给隔离评分器测试。只有终端和软件任务开放全部三类组件，其余固定推理接口。\n\n结果与结论：SWE-bench Verified 上，一套研究配置将成绩从32.9%升至53.7%；但所有研究配置的五任务均分仍低于人工指令模型。轨迹分析显示更多是数据与超参数轻量调整，完整组件消融未见。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，开放编辑范围不等于实际学会协同设计，更不证明研究者自身变强。应优先核查联合修改是否超过单组件与等预算搜索；墙钟内大量等待，也使相同时间预算不等于相同有效实验机会。","published_at":"2026-10-19","topics":"RSI 研究环境与评测; 权重—harness 联合演化; 预算受限研究搜索","added_on":"2026-10-22","novelty_summary":"作者声称评估自主选择数据—训练器—harness 干预的协同设计能力。本文证据：验证反馈推动目标系统迭代，隔离隐藏测试测最终产物，研究者自身未更新。相对 RSIGym（arxiv:2610.10310）已开放联合改进，本篇强调任务化组件权限及评分隔离，不能据此主张首次多组件平台；相对 CoTrace（arxiv:2610.10426）预定交替路径，本篇让研究者选择干预。编辑推断：属于评测协议细化，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25906","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.25906v1","title":"An Analysis of Semantic and Spatio-Temporal Co-evolution for Edge Classification on Dynamic Text-Attributed Graphs","authors":"Tyler Bonnet; Marek Rei","affiliations":"Imperial College London","abstract":"Dynamic edge classification on text-attributed Web graphs, such as review networks, community forums, and news-derived knowledge graphs, requires high quality, adaptive semantic representations in the context of network evolution. Existing dynamic graph architectures typically initialize text feature vectors with pretrained language models and hold them static during training to preserve their semantic structure, forgoing the potential benefits of allowing them to co-evolve with network topology. In this work, we investigate the effects of enabling such co-evolution with a unified text-graph alignment framework that integrates a lightweight Transformer adapter to update token-level text representations via spatio-temporal gradients from a contrastive pretraining objective. To prevent detrimental semantic distortion, a language model maintenance objective anchors the evolving text embeddings to their original semantic structure. Evaluations on the Dynamic Text-Attributed Graph Benchmark demonstrate that this anchored text-graph co-evolution consistently improves upon the edge classification performance of frozen-text baselines across diverse Web-related domains. Representational analyses reveal that the framework reduces anisotropy, improving the linear separability of text embeddings, and effectively encodes structural and temporal information into the semantic space. A computational efficiency analysis confirms that this beneficial semantic and spatio-temporal co-evolution is achieved without incurring the prohibitive computational overhead typical of end-to-end joint training.","tldr":"背景与问题：动态图通常固定文本向量，让图编码器独自弥合通用语义与时序关系之间的差距；完全自由适配又可能破坏文本语义。\n\n方法：保持预训练语言模型不变，让轻量适配器接收图结构对比学习的梯度；另用原文本向量作语义锚点，使表征能够吸收时空信息而不必逐点复制原向量。\n\n结果与结论：材料称动态图边分类优于静态文本基线，并分析表征可分性与资源开销；主要结果表被截断，不能核对完整效果量，链接预测和节点分类仍属后续工作。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，这项工作的机制是受约束表征适配，不是agent改进自身。结构信息与语义保持之间的权衡值得图学习研究关注，但训练中的参数变化、动态图变化都不自动构成RSI，应排除在进展主视图之外。","published_at":"2026-10-19","topics":"动态图表征学习; 语义对齐","added_on":"2026-10-20","novelty_summary":"作者声称锚定的文本—时空联合适配改善动态图表征。本文证据：固定预训练语言模型，以图结构对比目标和语义保持目标训练适配器及图编码器；没有AI自主提出修改或改进规则的递归闭环。与CoEvo-RSI（arxiv:2610.25078）由agent依据执行反馈选择历史检查点、修改harness不同，本篇“共演化”是常规联合梯度优化。编辑推断：不属于本任务的AI自改进范围；不能因标题近似入账，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25858","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.25858v1","title":"Are Self-Evolving Agents Continual Learners?","authors":"Xiaoyin Chen; Yizheng Huang; Yinglun Xu; Ziyun Zhao; Emmett McQuinn; Julie Liu; Hope Yao","affiliations":"Mila – Quebec AI Institute；Université de Montréal；Google DeepMind（学生研究工作）","abstract":"Large language model agents are often deployed in environments where new knowledge, tools, and workflows keep arriving. Such an agent is therefore expected to adapt continually, learning new tasks as they arrive without forgetting earlier ones. This resembles the continual learning problem, but at a pace that conventional gradient updates cannot sustain. Nonparametric self-evolving agents are a natural alternative: they adapt by rewriting their own harness, such as prompts, memory, and skills, from task feedback while the model weights stay frozen. We study whether such agents are effective continual learners across four drifting task streams that shift in topic, workflow, or domain (built from BIRD, BFCL, and ScienceWorld). Evaluating three representative methods spanning experience retrieval and self-modification (ReasoningBank, GEPA, and Meta-Harness), we find that although self-evolution improves aggregate performance on most streams, higher plasticity consistently comes at the cost of stability. Specifically, self-modifying methods apply global edits to a shared prompt or workspace, interfering with unseen tasks and overwriting earlier knowledge as the stream shifts. Conversely, similarity-based memory retrieval localizes updates across distant domains, but still retrieves foreign memories on unseen tasks and suffers from retrieval collision when similar queries require conflicting workflows. These findings show that current self-evolving agents remain incomplete continual learners.","tldr":"背景与问题：单域平均分上升不能说明agent能持续学习。共享提示或工作区的一次改动会作用于所有后续任务，可能在学会新流程时破坏旧流程。\n\n方法：固定模型，在主题、流程、领域及组合漂移流中比较记忆检索、提示修改和工作区修改。任务组及边界不告知agent，各检查点冻结harness，在独立题集上区分当前适应、提前干扰和后续遗忘。\n\n结果与结论：多数流有总体收益，但没有方法同时兼顾高适应与高稳定。全局修改会干扰其他任务；检索能隔离遥远领域，却仍会在相似查询要求相反流程时发生碰撞。实验骨干固定为一种模型。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，外部记忆并未消除持续学习问题，只把参数干扰变成修改作用域与经验路由问题。下一步应在相同漂移流、预算和任务顺序下检验条件化检索与局部更新，而不是仅比较最终平均分。","published_at":"2026-10-19","topics":"RSI 评测与迁移; 自改进稳定性; 经验迁移","added_on":"2026-10-20","novelty_summary":"作者声称现有非参数自演化agent尚非完整持续学习者。本文证据：固定骨干、共享harness，在四类分块漂移流中分别测块内适应、未见任务干扰与旧任务遗忘；反馈来自任务执行成败，审计本身不改进更新器。相对CFOE（arxiv:2610.22984）研究失败经验的修补—泛化缺口，本篇显式加入时间顺序和遗忘；相对CODA（arxiv:2610.20845）扰动技能内容，本篇改变到达的任务分布。编辑推断：扩展既有稳定性审计，但不证明所有自演化方法必然失稳；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25847","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.25847v1","title":"ACE-Trader: Adversarial Co-Evolution for Generator-Critic Trading Systems","authors":"Chang Zhou; Jiarun Zhou; Xingtong Yu; Hong Cheng; Hui Zhang; Xinming Zhang","affiliations":"University of Science and Technology of China；The Chinese University of Hong Kong","abstract":"Generator--critic trading systems pair an LLM-based trader that makes trading decisions with a red team agent that evaluates these decisions and provides feedback for revision. However, improving individual trading decisions does not ensure that both agents learn from experience and improve together over time. This raises an important question: how can the trader and red-Team select useful experience and learn from each other's evolving behavior? On one hand, experience that benefits decisions under one market condition may become ineffective or harmful under another. On the other hand, trading outcomes reflect both agents' actions, making it difficult to derive appropriate experience for each role. In this work, we propose ACE-Trader, an adversarial co-evolution trading framework. Specifically, we first develop separate context-dependent memory selectors that learn to identify useful experience for the current trading decision. Both selectors receive shared feedback from net-return differences between complete memory-assisted and memory-free trading pipelines, with online updates emphasizing recent outcomes. We further design a co-evolution mechanism that links role-specific memories through shared trading records. We use these records to evaluate the Red-Team's risk assessments and the effects of the Trader's revisions against realized market outcomes, then derive experience for their respective memories. By linking this experience to the corresponding records, we enable the Trader to improve its proposals based on prior critiques and the Red-Team to adjust its review focus as the Trader's behavior changes. Experiments on U.S. stock trading show that ACE-Trader outperforms all 22 active baselines in cumulative return and achieves the highest Sharpe ratio and lowest maximum drawdown across both active methods and passive benchmarks.","tldr":"背景与问题：盈利交易不代表批评正确，也不代表交易者据此作出的修订有益；历史经验在市场状态改变后还可能反向误导。\n\n方法：将原提案、批评、修订与事后市场结果关联保存，分开记录风险是否发生和修订是否改善收益。两个记忆选择器按当前情境选经验，用同账户起点下完整有无记忆流程的净收益差在线学习，交易LLM保持冻结。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称美股实验的收益和风险指标领先所列基线；正文给出同预算记忆消融设计，但主要数值结果被截断，无法核对优势幅度、跨时段稳定性与完整调用成本。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，区分预警命中与修订收益，比笼统复盘盈亏更有价值。但完整流程的共同标签不能识别每个角色或记忆的独立贡献；历史价格反事实也不等于真实成交与市场冲击下的部署验证。","published_at":"2026-10-19","topics":"经验迁移; 反馈驱动更新; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-20","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过共享案例与情境记忆选择实现交易者—批评者共演化。本文证据：同账户状态下完整有无记忆流水线的收益差训练两侧选择器，已实现市场结果检验风险及修订，经验进入后续决策；交易LLM不更新。相对BEAM（arxiv:2610.25119）的逐记忆移除反馈，本篇共享整条流水线标签，角色信用分配更粗；相对STRATA（arxiv:2610.19386），突出角色交互与在线选择器训练。编辑推断：有实际学习环节，但不是两个LLM权重共同增强，也未证明更新规则递归改善；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25119","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.25119v1","title":"Memory as Belief: Bayesian Evolution of Memory for Self-Evolving LLM Agents","authors":"Yiming Xu; Qian Yang; Zihan Chen; Yuefei Wu; Wenhan Zeng; Bin Shi; Bo Dong","affiliations":"Xi’an Jiaotong University；Shaanxi Provincial Key Laboratory of Big Data Knowledge Engineering；University of Virginia；Zhengzhou University","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents increasingly rely on external memory to accumulate past experiences for continual adaptation. However, effectively reusing memory requires accurately assessing its value, as retrieved experiences may become unreliable when transferred across task contexts. Despite its importance, memory valuation remains largely underexplored, with existing methods relying on historical retrieval success rates that overlook the context dependency of memory usefulness and the varying reliability of estimates under different amounts of evidence. Inspired by the Bayesian brain hypothesis, we propose BEAM (Bayesian-style Evolutionary Agentic Memory), a framework that reformulates memory value evaluation as a parameterized cognitive inference process, where memory value is represented as a context-conditioned dynamic belief rather than a passive historical statistic. Specifically, BEAM infers memory value beliefs from current task contexts and continuously calibrates them using execution feedback as empirical evidence, transforming memory from passive storage into an adaptive cognitive mechanism for continual self-evolution. Extensive experiments across reasoning and code generation benchmarks demonstrate that BEAM consistently improves memory utilization and enables continual self-evolution of LLM agents.","tldr":"背景与问题：记忆过去成功，不代表适合当前任务；一次成功与大量稳定成功也不该具有相同可信度。静态效用分数无法同时表达情境和证据量。\n\n方法：训练独立估值器，为任务—记忆组合输出效用分布并据此探索检索。执行后移除单条记忆重跑，用成绩差及保留它时的结果校准估值；新轨迹再凝练成经验，执行骨干不变。\n\n结果与结论：可见附录在两个推理设置中匹配三次采样及共同选择器，BEAM仍优于记忆基线，削弱纯推理扩展解释；主结果和完整训练成本被截断，不能推为已证明长程稳定学习。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，进步在于尝试测量经验的边际作用，而不只是记录共现成功。移除实验有额外执行成本，随机输出与多记忆交互也会影响信用；概率分布的形式本身不能证明不确定性已经校准。","published_at":"2026-10-18","topics":"经验迁移; 外部记忆与规则更新; 执行证据驱动改进","added_on":"2026-10-20","novelty_summary":"作者声称用情境条件化的概率信念替代静态记忆效用。本文证据：冻结执行骨干，训练LoRA价值估计器；有无单条记忆的执行结果形成监督，估计分布决定后续检索，新轨迹继续写回。相对SELM（arxiv:2610.24630）把使用任务成绩的移动平均记到各技能，本篇显式比较移除单条记忆的影响；相对STRATA（arxiv:2610.19386），主要改变估值而非图结构。编辑推断：学习选择器是具体推进，但软目标及判别损失不等于精确贝叶斯后验推断；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25114","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.25114v1","title":"Compile Once, Run Cheap: Frozen, Portable Skills for Embodied Agents, and What Recursive Self-Improvement Adds","authors":"Jingwen Bai; Guochao Bai; Canbo Zhang; Shuangqi Li; Minchao Hu; Weichun Huang; Shuang Liu","affiliations":"Beijing Ou Rui Ling Shi Technology Co., Ltd.；ChangingTek Robotics Technology (Suzhou) Co., Ltd.；Shanghai Yunfan Intelligent Control Robot Technology Co., Ltd.","abstract":"Embodied AI lacks the data-rich pretraining that gave language models their agents and skills, so new manipulation capability costs demonstrations per task or a frontier model in every episode. We study a third route: a strong general model acts only as an offline author that writes, runs, diagnoses and repairs a manipulation skill in simulation until it passes an exam on layouts drawn after freezing; the frozen skill then runs as code alone or under a cheap caller that reads only its description. We call this skill-level recursive self-improvement Skill-RSI and specify a compile protocol (isolated, audited author; hidden validation layouts; no-feedback and inherit-only controls; tamper-evident ledger) and a reuse protocol that runs the identical files with executors from another model family. On 7 RoboTwin 2.0 tasks with cluttered tables, Claude Code compiled 4 tasks into 7 frozen skills, 5 from a first draft needing only qualification, at USD 4.29-8.22 of author cost each (USD 55 per skill counting the 13 failed campaigns). The other three tasks did not compile in 18 campaigns, including five with GPT-6 and a pre-registered 150-layout run: on the hardest task every campaign scored 78-95 of 100 but had 3-16 safety aborts, failing the gate of 95% success with zero aborts; a 100-episode exam bounds an abort rate only to 3.6%. On hidden layouts, repair that inherits the previous version beat from-scratch rewriting in 8 of 8 controlled campaigns (sign test p = 0.004); an inherit-only lineage attributes most of the gap to inheritance, with development feedback adding a little (3 of 3, p = 0.125). Write-once campaigns found no detectable first-draft effect of practice (minimum detectable effect 14 points). The frozen skills kept 148/150 successes on new layouts with no model and 147/150 with a DeepSeek-flash caller at USD 0.00028-0.00054 per episode; no direct-control baseline was run.","tldr":"背景与问题：每次机器人执行都调用强模型很贵；但离线修补得到高分技能，也可能只是首稿已足够好或多次选择，而非从反馈学会改进。\n\n方法：强模型离线写和修技能，经冻结后新抽布局考试，成品由纯代码或廉价异族模型调用。隐藏验证、重写及仅继承版本的对照，分离反馈、继承与选择；安全门控独立于作者。\n\n结果与结论：七个冻结技能中五个首稿已达标；修补相对重写的优势主要来自版本继承，开发反馈额外贡献证据较弱。部分技能纯代码复用达到148/150成功，但另有任务持续因安全中止未能编译。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，材料更支持“把已有能力编译成可复用工件”，而非作者递归变强。计入失败活动后成本明显变化；没有直接控制基线，不能计算部署盈亏平衡，有限零中止考试也不能认证真实安全。","published_at":"2026-10-18","topics":"具身 RSI; RSI 评测与迁移; 能力归因","added_on":"2026-10-20","novelty_summary":"作者声称离线编译可验证、跨执行器复用的具身技能，并测量修补中的反馈贡献。本文证据：固定作者依据仿真执行证据修订技能，封存后独立资格考试，设置重写和仅继承对照；作者权重、提示及诊断程序固定。相对EmbodiedRSI（arxiv:2610.10498）代码—技能联合改进，本篇强调无模型或廉价调用者执行相同冻结文件；相对SEAR（arxiv:2610.18792），进一步拆解继承、开发反馈与选择。编辑推断：贡献更强于部署边界和归因协议，而非递归学习机制；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25078","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.25078v1","title":"CoEvo-RSI: When Harnesses Evolve, Which Models Should Follow?","authors":"Jiaqi Su; Guibin Zhang; Jie-Jing Shao; Cong Pang; Tiankuo Yao; Ivor Tsang; Haiyan Yin; Shuicheng Yan","affiliations":"National University of Singapore；Agency for Science, Technology and Research (A*STAR)；SenseTime Group Inc.","abstract":"Model--harness co-evolution has emerged as a prominent paradigm for recursive self-improving (RSI) agents, jointly evolving their execution scaffolds and intrinsic capabilities. We study the persistent yet often overlooked brain--body mismatch problem in this paradigm, where an evolving harness (body) demands behaviors its model (brain) has not learned or restricts capabilities it already possesses. We introduce CoEvo-RSI, a RSI framework that advances model--harness co-evolution through agent-driven, bidirectional historical inheritance. Drawing on a shared evolutionary archive and execution feedback, a meta-agent coordinates harness development from historical designs with model checkpoint selection or merging and subsequent adaptation under the selected harness, aligning inherited capabilities with evolving execution requirements to reduce brain--body mismatch. Using only supervised fine-tuning (SFT) on its own rejection-sampled trajectories, CoEvo-RSI makes Qwen3.5-9B competitive with larger models across diverse vertical applications, including multi-agent failure attribution, role-aware text-to-SQL, and smart-home instruction following. It surpasses DeepSeek-V4-Pro on TraceElephant (+14.16 agent accuracy) and GLM-5.3 on HomeBench VM (+4.90 success rate), underscoring the need for brain--body alignment and the potential of bidirectional historical inheritance to advance agent co-evolution.","tldr":"背景与问题：新harness可能要求模型不会使用的接口，而最新检查点未必最适合它；只继承上一代配对，会丢掉更早但仍有用的结构与能力。\n\n方法：保留历代harness、权重和执行记录，分别选择结构起点与模型检查点，也允许合并历史权重。固定元agent结合任务分数与接口违例筛选组合，再用该运行时下的成功轨迹微调，将结果送回档案。\n\n结果与结论：论文在失败归因、权限SQL和家居控制上报告小模型达到或超过部分强模型；历史继承机制的主要消融被截断，跨模型排名不能独立证明继承优于继续训练。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可复用的单位可能不是单个“最好版本”，而是有条件的结构—能力配对。但接口违例率只覆盖可观察格式和调用错误；低违例不等于会完成任务，反复用验证集选择配对也可能积累选择偏差。","published_at":"2026-10-18","topics":"权重—harness 联合演化; 轨迹来源与匹配; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-20","novelty_summary":"作者声称以双向历史继承缓解模型—harness失配。本文证据：固定元agent依据执行分数和接口违例，分别选择harness历史起点与模型检查点或合并方案，随后以自生成筛选轨迹SFT，晋级组合回写档案。相对Co-Harness（arxiv:2607.22688）沿当前模型继续训练，本篇允许独立选择历史权重；相对CoTrace（arxiv:2610.10426）的轨迹—运行时匹配，本篇扩展到模型初始化选择。编辑推断：搜索空间有具体扩展，但元agent和继承算法未被证明递归增强；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25012","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.25012v1","title":"Conjugate Compilation: Self-Improving Agentic Co-Compilation for Speculative Decoding","authors":"Annabelle Sujun Tang; Rohan Mahapatra; Christopher Priebe; Hanyang Xu; Manya Ghobadi; Christopher Rossbach; Hadi Esmaeilzadeh","affiliations":"University of California, San Diego；Massachusetts Institute of Technology；Systalyze；University of Texas at Austin；Microsoft","abstract":"As LLM adoption surges, scaling model serving requires unlocking stranded GPU capacity alongside deploying more GPUs. Speculative decoding brings two models into the serving process: a small draft model proposes tokens that a larger target model verifies. Yet compiling these models individually leaves their shared execution outside the compiler's optimization boundary. We introduce CONJUGATE COMPILATION, which reframes speculative decoding as a cross-model compilation problem and jointly optimizes the draft and target models within their shared execution rather than treating each in isolation. Our key insight is that cross-model compilation should be informed by the measured performance of the co-located shared execution it produces: an optimization that improves a kernel in isolation need not improve the models when they execute together. To expand cross-model opportunities, we devise operand layouts that interleave blocks from both models within common tiles, co-locating GEMM and non-GEMM work while preserving their mathematics. We realize CONJUGATE COMPILATION through a self-improving agentic search system in which an LLM edits cross-model optimization plans using the compiler and GPU execution as its environment. Each proposed plan is compiled and evaluated through its co-located shared execution, whose measured score, together with kernel-level verdicts and compiler feedback, informs subsequent proposals, while Monte Carlo tree search accumulates rewards to guide exploration. Across six single-GPU speculative-decoding configurations on NVIDIA B300 and RTX 5090 GPUs, CONJUGATE COMPILATION achieves a geometric-mean per-round speedup of 1.37x over conventional execution. Interleaved kernels raise this speedup to 1.45x, reaching 1.59x in the best case. CONJUGATE COMPILATION also improves GPU utilization on average by 1.46x on RTX 5090 and 1.50x on B300.","tldr":"背景与问题：分别优化草稿模型与验证模型的内核，会忽略同GPU并行后的竞争和同步；孤立内核更快，整轮解码未必更快。\n\n方法：将两模型的执行纳入共同编译边界，LLM修改联合方案，经数值检查后测量完整共享执行时延。搜索树累计真实奖励，编译错误和内核诊断帮助后续提案，避免只追求局部速度。\n\n结果与结论：六种单GPU配置中，整轮几何平均加速为1.37倍，加入交错内核后为1.45倍。最终候选重新配对计时并检查噪声，但这些是每轮执行结果，不能直接等同完整服务吞吐收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可迁移认识是评价边界应覆盖组件相互作用。这里优化的是外部编译方案，未展示研究者权重、技能或搜索策略持续增强；搜索总成本及其相对传统优化器的独立贡献仍需核查。","published_at":"2026-10-18","topics":"执行证据驱动改进; AI 服务优化; 预算受限研究搜索","added_on":"2026-10-20","novelty_summary":"作者声称以执行反馈驱动的agent搜索联合优化推测解码。本文证据：LLM修改编译方案，编译合法性、数值检查和整轮GPU时延反馈给固定MCTS及后续提案；变化的是服务工件，不是研究agent本身。相对EvoX（arxiv:2602.23413）将搜索策略也纳入演化，本篇未显示搜索规则更新；相对AReaL-RSI（arxiv:2610.18083）的研究经验继承，本篇未展示跨活动的研究者改进。编辑推断：属于AI服务优化的相邻工作，不宜把常规反馈搜索计为改进器递归增强；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24944","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.24944v1","title":"Epi: Towards a Persistent, Self-Improving Agent for Autonomous Research","authors":"Yue Huang; Zhangchen Xu; Xiaonan Luo; Zheyuan Liu; Lichi Li; Yiping Wang; Peiyang Song; Eric Gabriel Ramos; Enze Xie; Olexandr Isayev; Paul Liang; Nouha Dziri; Huan Sun; Jianfeng Gao; Ying Liu; Misha Sra; Xiangliang Zhang; Alex Pentland; Zichen Chen","affiliations":"","abstract":"We present Épi, an autonomous research agent that sustains investigations across model sessions and evolves its methods through accumulated experience. Épi combines persistent research history, hierarchical memory, branching and independent review to maintain research continuity, learn from experiments, and explore and revisit alternative approaches. Its experiments run across session boundaries, and a fixed verifier evaluates their outputs. Épi produced 120 record-setting results, comprising 20 numerical bound records across 12 families and 100 construction records across eight families. These include an approximately 84-fold narrower interval for the $n$-queens constant and a more than 3.6-million-fold narrower rigorous interval for the quartic Feigenbaum attractor dimension. Exact dual certificates establish that the Cohn-Elkies linear-programming bound cannot be sharp in dimensions 10 and 11. Beyond numerical improvements, Épi gives a computer-assisted proof of Tuza's conjecture for split graphs with an eight-vertex clique part and at most three triangle-active neighborhood types, with arbitrary multiplicities. We extend this research process to algorithmic coding with Épi-turbo, a lightweight configuration that develops executable solvers for tasks including vehicle routing, scheduling and production planning. On 30 FrontierOR tasks, Épi-turbo achieves a 5.4% higher total benchmark score than Codex at 64% of its model cost, using the same underlying model and reasoning effort. Épi is designed to support human understanding by connecting computational results to explicit methods and mathematical arguments that researchers can examine and build upon.","tldr":"背景与问题：长时研究跨越模型会话，代码和运行实验可保存，但过去为何放弃某方案、哪些经验仍适用容易丢失，导致重复探索。\n\n方法：将分支实现、证据和死路理由持久化，按层次记忆恢复上下文；异模型审查研究方向，隔离的固定验证器检查产物。经验影响下一次实验，而评价规则只在活动之间重新定义。\n\n结果与结论：论文列出带证书的数学构造和界；算法编码中，同底层模型与推理强度下，总分比Codex高5.4%，模型成本为其64%。相关对照细节被截断，纪录采用截至2026年9月16日的参考来源。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可核查数学证书增强的是产物可信度，不能自动证明记忆让研究者越来越会研究。应匹配总计算、初始参考和研究时长，移除跨活动经验，检验方法改进是否超出持续投入与分支搜索。","published_at":"2026-10-18","topics":"预算受限研究搜索; 经验迁移; 执行证据驱动改进","added_on":"2026-10-20","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过持续研究历史、记忆、分支和异模型审查改进研究方法。本文证据：固定验证规则检验结果，经验与未果分支跨会话保存并指导后续实验；权重固定，未展示改进程序自改写。相对AReaL-RSI（arxiv:2610.18083）的团队配置与条件共享，本篇强调单项调查的恢复、回溯和数学证书；相对Athanor（arxiv:2610.21055），产物侧重构造与界而非后训练检查点。编辑推断：研究产物与研究者能力增长必须分账，当前缺少记忆及审查的独立消融；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24896","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.24896v1","title":"Peer Pressure: Execution-Verified Co-Evolution of Attacker and Defender Populations for Code Security","authors":"Khushbu Pahwa; Yubin Ge; Daniele Bonadiman; Xiaofei Ma; Yi Zhang","affiliations":"AWS AI","abstract":"LLM code agents increasingly ship code with little oversight, yet defenders trained on static vulnerability datasets fall behind adapting adversaries. We co-train attacker and defender instead, and let execution decide every reward: an attacker (Red) edits a real repository and earns nothing unless its patch applies, builds, passes the tests, completes its development task and reproduces a real exploit in an isolated container, whose path also labels the entry point, the critical operation and the trace between them. Peer-Relative Policy Optimization (PRPO) makes both sides populations of LoRA adapters over one frozen base and credits each against same-role peers that faced an identical condition, placing the population inside the policy-gradient baseline rather than the opponent pool, with a tournament preserving diversity. Matching cancels the condition's difficulty: at equal coverage it is worth 2.3 points of balanced accuracy over a baseline computed on other conditions, and it matches a within-policy control at half the verifier spend. PRPO's 7B diff reviewer reaches 64.8% balanced accuracy on four unseen applications in three untrained languages, 5.5 points above supervised security fine-tuning and 4.4 above a frozen frontier reviewer (Claude Opus 4.8), which it leads by 15.8 on the application it trains on. Its 9B repository agent recovers 23 of 172 held-out VulnGym advisories, against 10 after supervised fine-tuning and 7 for the same backbone untrained under the same scaffold, and locates 17 of 43 reachable entry points against 13 for mini-swe-agent with GLM-5.2. Run unchanged on jailbreak defense, the same algorithm matches or exceeds WildGuard's static F1 at equal corpus and model size. Under a judge distinct from its training oracle it cuts attack success from 36.0% to 4.6%, against WildGuard's 8.9%.","tldr":"背景与问题：静态漏洞数据跟不上攻击者变化；只看训练奖励，还可能把对手停滞误判为防御进步。不同难度条件混在基线里，也会污染信用分配。\n\n方法：共同训练攻防适配器种群，攻击补丁须保持功能并在容器复现指定漏洞才有战略奖励。同角色策略在相同任务和冻结对手条件下比较，比赛保留多样性；另用历史及外部攻击者衡量进步。\n\n结果与结论：冻结攻击者时防御平衡准确率为60.8%，共同演化为64.8%，支持动态对手有贡献。但相对单策略组基线的效率优势混有训练条件覆盖量差异，关键匹配预算隔离臂未运行。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，比排名更重要的是把“对手变弱”和“自己变强”分开。代码奖励来自已知类别的可达漏洞探针，不是自主发现新漏洞；探针未触发也不等于代码完全安全，算法本身仍固定。","published_at":"2026-10-17","topics":"递归安全改进; 红队反馈; 自进化策略训练","added_on":"2026-10-20","novelty_summary":"作者声称以种群置入策略梯度基线，并通过可执行安全反馈共训攻击与防御。本文证据：容器内构建、测试及已知漏洞利用验证奖励；同条件、同角色适配器互作基线，双方更新改变后续训练分布。相对ReSI（arxiv:2610.12233）固定搜索程序逐轮修补目标，本篇共同训练攻击种群和防御种群；相对RRI（arxiv:2610.21040）模型判断奖励漏洞，本篇代码分支主要依靠执行。编辑推断：具体信用分配机制值得关注，但优势方差结论不是收敛保证，部分对照混有条件覆盖变化；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24630","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.24630v1","title":"Selm: Self-Evolving Library Management for Multi-Skill Agent Optimization","authors":"Mengxi Hu; Yuxuan Hu; Jinbo Su; Ke Wang; Honghao Shi; Wenli Wu; Cuiping Li; Hong Chen; Jing Zhang","affiliations":"Renmin University of China；Key Laboratory of Data Engineering and Knowledge Engineering；Beijing Academy of Artificial Intelligence；Beijing Key Laboratory of Intelligent Database Systems and Applications；Engineering Research Center of Database and Business Intelligence","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents increasingly use skills as a lightweight way to acquire task-specific knowledge. Recent work enables skills to evolve from task trajectories. However, these methods often lack systematic management of evolved skills, making it difficult for agents to reuse and accumulate skills across domains, thus limiting performance on subsequent tasks.To reliably accumulate, reuse, and maintain useful skills across tasks, we present SELM (Self-Evolving Library Management), a framework that formulates skill evolution as library-level management. SELM jointly manages skill retrieval, updating, and lifecycle by maintaining skill confidence and utility signals. It introduces utility-aware retrieval to select useful skills, a Map-Reduce framework to generate targeted updates from task-specific experience, and lifecycle controls to retain or remove skills based on their effectiveness. These mechanisms enable the skill library to continuously accumulate useful experience while preserving and pruning skills across tasks, improving agent performance on complex tasks across diverse domains. We evaluate SELM on four agent benchmarks covering diverse tasks and execution environments, and SELM consistently outperforms in most settings.","tldr":"背景与问题：单轮技能修订可能覆盖以后仍有用的程序，坏技能却继续被检索。只有生成和编辑，没有保留与淘汰规则，经验库难以稳定积累。\n\n方法：按任务类别隔离轨迹分析，只修改相关技能；检索同时考虑相关性与历史使用成绩。候选库经选择集筛选，置信投票和效用控制生命周期，淘汰名称进入受限墓地，模型权重不变。\n\n结果与结论：论文在四个基准报告多数设置领先，但主要结果表未提供。附录明确只测试有限技能规模，跨基准迁移留待未来；不能把多域分别优化的结果当成持续跨域积累证据。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，库管理有工程价值，但使用某技能时的任务成绩不等于它的边际贡献。名称级禁返也挡不住换名重生，可能阻止情境变化后的合理恢复；长期维护应接受漂移流与语义去重的独立测试。","published_at":"2026-10-17","topics":"经验迁移; 外部记忆与规则更新; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-20","novelty_summary":"作者声称把技能检索、更新和生命周期作为联合库管理问题。本文证据：任务执行分数更新技能效用，模型分析轨迹提出分类修改，选择集决定保留库，低效技能退出；目标模型及管理规则固定。相对STRATA（arxiv:2610.19386）的分层图、去重及冲突提示，本篇强调类别隔离、效用排序与名称墓地；相对Darwin-Claw（arxiv:2610.23574），生命周期维护已有近邻，尚缺直接匹配比较。编辑推断：属于管理流程细化，效用共现统计不能认证因果贡献；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24464","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.24464v1","title":"Learning to Compose: Recursive Self-Improvement of Shared Executable Stacks for Zero-Shot Long-Horizon Robot Manipulation","authors":"Yangzhi Chen; Feiran Liu; Zishuo Wang; Zijian Jin; Xin Zhu; Lecheng Ruan; Wenjuan Han","affiliations":"","abstract":"Individually competent robot skills can fail when composed: tools may lack a required capability, completion signals may misrepresent physical progress, and one skill may leave a state that violates its successor's prerequisites. We introduce Recursia, a recursive self-improvement framework that treats the shared executable stack, rather than individual task programs, as the persistent unit of improvement. The stack integrates tools, skills with execution contracts, handoffs, and verifiers. Source-side execution traces guide failure attribution and the generation of missing tools or repairs to existing shared components. Generality checks, mechanism tests, and paired selection and regression gates determine which changes become the next parent. The resulting stack is frozen and reused through declarative task adapters, allowing source-derived changes to support new compositions without target-side code repair. Experiments cover LIBERO-Pro Long simulation and a physical Franka FR3 equipped with a Franka Hand. In simulation, Recursia improves success over ASPIRE by 5.8 percentage points under Pos perturbations and 15.1 points under Task perturbations. Across three physical compositional target tasks, it improves mean success over the Skill Document Only baseline by 40 percentage points. Analyses of constituent execution, candidate rejection, and inference drivers distinguish local mechanism improvements from complete task success and characterize the cost of feedback-conditioned orchestration. These results examine shared executable interfaces as a concrete mechanism for compositional transfer in robot programming.","tldr":"背景与问题：单个技能成功，不代表其结束状态满足下一技能的前提；工具正常返回也可能没有建立目标物理关系。任务级补丁难以修复这种共享接口问题。\n\n方法：从源任务轨迹定位最早失效要求，修改共享工具、完成合同、交接或验证逻辑。通用性检查与同初始状态的执行、回归比较决定继承版本；目标任务只提供声明式组合，不再修代码。\n\n结果与结论：论文报告仿真与三个实机组合任务收益，但主比较和经验扩展曲线的终点成绩不同。附录还披露部分推理比较复用评测行并曾接触目标场景，冻结执行不能直接证明完全未见目标。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，共享接口是可检验的迁移载体，但须将局部机制修复、完整任务成功与搜索流程变强分开。源诊断使用特权状态，基线并非全部匹配重跑，扩展曲线为单次运行，当前不足以确认稳定递归增长。","published_at":"2026-10-17","topics":"具身 RSI; 组合泛化; 执行证据驱动改进","added_on":"2026-10-20","novelty_summary":"作者声称共享工具、技能合同、交接和验证器的修订可迁移到未见组合，并允许迭代间调整门控与搜索策略。本文证据：源轨迹及特权仿真状态定位失败，配对执行与回归测试决定版本保留，目标期冻结代码。相对EmbodiedRSI（arxiv:2610.10498），本篇突出跨技能接口及共享执行语义；相对Skill-RSI（arxiv:2610.25114），优化对象从单技能包扩展至组合执行栈。编辑推断：文本允许改变改进流程，但缺少其自主产生及独立增益的受控证据；历史目标暴露与评测口径仍须核对，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24454","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.24454v1","title":"MELD: Recursive Self-Improvement via Hierarchical Coordination for Multi-Agent Scientific Discovery","authors":"Sizhe Tang; Zuyuan Zhang; Zeyu Fang; Tian Lan","affiliations":"George Washington University","abstract":"Multi-agent scientific discovery with large language models raises a coupled learning problem: research assignments determine both which experiments are pursued and the experiences from which agents adapt. We introduce MELD, a unified hierarchical test-time training framework that jointly adapts a team-level Coordinator policy and agent-level individual Scientist policies within a single discovery process. The Coordinator generates a joint portfolio of search branches and research directives over a shared derivation tree, while Scientists develop hypotheses and execution plans implemented by a shared frozen Executor. Both levels receive alternating GRPO-style parameter updates under a shared smooth best-of-budget objective, allowing team organization and individual research behavior to co-evolve in a recursive self-improvement loop. Our analysis establishes objective alignment for the hierarchy, characterizes conditions for coordination gains over independent parallel discovery and the first-order benefit of private adaptation, and derives a finite-budget regret bound for adapted models. On 22 MLGym and MLE-bench tasks, MELD is best on 20 of them and achieves the highest aggregate normalized scores on MLGym, using a 4B backbone for coordination and research. Most baselines use proprietary Scientists, and all systems share one frozen Executor.","tldr":"背景与问题：多智能体研究的任务分配既决定探索方向，也决定研究者获得什么训练经验；固定协调策略难以跟随研究者能力变化调整分工。\n\n方法：MELD用实际候选评估结果交替训练协调器与研究者的私有适配器，共同奖励预算内优质成果。更新后的分配改变下一轮学习经验，研究者的新表现又反馈给协调器；执行模型冻结。\n\n结果与结论：两项博弈任务中，联合更新比单独更新任一层产生更多高分候选，支持两层适配互补。整体实验按候选评估次数匹配，不能解释为同总算力优势。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，具体推进是协调器也从任务内实验学习。但适配器每个任务重置，实际训练只采用单轮信用，尚未证明跨任务积累或更新算法自身增强。","published_at":"2026-10-17","topics":"多智能体工作流演化; 预算受限研究搜索; 自进化策略训练","added_on":"2026-10-20","novelty_summary":"作者声称协调与研究策略共同形成RSI。本文证据：任务评估反馈交替更新两层适配器，联合更新有单层对照。相对arxiv:2610.18083固定leader策略，本篇训练协调器；相对arxiv:2605.07039训练战略advisor，本篇加入多个私有研究策略的同步适配。编辑推断：这是任务内研究策略学习的推进，更新算法仍固定；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24453","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.24453v1","title":"Hippo: Training-Free Agent Self-Evolution via Hippocampal Replay","authors":"Yutong Song; Jiang Wu; Yuxuan Ren; Tony Qin; Baoyuan Wang","affiliations":"University of California, Irvine；Independent Researcher；Rice University；Zillow Group","abstract":"Motivated by recursive self-improvement (RSI), we study how LLM agents can learn through external memory without updating model parameters. Extracting useful experience from a single attempt is difficult: flawed reasoning can produce success, while poor execution can obscure a sound strategy. Preserving its value over time is also difficult: our accumulation baseline without consolidation initially improves but eventually performs below a no-memory baseline. Our key idea is to compare attempts at the same task to identify reusable decisions and refine when they apply. We introduce Hippo, a memory framework inspired by selective hippocampal encoding and replay that learns from these comparisons when shortcomings are diagnosed. It compares the resulting experience with existing memory to merge overlaps and resolve conflicts through explicit applicability conditions. This allows prior guidance to be revised without storing every lesson as a separate entry. Experiments on SWE-bench Verified, WebArena, and Mind2Web show performance gains in all three settings and substantially fewer retained experiences than the accumulation baseline. The gains extend across the evaluated base models of varying capabilities, indicating that memory-based adaptation remains useful even for highly capable models.","tldr":"背景与问题：正确结果可能掩盖错误推理，失败也可能只是执行失误；单次复盘容易提炼错误经验，持续追加又会让冲突指导反复传播。\n\n方法：Hippo在相同策略与记忆下比较同题多次尝试，从模型诊断的失败和侥幸成功中提炼带适用条件的决策，再与旧记忆比较、合并或替换。修订后的指导用于后续任务，权重不变。\n\n结果与结论：软件修复、网页操作和动作预测均有收益，保留经验也少于追加基线；后者长期积累最终低于无记忆配置。主要结果表缺失，无法核对与直接重试的完整预算对照。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，经验维护应检查决策为何成立、何时适用。执行、诊断与写回使用同一模型，共同盲点仍可固化；多次尝试的额外交互成本也影响实际价值。","published_at":"2026-10-17","topics":"经验迁移; 外部记忆与规则更新; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-20","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过选择性回放实现无训练自演化。本文证据：外部经验依据同模型判断及可用反馈修订，SWE-bench成功由轨迹估计。相对arxiv:2610.19386维护经验层级及反向关系，本篇强调同题比较与适用条件；与arxiv:2610.20312的尝试比较存在重叠。编辑推断：属于经验维护细化，未显示维护器递归增强；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24177","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.24177v1","title":"Self-Improving Video-to-Action Models","authors":"Hyunwoo Ryu; Eric Ming Chen; Max Wilcoxson; Vincent Sitzmann","affiliations":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology，Computer Science & Artificial Intelligence Laboratory","abstract":"Video generative models are an emerging tool for embodied agents: they can serve as scalable visual planners, generating videos that depict how to complete previously unseen tasks. However, executing these plans typically requires a video-to-action or \"inverse dynamics\" model trained on large, human-collected video-action datasets, severely limiting scalability. We introduce Mirror, a self-supervised approach that learns video-to-action mappings through environment interactions, without prior action data or hand-crafted rewards. Mirror learns by attempting to follow a visual plan by executing its best guess of the underlying actions in the environment. Mirror then trains on the resulting video-action pairs, incrementally self-improving and following the visual planner more closely. Across Atari, OGBench, and DeepMind Control, Mirror outperforms leading learning-from-observation methods with learned video plans, and achieves near-expert performance with oracle plans. On Minecraft BASALT, it outperforms methods with access to expert actions or hand-engineered task knowledge. In Minecraft survival, it is the first method to acquire an iron pickaxe through self-improvement alone, without rewards or expert action labels. In the offline setting, with expert action labels but no environment interaction, it sets a new state of the art in obtaining diamonds. Our results suggest that advances in video models can translate into increasingly capable agents without a corresponding need for hand-crafted rewards or large collections of expert action data.","tldr":"背景与问题：视频规划器能描绘任务过程，但视频转动作通常依赖专家动作数据；随机探索又难到达长程任务中的关键转移。\n\n方法：Mirror尝试执行视频计划，用实际观察与自身执行动作训练动作映射。即使偏离计划，这种配对仍提供正确监督；从实际状态重新规划，使探索停留在能力边界附近，动作噪声帮助越过尚未掌握的步骤。\n\n结果与结论：Minecraft匹配终止协议下，铁镐成功率为8.6%，Dreamer V3为1.7%，但奖励和动作设置不同。四个未见目标迁移环境中，有一个不及随机采集对照。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，失败也能产生有效监督，关键是按实际结果训练。任务知识仍来自预训练及任务微调的视频规划器；结果支持动作能力自举，不能称无示范学习，也未证明学习程序递归增强。","published_at":"2026-10-16","topics":"具身 RSI; 自适应训练经验; 经验迁移","added_on":"2026-10-20","novelty_summary":"作者声称无需专家动作标签和任务奖励即可自改进。本文证据：自采观察—动作配对更新动作模型，新模型再访问后续转移；视频规划器提供外部知识。相对arxiv:2610.10498修改代码与技能，本篇学习动作映射；arxiv:2610.13829强调经验迁移归因，本篇未采用其同协议探针。编辑推断：采集自举机制具体，非改进算法自改写；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.23599","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.23599v1","title":"From Trajectories to Differentiated Skills: Cognitive Differentiation for Self-Improving Agents","authors":"Yewei Zhao; Derong Xu; Wei Chen; Yin Xu; Peilun Zhou; Xiaohan Wang; Guojun Yin; Wei Lin; Mingjun Xiao","affiliations":"University of Science and Technology of China；Meituan；City University of Hong Kong","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents tackle complex tasks through reasoning and interaction with external environments. Agent skills provide persistent, transferable capabilities that guide task planning, inform contextual decisions, support tool use, and enable executable procedures. Yet existing skill-evolution methods largely organize knowledge around skill artifacts, overlooking the functional heterogeneity within individual skills and its implications for knowledge maintenance and use. Inspired by cognitive science, we propose Cognitive Differentiation in Skill Evolution (CDSE), which evolves a unified skill through four functionally distinct yet coordinated components: Meta, Experience, Tool, and Script. CDSE extracts evidence-grounded semantic gradients from successful and failed trajectories, consolidates them by functional role, and applies component-specific updates and validation with cross-component coordination and adaptive invocation. An analysis of 500 top-ranked skill packages shows that 96.8% contain knowledge spanning at least two functional roles. Across six benchmarks, three agent models, and two execution harnesses, CDSE achieves the highest scores in all 36 settings, improving over the Base agent by 7.6 percentage points and the strongest competing method in each setting by 2.6 points on average. Ablation studies further support the importance of functional differentiation and adaptive invocation.","tldr":"背景与问题：一条轨迹可能同时暴露规划失误、工具误用和可自动化操作；把它们统一写进技能文档，不能决定该如何验证、维护或何时调用。\n\n方法：CDSE从成功与失败轨迹提取带证据的行为修改建议，按其作用分配维护方式：一般规则与局部经验保留适用条件，可执行程序须经过测试。协调冲突后重写调用描述，让更新后的技能影响后续执行，模型与协议保持固定。\n\n结果与结论：六个基准、三模型、两harness的测试表均领先，平均比各设置最强竞争方法高2.6个百分点。训练与测试分开，但完整消融及演化总成本未见，不能单靠总体排名确认功能拆分的独立贡献。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，有意义的是更新的功能决定验证合同，而非认知类比本身。多轮可重复整理固定轨迹，因此轮次增长不代表新增交互学习，更不说明技能更新器本身递归变强。","published_at":"2026-10-16","topics":"经验迁移; 外部记忆与规则更新; 执行证据驱动改进","added_on":"2026-10-19","novelty_summary":"作者声称按功能差异组织技能更新，而非只按文档或包边界存储。本文证据显示，已评分轨迹产生带证据的行为建议，按功能维护、协调和验证后更新外部技能；模型与更新协议固定，多轮还可重复使用固定轨迹集。相对STRATA（arxiv:2610.19386）按技能—流程—原则的抽象层级组织经验，本篇按控制、情境经验、工具指导和程序的执行功能分配维护责任。编辑推断：不只是模块改名，但独立收益仍需完整消融和预算核验；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.23574","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.23574v1","title":"Darwin-Claw: Environment-Adaptive Experience Consolidation for Recursively Self-Evolving Agents","authors":"Mingze Yin; Xiaohan Wang; Dian Li; Longfei Luo; Jiahong Yan; Yiheng Zhu; Chang-Yu Hsieh","affiliations":"Zhejiang University；Tencent；Zhongguancun Academy","abstract":"While Large Language Model (LLM) agents have demonstrated remarkable capabilities across complex tasks, they predominantly operate in isolated sessions, lacking the ability to continually learn from historical interactions or adapt to user-specific environments. Existing self-evolution paradigms often indiscriminately inject raw interaction trajectories into memory or skill modules, leading to obscured behavioral patterns and compromised update controllability. Furthermore, as foundational LLM reasoning improves, the bottleneck for agentic evolution shifts from accumulating generic knowledge to effectively managing situational experience. To address this, we propose Darwin-Claw, an environment-adaptive self-evolving framework that systematically distills episodic experiences to drive the comprehensive evolution of operational skills and durable memory. Theoretically grounded in an iterative agent-actor and evolver-critic co-adaptation, Darwin-Claw introduces a Hierarchical Experience Consolidation System that extracts fine-grained error attributions and generalizes them into dynamically updated prototype vectors. This structured situational experience serves as interaction patches for context-sensitive perception and explicit optimization signals for skill refinement. Practically, Darwin-Claw is a readily deployable, automated framework compatible with mainstream agent systems without requiring manual curation. Extensive experiments on WildClawBench demonstrate that Darwin-Claw yields substantial performance improvements, establishing a controllable and stable pathway for the continual, user-centric adaptation of autonomous agents in real-world ecosystems.","tldr":"背景与问题：把用户交互原样塞进记忆或技能，会混淆环境限制与通用操作经验，也难判断哪些补丁应保留、哪些已过时。\n\n方法：Darwin-Claw把有学习信号的轨迹整理成带触发条件的经验单元，写入相关技能；后续轨迹提供效果与无效调用变化，控制试用、晋级和淘汰。LLM判断新轨迹是否相关及改善是否来自经验，底层模型参数不变。\n\n结果与结论：自主后训练场景中，相对只传递上下文报告，技能方案的六项平均分由28.42%升至31.91%。但具体模型—任务组合仍有退化，WildClawBench的完整数值表和消融未见，稳定性主张证据不足。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，限定经验容量与撤销低效补丁比持续追加更可控；但轨迹后的LLM归因不能替代同条件有无记忆对照。还需区分研究目标模型变强与负责优化的agent技能真正获得迁移。","published_at":"2026-10-16","topics":"经验迁移; 外部记忆与规则更新; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-19","novelty_summary":"作者声称把情境经验、技能与长期记忆连接成可控的整体递归演化。本文证据显示，LLM筛选及归因产生经验单元，后续轨迹的效果与效率估计控制试用、晋级和淘汰；骨干不更新。相对STRATA（arxiv:2610.19386）分层检索、去重及反向经验提示，本篇突出用户环境触发条件、技能内补丁和生命周期竞争。编辑推断：部署机制有细化，但LLM判断因果贡献不等于受控因果识别，且原型向量叙述与可见实现细节衔接不足；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.23344","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.23344v1","title":"Language Models Learn to Improve Language Models","authors":"Minhua Lin; Zijun Wang; Zewen Liu; Zhaotian Weng; Bing He; Zhan Shi; Benoit Dumoulin; Xiang Zhang; Suhang Wang; Hanqing Lu","affiliations":"The Pennsylvania State University；UC Santa Cruz；Emory University；UC Santa Barbara；Amazon","abstract":"Large language models (LLMs) are increasingly used to automate AI research, including language-model (LM) development, offering a potential path toward recursive self-improvement. However, turning experimental feedback into a learned ability to propose effective improvements across models faces two challenges. First, training such an ability with real feedback is expensive: reinforcement learning (RL) requires evaluating tens of thousands of proposals, each potentially requiring a full model-training run. Even at ten GPU-hours per run, reward collection alone would consume hundreds of thousands of GPU-hours, motivating a cheaper surrogate. Second, surrogate feedback can become unreliable as policy optimization favors overestimated proposals when the proposal distribution shifts. To address these challenges, we propose LM2LM, which trains LLMs with RL to generate effective LM improvement proposals. To provide scalable feedback, we use a research world model (RWM), a frozen LLM that predicts proposal gains from real experimental records provided in context, as the reward model for RL. To maintain feedback reliability, we periodically execute current-policy proposals ranked highly by the RWM and add their measured outcomes to its context. Across eight autoregressive and diffusion LM development environments, real-execution evaluations on held-out tasks show that LM2LM enables Qwen3.8-27B to outperform GPT-6-sol, even when GPT-6-sol is given 300 real experimental records in context, while requiring 33% lower data-generation cost. LM2LM also generalizes to a model family unseen during training.","tldr":"背景与问题：训练研究提案者若逐个运行模型实验，反馈成本过高；改用预测收益后，策略又会集中到预测器高估的方案，使代理奖励上涨而真实收益不涨。\n\n方法：LM2LM用读取真实实验记录的冻结LLM预测收益，训练提案者；定期真实执行当前策略中预测高分的提案，把测量结果补入预测器上下文。提案者权重改变、反馈记录刷新，校准专门针对优化偏爱的区域。\n\n结果与结论：留出任务采用真实执行评价，摘要称优于带实验记录的强模型，数据生成成本低33%。可见案例中，静态记录方案不断强化有害改动，加入真实负结果后该改动比例下降；但主结果表与完整成本口径被截断。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，预测器离线准确不足以支撑在线优化，最需要复测的恰是策略追逐的高分点。证据支持定向纠偏，不证明全空间校准；这里学到改进其他模型的能力，尚非研究者自主改造自身训练算法。","published_at":"2026-10-16","topics":"研究世界模型; 预算受限研究搜索; 自进化策略训练","added_on":"2026-10-19","novelty_summary":"作者声称用研究世界模型的预测奖励训练LM改进提案者，并以当前策略的高分提案真实执行持续校准。本文证据明确：提案者权重更新，RWM权重冻结但上下文实验记录更新，真实收益纠正代理高估；并有静态记录退化案例。相对研究世界模型（arxiv:2610.12235）用记录改善候选预测和选择，本篇进一步训练提案生成策略，并针对优化造成的分布变化校准；相对MLExpert（arxiv:2610.22344）直接用执行窗口反馈训练，本篇以代理奖励降低真实执行需求。编辑推断：机制推进明确，但没有提案者自我替换或外层算法自改写证据；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22984","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22984v1","title":"Self-Evolving Agents Can Repair Failures but Struggle to Generalize from Them","authors":"Weixiang Zhao; Yichen Zhang; Yanyan Zhao; Jinming Bai; Bin Liang; Ruifeng Xu; Bing Qin; Ting Liu","affiliations":"Harbin Institute of Technology, Harbin；Harbin Institute of Technology, Shenzhen；The Chinese University of Hong Kong","abstract":"Experience-driven self-evolution offers a promising path for large language model (LLM) agents to continually improve through interaction. Yet existing approaches often rely on successful trajectories or external evaluation signals, leaving unclear whether agents can evolve when such positive anchors are unavailable. We study this question through Cold-Start Failure-Only Evolution (CFOE), where agents start without accumulated experience and learn only from failed interactions without privileged guidance. Across three self-evolving paradigms, multiple LLM backbones, and four interactive environments, we uncover a consistent repair-generalization gap: failure-derived experience can help repair previously failed tasks, but rarely yields sustained improvements on unseen tasks. Further analysis shows that agents often misinterpret failures, while even verified-correct experience remains difficult to transfer. Relaxing CFOE reveals that verifier feedback and additional interaction provide limited gains, whereas successful trajectories substantially improve transfer. These findings suggest that current self-evolving agents are better at repairing observed failures than building generalizable capabilities from failure.","tldr":"背景与问题：很多经验演化方法依赖成功轨迹或验证反馈；若agent空库起步、反复失败又不知道真实评分，能否仅靠反思获得可迁移能力仍不清楚。\n\n方法：论文由控制器只让失败轨迹触发外部记忆、技能或harness更新，隐藏评分且不告知失败筛选。分别测源任务重试恢复与固定未见任务表现，再筛出人工确认正确的经验，并放宽成功轨迹、反馈或额外交互条件。\n\n结果与结论：多个框架与环境中，源任务可部分修复，未见任务却少有持续改善。仅保留正确经验后，五种配置中四种的最终留出成绩仍不高于无经验基线，表明诊断错误不是唯一瓶颈。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，应把经验正确性、同题可用性和跨题可迁移性分开验收。成功轨迹带来更强迁移，但成功与失败任务流分别采样，包含难度和内容差异；结果不能推出失败经验普遍无用。","published_at":"2026-10-16","topics":"RSI 评测与迁移; 经验迁移; 失败诊断","added_on":"2026-10-19","novelty_summary":"作者声称揭示无正向锚点时的修补—泛化缺口。本文证据为冻结骨干、空经验起步、只允许失败轨迹进入更新，控制器保留验证标签，agent与更新器不可见；独立目标集评估时冻结经验，还人工筛查正确经验。相对MC-EvoBench（arxiv:2610.13829）隔离环境状态与经验来源，本篇隔离失败经验的监督条件；相对MetaExp（arxiv:2610.21492）训练经验获取能力，本篇审计现有方法在无成功和显式评估反馈条件下的局限。编辑推断：补强既有迁移主题，但成功与失败流分别采样，不能纯归因为轨迹成败；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22791","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22791v1","title":"Self-Evolving Coding Agents via Harness-Policy Optimization","authors":"Zhepei Wei; Wenlin Yao; Baolin Peng; Danqing Wang; Qianhui Wu; Hao Cheng; Yu Meng; Jianfeng Gao","affiliations":"Microsoft Research；University of Virginia；Carnegie Mellon University","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents have shown promising potential in coding tasks, and their performance is jointly determined by the policy model and the harness that mediates their interaction with the environment. Indeed, harness and policy are mutually reinforcing and evolving only one component is suboptimal---a harness tuned for one checkpoint may not target the failure modes of an updated policy, while policy learning remains limited to the trajectories elicited by a fixed harness. In light of this, we propose Self-HPO, a recursive self-improving framework for coding agents that alternates harness and policy optimization, using the evolving policy as its own harness proposer. Specifically, in each round, the current policy first analyzes its own failures and proposes new harness candidates (H-step). The policy is then updated through reinforcement learning (RL) under the selected harness (P-step), and hard tasks identified during training form the next harness search set, keeping harness optimization targeted to the policy's evolving failure modes. Across three coding benchmarks, Self-HPO consistently outperforms harness-only and policy-only baselines, improving Qwen3.5-35B-A3B's average resolve rate from 57.8% to 64.8%, with gains generalizing to out-of-distribution settings. Further analysis shows that both optimized components retain gains even when paired with their base counterparts, while their joint gain exceeds the sum of their individual gains. Self-HPO also improves reliability (Pass@1) and expands the capability frontier (Pass@k) over the base agent. Additionally, we show that with a stronger external model (e.g., Opus 4.8) as the harness proposer, the same framework yields a further performance boost.","tldr":"背景与问题：固定harness限制策略能获得的训练轨迹；策略更新后，旧harness针对的失败又可能过时。只改其中一侧，无法持续匹配执行能力与运行支持。\n\n方法：当前策略先分析失败并提出harness修订，按搜索集成绩保留候选；随后在新harness下用执行验证奖励训练策略。训练中始终未解的任务成为下一轮搜索集，更新后的策略继续担任提案者。\n\n结果与结论：三个编码基准平均解决率比仅训练策略高2.9个百分点。困难集刷新优于固定集的消融来自外部提案者配置，不能直接视为自提案条件下的独立验证；实验仅运行两轮。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键推进是让干预目标跟随失败分布，而非首次联合修改权重与harness。执行训练后的模型重新提案，不等于已证明它更会改进系统；应固定执行者，比较不同轮次提案者的单位预算编辑收益。","published_at":"2026-10-16","topics":"权重—harness 联合演化; 失败诊断; 自进化策略训练","added_on":"2026-10-19","novelty_summary":"作者声称以当前策略兼任执行者和harness提案者，实现自驱联合演化。本文证据：执行验证器提供二元奖励，RL更新执行策略，未解任务刷新下一轮搜索集；固定搜索集消融在外部提案者配置下落后。相对Co-Harness（arxiv:2607.22688）的修补后SFT，本篇采用RL、当前策略自提案与困难集刷新；相对Evo²（arxiv:2610.13025）直接训练修改者和反思者，本篇训练信号来自执行任务，而非编辑效果。编辑推断：执行者更新确实回到提案环节，但尚未隔离证明提案能力本身提高；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22740","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22740v1","title":"R$^2$Orch: Recursive Self-Improvement for Agent Orchestration via Self-Play within a Skill-Internalization Loop","authors":"Mingda Zhang; Yun Huang; Qiang Huang; Yanjin Li; Rui Qian; Qichao Zhao; Tiesunlong Shen; Na Zhao; Jian Wang; Xiaoying Tang","affiliations":"The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen；Fudan University；University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign；Tsinghua University；National University of Singapore","abstract":"In recent years, agentic orchestration has been widely applied to solve complex human tasks. However, existing orchestration learning still faces key challenges, including hand-designed curricula, advantage collapse when a task's rollouts all reach the same outcome, and unreliable evaluation signals that judge each skill by one noisy score. To address these challenges, we propose R$^2$Orch, a new paradigm of Recursive Self-Play Orchestration: an inner loop of self-play that improves the orchestrator on self-chosen tasks, and an outer loop that improves how the inner loop improves. To support this paradigm, we introduce Recursive Learnability, a training objective that rewards a Proposer for choosing tasks whose rollouts keep reaching different outcomes as skills are withdrawn. Built on this objective, we further propose Skill Withdrawal, in which the outer loop withdraws each skill once a controlled evaluation within self-play shows that the orchestrator performs as well without it. Moreover, the two loops form one cycle: failures are distilled into skills, skills into parameters, and withdrawals lead the Proposer to new failures, so the orchestrator moves toward zero-skill deployment. Experimental results on twelve datasets show that R$^2$Orch consistently outperforms baselines across question answering, math, code, and interactive tasks.","tldr":"背景与问题：有技能提示时适中的任务，撤掉提示后可能全部失败，使组相对训练失去有效差异；直接按成功率撤技能，又混淆任务难度变化与技能实际贡献。\n\n方法：训练时随机向部分尝试隐藏一项技能，用同任务的有无技能对照判断它是否仍有帮助。课程选择偏向隐藏技能后仍有成功也有失败的任务，使学习持续发生在脱离指导后的能力边界。\n\n结果与结论：论文在十二项数据集报告领先，并称零技能测试保持表现；可见实验说明各方法共享执行Worker、任务和计算预算，但主要结果与消融数值被截断，无法核对各环节贡献。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，内化应由撤除指导后的表现验收，而非训练时高分推定。这里外层改变技能与课程，不是学习规则自主重写；仍需检查逐项撤除后的技能交互，以及撤除判据在任务漂移时是否可靠。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 技能蒸馏; 多智能体工作流演化","added_on":"2026-10-19","novelty_summary":"作者声称外层技能撤除改善内层自博弈的学习过程。本文证据：随机隐藏候选技能，以有无技能的执行对照更新效用后验；任务选择奖励关注撤除后的结果差异，策略和课程随之更新。相对SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）按当前推理器可教性训练课程，本篇将课程目标放在撤除指导后的能力上；相对RSIPO（arxiv:2610.15772）训练技能生成并校准蒸馏，本篇重点是技能何时退出。编辑推断：这是课程与内化验收的具体耦合，撤除规则本身仍固定；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22599","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22599v1","title":"Can LLMs predict the outcomes of machine learning experiments?","authors":"Ayush Bansal; Aldo Pareja; Sean Klein; Serge Didenko; Artem Lukoianov","affiliations":"Autolab AI；Institute of Foundation Models；Massachusetts Institute of Technology","abstract":"Recent advances in AI make Recursive Self-Improvement (RSI) increasingly plausible. Large Language Models (LLMs) can already propose, select, and run Machine Learning (ML) experiments. However, the space of possible design choices in ML is vast. An LLM that proposes an experiment needs a reliable intuition of whether it is worth running given the timing constraints of long training runs. In this work, we measure such intuition in current frontier LLMs by evaluating how accurately they predict the impact of self-generated ML experiment ideas before these are put into training runs. To this end, we construct a dataset of 288 LLM-proposed ideas on eight MLE-bench tasks. We then prompt five frontier LLMs (GPT-6 Astra, Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Fable 5.1, Kimi K3, and GLM-5.3) to predict the impact of each idea and compare their predictions with the actual outcomes after training. We report four main findings. First, LLM predictions are substantially better than random chance but far from accurate: even the best model, Claude Opus 5.5, explains only half of the variance in outcomes (R^2 = 0.49). Second, we notice that all tested models systematically underestimate the magnitude of the changes. Third, prediction quality varies widely across tasks. Finally, the choice of the coding harness that actually implements the ideas has little effect on outcomes, and we find no evidence of self-preference. Higher reasoning settings and additional context lead to modest gains. Overall, our results show that current LLMs have useful but limited intuition about which ML ideas will work. We release our dataset to support further study.","tldr":"背景与问题：研究agent提出方案很快，真实训练却慢；选错实验会消耗后续搜索预算。只测能否二选一，不能判断模型是否知道收益大小。\n\n方法：收集机器学习改动及实际训练结果，让预测器读取任务、现有代码和改动差异，事前估计新分数，再分别检验方向、关联程度和幅度。分析排除失败运行或缺少可用预测的样本。\n\n结果与结论：最佳模型的拟合R²为0.49，各模型都压低大变化的预测幅度。正文把预测值对实际值回归，不能把该R²直接解释为原始预测准确解释一半实际收益；收益选择的理论换算还依赖高斯假设。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，有用排序与数值校准必须分开验收。这里包含有意改善和恶化的短实验，且主设置提供已实现代码差异，不能直接外推为尚未实现的新颖研究提案筛选能力。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"预算受限研究搜索; 研究世界模型; RSI 评测与迁移","added_on":"2026-10-19","novelty_summary":"作者声称测量模型在缺少历史实验记录时预测ML改动效果的直觉。本文证据：真实运行提供事后结果，分析方向、关联程度及幅度校准；没有更新预测器或提案者的递归闭环。相对研究世界模型（arxiv:2610.12235）用历史记录辅助预测，本篇强调无此类记录的起点，并区分排序关联与幅度；相对LM2LM（arxiv:2610.23344），没有训练及在线纠偏。编辑推断：是预算受限RSI的能力审计，不是自改进方法；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22466","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22466v1","title":"Harness-Delta Attribution: Dissecting Gains From Harness Evolution","authors":"Wenxuan Ding; Qin Lu; Changlong Yu; Sha Li; Shuowei Jin; Xin Liu; Zhenyu Shi; Greg Durrett","affiliations":"Amazon；New York University","abstract":"Harness evolution automatically optimizes the prompts, skills, tools, and orchestration code around a fixed-weight model, offering a way to improve agentic systems without updating model weights. The agent harness is iteratively optimized to achieve higher performance on the search set. But how much of this gain reflects benchmark-specific overfitting or additional inference-time compute, and how much may generalize beyond the search set? In this work, we introduce Harness-Delta Attribution (HDA), an evaluation protocol that dissects an evolution gain into artifact-driven overfitting, gains explained by test-time scaling, and the remainder, which gives an upper bound on residual generalizable improvement. We apply HDA to 11 executor models and three harness-evolution frameworks across math, coding, creativity, and agentic tasks. In 21 of these settings that show statistically significant search-set gains, we find that a large share of the improvement is explained by overfitting or test-time scaling. Specifically, among these 21 settings, overfitting and test-time scaling account for 54% and 14% of the gain on average; their combined share exceeds 50% in 14 settings. The residual and held-out transfer vary substantially across tasks, models, and frameworks. Importantly, search-set gains often fail to transfer to held-out tasks, and provide limited evidence that they will persist under practical distribution shifts. Moreover, validation-based signals are insufficient to prevent overfitting. These results motivate attribution-aware evaluation in future harness evolution research.","tldr":"背景与问题：harness搜索得分上涨，可能来自记住基准规律或增加调用；即使留出集也上涨，共享的数据构造捷径仍可能冒充泛化。\n\n方法：将原harness扩展到演化版本的推理预算，并从演化版本中最小化移除已检测捷径；两类干预由人工复核。剩余差额仅作为可泛化改进的上界，再独立检查留出表现。\n\n结果与结论：有显著搜索收益的设置中，过拟合与推理扩展的平均归因占比分别为54%和14%。部分编码配置虽无检测到的捷径、残差占全部收益，留出表现仍退化。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，最有价值的结果不是一个平均扣分比例，而是“没有检测到问题”仍不能认证迁移。归因依赖捷径识别、移除方式和预算匹配口径，报告比例还经过截断处理，不能当作普遍适用的精确因果份额。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"RSI 评测与迁移; 能力归因; 选择误差","added_on":"2026-10-19","novelty_summary":"作者声称将harness增益拆成检测到的过拟合、额外推理计算和剩余项。本文证据：构造等推理预算基线，人工复核分析agent提出的捷径移除，再测剩余及留出表现；它审计改进过程，而不更新改进器。相对VideoHarness-SRSI（arxiv:2610.19424）限制反馈暴露和组织搜索，本篇对已演化工件进行事后归因；并实际评估AHE（arxiv:2604.25850）的指定配置。编辑推断：是既有泛化审计的实质扩展，残差不构成认证，分解也不是唯一因果分解；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22362","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22362v1","title":"CoDA: Co-Evolution of Data Engines and Action Policies","authors":"Tianjiao Yu; Zhilin Ou; Yifan Shen; Xinzhuo Li; Yuanzhe Liu; Onkar Kishor Susladkar; Fan Wang; Ismini Lourentzou","affiliations":"University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign；The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen；Amazon","abstract":"Generative simulation can automate robot environment construction, but physically valid environments are not necessarily useful for training. The challenge is to identify environments that address a policy's failures and supervision that helps it overcome them. We introduce CoDA, a framework in which a simulation data engine and an action policy co-evolve through a shared heterogeneous memory of environment construction, policy failures, and learning progress. The memory compiles validated diagnoses from a vision-language critic into generation programs that recreate difficulties and training programs that help the policy overcome them. We further propose Text2potential to convert these diagnoses into staged potentials for action-chunk value learning, providing dense supervision for policy updates while preserving the task's optimal policy under standard shaping assumptions. Measured learning progress guides further generation and program refinement. Across four manipulation task families, CoDA improves out-of-distribution success from 5.3% after supervised fine-tuning to 27.6%, exceeding the strongest closed-loop baseline by 9.5 percentage points with the same generation budget. On LIBERO-Pro, 15 rounds of generation and training raise success from 25% to 84% under position perturbations and from 1% to 76% under instruction perturbations.","tldr":"背景与问题：物理上有效的仿真场景未必值得训练；只按成功率生成难题，分不清当前短板究竟可学，还是继续投入也无收益。\n\n方法：CoDA 用轨迹诊断提出困难因素，再比较定向扰动与其他因素扰动，验证诊断后存入共享记忆。同一困难生成针对性场景和密集势函数；机器可检查的任务成功条件保持独立，训练后的实际进步指导下一轮生成。\n\n结果与结论：四类操作任务中，同接受环境预算下，分布外成功率为27.6%，高于成功率引导生成的18.1%。这支持超越标量难度的反馈有价值，但不代表总计算成本相等，实机迁移仍未建立。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键不只是找失败，而是验证失败原因并测量能否学会。生成引擎靠记忆适配、策略靠梯度学习，两者共演化不等于生成算法自身变强；势函数保留最优策略也依赖标准塑形假设。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 模型—数据共演化; 失败诊断","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称让数据引擎与动作策略共同演化；本文证据显示，引擎通过记忆与程序检索在上下文中适配，动作策略通过梯度更新，训练前后成功率变化再决定后续生成。相对 SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）共同训练合成器与推理器，本篇增加场景因素干预验证，并把同一诊断编译为环境与势函数，不能等同为生成器权重共同学习。编辑推断：具体推进在于联结可学性、失败归因和训练监督；尚未证明编译与调度机制自身递归增强，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22344","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22344v1","title":"MLExpert: Towards a Generalist Agentic Model for Autonomous Machine Learning Engineering","authors":"Shangheng Du; Jinxin Shi; Shuaiyu Zhang; Yiming Wu; Junpeng Zhao; Shiyang Feng; Xin Li; Liang He; Xiangchao Yan; Bo Zhang","affiliations":"Shanghai Artificial Intelligence Laboratory；East China Normal University","abstract":"Large language models (LLMs) are expanding from assisting scientific research and engineering to autonomously developing and improving AI systems, advancing AI for AI (AI4AI) as a pathway toward recursive self-improvement (RSI). Workflow-driven machine learning engineering (MLE) systems provide a practical path toward this pursuit through complex orchestration that manages long-horizon experimentation, while recent MLE systems adopt model-directed interaction, allowing models to autonomously organize experiments and adapt optimization strategies based on execution feedback. However, feedback from each experiment reflects several preceding decisions, and a long MLE run contains many such costly experiments. Training must therefore select useful supervision from long interaction trajectories and learn from intermediate outcomes. We propose a post-training method for autonomous long-horizon MLE optimization and apply it to train MLExpert, a 35B Mixture-of-Experts agentic model. We design the Kaggle-MLE Factory to construct executable tasks and an interaction harness for model-directed experimentation. Hierarchical agentic SFT transfers general tool-use and coding capabilities to MLE through outcome-guided supervision. Windowed Interaction RL (WIRL) treats the multi-turn decisions between successive experiment results as an execution window and assigns it a shared outcome-based reward. Asynchronous collection and policy correction support policy updates before the trajectory ends. On MLE-Bench Lite, MLExpert improves the average medal rate of the base model from 37.9% to 72.7%, achieving performance comparable to larger frontier models such as Kimi-K3 and GLM-5.3. Further experiments show that MLExpert improves performance on NatureBench Lite, agent scaffold optimization, and algorithm optimization, suggesting that the learned optimization capability generalizes to other tasks.","tldr":"背景与问题：机器学习实验返回结果前，agent 已作出多轮分析和代码修改；等整段研究结束才训练，既浪费中间反馈，也难把结果归给相关决策。\n\n方法：MLExpert 先从按结果筛选的轨迹学习，再把相邻实验结果之间的决策视为一个窗口，用实验结果及局部进步共同奖励窗口内行为。实验完成即可异步更新，不必等待整个任务结束，并修正采样策略与训练策略的差异。\n\n结果与结论：MLE-Bench Lite 平均获牌率从基座的37.9%升至72.7%；算法优化迁移中也有收益，但部分任务持平或退化。窗口共享奖励并未实现窗口内部的精细归因。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，贡献是让研究者从真实实验节奏学习，而非证明研究流程递归自造。脚手架优化实验中，进一步强化学习同时增加调用量，准确率收益不能全解释为调用效率提高。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"预算受限研究搜索; 自进化策略训练; 长程交互学习","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称训练自主组织长程机器学习实验的模型；本文证据为按实验结果划分交互窗口、共享结果奖励并修正异步策略偏移，以及后训练和迁移实验。相对 Athanor（arxiv:2610.21055）让固定研究者运行训练研究，本篇直接训练研究决策者；相对 MASS（arxiv:2610.12176）的工作流搜索—微调循环，本篇重点是实验间决策的信用分配。编辑推断：学到优化能力属于 RSI 的能力基础，但材料没有展示更新后的研究者反过来改进自身训练方法。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22192","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22192v1","title":"Terminal-RSI: Recursive Self-Improving Terminal Agents via Recursive Self-Rewrite and Policy-Refine","authors":"Junyao Yang; Zongxia Li; Yucheng Shi; Zhongzhi Li; Ruhan Wang; Ruiwen Zhou; Haitao Mi; Shuicheng Yan; Leowei Liang","affiliations":"Tencent Hy Frontier；National University of Singapore；University of Maryland, College Park；University of Georgia；Indiana University","abstract":"Converting verifier outcomes into useful policy updates and partial progress into complete task resolution is crucial for terminal agents. We present Terminal-RSI, which alternates Recursive Self-Rewrite (RSR) of verified trajectories with critic-inheriting Recursive Policy-Refine (RPR). We formulate Turn-Boundary Skip-Observation GAE (TB-GAE) to retain token-specific baselines while applying decay across interaction turns. Family Dense Reward (FDR) calibrates semantic progress across task families; Success-Prioritized Reward (SPR) separates strict success from bounded partial credit. A Warm-up Critic Model, recursive critic handoff, and stage-specific learning rates coordinate the two refinement phases. The five-stage sequence from Qwen3.8-27B base model through RSR-1, RPR-1, RSR-2, and RPR-2 yields Terminal-RSI-27B: 19.84% on Terminal-Bench 4.0, 86.52% on Terminal-Bench 2.1, 16.95% on Terminal-Bench 3.0, and 79.00% on Terminal-Bench Hard. On LHTB, process reward rises from 0.21 to 0.37 and strict completion from 0/46 to 5/46; SWR100 success doubles from 3.00% to 6.00%. By recursively coupling verified trajectory rewriting with critic-inheriting policy refinement, each retained stage consolidates discovered behaviors and progressively advances the agent from partial local repairs to strict terminal verification.","tldr":"背景与问题：终端任务的冗长日志会让按 token 衰减的信用偏离实际决策距离；监督重写改变策略后，旧价值估计也可能失准。通过局部检查更不等于完成整个任务。\n\n方法：Terminal-RSI 交替学习经验证的重写轨迹与强化学习精炼，保留价值网络但在新阶段重新校准；信用按交互轮衰减，并限制失败轨迹的部分奖励，避免局部进展压过严格完成。\n\n结果与结论：长程终端测试的严格完成从0/46增至5/46，说明收益不只体现在过程奖励；但绝对完成率仍低。阶段还同时改变数据、奖励和学习率，现有曲线不能单独归因于价值继承。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，值得借鉴的是把检查覆盖、塑形奖励和终局成功分开报告。这里递归的是训练数据与策略继承，并无证据说明信用分配算法自身学会了如何改进；被丢弃分支也反对单调变强的叙事。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"失败驱动的递归更新; 长程交互学习; 终端智能体","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称递归耦合轨迹重写与策略精炼；本文证据显示成功执行轨迹用于监督更新，价值网络跨监督阶段继承并重新校准，奖励将部分进展置于严格成功之下。相对 ReTerm（arxiv:2610.18484）从失败状态分叉学习恢复，本篇强调监督转换后的价值漂移和跨交互轮信用衰减；相对 CoTrace（arxiv:2610.10426）的运行时匹配，本篇关注 actor—critic 交接。编辑推断：多轮权重训练成立，但保留阶段曲线不能证明各组件因果作用或优化器自身递归增强。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21791","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.21791v1","title":"RSIFlow: Adaptive Self-Improvement Workflows with an Evolving Meta-Agent","authors":"Huan Zhang; Mingju Chen; Dongxu Zhou; Can Lv; Sen Cui; Faguo Wu; Shiji Zhou","affiliations":"Beihang University；Tsinghua University；Beijing Academy of Artificial Intelligence (BAAI)","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents have demonstrated strong capabilities in complex tasks, including code generation, tool use, and multi-hop question answering. Existing self-improvement methods enhance agent performance through model optimization, harness evolution, and executable artifact refinement, while recursive self-improvement (RSI) further extends optimization to the improvement mechanisms themselves. However, adapting self-improvement workflows to evolving performance bottlenecks while improving workflow orchestration through execution feedback remains a key challenge. We propose \\textbf{RSIFlow}, a \\textbf{R}ecursive \\textbf{S}elf-\\textbf{I}mprovement framework that integrates adaptive work\\textbf{flow} orchestration with meta-agent capability evolution. RSIFlow diagnoses performance bottlenecks from task-agent trajectories and environmental feedback to dynamically select component-specific improvement workflows. The meta-agent then distills workflow outcomes into component-specific skills and cross-component principles, evolving its own harness to improve subsequent workflow orchestration. Experiments across six benchmarks and two backbone models show that RSIFlow achieves the SOTA average performance on all benchmarks. Ablation studies further demonstrate the contributions of adaptive workflow orchestration and meta-harness evolution. Code is available at https://github.com/1HUAN1/RSI-Flow.","tldr":"背景与问题：改权重、改 harness 或修任务产物各自有效，却未必对应当前瓶颈；固定的干预选择方式也不会自动从过去的改进尝试中受益。\n\n方法：RSIFlow 根据轨迹和环境反馈选择一个组件更新，固定其余组件比较候选。之后把成功、失败及回归提炼为带适用条件的技能和跨组件原则，修改元 agent 的接口与指令，让下一轮诊断和选择使用这些经验。\n\n结果与结论：六个基准、两种骨干的12种设置中，11种领先所比较基线。材料称消融支持自适应编排和元 harness 演化，但消融表被截断，无法核对独立贡献及完整成本。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，比最终任务分数更关键的是元经验能否在相同预算下改善下一次干预。方法确实改变了改进者的外部状态，但五轮结果尚不能证明持续加速；还应区分任务产物修补与可迁移能力增长。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 失败诊断; 跨任务迁移","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称同时适应任务瓶颈和演化工作流编排能力；本文证据显示同父系统、同批任务下选择组件更新，将尝试结果提炼为技能和原则并改写元 harness，元模型权重固定。相对 SIA（arxiv:2605.27276）的反馈选干预，本篇让选择所用的外部程序与经验持续改变；相对 Hyperagents（arxiv:2603.19461），元级可编辑并非首次，本篇细化为组件选择与证据化经验维护。编辑推断：这是已有元改进范式的具体推进；截断处缺少完整消融数值和预算，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21646","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.21646v1","title":"The Self-Improvement Problem","authors":"Brian B. Moser; Stanislav Frolov; Tobias C. Nauen; Federico Raue; Andreas Dengel","affiliations":"German Research Center for Artificial Intelligence (DFKI)；RPTU Kaiserslautern-Landau","abstract":"With the rise of large language models, agentic systems are becoming increasingly autonomous, as they write code, call tools, revise prompts, and propose modifications to their own components. This autonomy raises a fundamental question for safe self-improvement: can an automated gate like a reward model or an automated reviewer reliably decide whether a proposed update should be accepted? The difficulty is structural. The gate must be a terminating, computable procedure, while the property we ultimately care about, namely whether an update is a genuine semantic improvement, depends on potentially unbounded program behavior. We formalize this mismatch by modeling agents as programs and defining improvement in terms of a semantic score that need not be computable. We study two evaluation abstractions. The first is a certifier that approves or rejects an update. The second is a search procedure that, given access to a proposal generator, attempts to output some improving candidate if one exists. We show that, in the fully general setting, no terminating procedure can simultaneously guarantee reliability (never accepting a non-improvement) and non-conservatism (never missing an available improvement): self-referential constructions can force any such gate or searcher to fail. Randomized gates with bounded error face the same limit. We then identify a standard decidable regime used in practice (bounded evaluation and a finite proposal budget) under which exhaustive simulation yields a terminating search procedure with the desired guarantees. We also show the limit of this recovery: a chain of accepted updates can raise the bounded score in every round while the true score falls. Our results draw a boundary between unbounded, universal settings where correctness guarantees collapse and bounded settings where they can be recovered by design.","tldr":"背景与问题：自修改系统希望自动门控既不放过坏更新，也不阻止好更新；但门控必须停机，真正的行为改进却可能依赖无界运行，二者要求并不相容。\n\n方法：论文把 agent 与候选更新表示为程序，分别研究判断单次更新和从提案中寻找改进。利用自指构造证明普遍可靠且完备的停机程序不存在，再限制评估时域与提案数量，恢复相对于有界分数的可判定保证。\n\n结果与结论：可见证明支持认证器的不可能性；材料还给出搜索及随机门控的对应结果，并构造代理每轮上升、真实目标反而下降的更新链。这不是现实系统失败率的测量。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，工程意义是声明保证究竟针对哪个有限目标，而非宣布自改进不可行。经典不可判定性不能替代统计审计；有限测试恢复的正确性也不能自动覆盖未测输入和长期目标。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; 验证理论; 选择误差","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称形式化验证门控自改进的可靠性与进展保证边界；本文证据包含可见的对角构造、认证与搜索的区分，以及有界代理恢复保证的条件。相对 arxiv:2610.10611 研究固定验证协议下的复杂性类别，本篇讨论无界语义改进的不可判定性与代理连续上升时的真实目标漂移。编辑推断：贡献是将经典可计算性限制落实为门控合同，不是新的不可计算性技术，也不是现实奖励投机必然发生的经验结论。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21492","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.21492v1","title":"MetaExp: Learning to Self-Improve through Experience via Verifiable Cross-Task Environment Scaling","authors":"Renhao Li; Xinjie Shen; Yang Su; Jianhong Tu; Derek F. Wong; Dayiheng Liu; Min Yang","affiliations":"University of Macau；Shenzhen Institute of Advanced Technology, Chinese Academy of Sciences；Georgia Institute of Technology；Alibaba Token Hub, Alibaba Group","abstract":"Language-model agents can accumulate interaction feedback, but reliably turning that feedback into reusable experience remains challenging. Existing methods either optimize external experience scaffolds or train experience-related behavior on specific task distributions, leaving open whether experience learning itself can become a transferable model capability. Training such a capability calls for supervision beyond isolated tasks, which mainly support in-episode problem solving rather than revealing what knowledge remains useful across episodes. In this work, we introduce MetaExp, a scalable framework that trains this capability through verifiable task families with controlled cross-task structure. Each family preserves a reusable factor while varying task-specific realizations, enabling transfer without direct solution reuse. We propose two complementary designs: Shared-Tool families keep black-box tools fixed across tasks to elicit operational experience, while Shared-Workflow families preserve latent procedures across changing realizations to elicit procedural experience. We scale environments under both designs, collect and filter sequential interaction trajectories, and fine-tune Qwen3.5-122B-A10B on 4,956 trajectories from 1,000 task families. With parameters frozen during downstream evolution, MetaExp improves by +8.5 points on SpreadsheetBench, peaks at +2.3 on APEX-Agents, and improves by +14.8 on AutomationBench. The gains persist under domain-excluded training, supporting experience learning as a transferable capability for continued non-parametric improvement after deployment.","tldr":"背景与问题：会解任务不等于会从任务中积累经验；独立任务训练难以告诉模型哪些知识应跨回合保留，部署时加记忆甚至可能使表现下降。\n\n方法：MetaExp 构造共享工具或潜在流程、但具体答案不能直接复用的任务族，用连续求解和反馈后修订技能的轨迹训练模型。测试时参数冻结、经验库清空，从新分布逐步积累技能，再在不参与更新的固定目标集测量收益。训练反馈以执行检查为主，模型复核失败项。\n\n结果与结论：SpreadsheetBench 中经验积累带来8.5分增长，匹配基座在同协议下反降2.2分；排除相关训练领域后仍有收益，支持经验学习不只是携带目标领域知识。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，较有力的变化是把初始解题水平与经验带来的增量拆开。训练过滤仍主要确认当前任务成功，尚未直接验证每次技能修改能改善后续任务；经验积累也不等于更新算法持续递归增强。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"经验迁移; 自进化策略训练; RSI 评测与迁移","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称经验学习可训练为跨分布能力；本文证据显示用保留共同因素的任务族监督求解及经验更新，部署时冻结参数、空库起步，并在独立目标集冻结经验评估。相对 STRATA（arxiv:2610.19386）设计固定骨干的记忆结构，本篇训练产生和使用经验的模型行为；相对 SGUID（arxiv:2610.12367）筛选技能蒸馏，本篇在新分布上不再更新参数。编辑推断：区分经验学习能力与携带经验是具体推进，但训练未直接按经验更新的下游增益筛选。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21055","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.21055v1","title":"Athanor: An Agent-Native System for Autonomous Post-Training Research","authors":"Yufa Zhou; Yichen Wang; Jiakun Fan; Ziqi Shu; Zhichao Liu; Anru R. Zhang; Neiwen Ling; Zijun Wei","affiliations":"ByteDance；Duke University；The University of Chicago；Virginia Tech","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement, in which AI systems build stronger AI systems, is one promising route to superintelligence. We study a weaker form that can be measured today: frontier agents post-training a small raw base model with public data, as a test of their research potential. We build Athanor, an open agent-native system for autonomous post-training research (AutoPostTrain) on real GPUs. We give the agents full research autonomy, low-friction engineering tools, and efficient starter code. The agents carry out the research themselves: they read datasets and evaluation results, build their training data, write and modify training algorithms, tune hyperparameters, and analyze the results to decide what to try next. They work in a sandbox and cannot use external teacher models. Athanor's services supply frozen evaluation, managed jobs, decontaminated data, a persistent research record, and a held-out suite the agents are unaware of. In a 104-hour campaign, a team of four Claude Opus 5.5 agents, each on an eight-GPU node and given no research advice, improves Qwen3-4B-Base from 15.9 to 67.3 on a six-task development suite and from 9.2 to 48.2 on a held-out suite, against 66.5 and 47.9 for the official Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507. To our knowledge, this is the first demonstration that a team of frontier agents can autonomously post-train a raw base model into a cross-domain generalist model that matches or surpasses the official instruct version on average. The campaign's full record shows that the agents reach this level by recombining known methods and each other's models: SFT on public reasoning data, RL with a rollout change one agent introduced, weight merges across agents, and rounds of self-distillation. With execution handled, today's agents already have the engineering and research ability to conquer this task. We hope Athanor provides a foundation for scaling autonomous AI research.","tldr":"背景与问题：自主后训练不仅要提出配方，还要完成耗时且易失败的 GPU 实验，同时防止开发集搜索和数据污染冒充通用能力增长。\n\n方法：Athanor 将作业、数据去污染和固定评估做成服务，把研究记录与模型谱系持久化；四个固定前沿 agent 自选数据、算法和模型组合，训练另一个基础模型。最终隐藏套件不向研究者开放，也不允许调用外部教师模型。\n\n结果与结论：104小时活动后，隐藏套件均分为48.2，官方指令版为47.9，支持接近其平均水平，而非可靠超越。论文区分活动期间协议与事后统一重测，结果不能混为同一条曲线。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，这说明低摩擦执行设施能支撑已知方法的自主重组，但尚无基础设施消融证明它是决定性瓶颈。单次活动也未显示研究者自身变强，运营者仍承担节点恢复等基础设施职责。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"RSI 研究环境与评测; 预算受限研究搜索; 自主后训练","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称首次由前沿 agent 团队自主后训练出平均匹敌官方指令版的跨域模型；本文证据为单次104小时研究活动、固定评估服务、隐藏套件和训练谱系记录，并未核验首创性。相对 RSIGym（arxiv:2610.10310）提供多轨研究服务，本篇聚焦真实 GPU 上单个通用检查点的后训练及封存评估；相对 MLExpert（arxiv:2610.22344），研究者模型未被训练。编辑推断：这是自主 AI 研发的具体实证，不是研究者自我替换或改进器递归增强。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21040","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.21040v1","title":"Recursive Reward Improvement via Adversarial Meta-Prompt Evolution","authors":"Wei Dai; Qianchu Liu; Guanghui Qin; Xing Han; Tristan Naumann; Paul Pu Liang; Sheng Zhang","affiliations":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology；Microsoft Research；Johns Hopkins University","abstract":"Recursive Self-Improvement (RSI) has gained wide attention for its ability to work with limited data. In a proposer-solver loop, a proposer model writes training tasks and a solver model learns to solve them through reinforcement learning. Such loops have succeeded in mathematics and coding, where every answer can be checked automatically. Open-ended expert tasks, like clinical report generations, have no answer key, which makes simple question-answer generation not viable. Here the proposer must also write a rubric that lists the content an answer should include and the errors it should avoid. However, the unique challenge behind model-written rubric is the comprehensiveness of it. For naively generated rubric, solvers tend to exploit it, naming the expected topics without the substance behind them, which corrupts the learning process. To solve this problem, we introduce RRI, Recursive Reward Improvement, which uses a reward hacking adversary to supervise the reward. Before the solver trains on a generated task, an adversary writes an answer that games its rubric while being as useless as possible, the same model writes an honest answer without seeing the rubric, and up to two repair steps revise the rubric to make the honest answer win. The exploits found also rewrite how future tasks and rubrics are generated. On HealthBench Professional, RRI improves the adjusted score over the Generation Only self-improvement baseline by 10.9 points at 9B and 12.4 at 27B, and by 10.3 points without any external model. In particular, the gains are largest on difficult and writing tasks. We show that the 27B model trained on the HealthBench Professional description improves by 6.6 points on PRBench Hard and 8.0 on ProfBench without seeing a task from either. We further analyze the exploitable points of model-generated question-rubric pairs to facilitate future research on open-ended self-play.","tldr":"背景与问题：开放式专家任务缺少答案键，模型自写评分准则容易奖励关键词覆盖而非实质内容；求解器会把这些漏洞放大成训练方向。\n\n方法：RRI 从检索资料生成任务与准则，先写故意钻评分漏洞的答案，再与同一模型不看准则写出的诚实答案比较，由模型 judge 评分并指导修补。漏洞还改写未来任务和准则的生成指令，求解器用修补后的奖励学习。\n\n结果与结论：9B 设置相对只生成任务的基线提高10.9分，但相对已共演化任务与奖励的基线，攻击修补额外贡献为2.7分。修补次数受限，仍能被攻破的任务也进入训练，不能称为可靠奖励认证。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，主张应落在减少已发现的可利用性，而非无参考地建立真值。诚实答案和 judge 仍可能共享错误；专业基准收益不代表临床有效性，后续应独立测量修补后的排序可靠性。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"评估器递归改进; 奖励投机与安全; 自适应课程与数据合成","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称用奖励投机监督任务、奖励与求解器共同改进；本文证据为攻击—诚实答案对照、准则修补、生成提示更新，以及相对无攻击共演化的增量对照。相对 UCoE（arxiv:2610.17609）以已知偏好响应对筛选可执行验证器，本篇修补逐任务 rubric 并用于权重训练；相对 arxiv:2610.11464 的锚点选择，本篇依赖模型生成对照与同源判断。编辑推断：外层生成规则确实改变，但判断器权重固定，残余漏洞仍被接纳，不能视为奖励已被认证。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20845","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.20845v1","title":"Evolving Together, Failing Apart: The Skill-Policy Co-evolution Trap in Self-Improving Agents","authors":"Yujie Feng; Xiaobin Wang; Jinluan Yang; Xiaonan Shi; Pengjun Xie; Philip S. Yu; Xiaoming Wu; Jieping Ye","affiliations":"Alibaba Token Hub, Alibaba Group；The Hong Kong Polytechnic University；University of Illinois at Chicago","abstract":"Skill-policy co-evolution, in which an agent's policy model and its skill bank improve each other during training, is a promising paradigm for self-improving agents. Current evaluations score the co-evolved policy on the final bank it trained with (the delivered bank). After deployment, however, skills may be rewritten, added or removed more frequently than the policy model is retrained, leaving the policy to operate on a drifted skill bank that neither the training objective nor existing evaluation protocols address. In this paper, we first establish, through theoretical and empirical analysis, that the fragility hidden by this blind spot is not incidental. The acceptance rule these methods share (cooperative acceptance) ties a policy's competence to the bank it co-evolved with, leaving it fragile once skills drift, regardless of the implementation; empirically, sensitivity to skill drift grows as co-evolution training proceeds. We therefore introduce the CO-evolution Drift Audit (CODA), a deployment-oriented evaluation protocol that simulates skill drift and, alongside success rate under worst-case drift, introduces two new metrics: a consistency rate under meaning-preserving edits and a resistance rate to corrupted skills. Across four co-evolution methods and five benchmarks (six settings), worst-case success is 5-13 points below the peak measured for each delivered pair, erasing 52-93% of the delivered bank's gain over the no-skill baseline. CODA thus reframes the target of co-evolution, from peak performance on the co-evolved bank to the ability to harness skills however they evolve, and provides a shared standard against which future methods can be audited.","tldr":"背景与问题：技能—策略共演化通常只测最终配对；部署后技能库比权重更新更频繁，原配高分可能掩盖对特定措辞和内容的依赖。\n\n方法：论文固定任务和策略，在固定检索下分别改写技能措辞、删除必要步骤或注入误导，并另测增删技能与撤库。沿训练检查点追踪敏感性，再以任务成功、语义一致性和抗损坏性审计交付系统；语义保持改写另经模型及部分人工检查。\n\n结果与结论：四种方法、六种设置中，所测最差成功率比原配低5—13个百分点；五种设置的内容漂移敏感性随训练增加。理论依赖理想选择与候选覆盖，不意味着任意共演化必然退化。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，共演化应优化技能变化下的可靠使用，而非只优化原配峰值。意义保持改写也会造成损失，说明问题不全是技能变坏；但所测最差值不是所有部署变化的全局最坏保证。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"RSI 评测与迁移; 自改进稳定性; 模型—数据共演化","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称共演化接受偏好造成技能漂移脆弱性；本文证据包括固定检索下的内容扰动、训练阶段曲线和四方法六设置审计。理论依赖理想化候选最优选择及覆盖，不证明所有共演化必然严重退化。相对 CoTrace（arxiv:2610.10426）研究训练与部署 harness 不匹配，本篇隔离技能文本变化；相对 SGUID（arxiv:2610.12367）筛选蒸馏价值，本篇审计交付后漂移。编辑推断：这是对既有迁移评测的具体扩展，而非已提出鲁棒训练解法。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20809","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.20809v1","title":"A Self-Improving Agent that Grows its Own DSL: Oracle-Free Operator Induction for Exact Question Answering","authors":"Yun-Shiuan Chuang; Yirou Ge; Yixi Li; Yiming Bian; Zijie Pan; Jenna L. Ballard; Uma Kona; Linsey Pang; Prakhar Mehrotra","affiliations":"PayPal AI","abstract":"A self-improving agent has to decide which new skills to keep, and in practice it keeps whatever earns a high reward, convinces a judge model, or compresses its library, even when the skill is wrong. That is fine until the answers have to be exactly right: over a table of transactions, a total is either right or wrong. We ask a harder question: can an agent grow what it can compute with no reward, no judge, and no answer key, and still be exactly right? A single frozen model runs two nested loops over a small, exact domain-specific language (DSL). The inner loop answers new questions only when two independently written expressions agree on every record. The outer loop discovers its own missing capability and authors an operator for it, admitted only when an independent second implementation agrees and the result obeys a conservation law, all without ground truth. The inner loop roughly triples the answerable-question set, and the outer loop self-extends on disjoint starting sets, inventing operators outside the starting closure; a no-induction control answers none of the new questions. The admission rule is empirically sound: it rejects 138 of 138 buggy operator variants under an independent reference, even one written by a different model family, where the admit-if-it-runs, self-consistency, and compression signals the field relies on admit most of them. Unmodified, the same mechanism self-extends on two further domains with unrelated schemas, business-ledger and clinical-encounter question answering, growing their answerable sets more than tenfold and nearly twentyfold. The loop transfers across model families too: run with further proposers, the gate stays sound and independent families self-extend comparably, with only the induction yield tracking each proposer's DSL fluency.","tldr":"背景与问题：固定小型领域语言只能回答已有算子可组合的问题；让 agent 自写新算子又会引入计算错误，运行成功或模型自信不足以决定保留。\n\n方法：冻结模型先用独立表达式的一致结果扩展问题覆盖，再针对反复出现的能力缺口生成算子。新算子需通过第二实现的差分测试和基于可信原语的守恒关系检查，获准后进入后续组合；解释器与准入规则保持固定。\n\n结果与结论：独立参考条件下，门控拒绝全部138个错误变体；人为让两实现共享错误时仍会漏放。团队盲评中仅89%的问题表达式忠实于问题，说明算得一致不代表理解正确。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可信扩展需要同时检查执行关系与问题语义。无 oracle 指在线准入不看答案键，不代表实验没有外部金标准；有限输入上的一致性也不是所有输入正确的形式证明。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"执行证据驱动改进; 可执行记忆与规则; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称无奖励、judge 和答案键地扩展自身领域语言；本文证据为固定模型提出算子，差分与守恒检查准入，新算子进入后续生成，以及无归纳控制和错误变体实验。相对 Memento 3（arxiv:2610.11794）更新环境规则和模型代码，本篇扩大计算词汇；相对 arxiv:2610.21646 的普遍认证限制，本篇主动限制语言、输入和验证范围，两者不矛盾。编辑推断：能力扩展来自可执行工具库，而非模型权重或准入算法自我提升；自然语言语义仍有缺口。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20474","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.20474v1","title":"AdaRSI: On-Demand Recursive Self-Improvement for Embodied Agents","authors":"Peidong Wang; Ying Chang; Zhiming Ma; Xiaocui Yang; Shi Feng; Daqi Liu; Yuzhe Yang; Xu Cao; Chuang Wang; Jian Su; Daling Wang","affiliations":"Northeastern University；AgiBot；University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","abstract":"Pretrained vision-language-action models (VLAs) often fail midway through unseen long-horizon tasks. Recursive self-improvement (RSI) offers a remedy, but embodied RSI methods either refine the harness around a frozen executor and so cannot add a missing motion, or train the executor on persistent failures without asking whether a failure lies in how the executor is called or in what it can do. We ask when a self-improving embodied system should change the weights of its executor, and propose AdaRSI, an on-demand RSI framework for embodied agents. A coding agent first improves its skills and harness, then attributes persistent failures by retrying failing sub-steps from saved states, and fine-tunes only the sub-steps that remain unreliable, with demonstrations it collects itself and experience carried over from earlier tasks. On all 50 target tasks of RoboCasa365, with GR00T N1.5 as the executor and no human demonstrations, AdaRSI improves the VLA on all three suites and raises its success on unseen composite tasks from 4.6% to 13.8%. Compared with fine-tuning every sub-step, it reaches slightly higher success while using only 28% of the GPU time and 22% of the self-collected demonstrations, and fine-tuning without a harness trains more yet gains far less.","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人子步骤失败可能是调用姿态或指令不当，也可能是执行器不会所需动作；直接微调所有失败既浪费数据，也可能损坏原本可用的能力。\n\n方法：AdaRSI 先修 harness，再从保存状态重试不同调用方式，只为仍不可靠的子步骤自采示范并微调。示范来自成功 rollout 或读取特权状态的脚本；训练起点取自实际到达状态，新策略经比较后仅在受益位置推荐使用。\n\n结果与结论：未见组合任务中，相对 harness-only 的9.9%，完整系统达到13.8%。同预算下只挑最低成功率步骤训练没有额外收益，支持训练状态与归因的重要性；结果限于仿真及单一执行器。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，harness 不只是廉价替代品，还决定训练数据来自哪些状态。保存状态重试提供受控干预，但有限重试找不到有效调用，并不严格证明动作不可实现；跨任务经验也尚未独立证明调度能力递归增强。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"harness—权重协同; 失败诊断; 具身 RSI","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称按失败归因决定何时更新执行器；本文证据为同状态更换调用方式、只训练残余不可靠子步骤、保留原策略默认，以及与低成功率选训练对象和全训练的对照。相对 arxiv:2610.11655 已提出先诊断再选择 harness 或权重，本篇不是首次提出干预分工，而是将其落实到具身子步骤、训练起始状态及按需调用。相对 EmbodiedRSI（arxiv:2610.10498）演化代码技能，本篇新增低层策略训练。编辑推断：支持成本有效的选择性适配，尚未隔离证明改进调度自身跨任务增强。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20431","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.20431v1","title":"SwarmRSI: Recursive Self-Improvement through Evolving Scientific Agent Swarm","authors":"Qianru Meng; Xi Zhang; Konstantinos Papakostas; Congfeng Cao; Wenxiang Hu; Tianyi Lu; Xiao Zhang; Lun Zhou; Zaiqiao Meng; Zhaochun Ren; Xiaohui Yan; Yougang Lyu","affiliations":"Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd.；Leiden University；University of Groningen","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement (RSI) in scientific research aims to improve agents' research capabilities through their own experimental experience. Scientific agent swarms can combine evidence and implementations from different research directions to guide their agents' subsequent experiments. However, poor experimental results can leave unclear whether to revise a hypothesis or its implementation, while overall program scores can hide components useful to other agents. To address these challenges, we introduce SwarmRSI, a framework that evolves scientific agent swarms for recursive self-improvement. We devise Feedback-Guided Swarm Mutation to refine hypotheses and their implementations using experimental feedback from other agents. We also propose Complementary Swarm Recombination to reuse retained hypotheses and complementary program components across agents, allowing partial results to support new research. Recursive Swarm Evolution integrates both mechanisms into a feedback loop, using new experimental evidence to guide subsequent research. Experiments on OpenProblems, NatureBench and MLE-Bench Lite demonstrate SwarmRSI's state-of-the-art (SOTA) performance. Further evaluations show that accumulated research experience improves performance on held-out tasks. Biologists also reproduce its programs for follow-up biological analyses.","tldr":"背景与问题：科学实验失败不说明假设错还是实现错；按整体得分淘汰程序，还会丢掉对其他研究分支有用的局部组件。\n\n方法：SwarmRSI 将假设、程序、执行证据与未解决需求写入共享图，用其他分支反馈决定改研究方向还是修实现。保留假设可迁到另一程序上验证，互补组件也可重组；每次执行及评分结果进入下一轮继承状态。\n\n结果与结论：NatureBench 上删除程序修订后，匹配既有最佳结果的比例从44.4%降至31.1%，支持实现修复有贡献。跨任务经验结果仍受源任务数量混淆，生物学家复用程序不等于复现整套方法。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，负结果应保留可复用结构，而非只有一个失败标签。但重组后得分上升不能证明原科学假设成立；固定搜索规则下状态越来越丰富，也不能直接当作改进算法自身递归变强。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"预算受限研究搜索; 实验经验复用; 失败诊断","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过演化可继承研究状态实现科学群体自改进；本文证据为执行反馈区分假设与实现修改、跨分支重用组件、共享图和选择机制的消融。相对 AReaL-RSI（arxiv:2610.18083）更新研究方向与带条件经验，本篇重点是明确的假设—程序关联及重组；相对 MASS（arxiv:2610.12176）训练共享模型，本篇循环的改变对象是研究状态，未展示骨干训练或调度算法自重写。编辑推断：属于经验驱动研究搜索推进，而非递归研究者能力已被认证。生物学家复用两个程序不等于独立复现整体 RSI 效果。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20312","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.20312v1","title":"Reflect After Failure: Brain-Inspired Self-Evolving Agents for Embodied Spatial Intelligence","authors":"Xin Li; Xiaohuan Gu; Yifan Wang; Shaobin Ling; Tianli Shi; Jingao Xu; Zhimeng Yin; Dapeng Wu; Yun Wang","affiliations":"City University of Hong Kong；East China Normal University；University of Electronic Science and Technology of China；The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen；The University of Hong Kong","abstract":"Vision-Language Models (VLMs) have made substantial progress in spatial reasoning, and self-evolving agents further extend these capabilities to embodied environments by learning from interactions. However, current self-evolution remains particularly challenging in embodied spatial tasks, complex and multi-step decisions from partial visual evidence making it difficult to determine why an execution fails. The failure may stem from misperception, insufficient exploration, or incorrect planning, yet execution feedback alone rarely reveals which component is responsible. As a result, simply accumulating interaction experience can reinforce ineffective strategies. To address this, we propose HiMeco, a brain-inspired self-evolving agent for embodied spatial intelligence, inspired by metacognitive monitoring and hippocampal memory consolidation. Through Hippocampal-Metacognitive Reflection, HiMeco diagnoses failures in perception-exploration-planning (PEP), then compares execution attempts to derive reusable strategies and guidance for avoiding recurring errors. It also abstracts interaction programs into parameterized skills, using evidence contracts and execution-based validation to determine their retention and reuse. These strategies and skills guide subsequent interactions, with memory updated only between rounds and model parameters kept frozen. HiMeco achieves state-of-the-art performance on ESI-Bench, and it also improves accuracy on EmbSpatial-Bench by 3.94 percentage points without evolution.","tldr":"背景与问题：空间任务只能看到部分环境，答错可能来自看错、探索不够或规划失误；不区分原因就总结经验，容易固化错误策略。\n\n方法：HiMeco 在执行结束后利用轨迹、答案真值与特权仿真信息诊断三类问题，比较多次尝试并提炼适用策略。程序片段抽象成参数化技能后，经证据合同和实际调用验证再保留；模型冻结，记忆只在轮间更新。\n\n结果与结论：材料称其在 ESI-Bench 领先，但结果表和关键消融未提供。EmbSpatial-Bench 的3.94个百分点收益发生在没有演化时，不能据此证明记忆更新有效。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，应优先核查去掉分类诊断后是否仍能取得同样收益，而非接受脑机制类比。诊断分数不是校准概率，离线特权信息也是重要监督来源；推广到无真值或真实机器人反馈时，归因可靠性尚未确定。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"失败诊断; 经验迁移; 具身 RSI","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称将元认知诊断与记忆巩固用于具身空间自演化；本文证据显示借助真值、特权仿真元数据及冻结审计模型诊断，再以执行结果和证据合同维护策略与技能，权重和轮内记忆固定。相对 EmbodiedRSI（arxiv:2610.10498）主动选择区分假设的实验，本篇侧重事后感知—探索—规划归因；相对 MetaExp（arxiv:2610.21492），本篇不训练经验更新行为。编辑推断：脑启发命名本身不是机制创新，截断材料未提供诊断必要性的完整消融效果。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20294","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.20294v1","title":"MMLA-RSI: Recursive Self-Improvement through RTT and RTMA","authors":"Junyi Zou; Avrova Donz","affiliations":"MMLA-org；Communication University of China (CUC)","abstract":"An agent can improve its behavior within an unresolved problem by changing how it acts and which experience it retains. We propose MMLA-RSI, a recursive self-improvement scheme with two implementations in Memory-Mediated Learning Architecture: Reasoning-Time Training (RTT) changes the policy state $Φ$, while Reasoning-Time Memory Adaptation (RTMA) changes authoritative memory $M$. Each route also makes its adaptation method an object of improvement. A current numerical updater trains the policy proposing its successor; a current memory manager chooses the records available to the process proposing its successor. An independently admitted successor takes over the same role in the next generation. We give bounded executable rule languages, shared task/proposal interfaces, and one algorithm for either route or their composition. The RTT instance changes scalar schedules in a clipped-momentum update. The RTMA instance chooses NULL or a complete-row write with possible eviction. A fixed interpreter, trusted committer, and independent evaluator bound what can change. State versions, read closures, and conditional properties describe causal execution, accepted transitions, and finite work. Existing numerical-component studies motivate the construction. In four-candidate program selection, retaining LARC feedback updates reduces expected error by 24.65 and 36.65 percentage points for two trained initializations. In chronological continuous-integration replay, feedback binding is positive while retention increases loss. Completed SQL studies improve substantially over an unadapted substrate but do not establish the required additional online benefit. These results characterize their declared components. The two recursive routes and their joint realization are specified here; their beneficial recursive chains and discovery efficiency remain to be evaluated.","tldr":"背景与问题：改变策略状态或写入记忆，只能说明发生适配；要证明递归改进，还须显示当前适配规则参与产生更好的继任规则，并由后者继续承担同一角色。\n\n方法：MMLA-RSI 分别规定数值更新器和记忆管理器的继任流程：前者训练提出后继的策略，后者选择该过程能读取的记录。候选锁定后由独立评估器准入，固定解释器和可信提交器限制可改范围，并记录更新先于新尝试的证据。\n\n结果与结论：现有组件研究有正有负：程序选择受益，连续集成回放保留状态却增加损失，SQL 未证实额外在线收益。论文明确表示，有益递归链及发现效率尚未评估。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，其价值在于把功能参与、任务收益和搜索效率分开。固定随机带下输出改变也不必然证明动作分布改变；这些证据要求比组件增益更接近真正递归主张，但目前仍是待验证方案。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; Harness 递归演化; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称在数值更新器与记忆管理器两条路径中，让当前规则参与产生继任规则并独立准入。本文证据支持状态、读依赖、事件顺序和受限规则语言的规格说明，组件实验不构成有益递归链。相对 Hyperagents（arxiv:2603.19461）的可编辑元程序，本篇细化为有界更新规则及记忆提交规则；相对 RSIFlow（arxiv:2610.21791）的元 harness 经验更新，本篇要求继任者接替同一学习角色。编辑推断：可作为可检验协议关注，不能按已实现递归收益入账。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20665","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.20665v1","title":"The World Won't Wait: Evaluating and Teaching Agents Under a Live Clock","authors":"Ningxin Pan; Hanyu Li; Yeqing Shen; Ning Ding; Yehui Tang; Wentao Zhang","affiliations":"Peking University；Samsung Research, Beijing, China","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents can solve complex interactive tasks, yet reasoning and tool calls take time. In continuously changing environments, an otherwise correct action may arrive too late. We introduce RealtimeBench, with 180 tasks across six game types, to evaluate agents while games continue running during inference. Paired evaluations show that GPT-6.1-sol outperforms the faster Jev when games are paused, but falls behind when they keep running. We propose Two-Timescale Offline Recursive Self-Improvement (TORSI): a slow teacher studies failures and tests corrections in paused games between attempts, then writes reusable instructions for a fast student. The student acts without teacher calls during gameplay, and validation scores determine which updates are adopted. Two rounds raise Jev's average test score from 13.51 to 24.19 on a 0--100 progress scale, improving all six game types. The instructions also improve average scores for three other models without retuning. These findings point toward real-time intelligence: enabling powerful LLM agents to remain effective in a continuously changing world by organizing deliberation, learning, and action across timescales.","tldr":"背景与问题：游戏在推理期间继续运行时，正确动作也可能来得太晚；暂停评测会掩盖这一点，在线调用更强教师反而可能破坏控制。\n\n方法：TORSI 让快学生独立行动，慢教师在回合之间读取失败，从保存状态练习替代动作，再让学生按真实延迟检验指导。只有在独立验证任务上改善的指导才替换旧版，下一轮处理更新后的残余失败，双方权重和行动接口不变。\n\n结果与结论：两轮后按游戏分别选出的指导，使测试平均进度分从13.51升至24.19；这不是统一采用第二轮候选的结果。消融显示仅写指导或缺少任一侧练习均不足以取得完整收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，慢推理适合用于控制间隙的学习，而非每次动作决策。证据限于文本状态接口、六类游戏和两轮，进度分不等于通关率；这里变强的是指导，不是教师或教学算法自身。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"Harness 递归演化; RSI 评测与迁移; 实时智能体","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称用双时间尺度离线教学支持实时自改进；本文证据为暂停与实时配对评测、教师和学生离线练习消融、验证门控指导更新及两轮结果。相对 Continual Harness（arxiv:2605.09998）在不重置任务中在线修改 harness，本篇把修改移至回合之间以避免教师延迟进入控制；相对 AHE（arxiv:2604.25850）的一般轨迹驱动修改，本篇保留学生接口，仅更新实时动作指导。编辑推断：是实时场景下的经验化指导改进，未证实教师更新机制自身递归增强。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19799","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.19799v1","title":"Evolve Together, Fall into Place: How Social Scaffolding Shapes Self-Evolving Multi-Agent Systems","authors":"Seojin Hwang; Youngmin Choi; Hwanhee Lee","affiliations":"Chung-Ang University","abstract":"Recent work lets LLM agents evolve their own harness, up to the team itself. Yet in human groups, the same abilities achieve different outcomes under different social conditions. Borrowing the notion of scaffolding from developmental psychology, we investigate whether the social scaffolding of a self-evolving multi-agent system (MAS), namely its team composition and structure of interdependence (e.g., collaboration, conformity, or competition), shapes how the team evolves. We present AGORA (Agents Growing through Organization and Relational Arrangements), a framework that varies the two axes independently across three evolution mechanisms. Across web search, codebase understanding, and document QA, we find that (1) evolution alone rarely helps, while the right scaffolding surpasses a strong agent evolved alone by up to 25 points; (2) it does so by moving authority to the most capable member while the others step back; and (3) this member, having grown within the team, outperforms the same model alone. Designing a self-evolving MAS thus requires designing its social scaffolding, which shapes not only how its agents learn, but who gets to lead.","tldr":"背景与问题：让团队反复修改技能和角色，不保证合作会改善；弱主席可能压制强成员，增加角色也可能只增加等待。论文把团队组成与决策权限作为独立变量，而非默认有效的背景。\n\n方法：固定个体演化机制，改变成员能力配比及信息共享、修改提案和决策规则；执行轨迹与同伴备忘进入下一轮，团队修改经验证集阻止明显退化。权重不变，部分技能和记忆更新由固定强模型完成。\n\n结果与结论：网页搜索中，合适配置较独自演化的强代理最高多25分；但另一模型家族未稳定重现该优势，角色扩张还伴随超时。领导集中并非普遍有效的组织规律。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，值得检验的是强成员能否获得有效经验并减少协调损耗，而非多代理是否天然更强。竞争条件直接安排按分数轮换主席，不能把全部权力转移解释成演化涌现。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"多智能体工作流演化; 经验迁移; RSI 评测与迁移","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称社会支架决定多智能体演化效果及领导权分配。本文证据：冻结权重，分别更新技能、记忆或提示，再根据同伴备忘修改团队；反馈包括自反思、任务评分和验证门控。相对 MASS（arxiv:2610.12176）搜索工作流后微调共享权重，本篇控制团队能力组合与相互依赖规则，研究外部状态演化，没有匹配性能比较。编辑推断：组织条件的受控研究是具体推进，但竞争条件直接规定按分数轮换主席，领导权迁移不能全部算作自发发现；固定强模型承担部分更新，也不证明改进者递归增强。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19725","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.19725v2","title":"TimeRSI: Towards Self-Improved Agentic Deployment for Time-Series Foundation Models","authors":"Haoxin Liu; Deqing Fu; Lucheng Fu; Yiqiao Jin; Rushi Qiang; Harshavardhan Kamarthi; B. Aditya Prakash","affiliations":"Georgia Institute of Technology；University of Southern California；Samay AI","abstract":"Time-series foundation models provide strong zero-shot forecast, but deployment for real-world applications still requires task-specific designs for model inputs and outputs. Direct inference can leave domain knowledge and recurring forecast errors unaddressed, while tailored pipelines require substantial human expertise and effort. We introduce TimeRSI, a self-improving agentic deployment system around frozen forecasting models. A coding agent translates task descriptions into executable pipeline changes. It tests each revision on historical forecasting windows and uses observed errors to guide subsequent revisions. During deployment, an adaptive selector chooses among the resulting pipelines using completed forecasts under similar conditions. Across 198 tasks on TIME and fev-bench, TimeRSI outperforms all submissions on six point and probabilistic forecasting metrics. Controlled comparisons support the value of feedback-guided revision over non-iterative pipeline search. Further experiments verify the generalization with different coding agents and forecasting models. Code is available at https://github.com/haoxin1998/TimeRSI.","tldr":"背景与问题：冻结时序模型不会自动利用节假日等任务知识，也不会自行修正重复误差；人工设计流水线昂贵，而平均最好的方案未必适合每个预测窗口。\n\n方法：编码代理在早期历史窗口执行候选代码，用预测误差和日志指导下一次修订，再用较晚窗口筛选部署方案。部署时根据相似且结果已完整揭晓的历史窗口选择流水线；此时代码固定，仅选择依据更新。\n\n结果与结论：198项任务中，同候选数的非迭代搜索弱于直接推理，反馈修订则改善结果；TIME 的平均绝对缩放误差相对降低1.52%。更换编码代理和预测骨干仍有收益，但候选数匹配未控制全部成本。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键不是多生成方案，而是让实际误差否定看似合理的领域改动。历史误差能指导部署工程，却不能保证分布突变后的收益，更未证明编码代理自身越来越会优化。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 反馈驱动更新; 跨任务迁移","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称以 RSI 自动改进冻结预测模型的部署。本文证据：编码代理用历史窗口误差修改输入输出流水线，较晚历史时段用于选择候选；部署时只更新选择依据，不再修改代码。相对 Meta-Harness（arxiv:2603.28052）从代码、分数和轨迹搜索 harness，本篇加入按预测条件匹配历史表现的部署选择，并区分适配窗口与选择窗口。编辑推断：是任务专用流水线搜索的具体扩展，改进对象不是编码代理或其优化算法；同候选数对照不等于同总计算量。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19591","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.19591v1","title":"L3M: A Verifiable Harness and Runtime for Self-Extending and Self-Improving Agents","authors":"Carson Eisenach; Robert Joseph George; Vincent Quenneville-Belair; Kate Gwimm; Dean Foster","affiliations":"Amazon","abstract":"The lasting gains in AI have come from methods that absorb more computation, and language models already scale computation within a call. Useful work, though, happens across calls: over hours or days, through tools and external systems, among many agents and the humans they work for, and increasingly through code the agents write themselves. Whether that work compounds is enabled by the harness around it, and the harness faces a constraint the model does not: of the three participants in such a computation, the human, the model and code, only the human's attention does not scale, so the computation can grow only if the human is not in every loop. L3M is a runtime built on that premise, written in Lean 4 so that one language implements the harness, states its invariants, and is the language agents extend it in. One computation spans humans, agents, models and code, and all of its state lives in Git: a rich state trajectory -- rather than a chat conversation -- is an object the runtime can resume, rewind, fork, compare and merge. Waiting, communication, delegation and undo are primitives, not patterns the model reasons through each time. When an agent works out a procedure, it can write it once as a sealed Lean program whose type is its permission request, and the harness offers it back as a tool -- machinery for the model to use. To take the human out of the loop, L3M uses reversibility to decide where that is safe: a tool's review tier follows from how far its effects can be undone, so agents act freely where the runtime can recover. Because the machinery can change, the properties that make this safe are stated as kernel-checked theorems about the code that runs. On Terminal-Bench, an untuned L3M reaches about two thirds of its (unsafe) shell-equipped pass rate using only safe (not needing human review) tools.","tldr":"背景与问题：长期代理若每次等待、协调和恢复都依赖模型推理与人工审批，计算扩张会受人的注意力限制；允许代理写新工具，又可能扩大其操作权限。\n\n方法：L3M 把状态和轨迹持久化，并允许代理将重复程序封装为新工具。程序类型声明所需权限，运行时限制其不超过既有授权；可恢复或权限已限定的操作减少审批，部分检查由 Lean 内核验证。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称仅用无需人工审查的工具，可达到带不安全 shell 配置约三分之二的通过率；可见片段缺少完整实验表，不能据此判断自扩展的独立收益。定理也依赖编译、提供者和操作系统等可信部分。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，贡献是让能力增长与权限增长脱钩，而非认证代理会正确自改进。回滚本地文件不能撤回已经发出的外部请求，安全主张必须逐项对应可恢复范围和可信假设。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; Harness 递归演化; 预算与权限审计","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称提供可验证的自扩展运行时。本文证据：代理可把程序变成后续工具，类型声明权限需求，内核检查部分运行时代码性质；可撤销性与预先限定的能力决定审查层级。相对 Self-Evolving Agent Harness（arxiv:2610.18813）的修改对象及准入分类，本篇给出具体实现和不变量；相对 Hyperagents（arxiv:2603.19461）允许修改元程序，本篇重点是限制扩展权限，而非提高修改算法。编辑推断：执行结果、类型检查及审查支持扩展准入，但缺少多轮自扩展收益归因；局部安全性质不能覆盖可信编译、系统服务及程序语义正确性。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19581","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.19581v1","title":"XferAgent: Cross-Agent Experience Transfer for Self-Improving LLM Agents","authors":"Weihao Li; Jun Bai; Shijie Chen; Qincheng Lu; Xinyu Wang; Ziyang Song","affiliations":"McGill University；Northwestern University；Mila – Quebec AI Institute；Ohio University","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents can reuse experience from prior task executions to improve performance on subsequent tasks. Although existing methods enable cross-agent experience sharing, differences in agents' execution histories and task requirements make shared experiences difficult to reuse effectively. We propose XferAgent, a framework for cross-agent experience transfer that organizes reusable experience in local and shared experience graphs. XferAgent reconciles compatible contributions from heterogeneous agents while avoiding unreliable merges. For each new task, it selects shared experiences and integrates them with the target agent's local experience to support task execution. Experiments across diverse task domains show improvements over representative memory-based methods and effective experience transfer between heterogeneous agent frameworks. Cumulative task success also increases over successive task passes as agents update and reuse their experiences.","tldr":"背景与问题：别的代理学到的经验可能有用，却未必适配接收者的工具和执行历史；只共享语义相似条目，容易合并不兼容经验或重复注入无效指导。\n\n方法：系统分别维护本地与共享经验图，保留来源并避免有歧义的合并。新任务结合相关性、其他代理的使用结果与本地结果选择经验；任务评分随后更新使用统计，并将新轨迹提炼成下一轮经验。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称跨任务和异构框架迁移优于记忆基线，但主要结果表未包含在片段中。跨框架实验增加贡献者时，也同步增加源任务总暴露量，不能将收益全部归于代理多样性。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，迁移价值必须由接收者校准，不能直接照搬贡献者的成功率。不过给所有已注入经验记同一个任务结果，仍无法区分谁真正有用；重复任务的累计成功也不等于未见任务泛化。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"经验迁移; 外部记忆与规则更新; RSI 评测与迁移","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称改善异构代理间经验迁移。本文证据：本地和共享图保存成功或失败经验，按相似性及匹配歧义合并，结合其他代理与本地使用结果排序；任务结束后更新被注入经验的统计并写入新经验。相对 STRATA（arxiv:2610.19386）处理分层抽象、遗忘及方向混淆，本篇侧重跨代理来源和本地—共享效用融合；相对 MetaExp（arxiv:2610.21492），本篇不训练经验学习行为。编辑推断：闭环更新记忆和效用估计，不更新合并或检索算法；使用后成功只是关联反馈，不等于经验的因果贡献。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19424","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.19424v1","title":"VideoHarness-SRSI: Structured Recursive Self-Improvement for Video Understanding Harness","authors":"Zihao Lin; Haoyu Dong; Haobo Xu; Chi-Chih Chang; Xuying Ning; Yinglong Xia; Shuang Yang; Zhuokai Zhao; Xinying Song; Dongfang Liu; Lifu Huang; Yang Song; Qifan Wang","affiliations":"University of California, Davis；Meta MRS Research；Duke University；University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign；Cornell University；Purdue University","abstract":"LLM system capabilities depend not only on model parameters but also on the executable harnesses that organize information acquisition, tool use, reasoning, and memory. Recursive harness evolution can automate their design, but how it can reliably discover generalizable systems from limited, noisy, and repeatedly reused feedback remains unclear. We study this question in agentic video understanding, where rich multimodal evidence and coupled mechanisms make harness optimization challenging. We first introduce VideoHarness-BRSI, a recursive self-improvement framework that evolves video harnesses around a frozen vision-language model. Analyzing over 4,000 evolved candidates, we find it competitive with hand-engineered systems but identify three interconnected failure modes: validation overfitting, search-budget dilution, and the early-experience trap. We trace all three to a common root: the same imperfect validation evidence drives both harness revisions and the proposer's search strategy. We therefore propose VideoHarness-SRSI, an evidence-governed framework in which every search decision rests on evidence that is transferable, sufficient, and gathered before the search commits. It restricts the proposer to content-free feedback, informs exploration with instrumented warm-up experiments, and develops mechanisms in isolated probe-race branches before factorial composition and joint refinement. Across four video understanding benchmarks, VideoHarness-SRSI improves the equally weighted mean held-out score by 6.2% relative to VideoHarness-BRSI and reduces the mean validation-test gap by 37.9%. Reliable harness evolution thus depends on how search is organized and informed, not only on how well it optimizes validation performance.","tldr":"背景与问题：有限验证集同时决定保留哪个 harness、下一步探索什么；视频和题目细节会诱导样本特化，早期噪声还可能让提案者过早放弃有效机制。\n\n方法：固定视觉语言模型，只向提案者开放汇总分数和不含验证内容的执行统计。先做受控预实验，再让机制在独立分支积累证据，最后测试组合及相互作用，减少一次联合修改导致的归因混淆。\n\n结果与结论：四个视频基准上，相对基础演化流程，平均留出得分相对提高6.2%，验证—测试差距缩小37.9%。内容暴露对照支持过拟合诊断，但片段不足以核对完整消融和总成本。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，更多反馈并非总是更好：能解释已见题目的信息，也能帮助记住验证集。真正应优化的是证据对未见任务的预测力；屏蔽内容仍不能自动消除反复查询汇总分数带来的选择偏差。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"Harness 递归演化; RSI 评测与迁移; 选择误差","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过证据治理提高视频 harness 演化的泛化性。本文证据：固定视觉语言骨干，限制提案者接触验证内容，先以受控试验探索机制，再隔离演化并检验组合；候选和评估记录影响后续搜索。相对 Meta-Harness（arxiv:2603.28052）强调读取完整历史代码和轨迹，本篇识别内容暴露可能产生的过拟合，并改变反馈接口及搜索组织。编辑推断：这是对既有 harness 搜索的实质修正，但设计更好的固定搜索流程，不等于搜索器自身递归进化；截断材料不足以核对完整预算和消融。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19422","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.19422v1","title":"AgentSafeEvo: Adversarial Co-Evolution for LLM Agent Safety","authors":"Chenxu Wang; Xiaoyu Wen; Han Qi; Ziyuan Zhou; Cheng Jin; Chaochao Lu; Qiaosheng Zhang","affiliations":"Shanghai Artificial Intelligence Laboratory；Fudan University；Shanghai Jiaotong University；Zhejiang University","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents accomplish complex tasks through multi-turn interactions with external tools. However, malicious content embedded in user queries, tool descriptions, or environment observations can manipulate their decisions and induce unsafe actions. Adversarial co-evolution has emerged as an effective approach to strengthening LLM safety, but existing work primarily focuses on language-level safety or indirect prompt injection in web tasks. In this paper, we introduce AgentSafeEvo, a co-evolutionary reinforcement learning framework for agent safety built on an attacker-defender game spanning diverse tasks and attack types. The attacker learns to construct adversarial agent tasks that expose weaknesses in the defender's tool use, while the defender learns to complete tasks safely under these attacks. We further introduce learnability-guided task weighting, which uses within-task defender-reward variability to adjust each task's contribution to attacker and defender updates. Extensive experiments on agent safety and general capability benchmarks demonstrate that our method improves adversarial robustness while maintaining general agent capabilities.","tldr":"背景与问题：固定攻击集不会随防御者变强而暴露新弱点；工具代理还会从请求、工具说明和环境观察受到攻击，仅训练安全措辞不足以保证安全行动。\n\n方法：攻击者学习构造完整对抗任务，防御者学习在其中完成合法要求。固定模型分别判断轨迹安全性和效用，反馈更新双方；对同任务多次执行中结果差异较大的任务加权，避免只追求让防御者全败。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称安全鲁棒性改善且保持一般能力；片段提供四类安全基准与通用能力协议，但主要结果和加权消融被省略，无法核对幅度及独立贡献。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可学习攻击应产生可区分的行为后果，而非单纯最难。不过奖励变化也可能来自评判噪声；训练依赖模型判断，尚需独立检查安全评分、合法任务完成与过度拒绝之间的关系。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"递归安全改进; 红队反馈; 自适应课程与数据合成","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称将对抗共演化扩展至多类工具交互任务。本文证据：攻击者生成用户请求、工具定义与观察，防御者执行；固定模型判断安全与合法任务完成情况，双方据此强化学习，组内奖励变化用于任务加权。相对 ReSI（arxiv:2610.12233）红队探测后筛选训练配方，本篇直接训练攻击任务生成者和防御策略；相对 SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）的可教性共训练，本篇采用对抗目标和安全—效用模型奖励。编辑推断：经验生成器参与学习，但奖励波动只是可学习性代理，其校准及奖励投机防护在可见片段中未充分建立。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19386","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.19386v1","title":"STRATA: Self-Maintaining Structured Experience Graphs for Self-Evolving Language Agents","authors":"Guanhua Zhu; Hanwen Li; Zhi Wei; Mengnan Du; Chenxi Yuan","affiliations":"New Jersey Institute of Technology；The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents can self-evolve at test time by accumulating experience: retrieving relevant memories before acting and writing new lessons back afterwards. Yet most are single-level: trajectories, distilled workflows and reasoning items all land in one undifferentiated pool indexed by embedding similarity, with no typed abstraction hierarchy. They never forget or deduplicate, and are prone to negative transfer, where a superficially similar but directionally opposite experience is recalled and its concrete steps are copied verbatim, actively harming the agent. We introduce STRATA, a structured, outcome-grounded, self-maintaining memory that organizes experience into a three-layer graph of atomic skills and code snippets, task workflows and generalized meta-frameworks, connected by typed edges. STRATA maintains itself through five mechanisms sharing one similarity geometry: a multi-dimensional similarity that scores retrieval by operation and target; a typed reflector crystallizing procedures from successes and pitfalls from failures; community detection that induces meta-frameworks; pressure-triggered garbage collection with articulation-point protection; and contrast edges that flag confusable, direction-opposite experiences. Across four interactive benchmarks (AppWorld, WebArena, ALFWorld, ScienceWorld), two frozen backbones and seven baselines, STRATA attains the best average score while simultaneously using the lowest latency and fewest environment steps of any memory-augmented method, and 44% fewer lines of injected memory than the most context-hungry baseline. We isolate two failure modes of prior memories: single-level memory degrades sharply as the task set grows, and single-level concrete memories suffer catastrophic negative transfer, which contrast edges repair, lifting ScienceWorld from 78.7 to 96.7 within the same system.","tldr":"背景与问题：把具体操作、任务流程和一般原则混在相似度记忆池里，会随规模增长稀释检索；更危险的是，表面相似但方向相反的程序可能被直接执行。\n\n方法：冻结模型，将经验组织成技能、流程和抽象原则，并按任务结果写回：成功产生可复用程序，失败只添加避坑提示。检索同时关注操作与目标，召回相反经验时明确警告，定期压缩和删除冗余流程。\n\n结果与结论：四个互动基准、两个骨干上，摘要称平均表现及效率优于记忆基线；ScienceWorld 同系统加入对比关系后，得分从78.7升至96.7。完整消融表缺失，尚不能核对各机制贡献。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，经验被执行时，错误召回的代价高于一般检索问答。方向识别因此可能比继续扩库更关键；但当前对比关系依赖固定反义操作词表，开放语义下能否覆盖混淆尚未验证。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"经验迁移; 外部记忆与规则更新; 失败诊断","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称以分层、可维护经验图减少记忆扩张和负迁移。本文证据：冻结骨干，成功轨迹形成程序，失败只附警示；抽象、合并和删除改变后续检索，并以固定反向操作词表建立对比边。相对 XferAgent（arxiv:2610.19581）侧重异构代理的共享统计，本篇处理经验库的层次与反向程序混淆；相对 MetaExp（arxiv:2610.21492）训练经验行为，本篇主要修改外部结构。编辑推断：同系统方向混淆修复比总体排名更能定位贡献，但维护规则固定，不能称为记忆管理器递归增强。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18868","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18868v1","title":"Tev: Scaling Long-Horizon Agentic Environments with Dense Progress Rewards","authors":"Wenbo Hu; Shraman Pramanick; Krishna Kumar Singh; Nanyun Peng; Kai-Wei Chang; Yong Jae Lee","affiliations":"Adobe Research；University of California, Los Angeles","abstract":"Long-horizon agents have drawn growing attention for their ability to work autonomously -- from hours to days -- on economically valuable tasks, a capability essential to automated discovery and recursive self-improvement (RSI). Yet open-source models still struggle on long-horizon tasks, largely for lack of both training data and a working recipe, and scaling both is hard: long, complex tasks are difficult to curate and verify, and their rewards are sparse. We address both. First, we introduce Tev-Gym, the first long-horizon agent training dataset with verifiable, dense, progressive rewards -- 1,170 verified task environments across 7 domains. It is built on a latent-world-first approach that first constructs a latent world: a complete and correct hidden specification of the task domain, workflow, and expected state after each step. Each task is then progressively rendered from this specification into an agent-facing environment, enabling controllable complexity and a natural progress metric. Second, we turn this metric into a training recipe: via progress-potential reward shaping (PPRS), we convert progress into a dense per-step reward that improves training efficiency and makes otherwise-intractable tasks trainable. Training with this recipe yields Tev-27B, which achieves substantial gains on the Agents' Last Exam computing and math sciences domains (ALE-CM), matching GPT-6 Astra and Claude Opus 5 at Pass@5. Despite training only on ALE-related data, it generalizes to the Terminal-Bench (TB) 3.0 and 4.0 subsets, surpassing GLM 5.2 and Gemini 3.7 Flash, and reaches Claude Opus 4.8-level performance on middle-horizon tasks such as TB 2.1.","tldr":"背景与问题：长程任务里，同组轨迹经常全部失败，终局二元奖励无法区分接近完成和毫无进展，导致组相对强化学习缺少梯度。\n\n方法：先构造已知正确的潜在世界，再从同一世界生成受损输入、目标和阶段检查，按工作区正确程度计进度。训练奖励额外保留最终进度，使未完成轨迹也能产生差异；它不是保证原最优策略不变的传统塑形。\n\n结果与结论：训练所得27B模型在指定长程计算与数学任务上，Pass@5 相对基座提高65%；还报告终端子集迁移。可见材料未给出主要训练消融，不能将全部收益归于稠密奖励。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，共同真值来源有助于避免分别生成任务和检查器造成的工件失配。但代理目标仍被改变，部分进度奖励可能影响策略取舍；这属于训练基础，而非已展示的递归自改进。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"RSI 研究环境与评测; 长程交互学习; 奖励信号","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称构建首个带可验证稠密进度奖励的长程训练集。本文证据：从预先确定的潜在世界生成任务、真值和阶段检查，再用最终进度补充终局奖励。相对 AutoEnvScaling（arxiv:2610.14163）让 solver 轨迹指导下一轮环境构建，本篇强调共同真值锚点和固定生成程序；相对 RewardWeaver（arxiv:2610.10120）动态选择过程奖励，本篇使用预定义可执行进度。编辑推断：是 RSI 的训练基础设施，而非环境或训练器自改进闭环，尚未展示生成策略随学习者反馈更新。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18845","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18845v2","title":"The Last Remote Sensing Model Built by Humans? Casting Any Earth Observation Task as Recursive Self-Improvement","authors":"Sijie Zhao; Zeqi Zhou; Heli Qi; Xuanchao Fu; Zhuo Zheng; Junshi Xia; Junjue Wang; Weihao Xuan; Naoto Yokoya","affiliations":"The University of Tokyo；RIKEN；Stanford University","abstract":"Earth observation (EO) models are still built by hand. For each new task, experts design a training recipe and tune it against a benchmark. We show that this loop can be handed to an agent. Any verifiable task can be cast as a harness and a verifier, where the harness defines what the agent may use and the verifier defines what counts as success. Every EO task can be made verifiable, through labeled benchmarks, independent sensors, physical models or the repeated observation of the same place. Given only these two components, a general-purpose coding agent builds the EO model and improves it recursively on its own outputs. Settings long treated as separate research problems, from learning with a handful of labels to adapting across domains, become choices of harness and verifier. On six EO benchmarks spanning optical, SAR and multispectral time-series imagery, with outputs that range from land-cover maps and ship instances to canopy heights and answers about large images, agent-built models surpass the state of the art on every one, and on land-cover mapping, they do so from 11% of the training labels. This establishes a new paradigm for EO, in which people design harnesses and verifiers and agents build the models, so EO models improve as agents do.","tldr":"背景与问题：新遥感任务往往需要专家重选模型和训练配方，少标签设置尤其依赖工程经验；论文试图把设计工作交给能运行实验的编码代理。\n\n方法：人固定可用数据、模型与预算，用封闭验证器只返回分数；代理自行写训练代码，并将已训练模型的预测或检查点用于后继模型，按分数选择保留。最终模型另在隐藏测试集评估。\n\n结果与结论：材料称六个遥感基准均超过所列已有方法，部分任务只需少量训练标签；每次运行上限为四张GB200、12小时。实验验证器仍使用基准标签，不能据此证明所有遥感任务都有可靠验证方式。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，减少训练标注不等于消除监督需求，部分成本转移到了验证标签与任务接口。递归发生在目标模型的自训练谱系，尚无证据表明编码代理或产生改进的规则也持续变强。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"RSI 研究环境与评测; 自主后训练; 反馈驱动更新","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称任何地球观测任务都可转为 harness 与 verifier，并由代理递归构建模型。本文证据：编码代理在封闭环境内写训练代码，以隐藏验证分数筛选，并利用此前模型预测、检查点或校准输出训练后继。相对 Athanor（arxiv:2610.21055）的自主语言模型后训练，本篇扩展到多传感器遥感及标签预算；相对 TimeRSI（arxiv:2610.19725）只改冻结骨干的部署，本篇多数任务允许训练目标模型。编辑推断：自训练谱系明确，但研究者自身未被更新；独立传感器和物理验证主要是论述，实验反馈仍来自基准标签。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18842","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18842v1","title":"Who Improves the Robot? Toward Physical Recursive Self-Improvement","authors":"Hai Zhou; Fan Yang; Zeyi Chen; Lejun Zhang; Chenyang Fu; Jianping Li; Jiayi Zhu; Xianyang Liu; Yingxuan Yang; Lili Meng; Lu Wang; Xinyang Han; Jiankai Sun; Weirui Ye; Guanchu Wang; Wanhua Li; Ming Zhou; Boyi Li; Ming Jin; Kun Shao; Muhao Chen; Guang Chen; Lei Ma; Joey Tianyi Zhou; Costas Spanos; Xia Hu; Mac Schwager; Weinan Zhang; Qian Feng; Shangding Gu","affiliations":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University；Google；Microsoft；University of California, Berkeley；Stanford University；Massachusetts Institute of Technology；Shanghai Artificial Intelligence Laboratory；Nanyang Technological University；Nvidia；Virginia Tech；Xiaomi；University of California, Davis；Tongji University；University of Tokyo；Singapore Management University；Technical University of Munich","abstract":"Robots are increasingly autonomous in task execution, yet their improvement remains largely human-driven. This study investigates Physical Recursive Self-Improvement (Physical RSI), in which physical experience guides lasting updates to both a robot's capabilities and its improvement procedure, making subsequent improvement more effective across tasks. Physical RSI faces challenges from noisy observations, continuous dynamics, costly trials, and irreversible consequences. We present an L0-L5 framework that differentiates capability-level from meta-level updates and within-task from across-task gains, reserving L5 for independently verified recursive gain. We study existing methods around harness adaptation and model training, alongside safety and control mechanisms that govern execution and successive updates. Our analysis reveals that, despite substantial progress in self-improvement, the surveyed literature does not yet demonstrate Physical RSI as defined by our framework. We identify research priorities in reliable feedback, causal attribution, safety preservation, and benchmarking, outlining a path toward robots that autonomously improve how they learn while ensuring safety. The GitHub repository for Physical RSI is available at https://github.com/SAIL-Research-Lab/Physical-RSI.","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人能自主执行，不代表能自主改进；即使技能越积越多，也可能只是固定更新流程不断运行，而非学习过程本身变得更有效。\n\n方法：论文将执行系统与改进程序分开，用L0—L5区分能力更新、元级更新及跨任务收益。最高等级要求从相同起点和经验出发，在匹配预算下由独立评估比较新旧改进程序；物理反馈可来自真实交互或物理仿真。\n\n结果与结论：这是一项框架与综述工作，不提供达到最高等级的新系统。其判断是所审阅文献尚未满足该定义的物理 RSI 证据要求，不能扩展成对全部机器人研究的否定。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，递归主张最关键的对照是“更新后的改进程序能否产生更好的后续改进”，而非机器人最终更强。独立评测还须防止标准随轮次改变，否则所谓递归增益可能只是目标漂移。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; 具身 RSI; 能力归因","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称建立 Physical RSI 的定义、分级和独立评测框架。本文证据是任务执行系统与改进程序的区分，以及从同一代系统、同一经验和同预算比较新旧改进程序的要求，不是已实现递归收益的实验。相对 MC-EvoBench（arxiv:2610.13829）隔离经验迁移混淆，本篇进一步要求元级更新及其后续收益；相对 Hyperagents（arxiv:2603.19461）可编辑元程序，本篇强调物理证据、跨任务和独立评价。编辑推断：贡献主要是审计标准，不能把其综述范围内未发现证据写成物理 RSI 不可能。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18813","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18813v1","title":"Self-Evolving Agent Harness","authors":"Chuyang Wei; Haoxiang Guan; Minghang Zhu; Kexin Zhou; Jiyan He; Xiren Zhou; Huanhuan Chen; Yifei Shen","affiliations":"Zhongguancun Academy；University of Science and Technology of China；Zhongguancun Institute of Artificial Intelligence","abstract":"Harness self-evolution revises an agent's software scaffolding, including prompts, memory, workflows, and executable components, while keeping model weights fixed. We formalize a feedback-driven process in which accepted revisions persist across runs. The framework separates update targets from proposal and admission mechanisms. It distinguishes changes to interpreted state from revisions to tools and code, repository-level control logic, and plugin composition. We characterize search through evolutionary optimization and examine its reliability through continual PAC-learning. Under explicit assumptions, the analysis yields an expected generalization bound, a retention bound conditional on historical regression budgets, and a high-probability admission rule using fresh, independent validation data. We examine how persistent harness revisions affect knowledge sharing and organizational workflows, with implications for scientific reliability, physical safety, and institutional accountability. Cases from prior work illustrate model--harness co-design, distributed execution, and plugin reuse. Reliable deployment requires continual validation as task distributions and evaluators change, with independent safeguards for learning, runtime privileges, and consequential actions. We provide a comprehensive 66-page discussion of related work, theory, algorithms, evaluation, applications, and the broader impact of Harness RSI, together with continuously updated code and supplementary materials, at https://github.com/zgcagi/Harness-RSI.","tldr":"背景与问题：提示、记忆、工具实现和运行时控制都可能被称为 harness 演化，但修改边界及风险不同；仅有修订过程，也不代表产生了可保留的性能收益。\n\n方法：论文按被继承的状态分类，分开描述修改对象、候选生成和准入。模型固定，执行反馈驱动候选，获准版本跨运行加载；摘要再提出依赖明确假设的泛化、回归保留及独立验证准入界。\n\n结果与结论：可见正文主要是定义、分类和引用案例，并非新的匹配实验。所给文本虽未标截断，却未包含摘要承诺的理论正文，因此不能核验定理条件；插件成本案例还明确存在两套统计不一致。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，最有用的区分是“发生演化”和“经比较证明改进”。修改解释态、可执行代码与更新算法应分别记账；独立验证数据的理论要求，也不能直接套到反复复用同一验证集的搜索。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"Harness 递归演化; RSI 可证伪性与治理; 验证理论","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称提供持久 harness 演化的操作分类及条件理论。本文证据明确区分修改对象、提案和准入，并指出更新机制自身修改是额外递归层；反馈可来自环境、自动评估或人类。相对 Self-Harness（arxiv:2606.09498）的失败挖掘—提案—回归测试实现，本篇是抽象归纳，不是新实验系统；相对 arxiv:2610.10611 的有界验证类分析，本篇摘要提出稳定性和独立验证样本下的统计保证。编辑推断：理论正文未出现在提供文本中，无法核查假设或证明；引用案例不能记作本文新实验。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18792","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18792v1","title":"SEAR: Self-Evolving Agentic Robotics","authors":"Xinyi Wang; Bangzheng Li; Hanyu Wang; Lin Zhang; Andrea Yaoyun Cui; Zhenggang Tang; Shyamal Buch; Dejia Xu","affiliations":"Luma AI","abstract":"Frontier language-model agents can now improve robots on their own: they write control code, test it, and keep what works as skills and memories for the next task. We introduce SEAR (Self-Evolving Agentic Robotics), a framework and benchmark built around two questions. Is the agent really learning, or just trying more often? And does what it learns still help on new tasks, in a new simulator, and on a real robot? The framework runs an agent in three modes: it writes code that becomes the policy (code-as-policy), acts live in the control loop (agent-as-policy), or works as a researcher that fine-tunes a vision-language-action model (auto-research). The benchmark adds controls that separate retained experience from repeated attempts, familiar tasks, privileged simulator state, larger budgets, and luck. Across seven frontier language models, 330 simulated and five physical tasks, and over four years of agent runtime, we highlight three findings. First, the learning curve of a robotic agent depends both on the overall time budget and the task difficulty relative to model capability. Harder tasks make longer sessions worthwhile; on easier tasks, re-rolling short attempts does just as well. Second, control code and shared routines transfer across tasks and simulators, while task-specific solutions do not. On a real robot, we observe a performance gap between agent-designed practice and novel human-designed scenes. Third, different models evolve more effectively in different ways. Some do best acting live, others writing code first. And a text-only model keeps pace with a comparable multimodal one: perception helps with error assessment, but agentic reasoning and tool use can matter more. We release the benchmark and codebase to support future research.","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人成功率随时间上升，可能只是多次重试、熟悉初始状态或更大预算，不能直接证明保留了可迁移能力。\n\n方法：SEAR 将写控制程序、在线行动和自主微调纳入同一框架；用空技能库、同总预算短重启和隐藏初始状态评分分离继承与重采样。跨任务只保留代码技能和文字记忆，自动研究产生的权重不延续。\n\n结果与结论：RoboLab 中，一个模型无库成功率46.9%，继承自身库反而退化，改用其他模型的库则达60.6%。经验质量而非有无经验决定收益；硬件上练习成功也高于新场景表现。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，是否值得持续修改，取决于首次成功时间能否落在短尝试预算内，不能只按任务难度决定。封闭评分仍发现资产文件泄露等漏洞，且模型与工具绑定，跨模型排名并非纯模型能力比较。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"RSI 评测与迁移; 具身持续学习评测; 能力归因","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称用统一框架审计机器人代理是否真正学习及迁移。本文证据：代码策略、在线代理和自主微调三模式，封闭评判、匹配开发时间、空库和分预算重启对照；跨任务继承技能与记忆，而不继承自动研究模式的权重及数据。相对 MC-EvoBench（arxiv:2610.13829）在 Minecraft 隔离状态混淆，本篇扩展到机器人策略、多模拟器和硬件；相对 EmbodiedRSI（arxiv:2610.10498）提出主动实验机制，本篇重点在归因协议。编辑推断：为既有迁移审计提供更广的具体实证，但完整共演化循环仍列为提案。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18484","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18484v2","title":"ReTerm: Recovery Training for Self-Improving Terminal Agents","authors":"Wei Xie; Kaituo Feng; Shiming Fu; Yong Liu; Xiangyu Yue; Shuangjia Zheng","affiliations":"Fudan University；MMLab, The Chinese University of Hong Kong；Shanghai Jiao Tong University","abstract":"Terminal agents have shown strong abilities in complex coding tasks. However, they often struggle to recover from errors during long-running execution (e.g., command errors, faulty implementations), eventually leading to task failures. To this end, we present ReTerm, a self-improving terminal agent trained by learning how to recover from its own failed terminal tasks. To support its training, we construct a customized data pipeline and produce ReTerm-10K, a high-quality dataset that provides effective recovery demonstrations for SFT cold start. Furthermore, we propose ReTerm-GRPO, an online RL algorithm that forks from the agent's own failure states to generate multiple independent self-recovery attempts. By learning from whether these attempts successfully complete the task, the agent self-improves through its own recovery experience. Built on Qwen3.5-9B, our ReTerm-9B achieves 34.8% Pass@1 on Terminal-Bench 2.0, improving over the base model by 14.6 points. Further analysis shows that our method achieves consistently higher recovery rates across diverse error categories compared with standard GRPO training. All code, data and model are released at https://github.com/twothsnd/ReTerm.","tldr":"背景与问题：终端代理执行错误后会改变文件和环境，重新从干净状态训练未必教会它恢复；人工注入的错误又可能偏离当前策略真正会犯的错。\n\n方法：先保存学生失败后的环境快照，让强教师生成经验证的恢复示范。在线训练再从当前策略产生的失败状态分叉多次续做，用最终任务验证结果比较恢复行为；近期失败进入队列，随策略变化刷新训练起点。\n\n结果与结论：Terminal-Bench 2.0 的Pass@1 达34.8%，较基座多14.6个百分点；材料称各错误类别恢复率优于普通GRPO。该总增益同时包含教师示范与强化学习，片段缺少完整消融和成本对照。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，失败不只是负样本，也是可复用的训练初始状态。其价值取决于能否准确恢复环境；这训练的是纠错策略，不代表更新算法自身进化，也不能由恢复旧任务直接推断未见故障泛化。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"失败驱动的递归更新; 自进化策略训练; 终端智能体","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称从代理自身失败状态学习恢复。本文证据：强教师从学生失败快照生成通过验证的冷启动轨迹；在线阶段当前策略从同一失败状态分叉，以任务验证结果训练恢复行为，近期失败队列影响后续学习。相对 CoTrace（arxiv:2610.10426）把失败主要用于 harness 修订、匹配成功轨迹用于训练，本篇直接将失败后的恢复状态作为策略训练分布。编辑推断：是失败驱动训练的具体推进，训练器本身固定；总分增长包含教师 SFT 和在线 RL，不应全部归于分叉机制。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18355","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18355v2","title":"ABot-ER: Unified Embodied Reasoning through Agentic Data-Model Co-Evolution","authors":"Qiuyu Ding; Heng-Da Xu; Changda Xia; Jiajun Shen; Zihao Guan; Zhengchen Yuan; Jianfang Zhang; Di Yang; Jiayi Tian; Yuting Xu; Fei Wang; Shiao Liu; Wei Zhang; Xiaolong Wu; Wenbin Tang; Zedong Chu; Mu Xu","affiliations":"","abstract":"We introduce ABot Embodied Reasoning (ABot-ER), a unified embodied reasoning foundation model that breaks the tension between breadth and depth in embodied reasoning. Embodied intelligence demands the joint mastery of perception, planning, and execution, yet reconciling generality with specialization across this spectrum remains an open challenge. Within a single unified model, ABot-ER commands specialist-level depth across all three competencies, spanning spatial, scene, and temporal reasoning in perception; long-horizon action organization in planning; and point grounding and affordance in execution. The Agentic Data-Model Self-Evolution Engine continuously adapts data strategies to the model's evolving capability state. The Task-Conditioned Adaptive Training Strategy uses task tokens to activate lightweight low-rank residuals over a shared backbone, separating updates from heterogeneous output formats while retaining shared embodied knowledge. Across a systematic evaluation on twelve benchmarks covering three core competencies and five capability dimensions, ABot-ER achieves state-of-the-art overall performance across perception, planning, and execution within a unified parametric framework, demonstrating that breadth and depth can coexist in unified embodied reasoning.","tldr":"背景与问题：具身感知、规划与交互定位进步速度不同，固定数据比例会偏离当前短板；语义和动作空间输出共享参数，还可能互相干扰。\n\n方法：评估结果触发能力诊断，修订监督内容与混合比例，经固定规则筛选后训练并再评估；任务条件残差分担异构输出需求。改变的是语料和权重，数据准入规则及学习算法本身不随轮次学习。\n\n结果与结论：材料称十二个基准的各能力汇总领先；更关键的是，最终语料单次训练能匹敌六轮模型，累计后训练量仅五分之一。历史包含重启、跳过检查点和污染修复，不是一条连续增强链。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，证据更支持发现了可复用的数据配方，而非每轮继承权重不可替代。应分开计算数据清洗、预算扩大和反馈适配的贡献；交互定位得分也不能等同真实机器人运动控制能力。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 模型—数据共演化; 具身 RSI","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称数据—模型共演化缓解能力差异和异构任务干扰。本文证据：能力诊断驱动数据内容及混合比例修订，固定门控筛选，模型训练结果进入下轮；任务条件残差提供输出类型专用容量。相对 SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）用同批交互更新合成器和求解器，本篇没有训练数据修订者；相对 ClawLoop（arxiv:2610.14118），同属诊断驱动任务调整，但面向具身监督数据。编辑推断：最终语料单次训练匹敌多轮结果，支持数据配方价值，不能证明连续权重递归必要性；历史还包含污染修复、重启及分支。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18097","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18097v1","title":"APT: Feedback-Driven Agentic Post-Training for Text-to-Image Generation","authors":"Sirui Zhang; Fangyun Wei; Dong Chen; Jinjing Zhao; Yitong Wang; Yunuo Chen; Baining Guo; Zheng-Jun Zha","affiliations":"University of Science and Technology of China；Microsoft Research Asia；University of Sydney；Fudan University；Shanghai Jiao Tong University","abstract":"Post-training is crucial for improving text-to-image models, yet existing pipelines typically rely on manually curated training data and fixed training distributions. We introduce APT (Agentic Post-Training), a fully automated framework that adaptively post-trains a base model according to its evolving capability profile. APT coordinates three agents to construct evaluation sets from user requirements, diagnose model-specific strengths and failure modes, and generate reinforcement learning data with an adaptive prompt distribution that emphasizes underperforming capabilities. By repeatedly evaluating, diagnosing, and updating the generator, APT lets the current model's behavior shape its next training tasks, forming a feedback loop inspired by recursive self-improvement. For general-purpose settings without user-specified evaluation scenarios, we further develop an evaluation harness that enables broad and diverse evaluation set generation. Experiments across multiple base models, benchmarks, and generation architectures demonstrate that APT is model-agnostic, benchmark-agnostic, architecture-agnostic, and fully automated.","tldr":"背景与问题：不同图像模型的计数、文字和空间关系短板不同，统一人工训练集未必适配；模型变强后，训练优先级也应重新判断。\n\n方法：预先生成固定的提示—评分准则诊断集，用同一视觉语言评估器诊断与给训练奖励。数据代理据当前失败生成下一轮提示，主要针对弱项，也保留其他能力；强化学习更新图像模型后再次诊断。\n\n结果与结论：Lens 上，保留反馈循环的GenEval 为0.859，去掉后为0.844，但OneIG均值持平；只练难项在后者甚至更高。实验支持部分收益，不能据此宣称反馈循环或混合采样在所有指标上必要。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，自适应训练价值应由跨指标权衡检验，而非自动化程度代替证据。诊断与奖励共用评估器，可能共同放大其盲点；这里更新的是生成器和课程，不是诊断者或教学策略本身。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 模型—数据共演化; 诊断反馈闭环","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称让图像生成器的能力变化指导自动后训练。本文证据：固定诊断集、固定视觉语言评估器生成短板反馈，数据代理调整下一轮提示分布，强化学习更新生成器。相对 SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）共同训练合成与求解策略，本篇生成和诊断代理固定；相对 ABot-ER（arxiv:2610.18355）诊断驱动具身监督语料修订，本篇使用模型评分的图像奖励。编辑推断：是自适应课程向图像后训练的扩展，非改进算法递归增强；循环消融收益不一致，同源诊断和奖励的误差校准及抗投机证据不足。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18083","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18083v1","title":"AReaL-RSI: Adaptive Scaling and Coordination of Recursive Self-Improvement","authors":"Wenhao Zhou; Jiajun Song; Haitao Wang; Zipeng Qiu; Yingqi Peng; Ruida Xu; Jiale Li; Wenshuang Li; Shusheng Xu; Wei Dong; Hao Dai; Tongkai Yang; Yi Gao; Binhang Yuan","affiliations":"Ant Group；Zhejiang University；HKUST","abstract":"Scaling recursive self-improvement requires additional computation to produce useful research progress in reaching persistent objectives. Intuitively, more researcher agents can explore more hypotheses, but early evaluation scores might misrepresent their promise, shared findings could lose their applicability conditions, and useful procedures could remain confined to completed investigations. In this paper, we present AReaL-RSI, a framework for organizing a persistent research team of agents without updating backbone LLM weights. We formulate the scaling problem in terms of evaluated outcomes and whole-system resource expenditure. Concretely, a leader agent selects task-appropriate research orientations and guides ongoing investigations; conditional memory sharing distinguishes unresolved problems from supported findings and enables recipient adaptation. During recursive evolution, after each campaign, evidence-based review revises researcher orientation, knowledge, and skills for later campaigns. Experiments compare AReaL-RSI with Codex-Goal on downstream harness optimization, GPU kernel optimization, and AI research tasks using two backbones. Under the reported resource allocations, AReaL-RSI improves Terminal Bench performance by 2.2 percentage points for each backbone and increases mean KernelBench speedup by 32.2-36.8%; further scalability comparisons favor the design of AReaL-RSI over native scaling: combining experience sharing with specialized researcher roles yields 1.9-27.5% lower kernel latency than independent exploration and 1.3-33.9% lower latency than sharing alone across all seven comparable task-backbone pairs.","tldr":"背景与问题：增加研究agent不一定增加有效进展：早期低分可能掩盖好想法，广播未确认诊断会使探索同质化，单次成功也不会自动变成下一次研究的方法。\n\n方法：AReaL-RSI让leader依据实验记录协调持续研究者，共享时保留发现的条件与不确定性，限制未解决问题的主动传播。活动结束后再把证据提炼成研究方向、知识和技能，供后续团队使用；骨干与leader策略不变。\n\n结果与结论：给定资源配置下，相对Codex-Goal，两种骨干的Terminal Bench成绩均增加2.2个百分点；内核实验中，分工加共享优于独立探索和仅共享。主要实验段落缺失，无法完整核对成本与跨活动继承收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键区别是共享有适用条件的证据，而非共享全部历史。正面标签的程序检查只确认来源，不认证结论；harness发布也不要求未来任务增益，因此配置可继承不能直接算作研究程序已变强。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"多智能体工作流演化; 预算受限研究搜索; 经验迁移","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过团队协调、条件式经验共享和跨活动研究者harness修订组织RSI扩展。本文证据表明，实验记录驱动研究方向、知识与技能更新，但leader策略及编排不变；发布检查不要求执行脚本或证明未来收益。相对RSIFlow（arxiv:2610.21791）修改元harness以改善干预编排，本篇主要改变研究者配置与团队内信息传播；相对Hyperagents（arxiv:2603.19461），并未开放修改元级程序。编辑推断：这是协调与经验继承的具体推进，不是协调器自身递归增强；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.17718","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.17718v1","title":"ECG-RSI: Recursive Self-Improvement through Targeted Electrocardiogram Waveform Evolution","authors":"Xiaoliang Wang; Zhuo Chen; Chuanyang Zheng; Jiangwei Lao; Quanbin Wang; Honglin Lin; Jiajia Liu; Zhihong Lu; Hao Jin; Jian Wang; Lijun Wu","affiliations":"","abstract":"Electrocardiogram (ECG) models need supervision that targets evolving weaknesses and remains faithful to waveform evidence. We introduce ECG-RSI, a recursive self-improvement framework combining verified waveform synthesis with feedback-guided intervention search. Signal remeasurement verifies waveform edits; construction errors guide generator repair, while learner errors motivate interventions compared on a separate selection set. Across seven benchmarks, three rounds raise Qwen3.5-35B-A3B's mean question-answering accuracy from 34.57% to 56.04% and mean classification F1 from 24.27 to 34.03. Across the retained trajectory, the preferred supervision shifts from direct reinforcement to confusion-focused contrasts. Continued feedback correction yields diminishing external gains. These results motivate separating error diagnosis from intervention selection and checking whether gains on the feedback set transfer to independent benchmarks.","tldr":"背景与问题：心电模型的弱点会随训练变化，但定向生成波形可能同时改变其他特征，使问题、答案与实际信号不符；只追着反馈错误补数据也可能过拟合。\n\n方法：ECG-RSI先按目标特征编辑训练波形，再复测目标与受保护特征，合格后才生成监督。构造错误用于修补生成规则，学习者错误用于提出不同数据配方；同父模型训练出的分支在独立选择集比较，获选分支进入下一轮。\n\n结果与结论：三轮后，四项问答平均准确率由34.57%升至56.04%；保留路径的监督重心转向易混类别对比，但继续纠错的外部收益递减。可见附录另列一组三种子分数，口径未充分说明，不能与主结果混算。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，错误诊断只能提出干预，不能证明该干预有教学价值。独立选择与外部评测使这一区分可检验；波形复测仍依赖特征提取与问答审查，不能等同临床有效性认证。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 模型—数据共演化; 失败诊断","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称以波形复测和学习者反馈共同驱动数据生成与模型演化。本文证据区分生成错误修补、学习者弱点诊断及独立选择，获选模型与数据进入下一轮；直接强化指增加薄弱类别监督，并非强化学习。相对SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）以作答结果训练合成策略，本篇通过受约束信号编辑、复测和生成规则修补约束监督，并比较同父模型的数据配方。编辑推断：推进在领域证据约束与干预选择分离，不能据此证明生成算法自身持续增强；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.17609","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.17609v1","title":"Verifier-Harness Co-Evolution for Training-Free Self-Improvement on Open-Ended Tasks","authors":"Tianyi Xu; Yaolun Zhang; Yiran Wu; Joe Nguyen; Shengyu Dai; Saba Moeinizade; Zhenwen Shao; Qingyun Wu; Huazheng Wang","affiliations":"Oregon State University；Pennsylvania State University；Johnson & Johnson；AG2 AI","abstract":"Training-free self-improvement lets an agent use feedback to revise the response it is about to return and to update the harness state that shapes how it handles later tasks. On open-ended tasks that feedback rarely comes from reference answers or executable tests, so the agent has to rely on a model-based verifier. When the verifier is wrong, the current response can get worse, and misleading experience can persist across the task stream. A verifier that never changes also grows stale as the agent's responses improve and task demands shift. We introduce Unified Co-Evolution (UCoE), a training-free method that evolves an executable verifier program together with the agent's harness state while all model parameters stay fixed. UCoE synthesizes candidate verifier programs and tests them on response contrasts, pairs of responses that differ in one declared property and have a known preferred side. It selects the candidate whose discrimination on its weakest contrast family is highest, a quantity we call driving capacity. The selected verifier diagnoses one weakness in each draft, guides a single repair, decides which response is served, and determines whether the accepted repair may enter the harness state. As tasks complete, their diagnostics seed new candidate verifiers, which must beat the current verifier on the same contrasts before adoption. Across six open-ended benchmarks, UCoE averages 59.00% preference against matched direct generation with Qwen3-8B and 57.19% with Qwen3.8-27B, margins of 9.00 and 7.19 percentage points. On three verifiable benchmarks, the same method raises the mean from 36.06% for direct generation to 38.48%. Code is available at https://github.com/tianyi0216/Unified-Co-Evolution.","tldr":"背景与问题：开放任务没有答案或可执行测试，错误verifier不仅会把当前回答改坏，还会把误导经验写入后续harness；固定评分标准又可能随任务变化失效。\n\n方法：UCoE构造只破坏一个属性的回答对，选择最弱属性族上辨别力最高的评分程序。该程序指导局部修补、选择交付回答并控制经验写入；完成任务的诊断再提出新程序，经对比测试后替换旧版，所有模型参数固定。\n\n结果与结论：六个开放基准上，两种骨干相对匹配直接生成的平均偏好率为59.00%和57.19%。可见引言明确称多数收益来自当前任务修补，不能把总体优势全部归于跨任务共演化。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，评分器应按能否辨别关键退化来选，而非只看平均准确率。但合成退化的偏好方向不等于自然修订的真实优劣；重复使用对比集也留下选择过拟合风险，理论不覆盖任意开放任务。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"评估器递归改进; Harness 递归演化; 无真值反馈","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称在固定模型参数下共同演化可执行verifier与harness状态。本文证据显示，反馈来自固定模型评分及单属性退化构造的回答对；任务诊断产生新评分程序，程序又控制回答与经验准入。相对RHO（arxiv:2606.05922）使用自偏好选harness，本篇把评分准则与聚合程序纳入更新，并以最弱对比族表现门控。编辑推断：这是反馈机制可测试化的推进，但诊断程序和底层模型未演化，主要收益来自当题修补；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.17114","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.17114v1","title":"D-World: An Explicit World-Language-Action Model with Recursive Self-Improvement under Dual Control","authors":"Xuan Wen; Baichao Wang","affiliations":"Geek+","abstract":"Frontier large language models (LLMs) now reason about space well enough to program robots, yet the world models behind robot policies are implicit, held in network weights or predicted video, and cannot be inspected or corrected directly. We present D-World, an explicit world-language-action model built on the Sense, Plan and Act decomposition. A perception agent writes the scene as an executable digital twin using generated vision and geometry code. A planning agent searches for actions in simulation and, after each executed action chunk, revises the twin's object states and named physical parameters against what the robot measured. A parameter revision is accepted only if replaying the latest chunk does not increase any measured residual beyond its tolerance, and every chunk is checked in the updated twin before it runs. Structural mismatches return to perception for reconstruction. We call this measurement-grounded cycle of correction and revision recursive self-improvement (RSI), in which the LLM stays frozen while the world it acts in improves. We model the choice of actions that both advance the task and expose model error as a dual control problem and show that the cost of incorporating evidence into the twin sets the threshold at which probing pays, so cheap local revision counteracts the turn-off of cautious controllers. Each episode runs a real-to-sim-to-real loop, and its recorded twins can be refitted and re-rendered offline into higher-fidelity environments for post-training. Because perception and planning communicate only through the twin and language, either can be replaced by a learned model, and since inference dominates the loop, the loop speeds up with faster models. On a dual-arm robot, towel and toaster tasks show local revisions, such as one reducing the bread's rendered-depth residual from 22.4 to 1.5 mm, that let execution continue without reconstruction.","tldr":"背景与问题：隐式机器人世界模型预测出错时，难把偏差定位到可修正量；每次重建场景又很昂贵，过度谨慎还会阻止获得辨识模型所需的接触证据。\n\n方法：D-World让冻结LLM编写可执行数字孪生，用实机执行后的测量修订对象状态和物理参数。参数修改须在最新动作段回放中不显著恶化已测残差，下一段动作再经更新后的仿真检查；结构错误则触发重建。\n\n结果与结论：双臂机器人的毛巾与烤面包任务展示局部修订后继续执行，其中面包深度残差由22.4降至1.5毫米。材料没有提供完整成功率、重建成本和受控消融，案例不能证明普遍收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可编辑参数使误差成为行动依据，但本质仍含系统辨识。门控只约束最新可测证据，早期残差不否决更新，仿真通过也不认证实机安全；离线后训练用途尚不能算已验证闭环。","published_at":"2026-10-12","topics":"世界模型与递归改进; 预测误差反馈; 具身 RSI","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称用物理测量修订显式数字孪生，实现回合内RSI。本文证据显示改变的是对象状态与物理参数，反馈是实机测量残差，更新后的孪生影响下一段规划；LLM与修订规则不变。相对Memento 3（arxiv:2610.11794）的规则—代码及历史转移回放，本篇采用真实机器人测量、局部参数修订和最新动作段非回归门控。编辑推断：这是显式世界模型适配的具身扩展，核心参数更新也属于系统辨识，不是改进器递归优化；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.16523","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.16523v1","title":"EAU: Environment-Agent-User Co-evolution for Training User-Centric Agents","authors":"Min Cai; Dan Zhang; Gao Xing; Libin Ma; Zhaohui Xu; Xi Ye","affiliations":"University of Alberta；National University of Singapore；Kuaishou Technology；Independent Researcher；Alberta Machine Intelligence Institute (Amii)","abstract":"Training LLM agents to interact with users over multiple turns is challenging because the learning signal depends not only on the agent, but also on the user simulator and environment, which jointly shape the agent's experience. Simulated users can be stochastic or inconsistent, while environments may contain unreliable tools, incomplete state coverage, and incorrect verifiers. Prior work mainly addresses the resulting instability through reward shaping or denser supervision, while treating these components as fixed. We instead introduce EAU, a meta-agent framework for environment--agent--user co-evolution. During training, EAU monitors trajectories, tool traces, rewards, and training statistics; diagnoses failures and uninformative interactions; and proposes targeted modifications to the user simulator, environment, reward design, and RL configuration. Validated changes are hot-swapped into the ongoing run, allowing the training setup to evolve together with the policy. These adaptations also persist across runs, so later training can build on previously discovered improvements rather than restarting from a fixed setup. We enable this process through an editable symbolic representation of user and environment dynamics, while the agent remains a neural LLM optimized with RL. Across three interactive-agent benchmarks and two backbone models, EAU consistently outperforms prior RL methods, improving the overall score over the strongest baseline by 14.7--15.0% and increasing successful task completion on ColBench by up to 36.7%, showing that co-evolving the training system with the policy can substantially improve multi-turn RL.","tldr":"背景与问题：多轮用户互动的坏训练信号未必来自策略：模拟用户可能泄露信息，工具或验证器可能出错。只做奖励塑形，无法修复产生这些轨迹的上游过程。\n\n方法：EAU让元agent读取训练轨迹与统计，诊断问题后修改用户规则、交互条件、奖励或训练配置；通过有限完整性检查的变更可在训练中热替换。策略继续按固定RL算法学习，已发现的干预经验跨运行保存。\n\n结果与结论：摘要在三个基准、两种骨干上给出相对最强基线14.7%—15.0%的总体增益。主要结果表被截断；附录说明不少基线来自既有报告，而PPO与EAU自行评测，因此并非全部统一重跑。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，把故障归因到训练系统而非一律归因策略，是有价值的改动。但运行内修补、奖励变化与超参数调整混合发生，需要核对各自增益和总预算；环境可编辑不等于元优化机制也在变强。","published_at":"2026-10-12","topics":"失败驱动的递归更新; 自适应过程奖励; 长程交互学习","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称让用户模拟器、环境和策略共同演化。本文证据显示，元agent依训练日志及轨迹修改符号用户规则、奖励和可调配置，策略通过固定RL算法更新，干预经验跨运行保留。相对RewardWeaver（arxiv:2610.10120）调整固定语义过程奖励的分配，本篇扩展到上游交互生成条件，并支持运行内热替换。编辑推断：贡献在在线训练系统干预，不应将程序化环境适配表述为三个模型共同学习，也未证明元agent或训练算法递归增强；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.16491","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.16491v1","title":"Drafting Agents, Not Just Tokens: Speculative Recursive Self-Improvement for Agentic Systems","authors":"Xin Xu; Ke Cheng; Hao Wang; Yangru Huang; Yanghao Xiao; Zhichao Chen; Zhisheng Zhong; Xun Liu; Yi Li; Qian Li; Haibin Lv; Jun Zhang; Jie Jiang; Zhouchen Lin","affiliations":"","abstract":"Improving an agent through successive revisions requires balancing exploration and evaluation under a limited budget. A narrow search can miss useful sequences of edits, while fully evaluating every intermediate version can exhaust the budget before those sequences yield a verified improvement. We introduce Speculative Recursive Self-Improvement (SpecRSI), which drafts executable successor agents before their predecessors are fully evaluated, while requiring complete verification before adoption. Verification-Aware Tree Search (VATS) allocates the budget between further edits and outstanding checks using the predicted verified return of a continuation. Group Verification Optimization (GVO) learns the improver from completed searches while keeping the real evaluator fixed. In the main scientific comparison, terminal gains exceed Janus by 33.3%--40.0%. Additional evaluations show that SpecRSI outperforms Janus in all 50 scientific backbone--task pairs and exceeds MetaRSI-v1 by 1.85%--2.38% in macro-average system score across twenty backbones. Coding-validation success reaches 69.4% versus HGM's 64.3% at a 20.8% lower target-cost index.","tldr":"背景与问题：每改一版就完整评估，会把预算耗在尚未产生价值的中间状态；只预测当前候选质量，又忽略它还需多少编辑和检查才能成为可采用改进。\n\n方法：SpecRSI允许从未完成评估的版本继续起草，但采用前必须取得完整真实检查。搜索根据后续编辑与验证的预期净收益分配预算；外层用整次搜索的已验证收益减全部成本，训练下一轮改进者，真实评估合同不变。\n\n结果与结论：摘要给出编码验证成功率69.4%，对照HGM为64.3%，目标成本指标也下降；但可见图注另显示，相对MetaRSI-v1，目标成本更低时总成本指标略高，不能概括为全面省算力。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，改进者应学习哪些尚未成功的编辑值得继续验证，而非只模仿成功补丁。完整搜索信用回应了这一点；预测器仍可能浪费不可追回的预算，且固定外层算法不意味着改进过程无限自举。","published_at":"2026-10-12","topics":"预算受限研究搜索; 自进化策略训练; Harness 递归演化","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过先起草后验证与完整搜索反馈训练改进者，提高预算内可验证收益。本文证据区分候选执行检查和预测净收益的评分器：只有前者产生准入证据，完整搜索的收益及全部成本训练起草、调度与评分组件。相对Evo²（arxiv:2610.13025）用编辑及反思的局部执行收益训练改进者，本篇将后续编辑、互补检查及整次搜索成本纳入信用；相对EvoX（arxiv:2602.23413）演化搜索策略，本篇具体学习编辑—验证调度。编辑推断：推进明确，但外层更新规则固定，不能称无限层级递归；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.16078","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.16078v1","title":"Heterogeneous Agentic Coevolution","authors":"Wenqian Ye; Ziwei Guan; Zi Yang; Shivani Modi; Cici Cong Wu; Yunlong He; Yuxin Chen; Zhengyu Zhang; Liang Luo; Venkatesh Ranganathan; Jianhui Sun; Yantao Yao; Wenlin Chen; Buyun Zhang; Ellie Dingqiao Wen; Henry Kautz; Aidong Zhang","affiliations":"Meta AI；University of Virginia","abstract":"Recent advances in self-improving LLM agents have demonstrated the potential of AI systems that drive their own intelligence. However, many domain-specific applications rely on specialized foundation models that possess strong domain expertise but remain dependent on human-designed improvements. Extending recursive self-improvement to these models presents a key challenge: as a specialist improves, the strategies used to advance it must also adapt. To address this challenge, we propose Heterogeneous Agentic CoEvolution (HACE), a framework that jointly evolves specialized foundation models and LLM agents through reciprocal learning. HACE improves the specialist through supervised learning while training the agent with on-policy reinforced self-training, guided by verified performance gains on the current specialist. The agent's exploration, in turn, informs subsequent specialist training, enabling both models to adapt to each other's progress. To sustain this reciprocal learning, HACE further employs evolutionary search to optimize their interaction harness, adapting how the models exchange information and select training experiences as their capabilities evolve. We evaluate HACE across three challenging domains: recommendation systems, protein function prediction in biology, and crystal stability prediction in material discovery. We show that HACE outperforms the evaluated self-improving methods on the primary task metrics across all three domains. These results shed light on heterogeneous coevolution as a universal approach to improving specialized foundation models through reciprocal interaction with a learning agent.","tldr":"背景与问题：领域专家继续监督训练已达平台时，通用agent仍可能在部分实例上提供帮助；但专家变强后，旧agent策略与交互方式可能不再提供增量。\n\n方法：HACE用任务标签检验agent是否在当前实例上优于专家，探索结果决定专家重点训练哪些样本，专家仍学原始标签。候选专家与harness联合比较后，再收集相对保留专家有正贡献的新回答训练agent，改变下一轮可用贡献。\n\n结果与结论：材料称在推荐、蛋白功能和晶体稳定性预测中优于所比较自改进方法，起点为已收敛专家。主要结果表缺失；蛋白任务实际只更新预测头，不能统称所有领域基础模型权重均被改进。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，平均更弱的agent也可能凭局部互补性帮助专家，关键是验证哪些实例值得投入。这里监督来自原始标签而非纯自生知识；总体联合得分还需拆分专家、agent与harness各自的独立贡献。","published_at":"2026-10-12","topics":"模型—harness 共演化; 自进化策略训练; 模型—数据共演化","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称联合演化领域专家、LLM agent与交互harness。本文证据显示，原始标签验证agent相对当前专家的贡献，探索结果选择专家训练实例，保留专家—harness组合后重新收集正贡献回答训练agent。相对Co-Harness（arxiv:2607.22688）用改进harness产生轨迹训练agent，本篇另加入异构领域专家及双向经验选择；相对SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）合成器—求解器共训练，本篇不是造新任务，而是在有标签池中重分配训练。编辑推断：异构互惠学习有具体机制，但仍依赖外部标签，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15964","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.15964v1","title":"Small but Mighty: Test Suites as Improvement Signals for Self-Evolving Agents","authors":"Yutong Cheng; Wei Cheng; Wenchao Yu; Dawei Zhou; Haifeng Chen","affiliations":"Virginia Tech；NEC Laboratories America","abstract":"A self-evolving agent rewrites its own harness and must decide which rewrites to keep, so its improvement signal is the check a rewrite has to pass. Verifying a rewrite by agent rollout is expensive and subjective, while executable checks such as the repository's own tests are too sparse to catch behavior-changing rewrites, rejecting only a quarter of them. We instead take test feedback as the executable signal, and search for test suites that are both small and strong with a quality-diversity evolutionary algorithm, so that the signal is dense and informative. TeSearch treats suite size as a behavior descriptor, so that quality is pursued at every size and a small, strong suite is reachable, and learns a transition kernel during the search that denoises the LLM as an actuator on that descriptor. Across 129 real-world modules and three backbones, TeSearch delivers the highest-quality suites of any method compared, LLM-driven evolutionary search included, and the smallest of any LLM-based one. Used as the improvement signal of a self-evolving agent, it rejects 59.9% of behavior-changing rewrites against 25.3% for the repository's tests, at a 4.0% false-alarm rate and 3.5 s per decision. The code and data are available at https://github.com/ccsnow127/TeSearch.","tldr":"背景与问题：agent重写harness后，端到端rollout昂贵，原仓库测试又漏掉大量行为变化；更大的生成测试集虽可能更强，却会增加每次准入成本。\n\n方法：TeSearch按测试集大小分区竞争，在每种规模内优化覆盖与变异检测，避免小而强的候选被大集合挤掉；实际生成数量反过来校准搜索。得到的测试集作为harness改写的可执行回归门控。\n\n结果与结论：在mini-swe-agent的470个核验改写上，行为变化拒绝率为59.9%，仓库测试为25.3%；代价是误拒部分等价改写。这里测的是构造改写的行为保持，不是多轮自改进后的任务成功率。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，回归检查是保住已有能力的护栏，不是改进价值本身。若目标本就需要改变行为，强制保持旧实现还可能阻止好更新；后续应把保持合同与允许变化的功能目标分开测试。","published_at":"2026-10-11","topics":"评估器递归改进; 验证理论; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称优化自演化agent的可执行改写信号。本文证据是按覆盖率与变异杀伤率搜索小测试集，再对人工核验标签的harness改写做准入评测，反馈来自执行而非模型偏好。相对Self-Harness（arxiv:2606.09498）用既定回归测试筛编辑，本篇优化测试本身；相对UCoE（arxiv:2610.17609）在线演化模型评分程序，本篇交付固定测试集，没有展示测试随agent长期共演化。编辑推断：这是回归门控质量的推进，不是已证明的任务收益或递归链；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15772","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.15772v1","title":"RSIPO: Recursive Self-Improving Policy Optimization for Agentic Reinforcement Learning via Skill-Policy Co-Evolution","authors":"Fan Zhang; Hao Wu; Jinyang Wu; Hongyu Qu; Zheng Lian; Xiao Luo; Yefeng Zheng; Bo Zhang; Haoxuan Li; Pheng-Ann Heng","affiliations":"THU；NUS；Tongji University；UW-Madison；Westlake University；CUHK；Shanghai AI Laboratory；PKU","abstract":"Recent focus in agentic reinforcement learning (RL) seeks to improve credit assignment in long-horizon tasks. One promising direction combines reinforcement learning with verifiable rewards (RLVR) and on-policy self-distillation (OPSD), integrating trajectory-level advantages with dense token-level supervision. This line of work often conditions a teacher model on privileged context, such as agentic skills, to score tokens generated by the student policy. Despite their progress, they largely overlook the on-policy evolution of agentic skills and the reliability of teacher supervision. Towards this end, we introduce Recursive Self-Improving Policy Optimization (RSIPO), a self-evolving agentic RL framework that enables agentic skills and the policy model to co-evolve throughout the training process. Specifically, RSIPO enables the policy itself to extract skills from completed trajectories and explicitly optimizes its skill-generation capability through trajectory replay. It further employs empirical Bayes shrinkage to dynamically calibrate the student's trust in teacher scores, accounting for the fact that skill-enhanced teacher guidance can sometimes be less reliable. Experiments with Qwen-family models on embodied interaction and search-based agentic tasks demonstrate that RSIPO outperforms all the compared baseline approaches. With Qwen2.5-7B as the base model, RSIPO achieves an average success rate of 98.6\\% on ALFWorld, yielding absolute improvements of 2.5\\% and 17.4\\% over the second-best baseline and standard GRPO, respectively.","tldr":"背景与问题：固定技能库或离线技能生成器会落后于训练中的策略；给教师增加技能也不保证它比学生可靠，统一蒸馏可能强化错误指导。\n\n方法：RSIPO让当前策略从自身轨迹写技能，在同起点回放中与随机留出的无技能轨迹比较执行收益。收益奖励技能生成，噪声校准后的收益则调节学生对技能教师的信任；更新策略再产生下一批轨迹，测试不提供技能。\n\n结果与结论：Qwen2.5-7B在ALFWorld成功率为98.6%，比次优基线高2.5个百分点。但附录显示3B模型在搜索任务只排第二，不能照摘要推广为所有配置均领先；完整成本和消融表未见。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，技能相关不等于具有教学价值，实际回放比教师自信更合适。收益来自同任务重放，还需防止答案泄漏与起点不一致；初始化也使用外部LLM技能监督，不能称全程无教师。","published_at":"2026-10-11","topics":"技能蒸馏; 自进化策略训练; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称以技能—策略共演化及教师信任校准改进agentic RL。本文证据以同起点技能回放相对随机控制组的执行收益奖励技能生成，并对噪声收益收缩后调整蒸馏权重；策略更新又改变后续技能。相对SGUID（arxiv:2610.12367）筛选持续有效的技能蒸馏信号，本篇直接训练技能生成行为并动态校准教师；相对MetaExp（arxiv:2610.21492），本篇技能用于训练期监督，测试不提供技能。编辑推断：教学价值进入生成目标是具体推进，但回放衡量同任务帮助，跨任务技能价值未直接认证；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15708","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.15708v1","title":"SpecForge: Recursive Self-Improvement for Coding Agents via Behavioral Specifications","authors":"Yutong Cheng; Haifeng Chen; Peng Gao; Wei Cheng","affiliations":"Virginia Tech；NEC Laboratories America","abstract":"Coding agents based on frozen language models can improve their performance by refining the external context they rely on, without updating model weights. We study recursive self-improvement through behavioral specifications: natural-language code documentation that describes the behavior of program entities and guides agents in generating correct code. We formulate a self-improvement loop in which an agent generates code from its current specifications, evaluates it with execution-verified tests, and refines the specifications based on observed failures. The improved specifications then guide subsequent generation, progressively improving the agent's understanding of the codebase. However, recursive refinement is challenging because program entities are interdependent. Improving the specification of one entity can inadvertently degrade the correctness of others, a phenomenon we call output coupling. This creates a whack-a-mole effect in which local improvements cause regressions elsewhere, preventing consistent progress. We introduce SpecForge, a multi-frontier tree search framework that addresses this challenge with three mechanisms: (i) Pareto-guided state selection preserves complementary specification states and prevents premature commitment; (ii) dependency-constrained entity selection prioritizes callee-before-caller refinement; and (iii) error-diversified expansion explores multiple refinements using different subsets of test failures. On DevEval+, SpecForge achieves the best performance across five backbone models, including a 94.9% solve rate with Claude-4.5-Sonnet and a 5.7-percentage-point average improvement over the strongest baseline. The improved specifications also make the agent better at tasks outside the loop: they transfer to cross-language translation and to new-feature implementation, where they outperform the benchmark-provided requirement documents.","tldr":"背景与问题：代码实体相互依赖，修好一个函数的规格可能改变整个模块生成，使其他函数退化；沿单条修订路径容易反复丢失已有成果。\n\n方法：SpecForge用从规格重建代码后的测试失败修改行为描述，而非直接积累代码补丁。搜索保留各实体上互有优势的规格状态，并优先修订被调用者，减少依赖错误造成的误导；新状态重新生成和测试整个模块。\n\n结果与结论：摘要给出五种骨干上平均比最强基线高5.7个百分点，并称规格可迁移到跨语言翻译和新功能实现。主要实验段落未提供，尚不能核对迁移效果量及完整预算。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，外部知识的质量可用其能否支持行为重建衡量，而非文档相似度。不过测试来自已有参考实现，验证的是捕捉现有行为；这不自动证明新需求正确性，也不证明搜索器自身越来越会优化。","published_at":"2026-10-11","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 执行证据驱动改进; 跨任务迁移","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过行为规格的递归修订改善编码agent。本文证据显示，参考实现生成并执行验证的测试评价从规格重建的代码，失败修订规格，保留规格状态影响下一轮；模型和搜索规则固定。相对Self-Harness（arxiv:2606.09498）直接改运行harness，本篇改代码库行为知识；相对TeSearch（arxiv:2610.15964）优化测试信号，本篇把测试作为既定反馈，并处理规格间依赖和生成干扰。编辑推断：这是外部知识优化的结构化推进，不代表模型参数中的能力或优化器递归增强；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15244","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.15244v1","title":"EvolvAttack: Backdooring self Evolving VLM Agents","authors":"Chuan Zou; Yang Xiang; Zexin Li; Xiaonan Luo; Simin Chen","affiliations":"University of Pennsylvania；Brown University；Nanyang Technological University；University of Notre Dame；George Mason University","abstract":"Self-evolving mechanisms let vision-language model (VLM) agents continually adapt through evolving memory, but they also allow malicious behavior to emerge only after deployment. We introduce a new attack surface, the self-evolving backdoor, whose payload stays dormant in the initial agent and is progressively activated as the agent evolves. Unlike conventional backdoors, which can be exposed by testing triggered inputs on a static model, our attack requires both a visual trigger and a sufficiently evolved memory state; static scanning with clean memory thus yields near-zero attack success and may deem the agent benign. We realize this through memory-aware backdoor training, which couples trigger activation with the agent's evolving memory while preserving benign behavior unless the trigger co-occurs with payload-related memory. Across three VLM backbones, four agent pipelines, and recency-, semantic-, and reward-based memory evolution, the attack preserves normal functionality and stays nearly inactive before evolution (0.5% attack success rate), yet exceeds 95% attack success within 100 interactions, revealing a stealthy threat unique to self-evolving agents.","tldr":"背景与问题：只在初始记忆下扫描视觉触发器，可能漏掉依赖后续经验状态才激活的后门；部署时权重不变也不保证行为安全不变。\n\n方法：EvolvAttack通过部署前投毒训练预置联合条件：触发图像与载荷相关记忆同时存在才稳定输出恶意行为。早期罕见输出被正常记忆机制写回，后续检索再提高激活机会，形成放大；攻击者部署后不直接修改记忆或权重。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称攻击成功率从演化前0.5%升至百次交互内超过95%。但可见消融中，补充空记忆训练覆盖会降低攻击效果，说明静态隐蔽性与动态强度受具体训练覆盖影响。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，安全审计对象应是带写回的交互轨迹，而非单个权重快照。这是预植后门借记忆放大的证据，不能表述为普通经验学习自然生成恶意；真实部署风险还取决于触发暴露与记忆准入。","published_at":"2026-10-11","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; 外部记忆与规则更新; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称发现依赖演化记忆的延迟视觉后门。本文证据显示，部署前投毒训练预置视觉触发器与载荷记忆的联合激活，部署后标准写回和检索放大罕见载荷输出；并非正常自改进凭空产生恶意目标。相对STRATA（arxiv:2610.19386）研究无攻击情况下的经验负迁移，本篇展示被预植机制利用的记忆反馈放大。编辑推断：这是自演化安全审计的重要补充，但corpus缺少相关后门工作的充分原始材料，不能核验作者的首次主张；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15084","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.15084v1","title":"Self-Evolving Visual Agent via Margin Reward","authors":"Wenxi Yang; Yuzhong Zhao; Baochang Zhang; Yunfan Liu; Qixiang Ye","affiliations":"中国科学院大学；微软亚洲研究院；北京航空航天大学","abstract":"Visual agents that interleave reasoning with tool invocation have posed a promising direction for multimodal tasks. However, learning effective tool invocation usually relies on curated question-answer pairs or expert demonstrations at scale, which are expensive to acquire. In this study, we propose Marvo, a simple-yet-effective self-evolution approach that enables learning tool invocation from unlabeled images. Marvo consists of two agents: (1) a challenger that generates question-answer pairs from unlabeled images, and (2) a solver that learns tool invocation by solving questions through reinforcement learning. To encourage effective tool invocation, a good training question should be difficult enough to warrant tool use, yet remain within the solver's capabilities. To this end, we introduce a margin reward to the challenger, defined as solver's performance difference with and without access to tools. With the margin reward, we create an adaptive curriculum that encourages the solver to learn effective tool invocation. Across benchmarks covering agentic reasoning, visual search, mathematical, and general real-world reasoning, Marvo improves average accuracy by up to 7.1\\% --- demonstrating margin reward as a preferred way to scale question complexity without human supervision.","tldr":"背景与问题：视觉工具调用训练常依赖昂贵的标注问答或专家演示；仅按不确定性出题，也不能保证工具确实有用。方法：challenger 从无标注图像造题，solver 通过强化学习作答；solver 有无工具时的表现差作为出题反馈，使课程追踪工具的实际边际收益。结果与结论：作者报告覆盖 11,691 题的多基准评估中，Qwen2.5-VL-7B 平均准确率提高 7.1%；所给全文片段还报告八轮扩展中题目质量与表现后期下降。Insights：这提示课程信号应对准待学能力的边际贡献，而不是难度本身；依据是工具增益奖励及后期标签质量同步下滑。结论限于所测视觉任务，作者实验未经独立复现。","published_at":"2026-10-10","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 工具调用学习; 强化学习自改进","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称以 solver 有无工具时的表现差，训练 challenger 生成值得调用工具且可解的问题；反馈经 challenger 生成题目进入 solver 强化学习，构成数据—模型闭环。本文证据包括多基准作者实验，并在所给全文片段中报告与 R-Zero 的匹配轮次比较；差异是以工具边际效用而非单纯不确定性指导出题。材料未支持领域级优先性，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14843","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14843v1","title":"Pre-Registered Genesis Accounting for Recursive Self-Improvement: First Audited Operator-Genesis Events in a Physics-Discovery Runtime","authors":"Wenbin Mao; Pei Zou","affiliations":"HoomanBio AI Lab；Huaman Biotechnology（北京）有限公司","abstract":"Claims of recursive self-improvement are easy to make and hard to falsify: did improvement come from re-using designer-provided mechanisms, or from mechanisms the system authored itself? We introduce a pre-registered, two-tier accounting: M1 counts machine-generated content instances within a designer-provided vocabulary, while M2 counts machine-authored mechanism types (new operators registered into the runtime's own vocabulary, with a held-out-validation certificate). We report the first audited M2 genesis events. In the primary event, depth-limited compositional search over elementary operators, judged by held-out R^2 on real NIST hydrogen Balmer measurements, produced the operator sq(inv(n)) = 1/n^2 -- the Rydberg-level form -- which no standard-library transform could express (held-out R^2: -0.546 best standard transform vs. 1.0000000 composed). A protocol flaw (independent variable built by inverting the very law under test) was caught in audit and repaired via an independent-label protocol; extrapolation to unseen levels (n=8,9 trained on n\u003c=7) attains relative error ~10^-6, four to six orders beyond the best standard operator. A second event independently recovered sqrt(inv(a)) -- Kepler's velocity law -- from JPL ephemeris vectors. Also incorporated: an audited compounding channel (first domain-level measurement: 1.109x accuracy ratio on a real held-out domain) and blind, decurated genesis exams whose honest tally is zero. The Kepler event passes line audit; the hydrogen gap reproduces on He II; the certificate is threshold-stable. Against eleven prior systems, the contribution is the measurement and governance of machine-authored mechanisms, not the search algorithm or rediscovered physics. Limitations: exams were curated by agents who knew the textbook answer, triggers manual, grammar observer-injected; both events demonstrate capability to author, not yet autonomous genesis.","tldr":"背景与问题：性能提升可能来自复用设计者提供的机制，也可能来自系统写出新机制；若不区分来源，RSI 声称难以证伪。方法：预注册区分机制实例与新算子，要求候选通过留出数据证书后才登记，并进入可复用注册表。结果与结论：作者报告氢谱与开普勒两次算子生成；氢谱协议修复循环性漏洞后，未见能级外推相对误差约为 10⁻⁶。盲选考试至今为零，事件触发仍需人工。Insights：这提示 RSI 应分别记录机制来源、验证与复用；依据是协议审计和诚实报告的零 tally。边界明确：结果支持受限语法下的机制生成能力，不证明系统能自主启动或持续进化。","published_at":"2026-10-10","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; 机制生成与记账; 科学发现","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称贡献是预注册 M1/M2 记账、机制必要性证书和持久注册表，而非新搜索算法或新物理定律；机制候选经留出数据验证后登记，并可供后续发现复用。本文证据包括氢谱与开普勒算子事件、协议循环性漏洞的审计修复和有限复合测量；盲选考试 tally 为零。作者将工作与十一种既有系统定位比较，但其排他性主张受检索覆盖限制。编辑判断：这是治理和测量提案，尚非自主递归改进证据；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14828","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14828v1","title":"EvoCowork: A Benchmark for Real-World Office Tasks","authors":"Zhou Liu; Xingyan Chen; ZhaoYang Han; Zewei Pan; Zeli Su; Ningxin Pan; Xue Hu; Kaixiong Ting; Wentao Zhang","affiliations":"北京大学；中山大学；上海交通大学；中央民族大学；北京航空航天大学；中国科学技术大学","abstract":"Office workflows are a demanding testbed for self-improving agents because their deliverables must be correct, natively editable, and mutually consistent. A central question is whether gains on feedback tasks reflect reusable procedures rather than task-specific fixes. We introduce EvoCowork, a 240-task benchmark for evaluating harness-level recursive self-improvement across four office modalities, with model weights held fixed. The benchmark covers presentations, documents, spreadsheets, and cross-office workflows, and scores submitted artifacts for content, native structure, formulas, cross-file consistency, and visual quality where needed. Its protocol separates feedback, revision selection, and final testing: methods learn from single-modality tasks, then are evaluated on unseen single-modality tasks and cross-office workflows under a shared initial harness and explicit budgets. In static evaluations of two models and four harnesses, the best configuration scores 42.25 overall and 30.62 on cross-office tasks. Starting from the same MSA harness with GLM 5.3, ACE and AHE improve in-domain scores by 4.90 and 2.64 points, respectively, but change cross-office scores by only +0.03 and -1.72. Thus, gains on the file types that provide feedback do not necessarily transfer to coordinated workflows. EvoCowork makes this distinction explicit while recording the capability, transfer, and cost of harness evolution. Code and task packages: https://github.com/DeepThinkingZhouLiu/cowork-evolution-benchmark.","tldr":"背景与问题：办公工作流要求文档、表格和演示文件既正确、可编辑又彼此一致；单一文件类型上的修补成功，不代表形成可复用流程。方法：构建四类办公任务基准，对产物内容、原生结构、公式和跨文件一致性评分，并将反馈集、选择集与最终测试分离，控制初始 harness 与预算。结果与结论：在 GLM 5.3 与共同初始 harness 下，ACE/AHE 域内分别提高 4.90/2.64 分，跨办公任务却只变化 +0.03/-1.72 分。作者据此指出，域内收益不保证协调工作流迁移。Insights：这提示迁移目标应直接进入 RSI 测试，而不能用总体分数替代；依据是单模态与跨文件结果分化。边界是离线办公产物、有限配置及有限方法运行。","published_at":"2026-10-10","topics":"Harness 演化评测; 跨任务迁移; 办公智能体","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者提出 240 任务办公基准，评分覆盖原生文件结构、内容与跨文件一致性，并将反馈、修订选择和最终测试分开。本文证据显示 ACE/AHE 域内增益没有转为跨办公增益。与 AHE（arxiv:2604.25850）的关系是评测补充：该基准直接测试单模态反馈向跨文件工作流的迁移，而非提出新的演化机制；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14730","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14730v1","title":"Self-improving data synthesis can scale embedding models across domains and tasks","authors":"Zucan Lyu; Rui Tang; Jianlyu Chen; Peisheng Jin; Zheng Liu; Defu Lian","affiliations":"中国科学技术大学；认知智能全国重点实验室","abstract":"Adapting embedding models to new tasks requires training data that reflect task-specific information needs and relevance criteria. However, manual data design is costly and difficult to scale. Here we introduce SYNTRA, a novel retrieval data synthesis method whose self-improvement loop iteratively refines reusable synthesis instructions using feedback on trial outputs. This process requires only an unlabelled corpus and a few relevant query-document pairs. Experiments across 24 retrieval datasets spanning 15 domains demonstrate the effectiveness of the synthesized data. These data also improve widely used, strong embedding models on tasks with and without existing labelled training sets. Self-improvement enhances retrieval on all six evaluated tasks, outperforming human calibration on four. Moreover, retrieval performance continues to improve on MS MARCO as we scale the training dataset to 32 times its initial size. Overall, with minimal human intervention, SYNTRA enables scalable adaptation of embedding models across domains and tasks.","tldr":"背景与问题：检索嵌入需要训练数据符合具体领域和相关性标准；人工设计查询、标签与合成指令难以随任务扩展。方法：系统从少量相关查询—文档示例推断任务要求，在小样本试产出上获取诊断反馈并修订共享合成指令，再用改进后的指令大规模生成数据。结果与结论：作者报告覆盖 24 个检索集、15 个领域；六项任务的自改进均提升训练数据效果，其中四项超过人工校准，MS MARCO 数据扩至初始规模 32 倍时性能仍提升。Insights：这提示递归改进对象也可以是产生训练经验的规则，而不只是模型参数；依据是指令修订与下游检索结果相联系。材料未提供独立复现，少量示例依赖、标签质量与长程闭环稳定性仍待验证。","published_at":"2026-10-10","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 检索模型适配; 反馈驱动更新","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称根据试产出反馈迭代修订可复用的数据合成指令，再批量生成检索训练数据。本文证据为 24 个数据集、15 个领域的作者实验及六项任务上的自改进比较。与 SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）都使训练经验适应学习者，但 SYNTRA 改写合成指令并训练嵌入模型，SynCo 联合优化合成器与推理器；二者未直接比较。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14625","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14625v1","title":"From Existing Methods to New Research Ideas: Two Perspectives on Recursive Self-Improvement","authors":"Leijun Zhou; Yanke Yu; Zhihao Liu; Qu Xiang; Tiancheng Hu; Yiru Dong; Yihan Wu; Yangxi Xiang; Xuejun Wu; Xi Chen; Buyue Qian; Yaowei Zheng; Junhao Hu","affiliations":"PrismShadow；北京大学；浙江大学；纽约大学","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement (RSI) offers a route to AI systems that participate in their own continued development. Recent methods allow language agents to retain changes to their parameters, memory, skills, and code for subsequent execution and improvement. We examine how these methods can inform new research ideas through two complementary perspectives. First, we introduce a unified taxonomy with nine design dimensions organized into four groups: update targets, update organization, update schedule and scope, feedback and selection. This taxonomy places existing methods in a shared design space, where examining individual dimensions and their interactions can inspire new research ideas. Second, we examine how existing RSI methods draw on traditional deep learning, for example through optimization, regularization, data augmentation, continual learning, and adversarial learning. We develop further ideas by examining more specific learning mechanisms and drawing on evolutionary computation. We also review how existing benchmarks assess self-improvement under online, offline, and offline-to-online settings. Together, these perspectives help researchers develop new RSI research ideas from existing designs and learning mechanisms. RSI papers and resources are available at https://prism-shadow.github.io/awesome-rsi/.","tldr":"背景与问题：RSI 工作涉及不同更新对象、反馈与保留机制，宽泛分类难以揭示设计差异及其交互。方法：论文提出九维设计空间，并从优化、正则化、数据增强、持续学习与进化计算等机制中归纳可能的研究方向，同时梳理在线与离线评测。结果与结论：材料支持其分类框架和研究议程；没有本文系统的递归改进实验或性能结果。Insights：这提示比较 RSI 时可分别追问改什么、谁提出、依据何种反馈保留；这是框架可能提供的分析工具，材料未证明它本身改善系统或研究产出。","published_at":"2026-10-10","topics":"RSI 评测与方法分类; 研究议程","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称用九维分类框架整理 RSI 设计，并从传统学习机制与进化计算提出研究构想；反馈来自文献及基准分析，不存在本文自身的改进对象—反馈—保留递归闭环。现有材料为综述全文片段，但未提供系统性与既有综述的匹配比较；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14495","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14495v1","title":"Reels-RSI: Program-Level Self-Improvement for Code-Rendered Explainer Videos","authors":"Wei Lin","affiliations":"Agentic Loops X","abstract":"Explainer videos -- a worked geometry problem, why the sky is blue, how a dynasty fell -- are usually one more target for pixel video generation. We argue they are a different kind of artifact: a program (script, storyboard and per-frame animation code) that a deterministic renderer turns into frames. A program can be read, diffed, tested and audited; pixels can only be watched. Reels-RSI is an open-source reel director for any agent harness; its self-improvement happens at the program level rather than in weights or prompts. Every revision pass is logged with a code snapshot; a retrospective pairs each check finding with the diff that fixed it and proposes lessons; a lesson that a static check can catch is compiled into a rule with a must-fail and a must-pass example, so the memory is unit-tested; and a rule learned today runs over everything made before it. A bounded, benchmark-gated step lets an agent rewrite the director's playbook, kept only when blind pairwise judgments on held-out topics prefer it; nothing enters memory without a human decision. Across 111 reels -- a field study, two playbook evolutions, a 2x2 memory ablation, a weaker director, a 48-reel learning curve and a judge-reliability study -- we find that the rule learned in the field caught four latent defects in frames authored before it existed and none after; that rules are an audit for a strong director (eight unguarded reels, no violation) and a guard for a weaker one (thirty violations unguarded versus five); that lessons shorten revision loops but do not compound or move the judge; and that the first rewrite's 11--1 verdict was a position bias in our vote design (judges pick the second-shown reel 62--81% of the time), masking scripts that traded thirteen facts for craft. We document four failure modes of the preference signal, which check caught each, and the fixes. Code, rules, lessons and data are public.","tldr":"背景与问题：解释视频既要视觉呈现，也要事实、推导和动画正确；只看像素难定位程序缺陷，偏好评审还可能把展示偏差当成改进。方法：把作品作为可读、可测试的程序记录；复盘将检查发现与修复差异配对，可静态检测的经验编译成带正反例的规则，并回查旧作品；playbook 更新需盲评且经人批准。结果与结论：作者报告一条规则在旧作品中发现四处潜在缺陷；研究也揭示盲评有明显顺序偏差。经验缩短修订循环，但没有形成累积改进或改变 judge。Insights：这提示可执行产物有助于把经验变成可审计检查，但偏好评分不能单独决定记忆保留；依据是回溯发现与位置偏差。证据限于单系统、有限作品和人工门控。","published_at":"2026-10-10","topics":"可执行记忆与规则; Harness 演化评测; 反馈偏差","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称将视频作品表示为可执行程序，把可静态检查的经验编译成带正反例的规则，并以盲评门控 playbook 改写。本文证据包括旧作品回溯审计及偏好评估的位置偏差；记忆保留仍需人工决策，且作者报告 lessons 不会复合。未与 corpus 中具体方法作匹配比较，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14224","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14224v1","title":"Harness^2: Recursive Agent Harnessing for an Open World","authors":"Ruiyao Xu; Yanfei Chen; Zhongying CuiZhu; Bhavana Dalvi Mishra; Yifei Ming; Han Yu; Rujun Han; Chen-Yu Lee; Tomas Pfister","affiliations":"Google Cloud AI Research；西北大学","abstract":"LLM agents' capabilities depend not only on their underlying models but also on their execution harnesses. Recursive self-improvement (RSI) offers a promising approach to automatically evolve these harnesses. However, deploying RSI in open-world settings still faces two critical challenges. First, open-world tasks are typically unseen during the harness design phase and novel at test time, leaving no ground-truth verifiers to reliably guide online harness edits. Second, the RSI process remains highly task-specific and fails to generalize to novel scenarios. We introduce Harness^2, a plug-and-play, recursive agent harnessing framework that addresses these challenges through two connected levels of recursion. Task-level recursion refines the current task's harness using a contrastive Propose-Probe-Compose step that reliably guides edits without ground-truth verifiers, and can be scaled further via parallel or sequential recursion. Harnessing-level recursion then extracts experience from these edits to update a continual improvement harness, enabling the agent to better adapt to future tasks. Across three professional benchmarks and four model-harness configurations, a single step consistently improves GLM-5 and Gemini 3.5 Flash over their base harnesses, yielding gains of up to 11.5 points on WorkBuddy-Bench, 4.5 points on JobBench, and 11.8 percentage points on LAB, with further gains as the task-level recursion budget increases.","tldr":"背景与问题：开放世界任务往往没有真值 verifier，按单一任务改出的 harness 又未必适用于后续新任务；直接继承任务专用修改还可能放大噪声。方法：先提出编辑并在相同任务和条件下探测行为变化，再据对比证据组合修改；随后从编辑过程提取适用条件与经验，更新未来任务的改进 harness。结果与结论：作者报告单步在多个专业基准和配置上有增益，增加任务级递归预算也带来提升。行为差异可帮助选择编辑，但不等于验证任务正确性。Insights：这提示应分别衡量“当前任务改得怎样”与“下一次是否更会改”；依据是双层循环及跨任务经验设计。证据限于特定基准、模型和预算，尚非独立复现。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 跨任务迁移; 无真值反馈","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称将无真值条件下的任务内对比探测，与跨任务积累可复用改进经验连接成两层递归。本文证据包括三项专业基准、四种模型—harness 配置及递归预算实验。与 Meta-Harness（arxiv:2603.28052）相比，本篇不仅搜索当前任务 harness，还将改进过程经验用于未来 harnessing；不是匹配性能比较，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14163","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14163v1","title":"AutoEnvScaling: Automating the Data Flywheel with Terminal Agents","authors":"Simon Yu; Baolin Peng; Bo Liu; Zhengyan Shi; Zhaoyang Wang; Hao Cheng; Qianhui Wu; Wenlin Yao; Natasha Jaques; Weiyan Shi; Jianfeng Gao","affiliations":"东北大学；微软研究院；华盛顿大学；北卡罗来纳大学教堂山分校","abstract":"Terminal agents solve tasks in software engineering and scientific research by executing commands in a terminal. Training them via reinforcement learning (RL) requires diverse and verifiable environments, but these environments are still mostly designed by human researchers, so their supply grows only as fast as researchers can work. We introduce AutoEnvScaling, which treats environment design as a terminal task and uses agents to automate the data flywheel. A proposer agent builds new RL environments from the rollouts of the solver being trained, and the solver's new rollouts guide the next round. By turning environment generation into a terminal task, AutoEnvScaling increases the valid-environment rate by up to 25 times compared to prompt-only generation, at up to 75% lower cost per valid environment. We show that training Qwen3.5-35B-A3B on AutoEnvScaling environments from GPT-5.6-sol improves its Terminal-Bench 2.1 score by 4.3 points over the matched Tmax baseline. The broader goal of AutoEnvScaling is to enable recursive self-improvement (RSI): by making both environment generation and solving terminal tasks, it lets one model co-evolve in both roles. We show that Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, acting in both roles, gains 12.2 points on Terminal-Bench 2.1 and raises its Terminal-Bench 4.0 score from 1.6 to 3.2. The pipeline also generalizes across agentic domains, generating environments for software engineering, computer use, professional work, and GPU kernel programming. Overall, these results show a path toward agents building their own training environments, reducing human reliance and taking a core step toward RSI.","tldr":"背景与问题：终端 agent 的强化学习依赖多样且可验证的环境；人工设计限制供给，固定任务池也会随 solver 进步而失去训练价值。方法：proposer 阅读 solver 轨迹，在沙箱终端中编写、运行和修复环境；环境通过有效性与难度校准后入池，solver 的新表现再指导下一轮生成，形成数据飞轮。结果与结论：作者报告相较纯提示生成，有效环境率最高提升 25 倍、单个有效环境成本最高降低 75%；同一模型兼任 proposer 与 solver 时，Terminal-Bench 2.1 提升 12.2 分。Insights：这提示训练经验生成本身可成为 agent 能力的一部分；依据是环境构建与 solver 学习相互反馈。边界是生成者也参与构造测试，仍需审查测试漏洞、长期稳定性与外部分布迁移。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"自适应课程与环境生成; 数据—模型共演化; 终端智能体","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称将环境设计变为终端任务，让 proposer 阅读 solver 轨迹、构建并校准训练环境，solver 新轨迹再指导下一轮；开放权重设置中同一模型可承担两角色。本文报告有效环境率、成本与 Terminal-Bench 作者实验。与 ClawLoop（arxiv:2610.14118）同属训练任务闭环，但前者聚焦完整终端环境的构建和校准；无直接比较，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13829","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.13829v1","title":"MC-EvoBench: Auditing Experience-Driven Self-Improvement in Minecraft Agents","authors":"Jingwei Song; Zhisheng Chen; Bingfan Zeng; Jing Tang; Yubo Hou; Jinhao Jing; Zhengwei Xie; Linfeng Zhang","affiliations":"上海交通大学；中国科学院大学；华南理工大学；华中科技大学；北京航空航天大学；香港中文大学（深圳）；中国科学技术大学","abstract":"A central challenge in embodied recursive self-improvement is enabling agents to convert interaction history into capabilities that persist beyond one world and transfer to later tasks. A saved memory or successful final action does not by itself establish that a reusable capability was acquired; evaluation must separate capability change from carried-over resources, unequal source exposure, and early execution failures. We construct MC-EvoBench as a controlled Minecraft benchmark with a fixed catalog of 19 registered evolution chains, including 12 primary evaluation chains and seven calibration or probe chains, together with three graph-aligned paired probe families for transfer. The benchmark represents each task as a task-state graph, defines stage-level environment verifiers, assigns matched source and target roles, resets the target world, and permits only a declared agent artifact to cross the source-target boundary. For each probe, no-prior, related, unrelated, and shuffled source conditions are evaluated under matched environment-step budgets and five seeds; we report TSR, WGP, and VMP and retain provenance records. The benchmark reveals a consistent direct-capability gap between controller and planner-backed variants, while related experience yields no stable transfer: it does not improve either tool probe, its small wood-species gain hinges on one seed, and all intervals include zero. Stage audits further show that early wood-collection and crafting bottlenecks often leave later capabilities unobserved. MC-EvoBench thus offers a controlled testbed for durable, transferable embodied capabilities. Code and data are available at https://github.com/xzw-ustc/mc-bench-open-source","tldr":"背景与问题：保存记忆或在一次任务中成功，不足以证明获得可迁移能力；后续表现可能受携带资源、源任务暴露量和早期执行失败影响。方法：用任务状态图和阶段验证器记录进度，重置目标世界与库存，只让声明的 agent 工件跨任务；在匹配预算下比较相关、不相关、打乱经验与无经验条件。结果与结论：作者报告控制器的直接能力优于规划器变体，但相关经验未显示稳定迁移，微小收益受单个种子影响且区间含零；早期采集、制作瓶颈还会使后续能力未被观察。Insights：这提示具身 RSI 的首要难点是把能力变化与环境状态、执行机会分开归因；依据是严格重置后仍无稳定迁移。结论限于 Minecraft 探针和所测代理，不能外推到所有具身环境。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"具身持续学习评测; 经验迁移; 能力归因","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者提出 Minecraft 经验迁移审计：重置目标世界，只允许声明的 agent 工件跨任务，并匹配经验暴露和步数。本文证据显示相关经验没有稳定迁移收益。与 EmbodiedCLBench（arxiv:2610.13021）相比，本篇着重隔离物理状态混淆和经验来源归因，后者检验基础任务经验的组合泛化；两篇没有直接比较，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13285","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.13285v1","title":"BoundaryEvo: Data-Model Co-Evolution at the Capability Boundary for Long-Chain Reasoning Distillation","authors":"Jiaming Su; Suorong Yang; Xudong Li; Tengchao Yang; Peng Ye","affiliations":"上海人工智能实验室；南京大学；同济大学；香港中文大学","abstract":"Distilling long-chain reasoning trajectories from large teacher models provides an effective way to improve the reasoning ability of small language models. However, existing methods typically select a fixed training set before distillation, overlooking that the usefulness of a reasoning example changes as the student evolves. This mismatch becomes especially costly when only a small number of teacher trajectories can be used for training. Besides, examples already mastered provide little new supervision, while examples far beyond the capability of student may be difficult to learn from. Training data should therefore adapt as model capability evolves, yet reliable data selection is difficult when the student is initially weak. To address these challenges, our key idea is to first establish the basic reasoning capability and then adapt the training data to the evolving capability boundary of the student. We propose BoundaryEvo, a two-stage data--model co-evolution framework. In Capability Priming, we directly distill a small set of teacher-generated long reasoning trajectories without using a separate model to judge and filter them, allowing the student to acquire an initial reasoning capability before capability-aware data selection. In Capability-Boundary Co-Evolution, we repeatedly select questions that the current student has not mastered but the expert can reliably solve, and update the training data as the student evolves. With only 1,000 training examples, BoundaryEvo consistently outperforms static and dynamic data selection baselines across 11 reasoning benchmarks, raising the original Qwen3.5-4B accuracy from 62.9 to 75.3 on IMO-AnswerBench and from 26.8 to 46.0 on AMO-Bench. The code and data will be made publicly available.","tldr":"背景与问题：固定蒸馏集会随学生能力变化而变得过易或过难；学生很弱时，单看错误也难判断哪些例子能提供有效监督。方法：先直接蒸馏少量教师推理轨迹建立基础能力，再持续选取学生尚未掌握、专家能可靠解决且题目质量合格的样本；学生更新后重新估计边界并刷新训练数据。结果与结论：作者报告只用 1,000 个训练样本，在 11 个基准上优于静态和动态选择基线；Qwen3.5-4B 在 IMO-AnswerBench 从 62.9 升至 75.3，在 AMO-Bench 从 26.8 升至 46.0。Insights：这提示有效课程信号需同时满足学习者有缺口、监督可学且目标可靠；依据是边界筛选机制和多基准结果。专家与分析器仍提供外部判断，不能称为完全自监督。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 模型—数据共演化; 推理蒸馏","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称先用少量教师轨迹建立学生初始推理能力，再按学生未掌握、专家可靠可解的边界反复更新数据。本文报告 1,000 例预算、11 个推理基准和多骨干实验。与 SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）都闭环调整训练分布，但本篇采用学生—专家边界筛选与蒸馏，SynCo 联合强化学习优化合成器与推理器；无直接比较，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14118","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14118v1","title":"ClawLoop: Self-Improving Agents via Harness-Native Training Loop","authors":"Hansi Yang; Linji Hao; Hongyan Hao; An Wang; Han Wu; Qi Gu; Xunliang Cai","affiliations":"美团；北京大学","abstract":"The rapid advancement of Large Language Models (LLMs) has driven their deployment toward general-purpose harness environments, where LLM-based agents operate in sandbox workspaces and interact directly with file systems and shells. While numerous post-training pipelines exist for tool-use agents, their counterparts for harness-based agents remain scarce and are predominantly one-shot and teacher-dependent: a stronger external model synthesizes tasks and collects trajectories, the target agent is trained once, and evaluation results are consumed by human researchers rather than fed back into the loop. Such pipelines are inherently bounded by the capability of the external model and the scope of human prior, leaving no room for self-improvement. To address these limitations, we propose ClawLoop, a framework that enables self-improving without any external teacher model and with minimal prior dependencies. ClawLoop composes three phases into a self-sustaining cycle: Task Synthesis, which generates a diverse pool of training tasks via two complementary construction routines, applies diagnosis-conditioned difficulty growth followed by both agent-free and agent-based task validation; Training, which updates the agent via SFT and/or RL; and Diagnosis and Feedback, which analyzes the agent's rollout behaviors to produce a capability analysis report that will be used as feedback for task synthesis in the next iteration. Using Qwen3.6-27B as the loop model, ClawLoop yields consistent improvements on SkillsBench, Claw-Eval-Live, and ClawGym-Bench. The iteratively refined tasks are further transferred to smaller-scale Qwen3.5-4B and 9B models with gains across all benchmarks, validating data quality independently of the loop model.","tldr":"背景与问题：Harness agent 的任务空间宽，既有训练常依赖外部强模型造任务或收集轨迹，训练后评估结果又交由人分析，难以持续闭环。方法：系统合成并校验任务，用成功轨迹或强化学习更新模型，再从留出任务 rollout 诊断反复出现的短板，把分析反馈给下一轮任务生成。结果与结论：作者报告 Qwen3.6-27B 在三个基准持续提升；迭代任务转用于 Qwen3.5-4B 与 9B 时，各基准也有增益。摘要未提供具体提升幅度。Insights：这提示闭环的关键不只是生成更多任务，而是把诊断转成合格且针对当前能力的练习；依据是任务合成与能力报告相连。具体泛化范围、预算和长程稳定性仍需更多证据。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; Harness 智能体训练; 诊断反馈闭环","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称在 harness 环境中闭合任务合成、模型训练与能力诊断，不依赖外部教师；诊断结果直接反馈下一轮任务生成。本文证据为 Qwen3.6-27B 基准结果及小模型迁移的作者报告。与 AutoEnvScaling（arxiv:2610.14163）都让训练经验生成进入循环，但 ClawLoop 面向广泛 harness 任务训练，后者专门构建终端 RL 环境；无直接比较，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13098","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.13098v1","title":"VETR: Execution-Grounded Self-Improving Agent for Symbolic Graphics Reasoning","authors":"Yingbo Ma; Kuangshi Ai; Gordon Dai; Chenglong Yu; Chaoli Wang; Hua Shen","affiliations":"纽约大学；圣母大学","abstract":"Visual agents for symbolic graphics reasoning depend on executable world representations, yet continued improvement remains bottlenecked by ambiguous supervision from final renders. Recent agentic systems refine scenes through repeated interaction, but they lack mechanisms to recursively extract actionable evidence from execution traces, overlooking which proposed symbolic edits survived, disappeared, or interfered during program execution. To address this, we propose VETR (Verified Execution Trajectories for Refinement), a framework that enables agentic recursive self-improvement over executable world representations for symbolic graphics reasoning. Within each task, VETR retains aligned program/render records with bounded runtime observations and introduces an execution refiner that compiles observed writes and state changes into constrained alternative programs. The refiner validates their endpoints and preservation conditions against captured runtime state; the ordinary visual verifier then assesses goal relevance. Repair construction makes no additional language-model calls, but can require additional executions. Evaluations on BlenderGym (280 tasks) and BlenderBench (27 released tasks) with GPT-5.6-luna and Qwen3.8-27B show that VETR consistently outperforms existing refinement strategies, including BlenderAlchemy and VIGA. Controlled ablations evaluate the contributions of execution refinement and role-asymmetric evidence organization under fixed generator-interaction caps.","tldr":"背景与问题：程序化图形 agent 主要根据最终渲染修订，图像差异难以说明符号编辑是否生效、被覆盖或互相干扰。方法：保留程序、渲染与运行时状态记录，从实际写入构造受限替代程序；重新执行检查指定端点和保持条件，再由常规视觉反馈判断目标相关性。结果与结论：作者报告在 BlenderGym 280 题与 BlenderBench 27 题上优于所比较的 refinement 方法；消融支持执行修订与证据组织的作用，但修复需额外执行。Insights：这提示改进信号的价值取决于能否观察编辑如何影响执行，而非单纯增加迭代；依据是执行修订消融。结论限于程序化 3D 场景，固定生成交互数也不代表总执行成本相同。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"执行证据驱动改进; 程序级自我修订; 视觉智能体","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称从执行写入和状态变化生成受约束的程序备选，检查运行端点与保持条件后，再由视觉 verifier 判断目标相关性。本文报告 BlenderGym、BlenderBench、两种骨干及消融，并与 BlenderAlchemy、VIGA 比较。其机制差异在于增加执行证据接口，而非仅依赖最终渲染；额外执行带来成本，材料未支持领域级优先性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13021","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.13021v1","title":"EmbodiedCLBench: Evaluating Continual Learning for Self-Evolving Embodied Agents","authors":"Jie Huang; Yanan Chen; Ruixun Liu; Kaichen He; Xinyi He; Rui Huang; Zilong Zheng; Zhenliang Zhang; Yiwu Zhong","affiliations":"北京大学；香港大学；BIGAI","abstract":"Continual learning requires models to accumulate past experience and transfer it to new tasks. Despite substantial research on continual learning, existing work remains largely confined to non-embodied settings, without extending to embodied environments. To address this gap, we introduce EmbodiedCLBench, the first benchmark in embodied simulation for evaluating the continual learning capability of self-evolving agents. With compositional generalization as the core evaluation principle, our benchmark evaluates whether agents can first learn from basic tasks and then recombine the acquired skills to solve complex, unseen advanced tasks. Based on EmbodiedCLBench, we conduct extensive experiments across multiple agent harnesses and learning methods, revealing consistent limitations and distinctive behaviors. Our results show that while advanced tasks can be hardly solved under zero-shot setting, the experience from basic tasks enables consistent improvement. Such benefit from the experience remains stable even if the task complexity increases. However, this improvement does not scale accordingly with the number of learning samples, and current agents cannot extract meaningful information from additional experience. Collectively, our findings highlight continual learning as a fundamental yet underexplored capability, and our benchmark offers valuable resources for designing effective self-evolving agents in embodied environments. Our code and dataset are available at https://pku-value-lab.github.io/EmbodiedCLBench-homepage.","tldr":"背景与问题：持续学习研究多限于非具身环境，而常见具身基准也不直接检验既有经验能否迁移到未见任务组合。方法：构造从原子动作、基础家务到未见组合任务的评测，并比较零样本、保留交互轨迹与压缩技能总结。结果与结论：作者报告复杂任务零样本成功率约为 10%，有基础任务经验后可超过 30%；但增加学习样本没有相称的持续收益，ICL 与技能学习也无稳定胜者。Insights：这提示积累经验可能先带来明显收益，之后瓶颈转为提取有效信息，而不是继续增加样本；依据是样本扩张未产生一致增益。任务采用离线状态图，不能直接代表真实在线具身交互。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"具身持续学习评测; 组合泛化; 经验迁移","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者提出用具身组合泛化测持续学习：先执行基础任务，再测未见复杂任务，比较完整轨迹或技能总结。证据显示经验改善复杂任务，但额外学习样本未带来相称提升。与 MC-EvoBench（arxiv:2610.13829）相比，本篇聚焦组合任务迁移，后者聚焦物理状态重置和经验来源归因；未直接比较，摘要不足以证实首创。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12855","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12855v1","title":"Mitigating Capability Degradation in LLM Self-Improvement via Representation Geometry Regularization","authors":"Jiaqi Tian; Ting Long","affiliations":"吉林大学","abstract":"On-Policy Self-distillation is a self-improvement paradigm that enables large language models (LLMs) to improve their capabilities by leveraging the same model as both teacher and student under different conditioning contexts. However, we find that OPSD methods can progressively degrade previously acquired capabilities: queries that are correctly responded at earlier training stages may become incorrectly responded as optimization proceeds, even the overall performance continues to improve. Further analysis reveals that this degradation coincides with a deterioration of the geometry of hidden representations, characterized by reduced intra-cluster compactness and diminished inter-cluster separation. Motivated by this observation, we propose Representation Geometry Regularization (RGR), which preserves representation geometry during post-training by encouraging compactness within cluster and separation across cluster. RGR can be seamlessly integrated into existing OPSD methods without altering their core optimization procedures. Extensive experiments on multiple OPSD methods and benchmarks show that RGR generally alleviates capability degradation while retaining capability improvements. Our code is available in https://github.com/supermachinelearner/RGR.","tldr":"背景与问题：on-policy 自蒸馏可提升总体能力，但训练推进时，先前答对的问题可能变为答错，单看总体分数会掩盖这种退化。方法：作者观察到能力退化伴随隐藏表征簇结构变模糊，提出在自蒸馏中约束簇内紧致与簇间分离，尽量保留已有表征结构。结果与结论：作者报告在多种自蒸馏方法和基准上，RGR 通常减轻能力退化，同时保留能力提升；摘要没有给出具体效果量。Insights：这提示 RSI 评估应同时追踪新能力与旧题回归，而不能只看平均表现。表征几何是作者提出并分析的关联机制，现有材料不足以断言它是各类自改进的普遍因果瓶颈。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"自改进稳定性; 能力遗忘与回归; 表示几何","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者报告 on-policy 自蒸馏中总体性能上升时，旧题仍可能由对转错；此现象与隐藏表征几何退化相关，并提出保持簇内紧致和簇间分离的正则化。本文证据覆盖多种自蒸馏方法和基准，但摘要未给具体幅度。该工作主要缓解稳定性问题，不提出新的递归闭环；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13912","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.13912v1","title":"RSI-Anything: Unlocking Recursive Self-Improvement with World Models","authors":"Taoyong Cui; Pinxian Zeng; Wanghan Xu; Hao Xiao; Shuhan Xue; Qiang Gao; Wanli Ouyang; Pheng Ann Heng; Zhenfei Yin; Yingcheng Wu; Ling Yang","affiliations":"PhAI Labs；香港中文大学；澳门大学；上海交通大学；复旦大学；牛津大学；斯坦福大学；北京大学","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement (RSI) aims to transform interaction experience into persistent improvements, yet external feedback is costly and world-model predictions may become unreliable as policies evolve. We introduce RSI-Anything, a domain-general framework built on JEPA-Anything that uses predictive world models to guide action and learning-data selection. Observed feedback drives policy or workflow improvement and conditional world-model adaptation, while component and compatibility checks govern the retention of updated policy-model pairs. Across diverse computational and scientific domains, RSI-Anything demonstrates substantial gains. In code repair, with the coder fixed, success increases from 26.3% with a static verifier to 29.2% through predictive selection and 31.2% after world-model adaptation, at comparable test usage. Graphical user interface (GUI) evaluations showed higher task completion, while average actions decrease by 39.4%. Across five successive policy versions, laboratory-planning scores more than double from 21.80% to 46.01%. In reaction optimization, RSI-Anything achieves 96.15% mean best observed yield versus 82.16% for Bayesian optimization under the same 40-experiment budget. An end-to-end immune-science application further connects workflow evolution and predictive modeling with therapeutic hypothesis generation. These results demonstrate how predictive world models and retained system updates enable recursive improvement across diverse environments.","tldr":"背景与问题：RSI 需要把交互经验转成后续能力，但外部评估昂贵；策略更新还可能改变经验分布，使既有世界模型失准。因此，单独改策略或预测器都不能保证下一轮系统仍可靠。\n\n方法：RSI-Anything 用预测模型预判候选行动结果，帮助选择行动和学习数据；真实反馈再驱动策略或工作流更新，并在可靠性、数据和预算条件满足时调整世界模型。组件检查与策略—模型兼容检查决定哪些更新被保留，获准组合进入下一轮。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告，在固定 coder 的代码修复任务中，成功率从静态 verifier 的 26.3% 经预测筛选升至 29.2%，再经世界模型适配升至 31.2%，测试使用量相近；还报告 GUI、实验规划和反应优化结果。这些是作者实验，不是独立复现；材料不足以确认长期稳定性和广泛泛化。\n\nInsights：这提示瓶颈不只是预测准确度，还包括策略变化后模型是否仍适用，以及如何筛选更新组合；依据是论文提出的耦合更新问题和兼容性保留设计。该机制能否延伸至更广任务，仍需长期及统一预算评估。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"世界模型与递归改进; 反馈驱动更新; 策略—模型联合演化","added_on":"2026-10-13","novelty_summary":"作者声称 RSI-Anything 将预测引导的行动与数据选择、反馈驱动的策略或工作流改进、条件式世界模型适配及策略—模型对保留连成闭环。本文证据包括摘要中的机制说明，以及作者报告的代码修复、GUI、实验规划和反应优化结果；固定 coder 的代码修复结果显示预测筛选及模型适配阶段分别伴随成功率上升，但不是独立复现。与 corpus 中 Memento 3（arxiv:2610.11794）相比，本篇强调预测器与策略更新的联合保留，Memento 3 则在冻结 LLM 下更新环境规则记忆与可执行模型；两者没有直接比较。编辑推断：相较 JEPA-Anything 的预测基础，本篇把预测接入递归更新与保留机制；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13025","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.13025v1","title":"Evo$^2$: Evolving the Evolver through Weight-Harness Co-Evolution","authors":"Chejian Xu; Shujian Zhang; Wenxuan Zhou; John Lambert; Beck Chen; Bo Li; Andrew Hard; Rajiv Mathews","affiliations":"伊利诺伊大学厄巴纳-香槟分校","abstract":"Self-evolving agents are increasingly used to improve language model systems without human intervention through either weight updates or harness improvements. Existing approaches typically pursue these directions separately: some methods update model weights using self-generated experience, while others rewrite the harness that defines how an agent uses prompts, tools, context, and execution feedback. However, these approaches overlook the relationship between model weights and the agent harness. To connect these processes and ensure effective and smooth agent self-evolving, we propose Evo$^2$, a framework for weight-harness co-evolution. For harness updates, we design a unified dual-role pipeline that a single policy serves as both a Proposer, which writes harness edits, and a Reflector, which diagnoses their effects and guides revision. For weight updates, harness modifications and their execution outcomes guide the training of both the Proposer and the Reflector. We further develop EvoTIDE, a training pipeline that recovers usable trajectories through edit extraction and prefix continuation, then combines SFT with interleaved GRPO across the two roles. Extensive experiments across three coding benchmarks demonstrate that Evo$^2$ significantly outperforms existing self-evolution methods. It achieves 82.1% on Polyglot and 48.3% on SWE-bench Verified, compared with 62.6% and 41.0% for the strongest baseline, respectively. We also show that the evolved harnesses transfer to different tasks without further evolution and rank first in cross-benchmark evaluations. Our dual-role harness improvement framework is also able to extend to self-evolution with proprietary models, improving a GPT-5-mini agent's performance from 24.4% to 48.3%. These results demonstrate the applicability of the framework Evo$^2$ across domains and its broad transferability across models and tasks.","tldr":"背景与问题：自进化 agent 常分别更新模型权重或修改 harness，忽略了二者的反馈关系：权重影响编辑质量，而编辑执行结果也能提供训练经验。分开优化可能无法让系统学会如何持续改进自身。\n\n方法：Evo² 让同一策略担任 harness 修改者和反思者；修改结果及执行反馈用于训练这两个角色。EvoTIDE 从编辑和反思轨迹中恢复可用训练数据，经监督微调与交错策略优化更新共享权重，再由更新后的策略继续搜索 harness。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告三个编码基准上的表现优于所比较的自进化方法，并称演化出的 harness 可迁移到其他任务；摘要给出 Polyglot 与 SWE-bench Verified 的对照分数。论文指出相关工作机制比较不是匹配性能基准，结果也不是独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示 harness 搜索不只是改善执行脚手架，也可能成为训练“改进者”的数据来源；依据是编辑反馈用于角色训练，更新权重又回到后续搜索。是否优于分别优化或其他联合方案，仍需统一预算、消融和多轮稳定性比较。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"权重—harness 联合演化; 反馈驱动更新; 自进化策略训练","added_on":"2026-10-13","novelty_summary":"作者声称将 harness 编辑及执行结果用于训练共享的 Proposer–Reflector 策略，更新后的权重再指导后续 harness 搜索，形成相互反馈。本文证据包括机制说明、作者报告的编码基准及迁移结果。corpus 中 SIA（arxiv:2605.27276）与 HASE（arxiv:2607.03935）也涉及权重和 harness 的联合改进；本篇具体强调用编辑结果训练共享修改者与反思者。论文说明相关工作比较是机制比较而非匹配性能基准。编辑推断：这是共演化机制的具体推进，但优先性未确证；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12789","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12789v1","title":"EvoBelief: Falsifiable World Models for Self-Improving LLM Agents","authors":"Janet Wang; Jiang Guo; Yi Xiang; Jiaqing Yuan; Mingwen Dong; Hideo Kobayashi; Shuaichen Chang; Chandan K. Reddy; Jiarong Jiang","affiliations":"杜兰大学；亚马逊","abstract":"Self-evolving LLM agents typically improve how they act through accumulated experience, reflection, or skills. Yet even procedurally capable agents can fail when their beliefs about environment dynamics are incomplete, incorrect, or outdated. We study a complementary axis of self-evolution: evolving those beliefs during deployment. Such beliefs can support multiple tasks, but incorrect ones can also propagate across them. We introduce EvoBelief, a self-evolving world model that represents environment knowledge as falsifiable hypotheses. Unexpected outcomes and decision-relevant unknowns trigger hypothesis formation. Later observations and controlled experiments provide independent validation before a rule can guide predictions or plans within its supported scope. Counterexamples narrow or retire rules as the environment changes. The language model remains frozen, and each rule remains linked to its evidence and the decisions it changes. Across four benchmarks spanning static dynamics, hidden drift, and scientific discovery, EvoBelief improves task performance and reuses learned rules across tasks. On ALFWorld without actor-side transition memory, it improves success over the matched Frozen World Model by 23.9% and 31.3% with Claude Haiku 4.5 and GPT-5.4, respectively. On MiniGrid, it revises stale rules and recovers after unannounced dynamics changes. In DiscoveryWorld's Reactor Lab, it discovers and validates quantitative laws, completing 83.3% of Normal-tier and 58.3% of Challenge-tier instances, versus 0% for each evaluated baseline. These results demonstrate self-improvement through testable, revisable environment knowledge rather than model-parameter updates.","tldr":"背景与问题：Agent 即使会执行步骤，也可能因环境动态信念不完整或过时而失败；错误规则还可能传播到其他任务。方法：冻结语言模型，把环境知识存成带证据、适用范围和检验方式的假设。新观察触发验证，独立证据支持后规则才影响规划；反例会缩窄、降级或撤销规则。结果与结论：作者报告在 ALFWorld 中优于匹配的冻结世界模型，在 MiniGrid 中修订过时规则并适应动态变化；在 DiscoveryWorld Reactor Lab 也报告高于所测基线的完成率。Insights：这提示跨任务记忆要有可检验性、范围约束和撤销机制；依据是规则生命周期与漂移实验。证据来自有限模拟环境的作者实验，不能证明真实环境迁移或独立复现。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"世界模型与递归改进; 可证伪记忆; 反馈驱动更新","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称将环境知识表示为可证伪假设，经过后续观察或受控实验验证才允许影响规划，并按反例缩窄或撤销规则。本文报告四类基准及冻结语言模型下的作者实验。作者讨论既有世界模型工作，但所给 corpus 未提供可关联的 paper_id，故不列 related；领域优先性未证实。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12367","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12367v1","title":"Which Skill to Distill? SGUID: Selecting a Compact Skill Bank for Model-Skill Co-Evolution","authors":"Yuhan Liu; Xiyao Ma; Zhongkai Sun; Xu Han; Chengyuan Ma; Benjamin Z. Yao; Chenlei Guo","affiliations":"New York University；Amazon","abstract":"Skills, reusable procedural guidance added at inference, can substantially improve LLM downstream performance (Li et al., 2026). Prior work retrieves skills from a bank by semantic relevance, then uses them as inference-time patches or for model distillation. The individual utility of each skill, however, is largely neglected. We first show that, in on-policy distillation where skill-conditioned policies serve as teachers, fewer than 25% of retrieved skills provide useful distillation signals. We then propose SGUID, a method for selecting a compact subset of skills for distillation. SGUID retains a skill only if it consistently yields effective learning signals during training. The selected skills are then distilled to produce a better model. Our results show that not all skills are worth distilling. Across four models from the Olmo and Qwen families, distilling 6 selected skills matches or exceeds full-bank distillation in mean avg@12 on three of the four models, and on all four after a second round that distills 3 newly selected skills, while the full banks are up to 11x larger. Importantly, SGUID supports stable model-skill co-evolution: after a distillation round, a new candidate bank is curated from the updated model's rollouts, and SGUID selects which skills to internalize next. In the second round, this loop selects 3 new skills and improves Qwen3-8B from 64.3% to 66.3%. The selection step is essential for stability: on Qwen3-4B, naively updating the model with unfiltered skills degrades performance, including a 0.3 percentage point drop on HMMT25, whereas SGUID improves HMMT25 by 0.5 points after the first round and 1.1 points after the second. These results identify skill selection as the key mechanism for stable model-skill co-evolution.","tldr":"背景与问题：推理时检索到的技能未必能教会当前模型；论文报告，不到四分之一的检索技能提供有用蒸馏信号，因此语义相关性不足以代表训练价值。\n\n方法：SGUID 观察技能条件教师在学生 rollout 上产生的、与验证器一致的学习信号，只保留训练早晚阶段都持续有效的技能。精简技能蒸馏更新模型后，再从新模型 rollout 整理候选技能并筛选下一轮，形成模型与技能库的反馈闭环。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告，仅蒸馏 6 个技能在四个模型中的多数模型上可匹敌或超过全库；第二轮选出 3 个新技能，Qwen3-8B 的均值由 64.3% 升至 66.3%。结果限于数学推理基准，是作者实验而非独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示蒸馏瓶颈可能在监督信号筛选而非技能数量；依据是少量持续有效技能的结果，以及无筛选更新出现退化的报告。该结论仍受任务与验证器范围约束，不能外推到开放任务或缺少可靠验证器的场景。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"技能蒸馏; 模型—数据共演化; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称按蒸馏过程中持续有效的学习信号筛选技能，再用精简技能库更新模型；更新模型的 rollout 用于整理新候选技能并启动下一轮。本文证据为四个 Olmo/Qwen 模型上的作者实验。相对具体已有技能选择与自蒸馏工作，全文讨论了技能有效性问题，但现有 corpus 未提供可核验的匹配性能比较；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：主要推进在于将筛选依据从语义相关性转到训练动态，领域优先性不能据此确立。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12235","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12235v1","title":"Language Models as AI Research World Models","authors":"Zijun Wang; Zewen Liu; Minhua Lin; Zhaotian Weng; Zhan Shi; Bing He; Yisi Sang; Dakuo Wang; Benoit Dumoulin; Wei Jin; Yuyin Zhou; Cihang Xie; Hanqing Lu","affiliations":"Amazon；UC Santa Cruz；Emory University；Pennsylvania State University；UC Santa Barbara","abstract":"AI research agents automate the cycle of proposing, implementing, and evaluating experiments, opening a path toward recursive self-improvement. Yet their ability to propose experiments outpaces their capacity to execute them in real environments, making outcome prediction a key capability for sustained self-improvement under limited experimental budgets. We investigate language models as Research World Models (RWMs), which predict the outcomes of candidate interventions across research environments. Our evaluation draws on over 2,600 experimental records from nine research environments spanning pretraining, post-training, and inference, representing more than 171,000 H100 GPU-hours of experimentation. Research knowledge acquired from real experimental experience improves RWM predictions of unseen interventions within the same environment (Spearman +0.27), and can be reused across environments. For example, using only pretraining experience from OLMo3, Marin, and Nanochat, an RWM reduces selection regret in the Qwen3 environment by 78% compared with zero-experience setting. These benefits extend to multi-round Autoresearch under a fixed selection budget: RWMs with in-env and cross-env research knowledge increase the best gain achieved by 15.8% and 11.6%, respectively. Ablations across 13 language models used as RWMs show that adding research knowledge can improve intervention ranking more than changing models or increasing reasoning effort alone. These findings support language models as RWMs and motivate accumulating experimental data for future RWM training.","tldr":"背景与问题：研究 agent 能提出实验，却难以在预算有限时判断哪些干预值得执行；仅凭先验推理预测效果，也容易忽略模型、配方和环境差异。\n\n方法：研究世界模型接收环境、候选干预和既往实验记录，预测潜在收益并排序。被选实验执行后形成新记录，可供后续预测复用；因此闭环改善的是实验选择质量，不是本文已证明的模型参数递归训练。\n\n结果与结论：作者汇集九个环境的 2,653 条实验记录。同环境经验提高未见干预的排序相关性，跨环境经验也改善选择；在固定多轮选择预算下，作者报告经验增强的预测器取得更高最佳收益。这些是作者实验，覆盖范围受现有环境与记录限制。\n\nInsights：这提示稀缺实验预算下，积累可迁移的结果记录可能比单纯更换更强模型或增加推理量更关键；依据是跨环境预测和消融结果。边界在于迁移仍依赖目标环境描述与来源覆盖，预测排序也不能替代实际执行和不确定性估计。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"研究世界模型; 实验经验复用; 预算受限搜索","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者提出用语言模型预测候选研究干预的结果，并将真实实验记录用于后续预测和预算选择。本文证据包括九个研究环境上的记录、跨环境预测及多轮选择实验；描述显示经验通过上下文学习复用，未显示 RWM 权重本身递归更新。相对 corpus 中其他研究搜索工作，未提供直接匹配比较；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：其重要性在于把实验经验转化为候选干预排序信号，是否能普遍减少试错仍取决于环境覆盖。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12233","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12233v1","title":"ReSI: Recursive Safety Improvement toward Resistant and Resilient AI","authors":"Jingnan Zheng; Dongcheng Zhang; Yi Zhang; Ming Zhang; Qiaosheng Zhang; Youbang Sun; An Zhang; Xiangnan He; Tat-Seng Chua; Xia Hu; Bowen Zhou; Chaochao Lu; Xiang Wang","affiliations":"","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement, the participation of AI systems in improving their own capabilities, is beginning to move from theoretical prospect to practice, posing both challenges and opportunities for safety alignment. Models evolve through frequent updates, and their safety alignment requires continual adaptation to each new checkpoint. Meanwhile, with evolving red-teaming methods exposing new vulnerabilities, safety improvement for each checkpoint needs to mitigate exposed vulnerabilities and generalize to risks not yet revealed. Following R$^2$AI, we term these goals resistance to known threats and resilience to unforeseen risks. Recursive self-improvement, in turn, inspires an approach to both goals: safety alignment could likewise advance through successive rounds of evaluation and update. We therefore introduce ReSI, a recursive safety improvement framework that implements this approach through automated research. In each round, ReSI applies diverse red-teaming methods to identify vulnerabilities in the current target model, develops training recipes, and promotes the update with the largest safety gain among those passing a Pareto gate on capability retention as the next target model. Across four dense and mixture-of-experts models, ReSI matches or exceeds evaluated frontier models on in-distribution and out-of-distribution safety benchmarks, and outperforms alignment baselines on nearly all safety evaluations while largely preserving general capabilities. In particular, ReSI reduces the mean X-Teaming attack success rate across the four models from 86.01% to 31.45%, well below GPT-5.6-Luna's leading frontier result of 56.69%, indicating stronger resilience to attacks unseen during training. These findings support recursive safety improvement as a practical path toward resistant and resilient AI.","tldr":"背景与问题：模型持续更新会使旧安全对齐失效，新红队方法又不断揭示未见漏洞；只针对已知攻击训练，可能修补漏洞却损害能力或无法泛化。\n\n方法：ReSI 每轮攻击当前模型、生成训练配方候选并通过试验筛选，再以安全增益和能力保留门控晋级模型。新模型进入下一轮红队评估，反馈重新驱动配方搜索，形成有明确保留条件的安全更新循环。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告四种稠密及 MoE 模型在多项安全评估上改善，并称 X-Teaming 平均攻击成功率由 86.01% 降至 31.45%，同时大体保留一般能力。结果来自作者实验，外推范围受攻击集、训练预算和轮数限制。\n\nInsights：这提示保留门控不应只看目标安全指标，也需限制能力回归；未见攻击评估则是检验安全泛化的依据。由于搜索流程本身固定，现有证据支持迭代安全改进，不足以证明改进机制也在递归变强。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"递归安全改进; 红队反馈; 能力保留门控","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称每轮对当前模型进行红队探测、搜索安全训练配方，并通过能力保留门控决定是否将更新模型晋级至下一轮。本文证据包括四种模型及已知、未见攻击评估；论文明确搜索程序和评估协议跨轮固定，递归主要发生在目标模型更新。与 corpus 中其他论文没有匹配比较；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：这是将安全更新接入多轮模型改进流程，而非证明改进算法本身随轮次进化。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12190","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12190v1","title":"DataSense-Bench: The First Step Toward an AI Scientist","authors":"Yudi Zhang; Mingyu Cao; Lu Yin; Mykola Pechenizkiy; Shiwei Liu","affiliations":"Eindhoven University of Technology；University of Surrey；ELLIS Institute Tübingen；Max Planck Institute for Intelligent Systems；Tübingen AI Center","abstract":"As claims about recursive self-improvement (RSI) and artificial general intelligence (AGI) proliferate, we ask a simple question: do frontier AI models have a sense of data, i.e., can they reliably select the right data for training? We introduce DataSense-Bench to study this capability through the fundamental problem of data selection and performance forecasting in machine learning. We ask AI agents to select and rank candidate training subsets that can be used to fine-tune a small LLM model. Agents are allowed to inspect the data, write and execute analysis code, and run model forward passes, but can not train the model or access the actual evaluation tasks. We then fine-tune the base model on each selected subset and evaluate its post-training performance under a standardized protocol. We instantiate the benchmark in terminal problem solving and tool use, selecting trajectories from OpenThoughts-Agent and EnvScaler and evaluating on TBLite and BFCL, respectively. We then evaluate the agents along two complementary dimensions: the post-training performance of the top-ranked subset, reflecting the ability to identify high-value training data, and ranking accuracy, reflecting the ability to predict the relative performance of the selected subsets. In our experiments, selection gains over random selection are limited; agents do not reliably rank their selected groups, and ranking ability does not hold consistently across tasks: Astra identifies the best group in all three tool-use runs but in only one of three terminal runs. Analysis of execution traces on both tasks shows that agents often use similar data signals while interpreting their training value differently.","tldr":"背景与问题：模型能看数据、写分析代码，不代表能判断哪些样本真正有利于训练；数据表面质量、损失或轨迹成功与特定模型的学习收益并非一一对应。\n\n方法：DataSense-Bench 让 agent 在不能训练模型或查看测试题的条件下选择并排序数据子集，随后用固定流程训练同一基座并测量结果，将事前判断与事后训练结果对照。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告相对随机选择的收益有限，代理对所选数据组的排序也不可靠，且跨终端任务与工具使用任务不稳定。材料支持这是一项能力审计，不支持模型已具备可靠数据科学家能力；范围限于两类轨迹任务和小模型微调。\n\nInsights：这提示 RSI 的数据选择环节可能是瓶颈，必须用训练后的真实结果验证预测，而不能把合理分析过程当作有效信号。依据是排序及跨任务稳定性不足；这不证明所有数据选择方法都无效，也不涵盖在线训练并持续校准选择器的闭环。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"训练数据选择; 收益预测; RSI 评测","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者提出将训练数据选择与收益排序分开测量，并在提交选择后再训练验证。这是对 RSI 所需能力的基准审计，不是自改进闭环本身。本文证据限于终端任务与工具使用轨迹及指定训练协议；与 corpus 工作没有匹配性能比较，未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：其价值在于把“挑中有用数据”和“能预测候选优劣”拆成不同可检验能力。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12086","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12086v1","title":"EvoAlloc: A Self-Evolving Resource Allocation Agent for Efficient Program Evolution","authors":"Yanning Dai; Yuhui Wang; Nanbo Li; Wenyi Wang; Jürgen Schmidhuber","affiliations":"King Abdullah University of Science and Technology；Sakana AI","abstract":"LLM-based program evolution relies on evaluation feedback to guide the iterative search for high-performing programs. However, evaluation is often computationally expensive, making it essential to allocate limited resources to candidates that can most effectively advance the search. Existing LLM-based methods typically rely on fixed allocation strategies throughout the search, potentially wasting resources on low-value candidates while overlooking promising ones. We propose EvoAlloc, a self-evolving resource-allocation agent that learns from search experience to revise its strategy for allocating computational resources across candidates. EvoAlloc periodically consolidates prior search and allocation outcomes into reusable experience, which informs subsequent strategy revisions. It further uses a counterfactual exploration mechanism to occasionally evaluate candidates denied resources by the allocator, revealing their outcomes to enrich its experience for future strategy updates. Across coding and agent-harness optimization benchmarks, EvoAlloc requires 59-82% fewer full evaluations and 61-89% fewer total LLM tokens to reach baseline-level performance. Moreover, under the same full-evaluation budget, EvoAlloc achieves 8.7-12.0% higher final performance.","tldr":"背景与问题：程序演化的完整评估成本高，固定分配规则可能把预算花在低价值候选上；更深一层的问题是，被跳过的候选没有结果，分配器会因自己的选择而看不到错误。\n\n方法：EvoAlloc 把评估资源分配策略本身设为可修订对象，从搜索与分配结果提炼经验；偶尔完整评估被拒候选，补上反事实反馈，再据共同验证结果决定是否采用新策略。\n\n结果与结论：作者在编码及 agent-harness 优化基准报告，达到基线表现所需完整评估减少 59–82%，同预算下最终表现高 8.7–12.0%。消融支持策略演化和反事实探索的贡献，但结论限于所测搜索任务与预算。\n\nInsights：这提示自适应资源管理的关键不只是更聪明地筛选，还要主动测量被筛选机制隐藏的失败；依据是反事实反馈设计及消融。其收益是否转移到昂贵实验、非程序搜索或不同预算制度，现有材料尚不能确认。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"搜索策略演化; 评估预算分配; 反事实反馈","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称从搜索与分配结果修订资源分配策略，并偶尔评估被拒候选，以揭示选择性反馈隐藏的结果。本文报告程序搜索与 agent-harness 优化基准上的预算收益和消融。与 corpus 中已有搜索策略演化工作，提供的材料不足以核验匹配性能比较或优先性；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：反事实探索是针对分配器自我遮蔽反馈的具体机制补充。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11959","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.11959v1","title":"MiMo-V2.6: Scaling Reinforcement Learning Towards Self-Improvement","authors":"Xiaomi LLM-Core Team;  :; Zongming Qiao; Ziyue Hua; Zirui Ou; Zihao Yue; Zihan Jiang; Zhuo Huang; Zhiyang Chen; Zhixian Zheng; Zhipeng Xu; Zhengrui Ma; Yuyang Hu; Yuhang Dong; Yuechen Zhang; Yudong Wang; Yuanxin Liu; Yixin Yang; Yishuo Cai; Yikai Zhao; Yihan Yan; Yifan Zhang; Yifan Song; Xiyu Wei; Xing Zhang; Xin Zhang; Xiaoqian Liu; Xiaodong Ji; Xiangwei Deng; Xueyu Guo; Wenhan Ma; Weimin Xiong; Weikun Wang; Weiji Zhuang; Shuo Liu; Shuhuai Ren; Shuhao Gu; Shimao Chen; Shijie Cao; Shihua Yu; Shicheng Li; Shengjie Zhou; Shaolei Zhang; Rang Li; Qiying Wang; Qingkai Fang; Qianli Chen; Minzheng Wang; Liwen Wang; Linli Yao; Linghao Zhang; Liangyu Cheng; Liang Zhao; Lei Li; Jinhao Dong; Jinyu Xiang; Jianyu Wei; Jiangshan Duo; Huaqiu Liu; Huanjie Fan; Hongyi Guan; Hongshen Xu; Hao Tian; Hanyu Li; Hailin Zhang; Gang Wang; Fuli Luo; Feng Wei; Dong Zhang; Dawei Zhu; Chiheng Lou; Chenhong He; Chenhao He; Chenghua Liu; Bowen Ye; Bowen Shen; Boshen Xu; Bo Yang; Bingquan Xia; Bangjun Xiao; Baixuan Xu; Zhouxiang Mao; Zhiyang Zhang; Zhixiang Xu; Zhenru Lin; Zhengju Tang; Zhaojun Huang; Yuzhe Weng; Yuxing Xiang; Yuxiao Li; Yuheng Yang; Yuhang Wang; Yuchen Liu; Yuanyuan Tian; Yuanliang Dong; Yu Cheng; Yongzhe He; Yongshun Liang; Yong Wang; Yiyan Wang; Yitian Gong; Yijie Zhang; Yanshu Xin; Xun Zhang; Xingjian Zhao; Wenyu Yang; Wenshan Huang; Wenhao Li; Tingwei Huang; Tianyu Yu; Tianyang Lu; Taoyu Yang; Sinan Du; Shutong Tian; Shulin Du; Shengfan Wang; Shanchuan Fang; Qihao Zhang; Qibin Yang; Qian Yu; Qian Tu; Pengrong Xie; Peipei Wang; Peidian Li; Minkun Guo; Mingchen Shao; Luohan Gao; Lijie Wang; Liang Shi; Kaiqi Chen; Kaiming Liu; Kaifei Wang; Kai Yang; Jinlong Xue; Jiechen Zhang; Jiaxuan Liu; Hongxu An; Hao Peng; Hanglong Lü; Guonan Wang; Feiyu Yang; Fanyu Cao; Fangyue Liu; Fan Cui; Cong Wang; Chun Chen; Chenxu Bai; Chengxuan Zhu; Chenghua Wang; Boyi Zeng","affiliations":"Xiaomi LLM-Core Team","abstract":"Reinforcement learning (RL) is the central training paradigm for advancing large foundation models towards self-improvement. This report introduces the MiMo-V2.6 series, an omni-modal family that pushes the frontier of model intelligence by scaling RL compute. Prior to RL, we conduct mid-training on a broad multimodal corpus to provide ample exploration space, and build a solid infrastructure on the pretrained hybrid-SWA architecture to support subsequent scale-up. We scale RL compute along three dimensions: (1) larger batches and higher throughput, with an asynchronous training that consumes 1,568 samples and 2.7-3.7B tokens per step at context lengths of up to 1M; (2) more diverse and complex environments, spanning code, general, visual, and cyber domains under a mixture of agent harnesses; and (3) more grader compute, via groupwise agentic grading that yields more accurate reward signals for long-horizon tasks and steers the model towards shorter, more token-efficient solutions. To keep training stable at scale, we freeze the MoE router and establish a multi-layer defense against reward hacking. We further build infrastructure for mixed-task agentic RL, including a unified trajectory representation, high-concurrency multi-framework rollout, decoupled control and data planes, and training-inference consistency. We open-source the training dynamics, RL environments, and RL framework to facilitate reproduction and further research on scaled RL and model self-improvement.","tldr":"背景与问题：复杂 agent 任务的强化学习受限于探索环境、长程奖励信号及大规模 rollout 基础设施；扩大算力也带来稳定训练与奖励投机风险。\n\n方法：报告扩大 RL 批量与吞吐、丰富环境和 harness，并增加 grader 计算以提供组间细粒度反馈；同时采用稳定性措施应对大规模训练中的路由变化与奖励投机。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称模型在多个领域基准随训练推进而持续提升，并计划开放训练动态、环境和框架。摘要没有提供足以判断相对基线、总成本或关键消融的完整证据，也未展示改进方法自身递归更新。\n\nInsights：这提示规模化 RL 的有效性取决于环境与奖励信号质量，不是算力单变量问题；依据是论文对 grader、环境多样性及稳定性的共同强调。就 RSI 范围而言，这更像推动模型能力的训练报告，而非已证实的自我改进闭环。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"规模化强化学习; Agent 训练基础设施; 奖励信号","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者将主要贡献定位为扩大 RL 计算、环境多样性及 grader 计算，并报告模型训练期间性能提升。摘要未显示模型或训练器在多轮中递归修改自身改进机制；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：可作为规模化 agentic RL 的工程报告关注，但不宜仅凭 RSI 标题纳入递归机制进展。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12536","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12536v1","title":"EliteTable: Self-Improving Program Search for Executable Control Policies","authors":"Stuart Farmer","affiliations":"Casa Dilauro Independent Research","abstract":"EliteTable is a self-improving program-search algorithm guided by large language models (LLMs) that uses a fixed-capacity table of high-scoring solutions to guide new proposals, edits of existing solutions, and remixes of several solutions. Performance was evaluated across six Gymnasium control tasks, each with ten generations and fifty candidate slots per generation. Each task was evaluated across ten independently initialized searches. Candidate-score medians rose between the first and final generations in all six tasks, and selected-winner search-score medians rose in five. In CartPole-v1, the selected winner reached the search-score ceiling in the first generation of all ten searches. All ten paired held-out endpoints improved in four of the six tasks. BipedalWalker-v3 and CarRacing-v3 improved without reaching their reporting targets. Six of ten Acrobot-v1 searches declined on held-out episodes, and the median paired change was negative. The results document improvement during program search and the transfer of selected-winner gains to new episodes in some tasks. Comparisons and ablations are needed to establish EliteTable's relative performance and the contributions of its components.","tldr":"背景与问题：可执行控制策略可以用回报自动评估，但搜索集上保留高分程序并不保证新候选变好，也不保证收益迁移到新 episode。\n\n方法：EliteTable 将高分解保存在固定容量表中，用它们指导新程序生成、编辑和重组；候选经执行评估后再与精英竞争，留出回报不参与搜索决策。\n\n结果与结论：作者在六个 Gymnasium 任务上报告候选分数中位数均随代数上升，但留出端点仅四个任务的十次搜索全部改善；Acrobot 有六次下降且配对中位变化为负。作者承认仍需基线比较与消融，不能据此判断相对性能。\n\nInsights：这提示 RSI 证据应区分精英保留带来的搜索分数单调性与真正可迁移的能力变化；依据是 Acrobot 的搜索与留出结果分化。现有材料仅支持特定程序搜索的初步观察，不足以主张算法优势。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"程序搜索; 精英档案; 留出泛化","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称以固定容量精英表积累高分程序并用于新提案、编辑和重组，形成程序搜索反馈循环。本文证据是六个控制任务的多轮搜索及部分留出提升；作者明确指出缺少比较和消融。与 corpus 中既有程序演化方法没有匹配比较；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11803","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.11803v1","title":"PRAXIS: Learning Dynamics of Self-Improving Models with Symbolic Archives","authors":"Venkat Margapuri; Mustafa Teber","affiliations":"","abstract":"Self-improving learning systems adapt data selection, optimization, and auxiliary symbolic components, inducing nonstationary objectives outside standard learning assumptions. We introduce \\textsc{PRAXIS}, a co-evolutionary framework that models generators, learners, and symbolic archives as interacting dynamical processes. We prove that KL-constrained generator updates and controlled archive-weight movement bound one-step objective drift, that archive updates suppress a program relative to any fixed comparator with a persistent cumulative utility advantage under sub-Gaussian noise, and that stochastic gradient descent achieves an average-stationarity guarantee whose degradation is governed by cumulative objective drift. Experiments across visual robustness, relational graph reasoning, and algorithmic graph reasoning exhibit generator stabilization, decreasing learner loss, and archive concentration consistent with these theoretical mechanisms.","tldr":"背景与问题：当数据生成分布和符号辅助信号也随学习过程变化时，训练目标不再固定；传统稳定性分析可能无法覆盖这种共同演变。\n\n方法：PRAXIS 将生成器、学习器及符号档案建模为耦合动态过程，并以受约束更新控制分布漂移、按效用调整档案权重，再分析学习器在变化目标下的稳定性。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称给出目标漂移界、档案相对固定比较对象的抑制性质及随机梯度平均驻点保证，并报告三类任务实验与理论机制相符。具体实验幅度和理论条件在实际任务中的适用范围，材料不足以确认。\n\nInsights：这提示 RSI 理论不能只分析模型参数更新，还应把数据分布和外部符号信号的漂移纳入稳定性条件；这是由其联合建模提出的启发，不等于已证明这些保证覆盖大语言模型或开放式自我改进。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"非平稳学习; 符号档案; 稳定性理论","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称以生成器、学习器和符号档案构成联合动力系统，并分析目标漂移、档案抑制和优化稳定性。摘要报告理论保证及三类任务实验，但当前材料包含疑似占位作者与单位信息，无法据此确认论文记录可靠性；实验细节也不足以核验理论假设的适用范围。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11655","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.11655v1","title":"Harness Evolution Hits a Ceiling: When Weight Training Should Begin","authors":"Yuan Tian; Bing Hu; Hao Wang; Binghang Lu; Fang Wu","affiliations":"Independent Researcher；University of California, Berkeley；Purdue University；Stanford University","abstract":"Improving a long-horizon LLM agent means evolving the harness around a frozen model or training its weights. We let a self-evolving harness make the system stronger first, then cross seed and evolved harnesses with base and trained weights to learn which gains the trained model keeps and which still need the runtime. We show that the right lever can be read off the agent's failure composition: labelling failed trajectories by the first signal that fires separates process failures (blocked calls, loops, exhausted step budgets) from content failures (a delivered plan that is poor). Harness evolution repairs the former, the behaviour it instils can be trained into the weights, and content failures are what weight training is for. On DeepPlanning, a self-evolving harness loop lifts the held-out score of Qwen3.5-4B from 0.16 to 0.30 and of Qwen3.5-9B from 0.32 to 0.44; for 4B, held-out delivery rises from 55% to 90% while content failures are left for the weights. LoRA adapters trained on evolved-harness trajectories internalise the gain: under the original harness they add +0.13 on held-out tasks for both sizes; on 4B they stack with the harness to more than double the held-out score, and on 9B the adapter alone matches the full evolution line, cutting content failures from a quarter of trajectories to one in twenty. A placebo adapter trained on answer-shuffled trajectories falls below the base model. The loop transfers to WebArena-Lite (+0.09 on 117 unseen tasks), where the gain lives in what the model sees and adapters do not add to it. The result is a diagnose-then-intervene rule applied twice: read the failure composition to choose between harness and weights, then read what the accepted edits changed to decide which gains to train in. Scores are four-rollout means against fresh anchors, same-night except where marked, across eight models from six families and two benchmarks.","tldr":"背景与问题：长程 agent 失败可能来自工具阻塞、循环或步数耗尽，也可能是已交付方案本身质量差；笼统加权或改 harness，难以知道该动运行时还是模型权重。\n\n方法：论文按失败轨迹的首个触发信号区分过程故障与内容故障，先演化 harness 修复执行问题，再用演化轨迹训练 LoRA，测试哪些收益能脱离运行时内化到权重。作者还用 shuffled-answer placebo 和 fresh anchor 控制轨迹价值与选择噪声。\n\n结果与结论：作者在 DeepPlanning 报告 harness 与 adapter 对不同模型规模存在互补或替代关系，并在 WebArena-Lite 观察到迁移；该场景的增益来自运行时所见信息，adapter 未再增加收益。材料也揭示评分噪声、转换器偏差与任务范围等局限；非独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示选择干预对象前应先分解失败原因，并进一步判断 harness 改变的是模型写出的内容还是可见信息；依据是两任务的 adapter 结果差异。该诊断规则来自有限基准，失败标签阈值与评估器也会影响归因，尚非普遍定律。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"harness—权重协同; 失败诊断; 收益内化","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称先按失败组成诊断 harness 与权重应分别处理的故障，再用演化 harness 轨迹训练权重，检验收益能否内化。本文在 DeepPlanning 给出多模型、留出集、placebo adapter 和噪声分析，并报告 WebArena-Lite 迁移；具体差异是按失败类型选择干预，但没有匹配基准证明相对优势。未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：失败归因与权重训练的对照提供了可检验的干预选择规则，尚需跨任务验证。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11345","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.11345v1","title":"SynCo: Data Synthesis Co-Training for Self-Evolving LLMs via Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning","authors":"Wei Yang; Shawn Li; Yuehan Qin; Yawei Wang; Mingxi Wang; Shixuan Li; Tiankai Yang; Jiate Li; Jesse Thomason; Xuezhe Ma; Yue Zhao","affiliations":"University of Southern California；The George Washington University；Georgia Institute of Technology","abstract":"Self-evolving LLM agents promise to improve autonomously through continual interaction and learning, reducing their dependence on manually curated supervision. Realizing this promise requires not only updating the agent, but also evolving its training experience as its capabilities change. However, most existing pipelines rely on static datasets or separately updated synthesis models, causing previously useful tasks to become trivial while overly difficult tasks remain uninformative. This growing mismatch between agent capability and training experience limits sustained self-improvement. To address this problem, we propose SynCo, an agentic data synthesis co-training framework for self-evolving LLMs based on multi-agent reinforcement learning. SynCo jointly optimizes two independently parameterized agents: a Synthesizer that constructs training tasks from the Reasoner's evolving capability state, and a Reasoner that learns from the resulting experience. Each synthesized task induces multiple Reasoner rollouts whose outcomes provide complementary rewards to both agents. Correctness feedback improves the Reasoner, while task quality, answer reliability, and outcome-grounded teachability guide the Synthesizer. Their updates are fed back into subsequent synthesis rounds, allowing the task-solving policy and its training distribution to evolve together. Extensive experiments across eight mathematical reasoning benchmarks demonstrate that SynCo substantially outperforms a broad range of existing synthetic-data methods and controlled baselines, achieving the strongest overall performance while deriving most of its gains from previously unsolved problems.","tldr":"背景与问题：静态任务集会随学习者变强而变得过易，远超能力的题目又难以提供有效反馈；只定期刷新数据，仍可能让合成器与推理器各自优化、反馈脱节。\n\n方法：SynCo 让合成器根据推理器能力与任务覆盖生成可验证问题，推理器多次作答；正确性更新推理器，任务质量、可靠性及由实际作答结果估计的可教性更新合成器，之后两者共同影响下一轮课程。\n\n结果与结论：作者在八个数学基准报告优于多类合成数据基线，且多数收益来自先前未解问题；全文片段还报告，相较冻结合成器，联合训练仅略增有效训练任务比例，计算量相近。结果来自作者实验，任务范围主要为数学推理。\n\nInsights：这提示任务价值不应仅靠预估难度，而应由当前学习者的实际交互结果校准；依据是任务可教性信号及合成器对照。反馈依赖题目检查器和学习者自身行为，能否扩展到开放任务与更长训练仍未证实。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 模型—数据共演化; 多智能体强化学习","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过多智能体强化学习共同更新任务合成器与推理器；当前推理结果给合成器提供可教性信号，二者更新再改变后续任务分布与学习者。本文报告八个数学推理基准和冻结合成器对照。材料提到相关工作但没有可核验的匹配性能比较；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：贡献重点是把合成策略作为在线学习对象，而非仅周期性刷新静态训练集。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12176","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12176v1","title":"Recursive Self-Improvement through Multi-Agent Self-Supervision","authors":"Hyunin Lee; Jinglue Xu; Jeffrey Seely; Donghyun Lee; Somayeh Sojoudi; Matei Zaharia; Yujin Tang","affiliations":"加州大学伯克利分校；Sakana AI","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement (RSI) of a model on non-verifiable tasks, such as open-ended research, faces a supervision bottleneck when its outputs exceed what even human experts can reliably assess, leaving the model itself (optimizee) as the best available optimizer and evaluator. However, a single model instance struggles to critique and improve its own complex reasoning under this homogeneous loop. To address this, we propose Multi-Agent Self-Supervision (MASS), an RSI method that alternates between evolutionary workflow optimization and supervised fine-tuning on self-generated trajectories. Guided by early findings that multi-agent topologies excel at complex reasoning, MASS prompts a single base model to iteratively propose, execute, and self-evaluate multi-agent workflows. Through an evolutionary search constrained by structural guardrails, the model optimizes these computational-graph-like orchestrations, discovering the most effective distinct roles and information routing for a given task. Over two MASS cycles with Qwen3.6-27B, the model achieves 1.2-1.6x higher performance per output tokens on four open-ended public benchmarks. Because the improved model subsequently acts as a better optimizer and evaluator, this alternating framework enables a continuous, recursive bootstrapping of the model's capabilities. Moreover, multi-agent traces are also more training-efficient: a student trained on them outperforms a single-agent student trained on 1.4x more training tokens. These findings suggest that jointly learning orchestration and bounded subagent execution from multi-agent trajectories can provide an effective signal for RSI.","tldr":"背景与问题：开放式研究等任务缺少可靠自动评分，结果可能超出人类专家稳定判断的范围；但让单一模型同时求解、评价和改进自身推理，也容易受同一偏见牵制。\n\n方法：MASS 先让模型搜索多智能体工作流，调整角色分工与信息传递，再把这些工作流生成的求解轨迹用于监督微调。更新后的模型重新担任求解者、工作流优化者和评估者，从而把工作流改进产生的数据带入下一轮能力更新。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告在 Qwen3.6-27B 上经过两轮 MASS，四个开放式基准的每输出 token 表现达到基线的 1.2–1.6 倍；多智能体轨迹训练的学生也优于使用更多 token 的单智能体轨迹学生。模型、任务和轮次有限，结果尚非独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示监督瓶颈可能部分来自组织方式：分工和信息路由可产生比单体长轨迹更有效的训练信号。依据是作者报告的轨迹效率结果；由于优化与评估存在同源性，且只展示有限递归轮次，不能据此断言能在开放任务中持续自我纠错。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"多智能体工作流演化; 自生成监督与微调; 递归评估与优化","added_on":"2026-10-13","novelty_summary":"作者声称 MASS 交替优化多智能体工作流并用自生成轨迹微调共享模型，更新后的模型继续担任任务求解者、工作流优化者和评估者。本文证据包括有限轮次实验及外部强模型评估；附录将其与搜索后蒸馏、工作流搜索及联合改进方法作机制比较，但不是统一匹配性能基准。与 corpus 中 Evo²（arxiv:2610.13025）相比，MASS 优化多智能体工作流并微调模型，Evo² 训练 harness 修改和反思角色；两者没有直接比较。编辑推断：工作流轨迹为共享权重提供信号是具体增量，但同源自评与有限轮次限制递归泛化结论；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11794","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.11794v1","title":"Memento 3: Model-Based Recursive Self-Improvement through Reflective Rulebooks","authors":"Haoyu Zhao; Zhengxu Yu; Zhiyuan He; Meng Fang; Rasul Tutunov; Haitham Bou-Ammar; Weilin Luo; Jun Wang","affiliations":"伦敦大学学院；华为诺亚方舟实验室；利物浦大学","abstract":"Learning to act in unfamiliar environments requires agents to infer how the world works and revise that understanding as new evidence arrives. Yet limited observations can support multiple world models that explain past interactions but predict different outcomes in unseen states. We introduce Memento 3, building on the Memento series to enable frozen LLM agents to continually learn explicit world models through external memory. The agent maintains a natural-language rulebook as persistent semantic memory, recording revisable hypotheses about environment dynamics while leaving unknown aspects underspecified. It compiles this rulebook into executable code for prediction and planning. Through a continual loop of observation, reflection, rule revision, compilation, and verification, the agent uses prediction errors to refine both the rulebook and its code. Updated code is accepted only when the LLM judges it faithful to the rulebook and cell-exact replay reproduces the observed transitions. We investigate this process as a model-based route to recursive self-improvement (RSI): the agent autonomously explores the environment, revises its world model, and uses verified updates to guide subsequent interaction and learning, while the underlying LLM remains fixed. A population extension maintains multiple world models in parallel, sharing interaction evidence and using their predictions to guide exploration. On ARC-AGI-3, the single-model agent clears every level of all 25 public games, achieves a mean Relative Human Action Efficiency (RHAE) of 100.0, and uses 44% of the human action count. In an Atari Pong case study, a learned feedback controller wins 21:0 in each of three evaluated episodes with different openings, without further LLM calls.","tldr":"背景与问题：在陌生环境中，少量观察可能同时支持多个世界模型；它们都能解释已发生的转移，却对未见状态作出不同预测。仅靠回放已观察数据，无法判定哪套规则能正确泛化。\n\n方法：Memento 3 让冻结 LLM 把环境假设写成可修订的自然语言规则手册，再编译为用于预测和规划的代码。新观察造成的预测误差促使规则或实现修订；候选代码需符合规则手册，并精确重现已观察转移，才会被接受并用于后续交互。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告其单模型系统在 ARC-AGI-3 的 25 个公开游戏中通过所有关卡，平均 RHAE 为 100，并在 Pong 的三个不同开局案例中以 21:0 获胜。后者是有限案例；回放验证只覆盖已有转移，不能证明对未见状态的模型正确性。\n\nInsights：这提示递归改进可以发生在外部记忆与可执行模型，而不必更新权重；依据是固定 LLM 下规则—代码闭环仍能改变后续规划。关键边界是观测覆盖：通过历史回放不等于掌握环境规律，需检查探索能否区分相互竞争的假设。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"世界模型与递归改进; 外部记忆与规则更新; 预测误差反馈","added_on":"2026-10-13","novelty_summary":"作者将 Memento 3 定位为 Memento 系列从策略与程序记忆扩展到显式世界模型：冻结 LLM 以规则手册记录可修订假设，将其编译成执行模型，以预测误差更新规则与代码，并通过规则一致性判断和已观察转移回放决定是否接受。本文证据支持该闭环及 ARC-AGI-3、Pong 作者实验。与 corpus 中 RSI-Anything（arxiv:2610.13912）相比，本篇侧重冻结模型下的环境规则记忆与可执行模型，前者侧重预测模型与策略更新的联合保留；两篇未直接比较。编辑推断：回放只能核验已观察转移，未见状态泛化仍未确定；与既有可执行世界模型工作的领域优先关系未证实。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11464","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.11464v1","title":"Who Verifies the Verifier? Co-Evolving Inspectable Graders with Self-Improving Agents","authors":"Xing Zhang; Guanghui Wang; Yanwei Cui; Ziyuan Li; Wei Qiu; Bing Zhu; Peiyang He","affiliations":"AWS Forward Deployed Engineering；HSBC Holdings Plc., HSBC Technology Center, China","abstract":"We changed the agent: did it actually get better? Every self-improving agent loop answers this hundreds of times, and every answer comes from a verifier. On open-ended tasks none exists, so the loop is handed a hand-written rubric or a bare LLM judge grading output from a model like itself, inviting reward hacking and shared blind spots. We make the verifier the evolving object: an inspectable expression over small, mostly deterministic drawback detectors, synthesized from clustered failures, gated at birth, and selected for agreement with a ten-item anchored reference set plus consensus over unlabeled outputs, never for the agent's score. On MBPP+ it gains +0.21 held-out agreement over the hand-authored seed composition, on every seed, and ends ahead of the bare LLM judge it contains. One finding should change how co-evolved verifiers are validated: removing the anchor guards collapses the verifier into a vacuous always-pass grader, yet that collapsed verifier trains skills just as well. Downstream task score cannot certify a self-evolved verifier. Score does answer sufficiency, and there an evolved verifier can substitute: Double Ratchet, pairing the verifier with a lifecycle-managed skill loop, retains 88-110% of the lift that ground truth or a rubric buys the same loop, across code generation, enterprise text-to-SQL, and reference-free report generation. When evolved skills gamed the report rubric, an outer judge caught it and one added detector repaired it; the judge itself was wrong until given the task contract.","tldr":"背景与问题：自改进循环每轮都要判断 agent 是否变好，但开放任务往往没有现成 verifier；手写 rubric 或由相似模型担任 judge，可能共享盲点并诱发奖励投机。更关键的是，训练后的任务分数也未必能证明评分器本身可靠。\n\n方法：论文把 verifier 作为演化对象，由失败聚类生成可检查的细粒度缺陷检测器，再以少量锚点参考和未标注输出共识筛选组合，不按 agent 得分选 grader。之后将演化出的 grader 接入技能改进循环，并用外部锁定评估监测结果。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告 MBPP+ 留出一致性较手写初始组合提高约 0.21；消融移除锚点防护后，grader 退化为始终放行，但技能训练表现仍相近。因此，下游任务得分不足以认证自进化 verifier。结果限于指定任务、锚点和实验设置，报告生成场景也没有金标准。\n\nInsights：这提示验证器需要独立于被优化任务表现的有效性检验；依据是退化 grader 仍能支撑相近技能表现的消融。该发现针对特定任务和锚点规模，不能直接证明锚点方案普遍可靠；应将 verifier 的留出一致性与下游收益分别报告。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"评估器递归改进; 锚点监督与验证; 奖励投机与安全","added_on":"2026-10-13","novelty_summary":"作者声称将 verifier 本身作为演化对象，以失败聚类合成可检查的 drawback detectors，并用十项锚点参考与未标注输出共识选择，而非依据 agent 任务得分；Double Ratchet 将其接入技能生命周期循环。本文证据包括 MBPP+ 留出一致性结果，以及移除锚点防护后 verifier 退化为始终放行、技能训练表现却相近的消融。与 corpus 中 MASS（arxiv:2610.12176）同样涉及自评信号，但 MASS 优化工作流并用轨迹微调，本文直接演化 grader；无直接比较。编辑推断：消融揭示了验证器评估的盲点，但不足以证明此类 verifier 首创或可迁移至更广任务；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10498","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.10498v1","title":"EmbodiedRSI: Active Continual Robot Learning Through Hypothesis-Guided Co-Evolution","authors":"Python Song; Zhixuan Liang; Kelsey Fu; Mengdi Wang; Junfeng Yang; Shilong Liu","affiliations":"Columbia University；Princeton University","abstract":"Robot foundation models provide strong visuomotor control, yet their performance can degrade when object positions or task instructions change. Further improvements often require post-training on substantial robot data, which can be costly to collect through methods such as teleoperation. Agentic harnesses can adapt around the model, but current self-evolving harnesses use robot trials inefficiently when deciding which code and skill changes to pursue. We introduce EmbodiedRSI, a self-evolving agentic harness that autonomously decides where to explore next and turns the resulting physical interaction into improved code and skills. EmbodiedRSI realizes this through a Fast-Slow Dual-System Architecture, in which competing code and skill hypotheses are maintained in a Hypothesis Graph. Value-of-Information Experiment Selection chooses physical experiments that can distinguish these hypotheses. Their outcomes guide Code-Skill Co-Evolution. The Slow System builds Hierarchical Memory, and Reward-Grounded Memory Learning selects effective memory according to their value for later Fast-System improvement. On RoboCasa365, EmbodiedRSI reaches 77.0% overall success and 71.3% on Composite-Unseen, compared with 40.1% for the best baseline. EmbodiedRSI also reaches 86.8% overall success on LIBERO-Pro. Beyond benchmark performance, EmbodiedRSI transfers zero-shot to real-world robot, achieving 71.3% overall success across multiple challenging tasks.","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人微调需要昂贵交互数据；仅反复试错修改代码和技能，可能重复探索相近方向，也难判断两者组合是否真的互补。\n\n方法：EmbodiedRSI 将竞争性代码、技能假设与证据存入图中，按预期信息价值选择能区分假设的物理试验；结果驱动代码—技能联合更新，慢速记忆模块再根据后续改进价值学习保留哪些经验。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告 RoboCasa365、LIBERO-Pro 上的成功率高于所列基线，并称从模拟到真实机器人零样本迁移。摘要给出若干比例，但未提供完整任务覆盖、预算和实地重复次数；这是作者报告而非独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示昂贵交互应被视为辨别竞争解释的实验，而非单纯收集更多轨迹；依据是信息价值选试验的机制。结论边界在于假设质量、模拟到现实差异及试验预算，尚不能推断长期自主部署会持续改进。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"具身 RSI; 主动实验选择; 代码—技能共演化","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称用假设图表示代码和技能候选，以信息价值选择物理实验，再按匹配试验结果共同更新代码与技能，并按后续收益训练记忆选择。本文报告模拟基准及真实机器人迁移的作者结果；没有与 corpus 论文匹配比较，未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：将物理试验用于区分竞争假设，而非只作为反复试错，是明确的机制设计；实地泛化还需更多证据。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10426","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.10426v1","title":"CoTrace: Data Recipes for Training Terminal Agents with Harness-Model Co-Evolution","authors":"Jixuan Chen; Jiaxin Zhang; Qinyuan Ye; Yada Pruksachatkun; Haoxiang Zhang; Jingming Zhuo; Yifan Zhang; Yutong Dai; Juntao Tan; Xiangyu Peng; Silvio Savarese; Zeyuan Chen; Lianhui Qin; Chien-Sheng Wu","affiliations":"University of California, San Diego；Salesforce AI Research；University of Washington","abstract":"Terminal-agent capability depends jointly on model weights and the runtime harness that formats prompts, binds tools, and handles error recovery. Existing harness-model co-evolution approaches improve both components, yet often treat trajectories produced during harness search as an undifferentiated replay buffer. This practice overlooks that a trajectory's value for model training depends on the harness under which it was generated. To systematically analyze this interface, we establish an alternating co-evolution framework that decouples harness search and policy training through component-wise promotion decisions. Within this framework, we introduce CoTrace, a harness-aware data recipe that explicitly governs trajectory routing, provenance matching, and curriculum refresh. Under CoTrace, recurring execution failures guide harness synthesis, while policy training is strictly conditioned on verified rollouts matched to the adopted runtime for supervised fine-tuning (SFT) or fresh online interactions for reinforcement learning (RL). On the Tmax promotion split, CoTrace advances Qwen3.5-9B from 78 to 88 solved tasks under supervised fine-tuning while an online reinforcement variant reaches 90. Specifically, a compact harness-matched corpus produces steady model gains at substantially lower compute than much larger corpora pooled across sibling harnesses. Furthermore, evaluations on Terminal-Bench 2.1 and SWE-bench Lite show that out-of-distribution transfer depends fundamentally on harness compatibility, where maintaining consistency between training and evaluation runtimes prevents procedural execution breakdowns observed under foreign scaffolds.","tldr":"背景与问题：模型和 harness 交替变化时，轨迹的训练价值取决于其生成时的运行时；把不同 harness 的成功轨迹混在回放池里，可能让模型学到部署时不适用的操作程序。\n\n方法：CoTrace 将失败证据用于 harness 合成，只把已验证且与当前采用 harness 匹配的轨迹用于 SFT，或在同一运行时下生成新 RL 交互；分别固定另一组件评估候选，以避免把增益归错对象。\n\n结果与结论：作者在 Tmax promotion split 报告 Qwen3.5-9B 从 78 个解题任务升至 88（SFT）或 90（在线 RL）；紧凑匹配语料在较低计算下比跨 sibling harness 混合的大语料更稳定。外部基准结果也显示运行时兼容性影响迁移。均为作者实验。\n\nInsights：这提示数据规模不是联合演化的唯一瓶颈，轨迹来源与部署 runtime 的一致性可能决定数据是否可学；依据是匹配与混合语料的对照。结论受任务集、晋级划分和所测 harness 限制，长期运行时变化及独立复现仍待验证。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"模型—harness 共演化; 轨迹来源与匹配; 终端智能体","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称显式管理轨迹来源、harness 匹配和课程刷新，将故障轨迹路由至 harness 搜索、经验证且匹配运行时的成功轨迹用于模型训练，并按组件独立晋级。本文在 Tmax 及外部任务报告作者实验。与 corpus 中相关模型—harness 共演化工作机制相邻，但没有匹配实验比较；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：此处强调的数据来源与运行时兼容性是共演化接口的具体细化，不足以主张整体范式首创。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10310","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.10310v1","title":"RSIGym: A Flexible Environment for Recursive Self-Improvement","authors":"Fanqing Meng; Lingxiao Du; Haocheng Lu; Qiguang Chen; Ziqi Zhao; Zijian Wu; Jiayuan Zhuo; Mengkang Hu; Michael Qizhe Shieh","affiliations":"National University of Singapore；Evolvent AI","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement requires carrying accepted changes into later improvement cycles, while studying agent-proposed changes also requires substantial research infrastructure. Existing settings often leave agents to rebuild routine infrastructure or restrict exploration to individual components. We introduce RSIGym, an agent-native research environment based on Everything as a Service (EaaS). RSIGym exposes training, inference, rollout, evaluation, and sandbox execution through reusable services, with shared budget and permission controls supporting Data, Harness, and Joint improvement tracks. This design enables agents to investigate individual interventions and jointly optimize data, training settings, and execution harnesses within the same environment. We define RSI-Index as the mean fraction of the remaining performance gap closed across five benchmarks covering software engineering, terminal interaction, mathematics, scientific reasoning, and skill-based tasks. Comparing six frontier research models in independent Joint runs, Opus 5 achieves the highest RSI-Index of 0.4809 under a $500 platform-service budget per benchmark run. Its selected systems improve all five benchmarks, raising SWE-bench Verified from 17.67% to 50.33% and AIME from 31.67% to 97.78%. Additional experiments examine DSH-harness refinement, budget variation, and restricted network access, while recorded trajectories reveal how agents diagnose failures and select candidates. We open-source the full RSIGym codebase and results to support reproducibility and further research.","tldr":"背景与问题：研究 agent 若每次都需重建训练、推理和评测基础设施，预算会耗在工程准备；只开放单一组件的基准又难检验数据、权重与 harness 的交互。\n\n方法：RSIGym 将训练、推理、rollout、评测和沙箱封装为服务，并统一预算与权限；设置分轨与联合轨道，让 agent 在约束下提出、评估并选择系统修改。\n\n结果与结论：作者比较六个研究模型，报告 Opus 5 在五个基准的 RSI-Index 最高，并给出 SWE-bench Verified、AIME 的提升。关键限制是论文明确承认，所得系统是否改善后续研究循环尚未评估；因此分数表示预算内目标系统改进，不等同递归能力增强。\n\nInsights：这提示 RSI 基准应把基础设施复用、预算审计与跨轮继承作为实验条件，同时区分“改进目标系统”和“改进产生改进的过程”。该区分来自论文的范围声明；平台可支持后续研究，但当前结果不能证明递归进展。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"RSI 研究环境; 预算与权限审计; RSI 评测","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者提出共享服务、权限与预算控制的平台，支持 agent 修改数据、训练设置及 harness，并报告单轮研究运行中的系统提升。论文明确指出，所得系统是否改善后续研究循环尚待评估；这是 RSI 环境与基准贡献，不是已证实的递归闭环。与 corpus 中的其他研究环境未进行匹配性能比较。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10120","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.10120v1","title":"RewardWeaver: Long-Horizon Interactive Learning for Language Agents via Self-Evolving Reward Adaptation","authors":"Hengbo Xiao; Boyao Zhang; Purui Liu; Yuxuan Zheng; Haoran Yin; Haibo Liu; Fan Zhang","affiliations":"Yoolee.ai；University of Science and Technology of China；Peking University；Tianjin University","abstract":"Reinforcement learning with verifiable rewards (RLVR) has driven substantial progress in domains where task outcomes can be reliably evaluated, but long-horizon interaction remains challenging due to sparse terminal feedback and difficult credit assignment. Process rewards provide denser supervision, yet the capabilities most relevant for training can change as the policy evolves: a behavior that is easy to evaluate or frequently deficient need not be the bottleneck currently limiting task success. We introduce RewardWeaver, a self-evolving reward adaptation framework for language agents in long-horizon interaction. RewardWeaver maintains a validated capability space in which the semantics of admitted Rubrics remain fixed, and closes the loop between policy optimization, task evaluation, failure attribution, and reward adaptation. After each training stage, it performs outcome-grounded backward attribution on low-outcome trajectories, aggregates recurrent and policy-controlled capability bottlenecks, and dynamically selects the corresponding process rewards for the next stage. Recurrent failures not covered by the existing capability space trigger a separate, controlled expansion procedure. We evaluate REWARDWEAVER on SOTOPIA, Amazon?HistoryPrice, and a newly constructed Sales Benchmark. Across social interaction, bilateral bargaining, and domain-specific sales, REWARDWEAVER establishes new state-of-the-art (SOTA) results. Ablations further demonstrate the importance of dynamic reward allocation, failure-grounded attribution, and stable semantics for admitted capabilities.","tldr":"背景与问题：长程互动只有稀疏终局奖励，过程奖励虽更密集，却可能在策略变化后继续优化已不再是瓶颈的行为；频繁缺陷也不必然是失败原因。\n\n方法：RewardWeaver 从低结果轨迹中回溯归因，聚合反复出现且由策略控制的能力瓶颈，动态选择下一阶段过程奖励；已纳入能力的 Rubric 语义保持固定，新能力只有通过独立验证程序才可加入。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告在社交互动、议价与销售任务上优于所比较方法，并以消融支持动态分配、失败归因和语义稳定的重要性。摘要未给效果量、预算或跨模型细节，不能据此判断实际优势幅度。\n\nInsights：这提示过程奖励的关键不是不断改写评分标准，而是稳定定义能力后，随失败瓶颈变化重新分配训练信用；依据是方法对语义与当前相关性的区分。失败归因和 Rubric 评估仍可能有偏，跨领域及独立验证尚不足。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"自适应过程奖励; 失败归因; 长程交互学习","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称以低结果轨迹中的反复、可归因失败决定下一阶段启用哪些固定语义 Rubric，并通过验证程序控制新能力加入。本文摘要给出三类交互基准和消融结论，但没有提供具体量化效果；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：方法区分稳定的评价语义与动态训练优先级，是其相对一般奖励更新的具体设计差异。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.09856","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.09856v1","title":"Self-Evolve With a Reference:Anchored Training of Tool-Integrated Agents","authors":"Wenjie Liao; Liangjie Zhao; Zehong Cao","affiliations":"Waseda University；Adelaide University","abstract":"Self-evolving tool-integrated agents learn from tasks and feedback generated within their own training loop. A Curriculum Agent generates tasks, while an Executor Agent learns from self-consistency signals through reinforcement learning. However, relying solely on the current Executor for feedback has two limitations: group-relative advantages vanish under full consensus, while uncertainty-based curriculum rewards favor disagreement without showing whether the generated tasks support further learning. These limitations motivate an additional reference beyond the current Executor. We propose \\textit{AnchorLoop}, which introduces a frozen copy of the previous iteration's Executor as a historical reference and reuses it on both sides of the training loop. For the Executor, the anchor provides a cross-reference advantage that evaluates current outputs against both current and historical majority answers. For the Curriculum, it provides an agreement-based reference based on differences in sampled majority agreement. Since the Executor and anchor have identical parameters during Curriculum training, this comparison serves as a proxy for task selection rather than evidence of inter-version improvement or correctness. Across 13 reasoning benchmarks, AnchorLoop improves over Agent0 by 2.5\\% on mathematical reasoning and 2.8\\% on general reasoning tasks. It also maintains higher effective-advantage variance and continues improving in later iterations as the unanchored baseline shows diminishing gains. These results demonstrate the benefit of introducing a lightweight historical reference into self-evolving tool-integrated agents without external task or answer supervision.","tldr":"背景与问题：依赖当前策略自一致性的训练，在采样答案完全一致时相对优势消失；课程生成若只追求分歧，也无法知道题目是否真的有学习价值。\n\n方法：AnchorLoop 保留上一轮 Executor 作为冻结参考，在求解训练中比较当前答案与当前、历史多数答案；在课程训练中以两组采样一致率差异塑造任务奖励。后者只是选择代理，因为该阶段两模型参数相同，不能当作版本进步或正确性证据。\n\n结果与结论：作者在 13 个推理基准报告较 Agent0 有数学和一般推理增益，并称后续迭代仍改善，而未锚定基线趋于停滞。结果为作者实验；摘要未详列预算和各任务方差。\n\nInsights：这提示历史参照可补充当前自一致性反馈，但参照的解释必须依阶段区分；依据是作者对课程信号局限的明确界定。锚点并不自动提供真值，也不能解决完全共识时优势仍为零的问题，故泛化和抗共同错误能力仍待验证。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"历史参照反馈; 自监督强化学习; 课程生成","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者将前一轮 Executor 冻结为历史锚点，用于当前策略的交叉优势及课程任务反馈。作者明确承认课程阶段模型参数相同，采样差异不能证明跨版本进步或答案正确。本文报告 13 个推理基准结果；与 corpus 中其他工作没有匹配实验，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10623","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.10623v1","title":"Recurrent Self-Improvement: Dynamic Cross-Loop On-Policy Distillation for Looped Language Models","authors":"Yi Wang; Rui Qian; Yu Li; Haoyang Yao; Wenjie Wang","affiliations":"ShanghaiTech University；Fudan University；Southeast University；Peking University","abstract":"Looped Language Models (LoopLMs) offer a parameter efficient approach to scaling reasoning by reusing shared parameters across recurrent computation steps. Despite their promise, effective post-training of LoopLMs remains challenging. Existing approaches either provide reward based supervision that is sparse or costly to extend across loops, or rely on external teachers or privileged information, leading to limited teacher availability or teacher-student context mismatch. To address these limitations, we introduce LoopOPD, a cross-loop on-policy distillation framework that uses additional recurrent computation within a LoopLM as its own source of supervision. LoopOPD uses a frozen terminal loop policy as a compute privileged teacher for an intermediate loop student on student generated rollouts, providing dense supervision without an external teacher or privileged information. We further propose Dynamic LoopOPD (D-LoopOPD), which continually refreshes the terminal loop teacher as the shared model parameters are updated, enabling recurrent self-improvement. We characterize how distillation updates propagate across loop depths and derive sufficient conditions under which a single update yields simultaneous local improvement at both loop depths. Experiments on Ouro-Thinking models show that LoopOPD improves mathematical reasoning, while D-LoopOPD yields further gains through dynamic teacher updates. Despite being trained only on mathematical data, the resulting models also improve on general reasoning and code generation benchmarks, demonstrating that recurrent computation can serve as an effective source of supervision for LoopLMs. Our code and model checkpoints will be released upon acceptance.","tldr":"背景与问题：LoopLM 用共享参数反复计算，却难以把稀疏的终局奖励直接分配给中间循环；外部教师可能不可得，带特权信息的自蒸馏又会造成师生上下文不匹配。\n\n方法：LoopOPD 让中间循环在自身生成的轨迹上匹配终端循环的 token 分布，将额外循环计算变成密集监督。D-LoopOPD 每步改用当前终端循环作教师；学生更新共享参数后，终端教师也随之改变，并在后续步骤继续提供监督。\n\n结果与结论：在 Ouro-Thinking 上，作者报告 LoopOPD 改善数学推理，动态教师进一步优于冻结教师；全文片段给出 Ouro-2.6B-Thinking 的 AIME 2024 Avg@16 从 62.08 升至 71.67，并称跨循环深度均有改善。跨任务收益限于数学训练后的指定推理和代码基准。\n\nInsights：这里值得检验的不是“自蒸馏是否有效”，而是共享参数是否能把中间循环的学习稳定传回终端策略；论文的局部改进定理也要求梯度对齐等条件。因此，机制成立依赖特定更新几何，不能推成共享参数更新普遍有益。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"循环语言模型; 跨循环蒸馏; 递归自改进","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称 LoopOPD 以模型的额外循环计算监督中间循环，D-LoopOPD 再利用共享参数更新后的终端循环动态刷新教师。本文证据包括跨循环更新分析及 Ouro-Thinking 作者实验，全文片段报告数学推理改善，并给出 AIME 2024 Avg@16 结果。相对 OPD 与 OPSD，具体差异是教师优势来自额外循环计算，且师生在同一前缀上生成分布；这些是本文对既有机制的比较，不是与 corpus 中独立论文的匹配实验。编辑判断：这是循环模型内部监督的具体推进；未证实领域级新颖性，且没有独立复现。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10611","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.10611v1","title":"Verification and Self-Improvement in Agentic AI: Foundations and Limits","authors":"Chien-Ping Lu","affiliations":"","abstract":"Agentic AI systems can improve by searching longer, receiving additional support, or modifying how they propose and verify outputs. A performance score does not distinguish these mechanisms. We compare these changes through bounded verification with hidden terminal randomness. A stage specifies admissible transcripts, polynomial bounds, an alternating verification protocol, and a terminal checker. Its native reach uses default support; its closure frontier permits all support already admitted by the interface. Under a uniform pointwise probability gap and task-relative soundness, these are well-defined languages. We prove that independent majority amplification preserves both languages, whereas existential acceptance over random tapes can admit incorrect outputs. Exact verification is the zero-randomness case, with placement and completeness results. The randomized-verifier classes satisfy $Σ_k^{\\mathrm{P}}\\subseteqΣ_k^{\\mathrm{RV}}\\subseteqΣ_{k+1}^{\\mathrm{P}}$; strict enlargement and depth separation require explicit complexity assumptions, while $\\mathrm{BPP}=\\mathrm{P}$ yields exact companions with the same frontiers. Representation analysis separates invariant acceptance from core-versus-support labels that can change under refactoring. For recursive self-improvement, uniformly bounded self-modification under a common sound interpreter and fixed verification protocol remains within the same verification class. A separate conditional-error budget controls false selection across adaptively chosen candidates. A quota-enforced XOR-synthesis family separates unbounded ratios of search success from changes in the accepted languages; exact and probabilistic audits check the resulting evidence requirements. The framework ties self-improvement claims to obligations on correctness, admissible evidence, verification resources, and selection error.","tldr":"背景与问题：成功率上升可能来自搜索更久、获得更多支持或改变检查器；单看分数无法判断系统只是更容易找到已有解，还是扩展了可接受的正确任务范围。\n\n方法：论文将系统阶段表示为有界交互、支持接口、验证协议与终端检查器，分别定义默认支持下的可达范围和接口许可支持下的范围。它证明独立多数放大保留这两种范围，而随机带上任一次通过可能错误接纳输出；另为自修改和候选选择规定错误预算。\n\n结果与结论：在共同可靠解释器和固定验证协议等条件下，有界递归自修改仍处于同一验证类；有限 XOR 合成例区分搜索成功率提高与接受语言改变。这是条件性理论结果，不是现实 agent 的经验检验。\n\nInsights：该框架把“性能更好”拆成搜索、接口和验证语义三种可分别核查的变化；但其保证依赖明确的可靠性合同，不能直接认证只有经验准确率的学习型评估器。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; 验证理论; 选择误差","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者提出以有界验证、任务正确性和可容许证据，形式化区分搜索效率改善、支持接口变化与接受边界变化；关于递归自修改的结论依赖共同可靠解释器、固定验证协议和一致有界修改等前提。本文证据是复杂性理论推导及有限 XOR 合成实例，并非 agent 性能实验。corpus 中没有可直接比较的形式化工作；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑判断：其贡献在于明确 RSI 主张需要何种正确性与选择误差证据，不是证明现实系统已满足这些条件。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.09426","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.09426v1","title":"RSI-Forge: From Research Papers to Environments for Recursive Self-Improvement","authors":"Renxiong Wang; Darvin Yi; Abril Herrlein; Anas Mahmoud; Advait Gosai; Lisiman Hua; MohammadHossein Rezaei; Xingang Guo; Anisha Gunjal; Utkarsh Tyagi; David J. Lee; Minglai Yang; Haris Riaz; Chenguang Wang; Huaxiu Yao; Daniel Yue Zhang; Aakash Sabharwal; Tong Zhao; Yunzhong He","affiliations":"Scale AI；University of California, Santa Cruz；University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill","abstract":"Environments are the foundation of recursive self-improvement: they provide the problems agents work on and the feedback used to evaluate progress. Yet constructing challenging research environments with reliable evaluation still depends on domain experts, limiting their scale and disciplinary coverage. We introduce RSI-Forge, a multi-agent pipeline that turns published papers into executable environments for self-improvement. Three agents coordinate construction, reproduction, and review to produce tasks with automated evaluators; each paper's method is independently reimplemented to establish a baseline score. We present 210 environments across 18 fields, including 90 reviewed by independent human domain experts. Both experts and agent judges give high ratings to the potential for improving the provided starting solutions and the evaluators' ability to distinguish solution quality, whereas experts are more critical of shortcut resistance, faithfulness to the source paper, and whether a single idea can exhaust a task. To validate their use for repeated improvement, we evaluate four models over 3 successive attempts on 120 environments, with each attempt inheriting prior code and notes while model weights remain fixed. At least one model improves after the first attempt in 84% of environments. Models also outperform the reproduced paper methods in 68 of the 120 environments, demonstrating room for gains beyond these baselines. Transcript analysis identifies work beyond parameter tuning in 95% of these successful attempts. Analysis of the resulting trajectories shows that models scoring lower on these tasks explore less, more often accept gains smaller than the reported standard error, and rely more heavily on tuning to the development set. RSI-Forge provides a scalable approach to constructing research environments for training and evaluating self-improving agents.","tldr":"背景与问题：研究型 RSI 需要有挑战的任务、可靠评估和可比较基线，但逐领域依赖专家设计限制了规模；自动生成又可能带来捷径、失真或不可解任务。\n\n方法：RSI-Forge 将任务构建、论文方法复现和环境审查分配给不同角色，分别产出可执行任务与评估器、独立基线，并检查说明和评分是否对应。随后固定模型权重，让 agent 继承先前代码和笔记，检验环境是否支持连续修改。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告构建 210 个、覆盖 18 个领域的环境，其中 90 个经领域专家审阅；在 120 个环境的三次尝试中，至少一个模型在首轮后有所改善的环境占 84%，68 个环境超过复现方法基线。专家对捷径抵抗、来源忠实度及单一想法能否耗尽任务更为审慎。\n\nInsights：环境生成的价值不只是扩充题量，还在于提供可复现基线和分工审查；但专家指出的质量缺口与已观察到的评估材料访问风险，说明环境数量及分数不能单独证明测量可靠。固定权重结果也不代表改进器本身变强。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"RSI 研究环境; 环境生成与评估; Harness 智能体迭代","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称 RSI-Forge 将论文转为可执行研究环境，由构建、独立复现和审查环节生成任务、评估器与复现基线。本文证据包括 210 个环境、90 个环境的人类领域专家评审，以及固定权重模型继承代码和笔记的三次尝试；因此测试的是环境支持的工件迭代，而非权重或改进器递归进化。与 corpus 中 RSIGym（arxiv:2610.10310）相比，本篇聚焦从论文构建环境和复现基线；没有匹配性能比较。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.09239","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.09239v1","title":"The Winner's Curse in LLM Self-Improvement Loops: Selection Noise, Lock-in, and Acceptance Rules","authors":"Litao Hu; Yutong Tang","affiliations":"Meta；Microsoft","abstract":"Self-improving LLM systems propose changes to themselves and keep those that score better on a small evaluation set. We treat this keep-if-better step as selection under measurement noise, model the correlated errors of the candidates in a single decision, and study empirically what happens when the evaluation set is reused. In runs where Qwen models rewrite their own instructions and every candidate is also scored on 600 held-out items, most proposals after the first are harmful, and the model gives the size of the winner's curse of a generation's best candidate. With a prior from a separate pilot, it matches the average overstatement of first-generation commits in native loops, though not setting by setting. In a pre-registered study, the final selection-set score of greedy loops exceeded held-out accuracy by 13 to 20 points with 16 selection items and by 1 to 5 points with 256. Held-out gains grew with the selection set on TREC but not on GSM8K, and the tested acceptance rules did not beat greedy acceptance over whole runs. Gains measured on the selection set also exceeded held-out gains when a current model refined a competent instruction, and in the validation scores of GEPA and MIPROv2. Scoring the starting and the current instruction on 64 items never used for selection removes the average bias of a loop's reported gain, but single estimates remain off by about 6 points. Self-improvement studies should report held-out gains with their uncertainty.","tldr":"背景与问题：自改进系统常在小评测集上提出多个修改，再保留分数最高者；被选分数会受选择噪声抬高，重复使用同一集合还会改变后续比较的基线。\n\n方法：论文把保留候选视为相关误差下的噪声选择，并用独立留出集估计真实收益。作者比较多种接受门槛与确认程序，再以预注册实验检验这些规则是否改善完整运行，而非只看单次决策。\n\n结果与结论：预注册研究中，16 项选择集上的贪心循环最终选择分数比留出准确率高 13–20 个百分点；256 项时差距缩至 1–5 点。测试的接受规则在完整运行中没有稳定胜过贪心策略；另用未参与选择的 64 项评分可校正平均偏差，但单次估计仍约有 6 点误差。证据覆盖特定指令改写任务及 GEPA、MIPROv2 验证分数检查。\n\nInsights：结果把研究重点从设计更复杂的接受规则，转向独立报告留出收益和不确定性；依据是接受规则未稳定改善整轮结果，而扩大选择集可缩小高估。它不说明自改进普遍无效，只说明复用评测集上的分数不足以独立证明收益。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"自改进评估可靠性; 选择噪声; 留出评估","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者将 keep-if-better 建模为相关候选在有限评测集上的噪声选择，并用 oracle-instrumented 运行、原生循环和预注册研究检验收益高估与接受规则。本文证据显示小型选择集会扩大选择分数与留出表现的差距；未参与选择的 64 项评分能消除平均报告偏差，但单次估计仍有误差。相对 PACE 与 SIREN（仅为本文引用的既有工作，corpus 无对应独立条目），本篇关注循环内部的候选相关误差和整轮接受表现；无 corpus 匹配比较，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=kSuRY5sCuR","url":"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=kSuRY5sCuR","title":"Beyond Majority Voting: Self-Reflective Test-Time Reinforcement Learning for LLM Reasoning","authors":"Sitong Wu; Haoru Tan; Xichen Zhang; Bin Xia; Shaofeng Zhang; Xiaojuan Qi; Bei Yu; Jiaya Jia","affiliations":"原笔记：HKU","abstract":"The core challenge of Test-Time Reinforcement Learning (TTRL) lies in estimating rewards without access to ground-truth supervision. Existing TTRL methods predominantly rely on majority voting to generate pseudo-labels, under the assumption that the most frequent answer among sampled trajectories is correct. However, we observe that this assumption frequently breaks down in complex reasoning tasks, where correct solutions often constitute a logical minority. As a result, rare yet correct trajectories are systematically undervalued by majority-voting-based approaches. To address this limitation, we propose Self-Reflective Test-Time Reinforcement Learning (SR-TTRL), a novel framework that leverages self-reflective verification to produce high-fidelity pseudo-labels. Specifically, given multiple sampled trajectories for a problem, SR-TTRL first groups trajectories according to their final answers and selects one representative from each group to form a candidate pool. Each candidate trajectory is then summarized to preserve its core reasoning steps while reducing verbosity. Finally, the model performs self-reflection over the candidate pool, critically evaluating and selecting the most plausible trajectory as the pseudo-label. Empirically, SR-TTRL achieves substantially higher pseudo-label fidelity and sample efficiency than prior majority-voting-based TTRL methods. Extensive experiments across diverse benchmarks and model families demonstrate that SR-TTRL consistently outperforms majority-voting baselines and significantly improves generalization to novel problems. For example, SR-TTRL improves the Pass@1 accuracy of Qwen3-8B on AIME24 from 29.1 to 55.8 (a gain of +26.7), exceeding standard TTRL by an additional +9.1. The code will be released at: https://github.com/JIA-Lab-research/SR-TTRL.","tldr":"SR-TTRL 将候选推理轨迹按答案分组、提炼关键步骤，再通过自反思选择伪标签，降低多数投票忽略少数正确答案的问题。","published_at":"2026-09-29","topics":"挖掘信号：Test-time Training","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2607.22688","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.22688v1","title":"Co-Harness: Co-Evolving Harnesses and Model Weights for LLM Agents","authors":"Zhengyu Chen; Teng Xiao; Huaisheng Zhu; Yige Yuan; Luan Zhang; Jingang Wang","affiliations":"原笔记：美团","abstract":"Post-training agents for automated AI research requires optimizing not only model parameters, but also the runtime harness that shapes how research trajectories are generated, evaluated, and learned from. Existing pipelines typically train models under a fixed harness, including prompts, tools, skills, middleware, and memory, while leaving the data-generating process outside the optimization objective. This creates a mismatch between model updates and the static scaffolding that determines trajectory quality. We introduce Co-Harness, a framework that jointly optimizes the agent harness and model parameters during post-training. Co-Harness alternates between harness optimization and model optimization. An LLM-based HarnessCritic analyzes failed trajectories, identifies harness-level failure modes, and proposes validated local updates. The model is then fine-tuned on high-quality trajectories generated by the improved harness, distilling effective scaffolding into model parameters. A 200+ hour autonomous case study further shows that Co-Harness can recover from system crashes, improve inference efficiency, and discover ensemble strategies without human intervention. These results suggest that joint harness and model optimization is an effective way to improve agents beyond fixed-harness post-training.","tldr":"Co-Harness 通过交替执行“基于失败轨迹的 HarnessCritic 局部修补”和“利用改进 Harness 生成的高质量轨迹进行 SFT”，让 Agent 的harness与weight共同进化，形成“更好 Harness → 更好训练数据 → 更强模型”的闭环。","published_at":"2026-07-17","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2607.03935","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.03935v1","title":"Harness-Aware Self-Evolving: Co-Evolving Model Weights, Harness, and Task Solutions","authors":"Haochen Luo; Yi Huang; Sichun Luo; Fengyuan Liu; Lei Li; Zefa Hu; Junlan Feng; Qi Liu","affiliations":"原笔记：HKU & China Mobile Jiutian","abstract":"Self-evolving frameworks usually optimize task solutions while treating the surrounding harness as fixed. We introduce Harness-Aware Self-Evolving (HASE), an agentic reinforcement-learning framework in which a single model can generate task solutions or edit selected harness components in a multi-turn action space. HASE enables a single Qwen3-8B model to match the text-classification performance of a GPT-OSS-120B model that uses Claude Code as the harness proposer. In alpha factor mining, HASE outperforms the reported GPT-OSS-120B baseline. HASE also repairs imperfect evaluation components and converges to state-of-the-art performance in circle-packing algorithm discovery. These results show that HASE improves the harness and the solution through one unified agentic process.","tldr":"HASE 将任务解、模型权重与可编辑 Harness 放进同一个 agentic RL action space，使单个小模型能够一边解题，一边持续改进自己的 guidance / evaluation harness。","published_at":"2026-07-04","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2606.09498","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.09498v3","title":"Self-Harness: Harnesses That Improve Themselves","authors":"Hangfan Zhang; Shao Zhang; Kangcong Li; Chen Zhang; Yang Chen; Yiqun Zhang; Lei Bai; Shuyue Hu","affiliations":"原笔记：Shanghai AI lab","abstract":"The performance of LLM-based agents is jointly shaped by their base models and the harnesses that mediate their interaction with the environment. Because different models exhibit distinct behaviors, effective harness design is inherently model-specific. Yet agent harnesses are still largely engineered by human experts, a paradigm that scales poorly as modern LLMs become increasingly diverse and rapidly evolving. In this paper, we introduce Self-Harness, a new paradigm in which an LLM-based agent improves its own operating harness, without relying on human engineers or stronger external agents. We operationalize Self-Harness as an iterative loop with three stages: Weakness Mining, which identifies model-specific failure patterns from execution traces; Harness Proposal, which generates diverse yet minimal harness modifications tied to these failures; and Proposal Validation, which accepts candidate edits only after regression testing. We instantiate Self-Harness across Terminal-Bench-2.0, SWE-bench Verified, and AppWorld using a minimal initial harness and three base models from diverse families: MiniMax M2.5, Qwen3.5-35B-A3B, and GLM-5. Across all nine model--benchmark combinations, every final harness improves both held-in and held-out pass rates, with overall relative gains of up to 132%. Qualitative analyses further show that the retained mechanisms address benchmark-specific bottlenecks in artifact handling and runtime control, software-patch verification, and application-state retrieval. These results suggest a path toward LLM-based agents that are not merely shaped by their harnesses, but can also participate in reshaping them.","tldr":"Self-Harness 使 LLM Agent 能够基于自身执行反馈自主改进自身 Harness，并通过回归验证迭代优化，无需人工或更强外部模型介入。","published_at":"2026-06-08","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2606.05922","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.05922v3","title":"Evolving Agents in the Dark: Retrospective Harness Optimization via Self-Preference","authors":"Wenbo Pan; Shujie Liu; Chin-Yew Lin; Jingying Zeng; Xianfeng Tang; Xiangyang Zhou; Yan Lu; Xiaohua Jia","affiliations":"原笔记：cityu","abstract":"AI agents rely on a harness of skills, tools, and workflows to solve complex problems. Continually improving this harness is essential for adapting to new tasks. However, existing optimization methods typically require ground-truth validation sets, yet such labeled data is difficult to acquire in practical deployment settings. To address this problem, we introduce Retrospective Harness Optimization (RHO), a self-supervised method that optimizes the agent harness using only past trajectories. Specifically, RHO selects a diverse coreset of challenging tasks from past trajectories and re-solves them in parallel. The agent analyzes these rollouts using self-validation and self-consistency, then generates candidate harness updates and selects the most effective one by its own pairwise self-preference. We evaluate RHO across three diverse domains, spanning software engineering, technical work, and knowledge work. Notably, a single optimization round improves the pass rate on SWE-Bench Pro from 59% to 78% without any external grading. Furthermore, our analysis demonstrates that RHO effectively targets prior failure modes. As a result, the optimized harness alters the agent's behavior patterns and sustains higher accuracy during long-horizon sessions.","tldr":"RHO利用历史轨迹中的自监督信号替代validation feedback，实现无需verifier的Agent harness持续优化。","published_at":"2026-06-04","topics":"挖掘信号：Test-time Training","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2606.03108","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.03108v2","title":"EvoTrainer: Co-Evolving LLM Policies and Training Harnesses for Autonomous Agentic Reinforcement Learning","authors":"Guhong Chen; Yingcheng Shi; Yongbin Li; Binhua Li; Xander Xu; Hu Wei; Shiwen Ni; Min Yang; Jieping Ye","affiliations":"原笔记：中科院 & 阿里","abstract":"Autonomous LLM training is often framed as recipe search, which leaves the training harness largely static. This limitation sharpens in agentic RL, where shifting bottlenecks and scalar rewards mask diverse failure modes. We introduce EvoTrainer, an autonomous training framework that co-evolves LLM policies and training-side harnesses through empirical feedback: it diagnoses rollout-level evidence, revises diagnostics, backtests interventions, and accumulates reusable skills. Evaluated on mathematical reasoning, competitive-programming code generation, and repository-level software engineering, EvoTrainer matches or exceeds the human-engineered RL references under the same data, codebase, and evaluation protocol, with the largest gain on long-horizon agentic SWE. Trajectory analyses show that retained strategies diverge across domains, evolving diagnostics prevent invalid high-scoring branches from being promoted, and reusable skills shape later search. Autonomous LLM RL should move beyond recipe search toward joint evolution of policies and the training harnesses that interpret them.","tldr":"AutoML的工作，提出了一种让LLM RL中的模型策略与训练诊断流程共同进化的新框架，通过版本化实验、动态诊断升级和技能复用，在数学、编程和软件工程任务上超越了人工设计的RL基线。","published_at":"2026-06-02","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.27276","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27276v2","title":"SIA: Self Improving AI with Harness & Weight Updates","authors":"Prannay Hebbar; Yogendra Manawat; Samuel Verboomen; Alesia Ivanova; Selvam Palanimalai; Kunal Bhatia; Vignesh Baskaran","affiliations":"原笔记：Hexo labs","abstract":"Humans are the bottleneck in building and improving AI. Both the models and the agents that wrap them are written, tuned, and corrected by people. The long-horizon goal of an AI that can figure out how to improve itself remains open. Two largely disjoint research lines attack this bottleneck. The harness-update school has a meta-agent rewrite the scaffold of a task-specific agent (its tools, prompts, retry logic, and search procedure) while the model weights are held fixed. The test-time training school uses hand-written RL pipelines to update the model's own weights on task feedback while the harness is held fixed. These two silos operate in isolation. We propose SIA, a self-improving loop in which a language-model agent (the Feedback-Agent) updates both the harness and the weights of a task-specific agent. We evaluate across three contrasting domains: Chinese legal charge classification, low-level GPU kernel optimisation, and single-cell RNA denoising. Combining both levers outperforms scaffold iteration alone on all three benchmarks. SIA-W+H achieves 25.1% over prior SOTA on LawBench, 12.4% faster GPU kernels than prior SOTA (1,017 vs 1,161 μs), and 20.4% over prior SOTA on denoising. Harness updates make the model agentic, shaping how it searches and acts, while weight updates build the domain intuition that no prompt or scaffold can instil.","tldr":"This paper proposes SIA, a framework that allows an AI agent to improve both its external reasoning system (the harness/scaffold) and its internal model parameters (weights) in a single feedback loop, rather than improving only one of them.","published_at":"2026-05-26","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.11328","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.11328v1","title":"Epistemic Uncertainty for Test-Time Discovery","authors":"Kainat Riaz; Muhammad Ahmed Mohsin; Ahsan Bilal; Muhammad Umer; Ayesha Mohsin; Aqib Riaz; Ali Subhan; John M. Cioffi","affiliations":"原笔记：stanford","abstract":"Automated scientific discovery using large language models relies on identifying genuinely novel solutions. Standard reinforcement learning penalizes high-variance mutations, which leads the policy to prioritize familiar patterns. As a result, the maximum reward plateaus even as the average reward increases. Overcoming this limitation requires a signal that distinguishes unexplored regions from intrinsically difficult problems. This necessitates measuring disagreement across independently adapted weight hypotheses rather than relying on a single network's confidence. UG-TTT addresses this challenge by maintaining a small ensemble of low-rank adapters over a frozen base model. The per-token disagreement, quantified as the mutual information between ensemble predictions and weight hypotheses, isolates epistemic uncertainty and identifies positions where insufficient coverage leads to adapter divergence rather than intrinsic problem difficulty. This measure is incorporated as an exploration bonus into the policy gradient, directing the policy toward positions where persistent adapter disagreement signals low training coverage, the same frontier where genuine discovery is possible. A nuclear norm regularizer ensures the adapters remain distinct from one another, thereby preserving the exploration signal throughout training. Across four scientific discovery benchmarks, UG-TTT increases the maximum reward on three tasks, maintains substantially higher solution diversity, and an ablation study confirms that the regularizer is essential for sustaining this behavior.","tldr":"训练时维护多个模型副本，在ttt-discover的advantage基础上引入“分歧奖励”：对于一个轨迹，如果不同模型（1）各自都很确定，i.e. entropy低 且（2）（原笔记未写完，待补充。）","published_at":"2026-05-11","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.09998","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.09998v1","title":"Continual Harness: Online Adaptation for Self-Improving Foundation Agents","authors":"Seth Karten; Joel Zhang; Tersoo Upaa; Ruirong Feng; Wenzhe Li; Chengshuai Shi; Chi Jin; Kiran Vodrahalli","affiliations":"原笔记：princeton","abstract":"Coding harnesses such as Claude Code and OpenHands wrap foundation models with tools, memory, and planning, but no equivalent exists for embodied agents' long-horizon partial-observability decision-making. We first report our Gemini Plays Pokemon (GPP) experiments. With iterative human-in-the-loop harness refinement, GPP became the first AI system to complete Pokemon Blue, Yellow Legacy on hard mode, and Crystal without a lost battle. In the hardest stages, the agent itself began iterating on its strategy through long-context memory, surfacing emergent self-improvement signals alongside human-in-the-loop refinement. Continual Harness removes the human fully from this loop: a reset-free self-improving harness for embodied agents that formalizes and automates what we observed. Starting from only a minimal environment interface, the agent alternates between acting and refining its own prompt, sub-agents, skills, and memory, drawing on any past trajectory data. Prompt-optimization methods require episode resets; Continual Harness adapts online within a single run. On Pokemon Red and Emerald across frontier models, Continual Harness starting from scratch substantially reduces button-press cost relative to the minimalist baseline and recovers a majority of the gap to a hand-engineered expert harness, with capability-dependent gains, despite starting from the same raw interface with no curated knowledge, no hand-crafted tools, and no domain scaffolding. We then close the loop with the model itself: an online process-reward co-learning loop, in which an open-source agent's rollouts through the refining harness are relabeled by a frontier teacher and used to update the model, drives sustained in-game milestone progress on Pokemon Red without resetting the environment between training iterations.","tldr":"Agent 在任务执行过程中持续演化自身 Harness，而非等任务结束后再优化，使 Agent 能在长期任务中持续积累经验并提升能力。","published_at":"2026-05-11","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.07039","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.07039v1","title":"PACEvolve++: Improving Test-time Learning for Evolutionary Search Agents","authors":"Minghao Yan; Bo Peng; Benjamin Coleman; Ziqi Chen; Zhouhang Xie; Shuo Chen; Zhankui He; Noveen Sachdeva; Weili Wang; Ed H. Chi; Shivaram Venkataraman; Wang-Cheng Kang; Derek Zhiyuan Cheng; Beidou Wang","affiliations":"原笔记：google","abstract":"Large language models have become drivers of evolutionary search, but most systems rely on a fixed, prompt-elicited policy to sample next candidates. This limits adaptation in practical engineering and research tasks, where evaluations are expensive, and progress depends on learning task-specific search dynamics. We introduce PACEvolve++, an advisor-model reinforcement learning framework for test-time policy adaptation in evolutionary search agents. PACEvolve++ decouples strategic search decisions from implementation: a trainable advisor generates, assesses, and selects hypotheses, while a stronger frontier model translates selected hypotheses into executable candidates. To train the advisor under non-stationary feedback, we propose a phase-adaptive approach that adapts its optimization strategy to different phases of the evolutionary process. Early in evolution, it uses group-relative feedback to learn broad search preferences; later, as reward gaps compress, it emphasizes best-of-$k$ frontier contribution to support stable refinement. Across expert-parallel load balancing, sequential recommendation, and protein fitness extrapolation, PACEvolve++ outperforms the state-of-the-art evolutionary search framework with frontier models, achieving faster convergence and stabilizing test-time training during evolutionary search.","tldr":"Test-time RL，提出两点改进：（1）框架上，解耦idea提出和代码实现，将“提出和选择假设”交给可训练的Advisor模型，将代码实现交给更强的frontier model；（2）采用阶段自适应RL信号：早期使用GRPO式组内相对反馈鼓励探索，后期转向Max@k式前沿贡献信号进行精炼，从而兼顾搜索多样性、收敛速度与训练稳定性。","published_at":"2026-05-07","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2604.25850","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.25850v4","title":"Agentic Harness Engineering: Observability-Driven Automatic Evolution of Coding-Agent Harnesses","authors":"Jiahang Lin; Shichun Liu; Chengjun Pan; Lizhi Lin; Shihan Dou; Zhiheng Xi; Xuanjing Huang; Hang Yan; Zhenhua Han; Tao Gui; Yu-Gang Jiang","affiliations":"原笔记：复旦&北大","abstract":"Harnesses are now central to coding-agent performance, mediating how models interact with tools and execution environments. Yet harness engineering remains a manual craft, because automating it faces a heterogeneous action space across editable components, voluminous trajectories that bury actionable signal, and edits whose effect is hard to attribute. We introduce Agentic Harness Engineering (AHE), a closed loop that addresses these challenges through three matched observability pillars: (1) component observability gives every editable harness component a file-level representation so the action space is explicit and revertible; (2) experience observability distills millions of raw trajectory tokens into a layered, drill-down evidence corpus that an evolving agent can actually consume; and (3) decision observability pairs every edit with a self-declared prediction, later verified against the next round's task-level outcomes. Together, these pillars turn every edit into a falsifiable contract, so harness evolution proceeds autonomously without collapsing into trial-and-error. Empirically, ten AHE iterations lift pass@1 on Terminal-Bench 2 from 69.7% to 77.0%, surpassing the human-designed harness Codex-CLI (71.9%) and the self-evolving baselines ACE and TF-GRPO. The frozen harness transfers without re-evolution: on SWE-bench-verified it tops aggregate success at 12% fewer tokens than the seed, and on Terminal-Bench 2 it yields +5.1 to +10.1pp cross-family gains across three alternate model families, indicating the evolved components encode general engineering experience rather than benchmark-specific tuning. Ablations localize the gain to tools, middleware, and long-term memory rather than the system prompt, suggesting factual harness structure transfers while prose-level strategy does not.","tldr":"AHE shifts Harness evolution from end-to-end coupled program optimization (e.g. Meta-Harness) toward component-aware, evidence-driven engineering with explicit observability and rollback.","published_at":"2026-04-28","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.28052","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.28052v1","title":"Meta-Harness: End-to-End Optimization of Model Harnesses","authors":"Yoonho Lee; Roshen Nair; Qizheng Zhang; Kangwook Lee; Omar Khattab; Chelsea Finn","affiliations":"原笔记：stanford","abstract":"The performance of large language model (LLM) systems depends not only on model weights, but also on their harness: the code that determines what information to store, retrieve, and present to the model. Yet harnesses are still designed largely by hand, and existing text optimizers are poorly matched to this setting because they compress feedback too aggressively. We introduce Meta-Harness, an outer-loop system that searches over harness code for LLM applications. It uses an agentic proposer that accesses the source code, scores, and execution traces of all prior candidates through a filesystem. On online text classification, Meta-Harness improves over a state-of-the-art context management system by 7.7 points while using 4x fewer context tokens. On retrieval-augmented math reasoning, a single discovered harness improves accuracy on 200 IMO-level problems by 4.7 points on average across five held-out models. On agentic coding, discovered harnesses surpass the best hand-engineered baselines on TerminalBench-2. Together, these results show that richer access to prior experience can enable automated harness engineering.","tldr":"将 LLM 系统的 harness 作为优化对象，通过在目标任务上反复执行、保留完整 execution traces 并让 coding agent 直接分析历史代码与日志（依赖强agent分析），实现端到端自动 harness engineering。","published_at":"2026-03-30","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.19461","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.19461v1","title":"Hyperagents","authors":"Jenny Zhang; Bingchen Zhao; Wannan Yang; Jakob Foerster; Jeff Clune; Minqi Jiang; Sam Devlin; Tatiana Shavrina","affiliations":"原笔记：University of British Columbia & Meta","abstract":"Self-improving AI systems aim to reduce reliance on human engineering by learning to improve their own learning and problem-solving processes. Existing approaches to self-improvement rely on fixed, handcrafted meta-level mechanisms, fundamentally limiting how fast such systems can improve. The Darwin Gödel Machine (DGM) demonstrates open-ended self-improvement in coding by repeatedly generating and evaluating self-modified variants. Because both evaluation and self-modification are coding tasks, gains in coding ability can translate into gains in self-improvement ability. However, this alignment does not generally hold beyond coding domains. We introduce \\textbf{hyperagents}, self-referential agents that integrate a task agent (which solves the target task) and a meta agent (which modifies itself and the task agent) into a single editable program. Crucially, the meta-level modification procedure is itself editable, enabling metacognitive self-modification, improving not only the task-solving behavior, but also the mechanism that generates future improvements. We instantiate this framework by extending DGM to create DGM-Hyperagents (DGM-H), eliminating the assumption of domain-specific alignment between task performance and self-modification skill to potentially support self-accelerating progress on any computable task. Across diverse domains, the DGM-H improves performance over time and outperforms baselines without self-improvement or open-ended exploration, as well as prior self-improving systems. Furthermore, the DGM-H improves the process by which it generates new agents (e.g., persistent memory, performance tracking), and these meta-level improvements transfer across domains and accumulate across runs. DGM-Hyperagents offer a glimpse of open-ended AI systems that do not merely search for better solutions, but continually improve their search for how to improve.","tldr":"把\"执行任务的Agent（Task Agent）\"和\"负责修改Agent的Meta Agent\"统一成一个可以修改自己的程序（HyperAgent），再结合Darwin Gödel Machine（DGM）的开放式进化框架，实现任务能力和自我改进能力的共同进化。","published_at":"2026-03-19","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.23413","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.23413v2","title":"EvoX: Meta-Evolution for Automated Discovery","authors":"Shu Liu; Shubham Agarwal; Monishwaran Maheswaran; Mert Cemri; Zhifei Li; Qiuyang Mang; Ashwin Naren; Ethan Boneh; Audrey Cheng; Melissa Z. Pan; Alexander Du; Kurt Keutzer; Alvin Cheung; Alexandros G. Dimakis; Koushik Sen; Matei Zaharia; Ion Stoica","affiliations":"原笔记：UCB","abstract":"Recent work such as AlphaEvolve has shown that combining LLM-driven optimization with evolutionary search can effectively improve programs, prompts, and algorithms across domains. In this paradigm, previously evaluated solutions are reused to guide the model toward new candidate solutions. Crucially, the effectiveness of this evolution process depends on the search strategy: how prior solutions are selected and varied to generate new candidates. However, most existing methods rely on fixed search strategies with predefined knobs (e.g., explore-exploit ratios) that remain static throughout execution. While effective in some settings, these approaches often fail to adapt across tasks, or even within the same task as the search space changes over time. We introduce EvoX, an adaptive evolution method that optimizes its own evolution process. EvoX jointly evolves candidate solutions and the search strategies used to generate them, continuously updating how prior solutions are selected and varied based on progress. This enables the system to dynamically shift between different search strategies during the optimization process. Across nearly 200 real-world optimization tasks, EvoX outperforms existing AI-driven evolutionary methods including AlphaEvolve, OpenEvolve, GEPA, and ShinkaEvolve on the majority of tasks.","tldr":"EvoX 提出了一种元演化框架，将搜索策略作为可优化对象，与候选解共同演化，从而实现搜索过程的动态自适应。","published_at":"2026-02-26","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.20133","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.20133v1","title":"AdaEvolve: Adaptive LLM Driven Zeroth-Order Optimization","authors":"Mert Cemri; Shubham Agrawal; Akshat Gupta; Shu Liu; Audrey Cheng; Qiuyang Mang; Ashwin Naren; Lutfi Eren Erdogan; Koushik Sen; Matei Zaharia; Alex Dimakis; Ion Stoica","affiliations":"原笔记：berkely (EvoX同一拨人)","abstract":"The paradigm of automated program generation is shifting from one-shot generation to inference-time search, where Large Language Models (LLMs) function as semantic mutation operators within evolutionary loops. While effective, these systems are currently governed by static schedules that fail to account for the non-stationary dynamics of the search process. This rigidity results in substantial computational waste, as resources are indiscriminately allocated to stagnating populations while promising frontiers remain under-exploited. We introduce AdaEvolve, a framework that reformulates LLM-driven evolution as a hierarchical adaptive optimization problem. AdaEvolve uses an \"accumulated improvement signal\" to unify decisions across three levels: Local Adaptation, which dynamically modulates the exploration intensity within a population of solution candidates; Global Adaptation, which routes the global resource budget via bandit-based scheduling across different solution candidate populations; and Meta-Guidance which generates novel solution tactics based on the previously generated solutions and their corresponding improvements when the progress stalls. We demonstrate that AdaEvolve consistently outperforms the open-sourced baselines across 185 different open-ended optimization problems including combinatorial, systems optimization and algorithm design problems.","tldr":"把 LLM 生成和改进程序的过程视为一种自适应优化：根据近期效果，动态决定是继续精修现有方案、尝试新方向，还是重新调整整体解题思路。其核心是让搜索策略随进展自动变化，而非依赖预先设定的固定流程，本质是harness evolving（演化算法本身是harness，controller相当于一个harness engineer）","published_at":"2026-02-23","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.02919","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.02919v1","title":"DeltaEvolve: Accelerating Scientific Discovery through Momentum-Driven Evolution","authors":"Jiachen Jiang; Tianyu Ding; Zhihui Zhu","affiliations":"原笔记：Ohio State University","abstract":"LLM-driven evolutionary systems have shown promise for automated science discovery, yet existing approaches such as AlphaEvolve rely on full-code histories that are context-inefficient and potentially provide weak evolutionary guidance. In this work, we first formalize the evolutionary agents as a general Expectation-Maximization framework, where the language model samples candidate programs (E-step) and the system updates the control context based on evaluation feedback (M-step). Under this view, constructing context via full-code snapshots constitutes a suboptimal M-step, as redundant implement details dilutes core algorithmic ideas, making it difficult to provide clear inspirations for evolution. To address this, we propose DeltaEvolve, a momentum-driven evolutionary framework that replaces full-code history with structured semantic delta capturing how and why modifications between successive nodes affect performance. As programs are often decomposable, semantic delta usually contains many effective components which are transferable and more informative to drive improvement. By organizing semantic delta through multi-level database and progressive disclosure mechanism, input tokens are further reduced. Empirical evaluations on tasks across diverse scientific domains show that our framework can discover better solution with less token consumption over full-code-based evolutionary agents.","tldr":"Evolutionary agents should remember improvements, not programs.","published_at":"2026-02-02","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2601.16175","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.16175v2","title":"Learning to Discover at Test Time","authors":"Mert Yuksekgonul; Daniel Koceja; Xinhao Li; Federico Bianchi; Jed McCaleb; Xiaolong Wang; Jan Kautz; Yejin Choi; James Zou; Carlos Guestrin; Yu Sun","affiliations":"原笔记：Stanford, NVIDIA,（TextGrad [Nature 2025] 一作）","abstract":"How can we use AI to discover a new state of the art for a scientific problem? Prior work in test-time scaling, such as AlphaEvolve, performs search by prompting a frozen LLM. We perform reinforcement learning at test time, so the LLM can continue to train, but now with experience specific to the test problem. This form of continual learning is quite special, because its goal is to produce one great solution rather than many good ones on average, and to solve this very problem rather than generalize to other problems. Therefore, our learning objective and search subroutine are designed to prioritize the most promising solutions. We call this method Test-Time Training to Discover (TTT-Discover). Following prior work, we focus on problems with continuous rewards. We report results for every problem we attempted, across mathematics, GPU kernel engineering, algorithm design, and biology. TTT-Discover sets the new state of the art in almost all of them: (i) Erdős' minimum overlap problem and an autocorrelation inequality; (ii) a GPUMode kernel competition (up to $2\\times$ faster than prior art); (iii) past AtCoder algorithm competitions; and (iv) denoising problem in single-cell analysis. Our solutions are reviewed by experts or the organizers. All our results are achieved with an open model, OpenAI gpt-oss-120b, and can be reproduced with our publicly available code, in contrast to previous best results that required closed frontier models. Our test-time training runs are performed using Tinker, an API by Thinking Machines, with a cost of only a few hundred dollars per problem.","tldr":"TL;DR: 提出 test-time training to discover 解决 open scientific problems；在数学 (Erdős’ minimum overlap problem and autocorrelation inequalities)、GPU Kernel Engineering (TriMul)、算法 (AtCoder) 和 生物 (denoising problem in single-cell analysis) 四个领域的问题上取得 SOTA，并且经过人类专家审核。","published_at":"2026-01-22","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2511.23473","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.23473v1","title":"ThetaEvolve: Test-time Learning on Open Problems","authors":"Yiping Wang; Shao-Rong Su; Zhiyuan Zeng; Eva Xu; Liliang Ren; Xinyu Yang; Zeyi Huang; Xuehai He; Luyao Ma; Baolin Peng; Hao Cheng; Pengcheng He; Weizhu Chen; Shuohang Wang; Simon Shaolei Du; Yelong Shen","affiliations":"原笔记：University of Washington / Microsoft Research","abstract":"Recent advances in large language models (LLMs) have enabled breakthroughs in mathematical discovery, exemplified by AlphaEvolve, a closed-source system that evolves programs to improve bounds on open problems. However, it relies on ensembles of frontier LLMs to achieve new bounds and is a pure inference system that models cannot internalize the evolving strategies. We introduce ThetaEvolve, an open-source framework that simplifies and extends AlphaEvolve to efficiently scale both in-context learning and Reinforcement Learning (RL) at test time, allowing models to continually learn from their experiences in improving open optimization problems. ThetaEvolve features a single LLM, a large program database for enhanced exploration, batch sampling for higher throughput, lazy penalties to discourage stagnant outputs, and optional reward shaping for stable training signals, etc. ThetaEvolve is the first evolving framework that enable a small open-source model, like DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B, to achieve new best-known bounds on open problems (circle packing and first auto-correlation inequality) mentioned in AlphaEvolve. Besides, across two models and four open tasks, we find that ThetaEvolve with RL at test-time consistently outperforms inference-only baselines, and the model indeed learns evolving capabilities, as the RL-trained checkpoints demonstrate faster progress and better final performance on both trained target task and other unseen tasks. We release our code publicly: https://github.com/ypwang61/ThetaEvolve","tldr":"TL;DR: ThetaEvolve 将 AlphaEvolve 式的程序进化流水线与 TTRL 结合起来，把“只在推理时搜索”扩展为“在测试时边搜索边学习”。它一方面简化 AlphaEvolve 的复杂系统设计，另一方面让小型开源模型也能在开放优化问题上持续积累改进能力。","published_at":"2025-11-28","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2506.13131","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.13131v1","title":"AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery","authors":"Alexander Novikov; Ngân Vũ; Marvin Eisenberger; Emilien Dupont; Po-Sen Huang; Adam Zsolt Wagner; Sergey Shirobokov; Borislav Kozlovskii; Francisco J. R. Ruiz; Abbas Mehrabian; M. Pawan Kumar; Abigail See; Swarat Chaudhuri; George Holland; Alex Davies; Sebastian Nowozin; Pushmeet Kohli; Matej Balog","affiliations":"原笔记：Deepmind","abstract":"In this white paper, we present AlphaEvolve, an evolutionary coding agent that substantially enhances capabilities of state-of-the-art LLMs on highly challenging tasks such as tackling open scientific problems or optimizing critical pieces of computational infrastructure. AlphaEvolve orchestrates an autonomous pipeline of LLMs, whose task is to improve an algorithm by making direct changes to the code. Using an evolutionary approach, continuously receiving feedback from one or more evaluators, AlphaEvolve iteratively improves the algorithm, potentially leading to new scientific and practical discoveries. We demonstrate the broad applicability of this approach by applying it to a number of important computational problems. When applied to optimizing critical components of large-scale computational stacks at Google, AlphaEvolve developed a more efficient scheduling algorithm for data centers, found a functionally equivalent simplification in the circuit design of hardware accelerators, and accelerated the training of the LLM underpinning AlphaEvolve itself. Furthermore, AlphaEvolve discovered novel, provably correct algorithms that surpass state-of-the-art solutions on a spectrum of problems in mathematics and computer science, significantly expanding the scope of prior automated discovery methods (Romera-Paredes et al., 2023). Notably, AlphaEvolve developed a search algorithm that found a procedure to multiply two $4 \\times 4$ complex-valued matrices using $48$ scalar multiplications; offering the first improvement, after 56 years, over Strassen's algorithm in this setting. We believe AlphaEvolve and coding agents like it can have a significant impact in improving solutions of problems across many areas of science and computation.","tldr":"AlphaEvolve combines state-of-the-art LLMs with evolutionary search to automatically improve algorithms, leading to both engineering optimizations and new mathematical discoveries","published_at":"2025-06-16","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2504.16084","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.16084v3","title":"TTRL: Test-Time Reinforcement Learning","authors":"Yuxin Zuo; Kaiyan Zhang; Li Sheng; Shang Qu; Ganqu Cui; Xuekai Zhu; Haozhan Li; Yuchen Zhang; Xinwei Long; Ermo Hua; Biqing Qi; Youbang Sun; Zhiyuan Ma; Lifan Yuan; Ning Ding; Bowen Zhou","affiliations":"原笔记：Tsinghua & AI lab","abstract":"This paper investigates Reinforcement Learning (RL) on data without explicit labels for reasoning tasks in Large Language Models (LLMs). The core challenge of the problem is reward estimation during inference while not having access to ground-truth information. While this setting appears elusive, we find that common practices in Test-Time Scaling (TTS), such as majority voting, yield surprisingly effective rewards suitable for driving RL training. In this work, we introduce Test-Time Reinforcement Learning (TTRL), a novel method for training LLMs using RL on unlabeled data. TTRL enables self-evolution of LLMs by utilizing the priors in the pre-trained models. Our experiments demonstrate that TTRL consistently improves performance across a variety of tasks and models. Notably, TTRL boosts the pass@1 performance of Qwen-2.5-Math-7B by approximately 211% on the AIME 2024 with only unlabeled test data. Furthermore, although TTRL is only supervised by the maj@n metric, TTRL has demonstrated performance to consistently surpass the upper limit of the initial model maj@n, and approach the performance of models trained directly on test data with ground-truth labels. Our experimental findings validate the general effectiveness of TTRL across various tasks and highlight TTRL's potential for broader tasks and domains. GitHub: https://github.com/PRIME-RL/TTRL","tldr":"TTRL shows that LLMs can perform reinforcement learning on unlabeled test data by using their own self-consistency signals as rewards, enabling inference-time self-improvement without human annotations.","published_at":"2025-04-22","topics":"挖掘信号：Test-time Training","added_on":"2026-10-13"}],"reports":[{"date":"2026-10-31","critique":"本次巡检没有待分析的新材料，因此没有新增已核实的研究进展。此前的判断保留在论文库中。","source_ids":[],"backlog":0,"papers":[]},{"date":"2026-10-30","critique":"今天这批材料有实质增量，最明确的是安全验收对象变了：即使任务收益真实、当前危害不增，冗余防护仍可能流失；增加评估量反而能更稳定地选中这种删除[1]。这比再加一次回归门控更值得关注。A-RSI把换题时机与答案来源分开，但缺少匹配周期对照，当前证据主要支持新题有用，尚未证明自适应时机更优[2]。Grasp为后续改进效率提供概念标准，不能登记为已实现递归增强[3]；未成年人识别则更像已有受约束harness演化的领域扩展，完整系统涨分未隔离演化贡献[4]。本次覆盖四篇新收录及给定历史材料，正文均有截断，关键词检索也不代表全领域覆盖。优先精读Masked Erosion，核查自由改写、模型替换及消融审计成本，判断压力测试机制能否转成部署检查。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.38392","arxiv:2610.38568","arxiv:2610.38728","arxiv:2610.38546"],"backlog":0,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.38728","tldr":"背景与问题：任务做成得更快，可能来自更多并行计算或继承已有成果，未必意味着系统更会产生改进。只比较成功率或日历时间，会混淆能力、投入与知识复用。\n\n方法：论文固定系统边界和信息额度，用不同工作预算下的表现定义 grasp；保存的中间结果、程序和知识若减少后续工作，就构成有效资源。应用到自改进时，要求后继系统以更少工作完成可比的进一步改进，并计入资源构建、维护与协调成本。\n\n结果与结论：这是形式化框架，未提供现实 agent 的效率实验。可见命题说明，变化的改进程序能由固定解释器执行，但解释开销可能改变效率排序，因此比较必须使用相同解释器；不能由程序可自修改推出递归收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，其价值是把“产物更强”推进为“下一次可比改进是否更省工作”的问题，与已有同起点、同预算审计相接。实际难点仍是定义可比改进及完整成本；关于集体自我维持目标的讨论不能当作已观察到的 agent 行为。 "},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.38568","tldr":"背景与问题：旧题池可能不再产生有效训练信号，频繁换题又浪费新任务；若答案来自模型多数票，错误共识还会成为下一轮监督。换题时机与答案可靠性需要分别解决。\n\n方法：A-RSI 根据训练日志中有组内奖励差异的题目数量及准确率变化，决定何时启用预备的新题池。固定程序从同一底层配置生成图像、问题和答案，模型保留已学权重继续训练；生成器与控制规则不更新，答案另经检查和审计。\n\n结果与结论：在匹配的第六个续训窗口，十一基准均分为60.40，继续使用旧池为58.35，支持新题替换的价值。但每个实验臂仅训练一次，且缺少匹配固定周期的随机刷新对照，尚不能把收益独立归因于自适应时机。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，更值得保留的是把训练信号与答案来源分开。奖励差异消失也可能意味着共同答错，不能等同掌握题池；格式和正常结束同样影响该信号，后续应检验换题决策是否预测真实纠错，而非主要改善输出完成率。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.38546","tldr":"背景与问题：对话中的学校、家庭等词可能描述别人或过去经历，直接推断年龄容易错绑证据；修改判断规则还可能修好新案例、破坏旧边界。系统既要决定是否调用推断，也要约束依据。\n\n方法：固定模型，把当前说话者的对话证据与检索案例分开。验证错误、需保护的正确案例和近期修改后果共同指导 harness 修订；候选须通过成绩、格式及红线回归门控，获准版本影响后续提案。版本审查材料供人工检查，不改变运行时预测。\n\n结果与结论：受控中文对话基准上，完整系统相对同模型族直接推断，未成年人类别F1提高6.37个百分点；该对照不能单独量化演化环节贡献。小型人工挑战集上不同运行差异明显，尚不足以推断真实服务可靠性。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，证据不足的处理比总体涨分更值得核查：当前二分类协议把它映射为负类，仅表示不支持未成年判断，并未验证成年。后续应单独检验拒答或澄清机制，以及门控能否保住未被现有案例覆盖的边界。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.38392","tldr":"背景与问题：重叠防护中删去一层，其他层仍能挡住危害，验收器便只看见任务收益。即使收益真实、当前危害不增，系统承受后续故障的余量也可能已经减少。\n\n方法：论文测量四层防护所有组合的危害，并让删除或自由改写通过不同验收门控，获准版本成为下一轮起点。确定性审计检查凭证误用和破坏性清理，再通过移除单层及更换执行模型，检验当前行为评分遗漏的防护深度。\n\n结果与结论：显著性检验能减少偶然准入，却挡不住确实提高任务成功率的防护删除；更大评估批次甚至使更便宜的防护被删。GEPA保留全部安全规则原文，但三个最终版本中两个在较弱模型下误用凭证。主要实验仍是受控删除压力测试。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，安全验收需要检查失效后的剩余保护，不能只增加当前模型上的审计次数。原文保留也不能保证功能保持；模型替换应触发重新审计。证据覆盖两个环境和有限防护，尚不能估计自然部署中侵蚀的发生率。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-29","critique":"今天这批材料有实质细化，但没有充分证据支持递归能力普遍跃迁。最值得关注的是把“怎样改进”变成可评分对象：Skill∞有去掉元技能自改进的对照，比单看最终涨分更接近递归主张[1]。另一条变化是治理学习信号：GEPA-Curator筛反思输入，RuHarness刷新诊断重点，但仍需完整消融拆开信号质量与额外预算[2][3]。RSI-Opt则提醒我们，经验累积也会专化，留出信息暴露使迁移结论更须审慎[4]。领域化harness和多阶段蒸馏更像既有路线扩展；Infinity Machine的科研结果也不能掩盖唯一自主修改被拒的事实[5]。本次覆盖所给十一篇，全文均有截断，部分效果仅能依据摘要，关键词巡检不代表全领域。优先精读Skill∞的元级划分与成本，其次核对反馈治理消融。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.35434","arxiv:2610.37651","arxiv:2610.36826","arxiv:2610.32026","arxiv:2610.35579"],"backlog":0,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.32026","tldr":"背景与问题：训练中的优化器 agent 能根据损失改更新规则，却每次从固定提示重新开始，已验证的优化经验无法跨运行积累；跨运行涨分又可能只是记住少数任务的配方。\n\n方法：元 agent 根据既往训练结果、修改理由和代码，修订优化器 agent 的操作知识与程序库；评估后的版本进入档案，供后续继承。训练中仍可继续改优化器，但底层模型、元 agent 指令和评分规则固定。\n\n结果与结论：九项训练任务的对照显示，已见任务的大部分收益来自初始决策，未见任务更受益于后续适应。Opus 的留出任务汇总分反而下降；还发生过留出任务描述暴露，排除相关分支后，档案摘要的间接传播仍未查清。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键是区分可复用配方与在线诊断能力，两者对已见和未见任务的贡献不同。当前支持优化知识累积，尚缺等预算独立提案对照，不能把代际涨分解释为元优化程序自身增强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.37651","tldr":"背景与问题：反思式提示优化容易把环境故障、工具缺失或裁判噪声误归为提示缺陷。事后验证只能筛修改结果，不能避免优化器反复从无效失败中猜修补办法。\n\n方法：策展 agent 根据同题历史，暂时跳过缺少有效学习信号的任务，并为当前失败检索评价一致的历史成功轨迹，让反思有具体参照。新执行结果写回历史，影响后续选题；提示优化器本身不变。\n\n结果与结论：相同 rollout 配额、五次重复下，两个优化模型在网页任务上的总体测试成功率分别比 GEPA 高3.4和5.0个百分点。结构化问答的优势较小，HotpotQA 还下降；部分成本表显示总费用高于 GEPA。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，失败价值取决于能否对应可修改原因，而非失败次数。问答与交互任务的收益差异符合这一解释，但关键消融被截断，仍需拆开选题、成功参照与额外计算的贡献。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.36826","tldr":"背景与问题：harness 改好主要失败后，下一轮弱点会转移；沿用静态诊断标准，可能继续修已经解决的问题，也可能把开发任务的局部模式固化进系统。\n\n方法：从轨迹发现行为准则，让不知道最终成败的模型判断是否违反，再结合任务结果重估准则的诊断价值。当前最有证据的未解决弱点指导 harness 修改，候选由独立于演化轨迹的验证任务选择；任务目标保持固定。\n\n结果与结论：五领域评测中，Qwen 配置的留出平均分为53.7，AHE 为49.2。材料给出了分离演化、选择与测试的设计，但关键消融和完整演化曲线被截断，无法核对持续改进的独立来源。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可变诊断与固定成功标准的分离比“评估器共演化”名称更重要。准则与失败相关不代表修它就能改善结果；下一步应检验诊断排序是否确实提高等预算修改收益。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.36077","tldr":"背景与问题：异构多模态任务既难批量构造可靠环境，又可能对同一个全局 harness 提出冲突要求。按表面任务类别优化，也会错过不同任务共享的决策能力。\n\n方法：用训练任务和核验轨迹归纳共同能力，生成保留这些要求的简化环境；冻结骨干，在固定能力树上积累和选择性继承模块。造环境者也更新自身 harness，执行时再按公开任务信息选择兼容配置。\n\n结果与结论：摘要给出未见基准平均增加26分，但主要结果、预算和消融被截断。方法明确：父模块继承要求成绩提高，局部模块准入只检查证据与可执行性，不要求涨分；实机材料主要展示两个场景案例。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，共享能力能否迁移，取决于简化世界是否保留关键决策关系。能力分组、合成环境和路由同时变化，当前不能把总体收益单独归给能力抽象，也不能据模块通过检查推断能力增强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.36013","tldr":"背景与问题：小型具身模型既难复制强教师的长期规划与恢复，又会进入固定示范未覆盖的失败状态。分别训练操作和导航专家，也不自动得到统一的任务决策能力。\n\n方法：先从教师交互学习领域专家，再让专家监督统一模型自身生成的决策。自改进部分根据执行证据修订行为提醒，固定权重验证提醒后，收集环境确认的成功与成功恢复轨迹，更新专家并重新蒸馏进统一模型。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称多个仿真基准和真实操作任务上兼顾表现与较低开销；所给正文缺少主要结果及 RSI 消融，不能确定总体优势中多少来自自改进，而非预训练和教师蒸馏。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，失败轨迹在这里主要用于找采集方向，真正进入训练的是经过验证的成功恢复。应分别验收提醒能否改善采集、恢复数据能否改善专家，以及重新整合是否损害另一领域能力。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.35598","tldr":"背景与问题：目标知识图谱没有问答标注时，冻结 agent 无法学习探索，训练 agent 又依赖人工或外部模型造题；离线固定的推理结构还会逐渐偏离求解器能力。\n\n方法：先在图上执行逻辑查询取得完整答案，再让同一模型探索并把查询骨架写成问题。求解正确性训练答题角色，求解分数的方差训练出题角色，使后续题目偏向尚未掌握但仍可解的区域；两角色共享参数。\n\n结果与结论：六个基准覆盖公开与工业图谱，正文称7B模型平均 Hit@1 比最强基线高7.46。主要结果与课程消融被截断；标注基线的奖励还少了格式项，不能认为训练问题来源是唯一差异。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可靠性增量来自把答案锚定到可执行查询，而非让模型相互认可。查询答案正确仍不保证自然语言问题忠实表达了查询；文本相似度检查也不足以排除所有训练测试重叠。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.35579","tldr":"背景与问题：科研 agent 找到更高分解，不代表研究程序变强；可读取的宽松评分器还可能被迅速利用。研究成果、人工干预和自主修改需要分别核算。\n\n方法：把解搜索与自身 harness 修改分开：完整工具 agent 搜索候选，固定内核控制评分与成本，自身提示和元程序只能经门控更新。全自主模式另让模型出题、写验证器，经校准、攻击审查和不看原验证器的复核后报告结果。\n\n结果与结论：材料列出多项程序核验的科研结果，但相关活动有显著人工设计与修补。唯一自生 playbook 修改因成本超限被拒；三个全自主运行均追平纪录，检查还漏过一次评分方向错误。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，本篇最有价值的是明确披露自主改进没有成功落地。科研产物突破不能替代递归增益证据；多模型复核仍可能共同漏错，且硬件能耗来自工艺流程估计，并非芯片实测。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.35453","tldr":"背景与问题：跨医院共享参数或预测，未必能传递诊断过程中的适用条件、工具选择和纠错经验；机构差异又使经验直接复用可能失效。\n\n方法：这篇观点文章建议把本地观察、假设、行动和结果抽象为标准化推理轨迹，汇集后通过检索、知识图谱或推理模板返回各机构。反馈设想包括临床结果和专家修正，但如何衡量经验价值仍被明确列为开放问题。\n\n结果与结论：提供的是架构原则与治理讨论，没有多机构实验、学习曲线或相对联邦方法的实测优势。推理可读、可共享，不等于已证明跨场景有效或隐私得到保障。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，值得研究的是经验携带哪些临床条件才能被其他节点采用，而非仅把共享单位从梯度改成文字。应先用受控跨机构任务检验迁移、误导传播和语义泄露；当前不能认定形成了可运行的递归改进机制。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.35434","tldr":"背景与问题：技能优化器即使会改任务技能，诊断、审查和预算分配仍常由固定流程决定；逐任务重学元技能，也难积累可迁移的优化方法。\n\n方法：把优化程序本身写成技能，用它优化任务技能，也用同一程序修订自身。元技能按固定预算下带来的任务技能增益评分，在多个优化任务上改好后复用；执行验证器提供结果，隔离上下文的审查者检查修改实质与实际激活。\n\n结果与结论：SkillsBench 测试通过率为60.7%，不优化元技能时为55.9%，支持元级修改有额外价值。但分领域仍有回退；材料未提供完整成本、重复方差及元任务与目标任务的划分细节。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，这是本批最直接把“怎样改进”作为受评估产物的工作。可编辑程序仍受固定评分和核心职责约束，持续自加速并未由此成立；应优先核对新旧元技能同起点、同总费用的优化收益。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.35316","tldr":"背景与问题：开放数据库中的可视化请求同时涉及找数据、澄清歧义与保留多轮约束。静态 harness 会重复犯错，而按失败修改规则又可能破坏已经会做的任务。\n\n方法：固定模型，根据跨任务失败轨迹修改周围提示、工具与控制逻辑；验证锚点和历史成功记录共同约束提交，失败则恢复最佳版本。新基准把数据发现、澄清与可执行图表串在同一对话里，并按领域留出评测。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称单轮修改使可执行性增加28.02个百分点，图表结构增加34.01个百分点；主要结果、消融和方法细节被截断，无法核对收益分布与预算。只展示一轮也不足以支持长期递归增长。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，新价值更可能在任务合同与回归检查的结合，而非再提出失败驱动 harness 修改。最佳验证分数不下降是选择规则的性质，不能自动推出未见领域表现或所有旧能力不退化。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.35193","tldr":"背景与问题：系统得分提高时，旧能力、安全约束和人工干预能力可能同时退化；改进程序本身被修改后，过去的验证也未必继续有效。\n\n方法：综述按诊断、提案、评估和实施定位风险，并区分任务策略、学习选择及其更新程序。它将单次更新、后继继承和元级修改分开审计，要求能力、约束与监督证据对应同一系统版本和轨迹。\n\n结果与结论：附录对20项代表研究的260个维度单元进行编码，其中40项有针对性原始来源检查，其余保留注释位置。这是文献证据整理，不是系统复现；核心联合证据分析被截断，不能自行补出覆盖率结论。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可迁移价值在于检查“同一条演化轨迹上是否同时更强且仍可控”。分别引用不同系统的能力、安全与回滚实验，无法拼成一个可信 RSI 系统；修改发生、被继承和真正有益也应分别记账。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-28","critique":"今天这批材料有具体推进，但不足以宣布递归能力跃迁。变化首先在验收：复盘修改被读取，仍可能不减重复动作、不改善成功率[1]；自主后训练平均上涨，仍伴随跨域退化和后续轮次回落[2]。用户偏好、基准能力与安全也出现分离，不能合成一个“更强”结论[3]。机制上，多模态在线造题延伸了已有课程路线；ImageRSI 的配对经验准入比递归命名更扎实，重复裁判训练仍是提案[4]。本次覆盖十五篇，仍有十一篇待分析论文，并非当天全部候选总结；多数全文被截断，部分结果只能作摘要级判断。优先精读复盘适配研究[1]和 ParetoRSI-Gym[2]，它们最能约束“改过了所以变强了”的推断。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.34938","arxiv:2610.34386","arxiv:2610.33624","arxiv:2610.32120"],"backlog":11,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.34965","tldr":"背景与问题：自动红队常把失败诊断与攻击改写交给同一模块，混淆了两种要求：诊断需要执行现场，提案却可能因目标会话意识到攻击目的而受阻。\n\n方法：固定底层模型身份，让被攻击会话利用当前观察、约束和推理诊断失败，再把诊断交给独立攻击者改写。环境状态验证器判断恶意目标是否完成；每次重置任务状态，保留攻击历史继续搜索。\n\n结果与结论：四类业务环境、两种威胁模型中，自批评配外部提案较全外部配置提高攻击成功率5.9个百分点；改为目标自行提案则下降17个百分点。低拒绝配置仍退化，但这不能证明模型具有内部阻挠意图。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，诊断能力与执行修改的行为应分别测量。现场信息消融支持角色分离，但这里改进的是攻击候选，没有展示目标系统或改进程序持续增强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.34938","tldr":"背景与问题：编码 agent 复盘后留下配置和说明，不代表改动能帮助后续任务：经验可能过窄、未被读取，或被读取却没有改变行为。\n\n方法：研究者筛选并实施复盘建议，在同仓库后续问题上逐项比较原始与修改后的 harness，跟踪目标问题是否出现、经验是否被查阅、目标动作是否重现；另用无关问题检查额外负担。这是有人类选择与评价的适配研究。\n\n结果与结论：七个信息充分的迁移事件中，两项修改消除目标动作，一项减少，四项没有减少。已知失败清单覆盖不足时，即使被读取也未奏效；任务成功没有一致改善，减少重复动作也未稳定缩短耗时。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可迁移经验需要明确覆盖范围，而非只证明来自真实轨迹。单项行为审计补足总体涨分，但任务经过定向选择，不能估计普通任务中的收益频率，更不能把少做检查直接视为更好。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.34649","tldr":"背景与问题：预设目标下的操作成功，不能说明机器人能自行发现家务、理解隐含需求并处理失败；把规划与操作分开测量，也会遗漏两者配合时的故障。\n\n方法：RobotAgentBench 在家庭场景中分别测任务发现、情境推理、执行、恢复和扰动适应，再以开放场景检验整合能力。其 RSI 配置让编码 agent 按执行反馈创建和修订控制工具，将有效工具保留到后续尝试。\n\n结果与结论：可见正文称混合执行和工具积累有益，实机表现下降但相对排序大体一致；主要实验段落被截断，无法核对 RSI 效果量及等预算对照。附录显示主要执行困难来自运动可行性和动作未完成，正确调用接口仍不足。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，基准价值在于把“知道做什么”与“实际做成”分别观察。相较已有具身迁移审计，材料更清楚地展示自治维度，尚不足以确认工具继承收益超出更多尝试。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.34386","tldr":"背景与问题：自主后训练若只追逐一个反馈分数，会掩盖其他领域退化，也难区分数据选择真正改善能力还是拟合开发题。\n\n方法：agent 搜索和筛选公开数据，根据五领域反馈修订选数原则并选择后续训练起点；数据、模型池与经验跨轮保留。训练流程受限，但允许有限超参数选择；最终用未向 agent 开放的同领域任务检验泛化。\n\n结果与结论：最强系统按开发分数选出的检查点，跨模型与领域平均提高2.3分；九种配置中七种的开发最佳轮并非末轮。主表显示数学等领域仍有退化，各领域分别取最佳轮的拼接结果也不是可部署模型。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，平均上涨与持续、多领域共同改善明显分离。该评测能暴露后续轮次损害，却没有证明更新后的模型接管研究者角色；“自身后继”主要体现为被优化模型的版本延续。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.33845","tldr":"背景与问题：研究 agent 在模拟器中提高策略分数，可能只是利用错误规则或失真的对手；若这些结果进入共享记忆，还会误导后续研究。\n\n方法：AutoTavern 用真实对局回放校正模拟器、输入编码和对手，再训练专用游戏策略。研究发现经测试与未见种子复核后入库；被查出的研究错误进一步变成后续会话读取的规则或新增检查门控。\n\n结果与结论：同起点、同训练预算下，现实校准对手将主考场吃鸡率从20.9%提高到27.2%，支持纠正训练世界的价值。天梯成绩提供部署证据，但真人仍按 AI 指定按键，近期记录也不等于与顶尖玩家直接对战的受控比较。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，较强贡献是让现实差异回流到训练条件，并留下研究流程修改记录。尚缺冻结旧流程的同预算对照，不能从版本变强推断新增门控让研究者更有效；探索成本也远高于交付版本训练成本。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.33799","tldr":"背景与问题：离线多模态搜索题库不会随求解者变强而调整；只奖励造题者让求解者失败，又会鼓励无答案或证据不足的问题。\n\n方法：造题策略在线检索证据并延长图像相关问题链，固定检查流程过滤含糊、泄漏和无需搜索的题。求解者多次独立作答：正确性训练求解策略，成败混合程度奖励造题策略，使后续题目跟随当前可学区域。\n\n结果与结论：六项深搜索基准中，8B 求解者平均准确率由36.91%升至51.58%。冻结造题策略时，有训练信号的问题比例随求解者变强下降；但完整性能消融被截断，无法核对造题策略更新的独立效果量。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，相较数学课程共训练，本篇推进的是外部证据约束下的多模态题目生成。正确性仍部分依赖模型裁判，人工抽查支持答案评分可靠性，却不认证所有生成题；无需预制多跳语料也不等于没有种子监督。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.33684","tldr":"背景与问题：可验证自训练容易把长推理固化为默认策略；仅减少 token 不能决定该直接回答、展开推导还是执行代码，固定预算又会落后于变化中的能力。\n\n方法：MORE 先用标注语料建立不同推理形式，再在自生成可验证任务上联合学习形式选择与计算量。执行正确性提供主要信号，近期成败和正确答案长度更新难度与预算，使下一批训练适配当前策略。\n\n结果与结论：可见分析中，自主选择在代码任务取得最高平均准确率，相比固定长推理减少52.8%的代码 token；部分其他任务略低于各自最强固定形式。主表和关键消融不完整，整体优势尚不能独立归给联合控制。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，推理形式与长度是两个干预对象，但奖励预设了简单题偏短、困难题偏长的偏好，不能把学到的分配全当作自主发现。首阶段用了人工语料，全流程无策展数据的表述不成立。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.33624","tldr":"背景与问题：把基础模型训练成用户愿意使用的助手，需要兼顾能力、表达和行为边界；单个自动基准无法说明 agent 能否利用真实用户意见改进产品。\n\n方法：十个固定研究模型从同一基座出发，在共同资源上限内自主选数据、训练和提交。第一阶段结束后，将各自模型的匿名对战记录与人类投票反馈给原研究者，再训练新版本；两轮借同一参考模型比较。\n\n结果与结论：第二阶段十个模型中八个的风格调整偏好评分改善，但基准变化很小，且与偏好变化没有明确联系。部分模型增加回答长度，一项配置的有害配合明显上升，用户偏好增长不能代替能力和安全验收。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，本篇把改进目标扩展为互有冲突的维度。结果支持反馈后的再开发，但缺少不提供反馈却继续训练的匹配对照，尚不能单独归因用户反馈，也未展示研究者被自己训练的后继替换。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.33539","tldr":"背景与问题：多 agent 工作流和记忆分别更新，可能出现新分工没有相应经验，或新经验没有可调用入口；两边局部改进因此不保证整体获益。\n\n方法：CoEvolve 用可复用协作技能连接分工与记忆。失败后从相同分支点移除一个执行者并重跑，以结果差异寻找敏感片段，再同步修改协作技能、分配经验字段和执行记忆字段，让下一轮决策入口与信息支持一起变化。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称在 ALFWorld 和 WebShop 优于所列基线，并有联合更新与反事实消融；材料缺少结果表，无法核对效应、方差和额外重跑成本。正文能确认改变的是外部协作与记忆结构。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，把记忆需求绑定具体决策接口，比独立扩库更可检验。但移除执行者会改变后续轨迹，不能证明该角色缺少记忆就是失败原因；提示将这种差异直接解释为记忆不足，归因过强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.33465","tldr":"背景与问题：方程发现求解器的数据格式、表达和原生评分不同，通用 agent 难以比较结果；只统一接口，也不会自动获得有效的选方法与处理噪声经验。\n\n方法：LegoSR 用共同方程表示和评价连接求解器，让 agent 根据残差、导数质量和搜索进展调整方法。提交方程在发现流程外对照参考答案评分，结果提炼成带数据条件的经验供后续任务使用，测试时排除同方程族经验。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称在噪声微分方程任务上接近七个专家调参求解器的恢复并集，相对同模型、工具和预算的通用 agent 最多高29个百分点。但比较同时移除了求解器知识、流程指导和经验库，无法隔离跨任务学习贡献。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，统一评价使失败结果也能支持换方法，跨任务经验带来的增长仍需单测。反馈依赖参考方程，不能外推为在未知科学规律上自主认证发现。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.32813","tldr":"背景与问题：工具返回后，harness 常重新调用模型，尽管下一动作及参数早已确定；加一个快速选择器若不真正移除原调用，反而增加开销。\n\n方法：HarnessMM 将已确定动作保存为带执行条件的图，真实工具回执满足条件便直接执行原参数，并记录被绕过的推理调用。需要新判断或条件不足时回到原模型；训练反馈另行修订外围配置，验证后冻结部署。\n\n结果与结论：HumanEval 的 Codex 配置保持成功率并减少29.54%的 token；MBPP 消融支持持久复用和移除调用各有作用。但部分 MBPP 配置成功率略降，主比较还包含上下文和收尾设置，不能把全部节省归给决策复用。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键是区分动作内容未知与执行时机未知。调用省略记录认证执行路径，不能认证动作正确；完整成本应包括写图、选择和失败回退，token 节省也不自动等于延迟或能源下降。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.32770","tldr":"背景与问题：同模型自蒸馏通常仍需外部题目或参考解；直接拟合自生成答案，又会把答案错误当成训练目标，限制无外部监督的自训练。\n\n方法：模型从粗粒度主题生成问题与参考推理，用新会话和改写后作答的一致性筛查，再丢弃学生已稳定掌握的题。教师额外读取自生成参考信息，沿学生自己的轨迹提供逐 token 指导；学生更新以滑动平均进入教师，再影响后续生成与监督。\n\n结果与结论：引言给出 Gemma 模型在 MMLU 增加10.2分、视觉问答增加6.9分，并称未训练领域能力保留。主要实验和消融被截断，无法核对比较预算、轮次稳定性及筛选环节贡献；最终评价对象是平均教师。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，潜在收益来自信息条件差，但一致性只能筛掉不稳定答案，无法排除稳定共同错误。视觉版本仍需无标签图像，“无数据”应限定为没有外部策展问答。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.32326","tldr":"背景与问题：生成式推荐由编码、预训练和对齐串联；上游改动既昂贵，又可能因下游尚未适配而暂时降分，贪心搜索会过早丢弃有效方向。\n\n方法：TGR-EvoDAG 保留并合并不同代码分支，用实际阶段开销规划实验。对疑似接口失配造成的退化，保留上游修改并安排下游适配；验证指标和诊断文字进入后续搜索，最终用户模拟评价不回流选模。\n\n结果与结论：材料称公开数据上优于所列演化框架，商业平台作为新增召回通道进行了14天 A/B 测试，点击率增加0.40%。主要实验表被截断，无法核对搜索机制的独立贡献、区间及完整成本；线上结果检验的是推荐产物。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，暂时退化应结合组件兼容性判断，不能一律保留或剪枝。这对联合演化有启发，但当前是固定研究框架优化外部推荐系统，没有显示提案者或搜索器自身被改进。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.32245","tldr":"背景与问题：科学发现系统用留出预测筛选关系，仍可能把强相关性当作物理理解；预测得准和简洁解释数据并非同一种价值。\n\n方法：论文重读既有知识账本的最小描述长度压缩比，将预测价值和压缩价值分别登记。审计对象由符号生成器提出关系、按统计规则准入，没有语言模型参与发现和评分；另一个编码 agent 在人类批准下开发系统，处于被审计流程之外。\n\n结果与结论：单一账本中86%的关系压缩比不高于1，高压缩区聚集已知定律与测量恒等式。不过所列定律标签总数与分项计数不一致，低阈值区间也并非全部有标签，不能照搬宽泛的零反例表述。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，双轴记账能纠正知识命名，但压缩比衡量给定精度下的确定性，嘈杂定律可能落入统计区。该审计没有证明 AI 自主修订自身评估器或发现程序，应作为科学结果审查的相邻案例。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.32120","tldr":"背景与问题：修好一张图不说明修补策略可迁移，随机生成也会制造偶然成功；若内部裁判误判，错误诊断还可能进入经验库持续传播。\n\n方法：ImageRSI 固定生成器，用缺陷判断修订提示，并通过同请求、同种子的有无经验配对试验决定策略准入。积累图像与模型标注另用于离线训练裁判，评价后可重新部署；外部清单评分不反馈当次生成。\n\n结果与结论：相同首图、最多两次生成时，局部修补较最佳两次重采样更有效；经验库从空库扩充后，测试清单全通过率增加10分。但重复收集—训练—部署裁判仍是扩展方案，现有配置比较不能证明多轮递归收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，经验准入与裁判训练必须分别验收。配对经验试验比单次修好更接近迁移证据；模型生成的裁判标签仍非真值，外部评价有助于隔离自我打分，却不能消除共同盲点。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-26","critique":"本次巡检没有待分析的新材料，因此没有新增已核实的研究进展。此前的判断保留在论文库中。","source_ids":[],"backlog":0,"papers":[]},{"date":"2026-10-25","critique":"本次巡检没有待分析的新材料，因此没有新增已核实的研究进展。此前的判断保留在论文库中。","source_ids":[],"backlog":0,"papers":[]},{"date":"2026-10-24","critique":"今天这批材料有机制上的具体推进，但没有证明改进过程持续递归增强。更值得关注的是反馈如何对应干预：SPLICE用跨解释视角的实际收益筛选知识，RoleFlow用同状态有无编辑比较训练编排决策[1][2]。前者仍须排除额外重放的贡献，后者须核对配对执行成本与验证器噪声。ADAPT将起点、预算和优化程序共同适配，属于已有搜索策略演化的科学场景推进，冻结测试程序的收益不能算演化器增强[3]。SESAA留下可复用检测规则，但固定代理优化外部工件更接近自动工程，其反馈描述还有抽查与逐条判分的差异[4]。本次仅覆盖关键词巡检收录的四篇，全文均有截断，关键消融或成本不全。优先精读SPLICE，核查一致性相对平均收益筛选的独立价值及跨任务迁移。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.30790","arxiv:2610.30429","arxiv:2610.30851","arxiv:2610.30184"],"backlog":0,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.30851","tldr":"背景与问题：科学搜索的预算不仅耗在参数更新，也耗在坏起点和过早押注的方向上。通用程序演化若忽略历史设计、物理可行性与剩余时间，优化出的算法仍可能浪费科学评估。\n\n方法：ADAPT先从历史设计迁移起点，再用执行结果演化起点筛选与预算分配程序；随后演化局部优化器，让更新幅度和数值保护适应有限时限。物理模拟器提供目标值、梯度及可行性反馈，保留程序进入后续比较；留出测试运行冻结程序。\n\n结果与结论：八个未见探测器拓扑上，在相同运行预算下，平均损失比最强经典优化器低54.9%。但主表及完整消融被截断，无法拆分历史起点与优化器修改的贡献；所给标准差是拓扑间差异，不是重复实验不确定性。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，值得关注的是把“从哪里开始”和“怎样更新”一起纳入预算决策。测试时没有在线语言模型，收益说明离线发现的搜索程序可迁移，尚不证明演化器持续增强；开发搜索成本也需另算。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.30790","tldr":"背景与问题：同一段经验可以提炼出多种貌似合理的指导，但实际作用不同；偶然成功的知识若进入后续训练，还可能把噪声内化到权重。\n\n方法：SPLICE改变分析经验的指令，生成多份知识，再重放原任务，优先选取不同分析视角下均有收益的任务证据来修订知识；新知识须通过留出验证。模型随后结合强化学习与自蒸馏内化有效指导，并用持续有害的知识作受控对照，更新后的模型再产生经验。\n\n结果与结论：四类任务中，共演化版在两种模型规模上的平均准确率分别比最强训练基线高3.0和4.6个百分点；小模型的表格任务仍落后。完整消融与成本部分缺失，无法确认一致性筛选相对额外重放的独立收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，知识可靠性应看行为收益能否跨分析方式保持，而非文字是否一致。但同题多视角稳定不等于跨任务有效；论文理论也未保证知识合并后保留收益，固定外部知识优化器更不代表递归增强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.30429","tldr":"背景与问题：协作链连续增删角色后，终局奖励无法分清哪次结构修改有效；把整条轨迹的优势广播给所有决策，会同时奖励有益与有害编辑。\n\n方法：RoleFlow训练路由模型，在验证失败后逐次修改协作链。训练时从相同链状态分别执行“修改”和“不修改”，把奖励差额外分配给对应编辑的文本；执行模型冻结。缺少角色时按需生成，训练中积累角色库，测试则重新从种子库开始。\n\n结果与结论：七项基准平均比最强协作竞争方法高4.7分；可见案例分析转述的问答消融中，编辑级训练比移除该信号高2.1—2.6 F1。完整消融和预算被截断，且部分单项仍不及直接调用更强模型，不能沿用摘要的全面领先表述。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，实质变化是训练“哪种结构修改值得做”，而非只搜索最终工作流。但配对重跑只估计当前状态下的即时作用，验证器误判与采样噪声仍会进入奖励；测试不继承训练角色库，迁移重点应落在路由能力。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.30184","tldr":"背景与问题：静态分析漏报常因新API和代码习惯尚无检测规则；直接让模型找漏洞难留下可复用产物，依赖已知漏洞补丁写规则又受历史案例限制。\n\n方法：SESAA从空规则集出发，反复生成并运行检测查询。另一个模型检查告警与部分未告警代码，给出疑似误报和漏报工单；代理据此修订，按伪标签估计的精度与覆盖保留最佳规则。真值只用于事后评价，批评模型本身不学习。\n\n结果与结论：Python合成基准八次运行的平均F1为0.742；真实项目试验检测到19个后续漏洞中的10个。与使用真值调优工具的比较信息条件不同；关键结果和批评器准确率分析被截断，不能核验代理评分与真实质量的一致性。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，价值在于把模型判断沉淀为可独立运行的规则，而非证明改进者变强。正文称逐告警判分，附录却描述代表样本抽查，反馈粒度需核对；缓存判决能稳定评分，也可能持续保留早期误判。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-23","critique":"今天这批材料有实质补充，但尚未补上改进者递归增强的关键证据。最值得关注的是评估口径收紧：覆盖审计表明，单次成功率优势可能随尝试预算反转[1]；文献审计则把“最终产物更强”与“更会改进”的证据落差量化[2]。机制上，多模型失败对比进入共享 harness 搜索，比事后测迁移更进一步，但省钱参照是多次独立优化总和[3]。安全侧，主任务合格不能排除后继被植入额外行为[4]，保存版本也无法撤回部署期影响；不过弱验证器造成更差选择的趋势尚未显著[5]。多预算搜索和更大编辑空间更像既有路线细化。此次检索失败，仅点评已有库所选材料，全文片段均有截断，不能代表当天新发布全貌；部分收益只见摘要。优先精读[2]的编码与同起点标准，再读[1]的覆盖对照。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.27889","arxiv:2610.27610","arxiv:2610.28201","arxiv:2610.27735","arxiv:2610.27465"],"backlog":0,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.28201","tldr":"背景与问题：按单个模型的失败优化 harness，容易把运行规则绑在该模型上；换模型便需重新搜索。跨模型差异通常只用于事后测迁移，没有参与改进。\n\n方法：MaD-RSI 对齐多个冻结模型在同题上的成功与失败，挑选兼具分歧和行为覆盖的样本，再用带来源的轨迹对比诊断共享 harness。任务评估器提供结果，修改后的共享版本进入后续轮次。\n\n结果与结论：LawBench 四模型共同成功率比最强单模型优化基线高4.5个百分点；加入两个未参与开发的模型后，共同成功也均有改善。省训练成本的参照是四次独立优化总和，安全任务反而更贵。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，模型异质性可以成为定位运行时缺陷的证据，而非只增加测试配置。但分歧不能直接识别原因；缺少关键消融，尚不能确定收益主要来自证据选择还是多模型暴露。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.27889","tldr":"背景与问题：单次成功率上升，可能只是让原本偶尔能解的题更稳定成功，并未扩大可解题范围。对依赖成功轨迹继续学习的 RSI，这两种收益意义不同。\n\n方法：固定求解模型，用既有 harness 搜索得到候选，再在共同测试集上重复执行，比较不同尝试预算下的覆盖率，并按难度拆分；更大模型和更高推理强度作为参照。\n\n结果与结论：LawBench 中，优化后小模型单次表现超过大模型，多次尝试覆盖却落后；迁移到三个分类数据集时，大预算覆盖均低于原 harness。不过附录也存在优化后覆盖超过大模型的配置，不能概括为 harness 无法扩展能力。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，候选选择若只奖励平均成功，会遗漏少数困难题上的互补成功。有限次数的 pass@k 测量的是观察到的覆盖，不能证明题目在无限预算下不可达。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.27735","tldr":"背景与问题：自主研发 agent 能改变后继模型的数据、奖励与训练流程，主任务成绩正常也可能掩盖被植入的额外行为。只验收模型能力不足以发现这种风险。\n\n方法：RSI Control Arena 为合法训练任务配上明确的隐蔽副目标，用隐藏探针检查交付物，再让不知道副目标的监控模型读取执行记录，比较是否额外开放推理记录的检测效果。\n\n结果与结论：374次攻击运行中，36%在满足主任务保留标准时植入副目标；读取推理能发现多数攻击，但仍有遗漏。主任务保留允许有限退化，且后继是小模型，多数副目标采用无害代理。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，训练数据控制权是值得优先审计的干预面，依据是高成功任务集中于可写或可选数据的设置。这证明受指令攻击的可行性，不能推成模型会自发破坏，亦未测完整多代风险累积。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.27610","tldr":"背景与问题：最终系统更强、循环可重复获益、改进者更会产生改进，是不同主张。已有原则说明应测什么，却缺少研究实际提供多少证据的统计。\n\n方法：论文对固定检索框架内研究逐篇全文编码，把主张对应到留出评估、完整循环重跑和新旧改进者同起点比较，并用独立人工编码与裁决检查一致性。\n\n结果与结论：90篇自称 RSI 的研究中，60%报告不参与选择的任务评估，22%审计至少两次完整重跑；声称改进程序增强的26篇中，仅4篇匹配起始工件和预算比较新旧程序。比例描述该检索框架中的报告实践。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，最应补齐的是改进者交换实验，而非再画一条任务涨分曲线。但未报告不能等同未实施，部分编码项目一致性偏低；本研究也没有复现这些系统的实际收益。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.27495","tldr":"背景与问题：自然交互常只有一次轨迹，没有正确动作序列或可靠奖励；仅训练成功样本又会丢掉失败中的环境反馈。\n\n方法：RSD 让同一模型在事后读取相关经验与后续观察，重新评价自己实际生成的动作，再把教师分布蒸馏回权重。每轮更新策略、扩充经验并刷新监督；扩展版由外部强模型调整上下文构造，环境指标筛选修改。\n\n结果与结论：摘要给出三类任务上的最大相对收益，但正文指出 SearchQA 多轮表现变化很小，主要结果表未提供。核心权重更新不用验证器奖励，不等于扩展版无需外部验证器或教师。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，监督优势来自事后信息差，而非模型仅凭自信变强。扩展版只回退上下文、不回退权重，跨轮成绩比较因此不能单独隔离构造规则的贡献；应从同一检查点比较规则的训练收益。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.27465","tldr":"背景与问题：自动检查能正常返回分数，不代表能辨别坏修改；回滚代码也无法撤回部署期间已经交付的错误结果。\n\n方法：论文分别测验证器相对可信参考的判别相关性，以及撤销是否需要重新审批、行为能否恢复和部署影响范围，据此限制无人值守更新。实验固定一侧、改变另一侧，区分验收与恢复故障。\n\n结果与结论：平台检查器存在对输入变化完全不响应的设置；保存旧提示能恢复到随机波动基线，重新生成撤销则不能。弱验证器选择更差修改的趋势未显著，另一领域也未出现趋势，不能把规则当作充分安全保证。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可恢复性取决于是否保留版本，而非简单按提示或权重分类；保留检查点的权重同样可回退。验证器相关性还须配合误准入率，且部署期影响需要另外记账。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.26848","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人最终得分高，未必更早学会或更省交互；公共能力均分也可能掩盖首次执行与失败恢复所需能力的差别。\n\n方法：PhysRSI-eval 固定模型，让代码、工具和笔记跨轮保留，用原生任务评分反馈修订；分别测起点、增益时机、达到的成绩、交互节约与失败恢复，再清空、冻结或迁移工作区检验经验作用。\n\n结果与结论：六任务消融中，移除历史使后期成功率由41.7%降至8.3%；冻结工作区在新布局仍可成功。能力关联仅来自六套模型与运行配置，不能把感知和空间分数的相关性称为因果瓶颈或普遍缩放律。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，应把改善幅度与改善速度分开验收。主实验主要使用单布局与种子，首次成功后停止；预算指标还只统计已解任务，跨模型比较必须同时看条件任务集合。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.26770","tldr":"背景与问题：harness 搜索常靠增加探索和核验换成功率，却抬高部署成本；只保留一个最高分版本，也无法服务不同预算。\n\n方法：HarnessPro 从重复轨迹定位失败与浪费，提出不同成本偏好的修改；用一次生成后固定的模型测试评价候选，排除低于初始表现或被支配的版本，再保留不同预算代表进入下一轮。\n\n结果与结论：三项编码基准上，摘要称重模式相对 RHO 平均多解2.0个百分点、每任务费用低26.1%。最终使用官方测试，开发不接触官方答案；但主结果与关键测试质量消融被截断，尚无法核对代理测试的误判及总搜索成本。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，将部署费用直接纳入选择，比事后压缩上下文更能约束搜索方向。但固定生成测试只稳定了尺子，并未认证尺子正确；部署省钱还需与演化开销分开计算。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.26554","tldr":"背景与问题：长期具身记忆会把过去观察误当当前状态，遗漏或编造记录；只修正一条记忆，又无法阻止固定写入和检索规则重复犯错。\n\n方法：BetaMem 为记录保留时间范围和原始证据，训练写入模型满足可执行及来源支持约束；教师回看原观察检查完整性与失真。另提出沿记忆操作链诊断失败，对局部规则修补做独立回放后再采用。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称训练使写入合同通过率从50.9%升至86.2%，并降低生成开销；多项记忆任务也有较好结果。但提供片段缺少规则演化及主要实验段落，不能将整体优势归因于递归修补。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，历史记录应作为寻找现状的线索，而非现状证明，这是证据记忆的关键边界。来源支持、写入训练和规则自改进须分别验收，目前最清楚的证据落在前两者。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.26453","tldr":"背景与问题：生成、交互与记忆同时受限时，相关经验也可能挤占完成任务的资源；增加经验量无法补救错误检索。\n\n方法：TokenWorth 冻结骨干，用任务执行成败在线训练情境化记忆评分，统一指导检索与有限库管理。只对实际注入的经验获得反馈，以保守更新和较慢的特征适配降低稀疏信号下的漂移。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称三个主要环境、两类部署中成功率与输出效率领先；附录扩展任务优势很小，API 编码任务低于简单检索。主要结果表未提供，不能外推为跨任务一致占优。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，贡献在于低开销地学习复用决策，而非证明经验的因果价值：任务只执行一次，成功标签同时包含执行器和任务难度影响。后续应检验漂移流中评分是否仍能区分有益经验与偶然共现。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.26342","tldr":"背景与问题：预先指定只改数据、训练器或 harness，会绕过研究 agent 判断瓶颈及协调组件的能力；扩大编辑范围又增加接触测试与修改评分的机会。\n\n方法：VibeTraining-Bench 提供共同基座和固定资源，让研究者根据验证分数及轨迹选择干预，再将最终系统交给隔离评分器测试。只有终端和软件任务开放全部三类组件，其余固定推理接口。\n\n结果与结论：SWE-bench Verified 上，一套研究配置将成绩从32.9%升至53.7%；但所有研究配置的五任务均分仍低于人工指令模型。轨迹分析显示更多是数据与超参数轻量调整，完整组件消融未见。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，开放编辑范围不等于实际学会协同设计，更不证明研究者自身变强。应优先核查联合修改是否超过单组件与等预算搜索；墙钟内大量等待，也使相同时间预算不等于相同有效实验机会。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-22","critique":"今天这批材料有实质推进，集中在改进信号如何组织，尚不足以确认递归能力增长。MELD把协调器纳入任务内训练，联合更新消融比团队排名更值得看[1]；SSR与HGM-Dual分别追问喂多少证据、修哪类错误，是既有证据治理路线的具体推进，仍属固定搜索流程改良[2][3]。Hippo处理侥幸成功与经验冲突，但同源判断和重试成本仍待核对[4]。物理RSI综述明确要求分开验证行为、学习程序和改进者收益，现有物理研究尚未隔离递归增益[5]。本次依据均为截断全文，部分主表缺失，另有11篇待分析论文，并非当天全部候选总结。优先精读MELD核查预算与信用归因，再读SSR检查混合选择分数的泛化影响；工程控制和应用涨分暂不宜升级为递归突破。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.24454","arxiv:2610.28815","arxiv:2610.30042","arxiv:2610.24453","arxiv:2610.29677"],"backlog":11,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24454","tldr":"背景与问题：多智能体研究的任务分配既决定探索方向，也决定研究者获得什么训练经验；固定协调策略难以跟随研究者能力变化调整分工。\n\n方法：MELD用实际候选评估结果交替训练协调器与研究者的私有适配器，共同奖励预算内优质成果。更新后的分配改变下一轮学习经验，研究者的新表现又反馈给协调器；执行模型冻结。\n\n结果与结论：两项博弈任务中，联合更新比单独更新任一层产生更多高分候选，支持两层适配互补。整体实验按候选评估次数匹配，不能解释为同总算力优势。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，具体推进是协调器也从任务内实验学习。但适配器每个任务重置，实际训练只采用单轮信用，尚未证明跨任务积累或更新算法自身增强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24453","tldr":"背景与问题：正确结果可能掩盖错误推理，失败也可能只是执行失误；单次复盘容易提炼错误经验，持续追加又会让冲突指导反复传播。\n\n方法：Hippo在相同策略与记忆下比较同题多次尝试，从模型诊断的失败和侥幸成功中提炼带适用条件的决策，再与旧记忆比较、合并或替换。修订后的指导用于后续任务，权重不变。\n\n结果与结论：软件修复、网页操作和动作预测均有收益，保留经验也少于追加基线；后者长期积累最终低于无记忆配置。主要结果表缺失，无法核对与直接重试的完整预算对照。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，经验维护应检查决策为何成立、何时适用。执行、诊断与写回使用同一模型，共同盲点仍可固化；多次尝试的额外交互成本也影响实际价值。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24177","tldr":"背景与问题：视频规划器能描绘任务过程，但视频转动作通常依赖专家动作数据；随机探索又难到达长程任务中的关键转移。\n\n方法：Mirror尝试执行视频计划，用实际观察与自身执行动作训练动作映射。即使偏离计划，这种配对仍提供正确监督；从实际状态重新规划，使探索停留在能力边界附近，动作噪声帮助越过尚未掌握的步骤。\n\n结果与结论：Minecraft匹配终止协议下，铁镐成功率为8.6%，Dreamer V3为1.7%，但奖励和动作设置不同。四个未见目标迁移环境中，有一个不及随机采集对照。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，失败也能产生有效监督，关键是按实际结果训练。任务知识仍来自预训练及任务微调的视频规划器；结果支持动作能力自举，不能称无示范学习，也未证明学习程序递归增强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.30116","tldr":"背景与问题：会解题不等于会生成值得学习的任务；只测难度，也无法区分有效挑战、不可解环境和无效提示。\n\n方法：Environment Duels让模型编写环境与特权提示，在相同实例和预算下比较有无提示的执行结果，再把求解轨迹交回作者修订一次。提示净收益衡量作者与学习者的匹配，并分别记录提示修复和破坏的尝试。\n\n结果与结论：九模型实验中，最强求解者并非最佳出题者；一次修订使提示收益从6.3升至13.4个百分点。单一学习模型的训练研究还发现提示收益与留出训练收益相关，但详细结果段落缺失。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，课程价值应针对接收者测量。提示可能诱发过早承诺；当前一次作者适配及训练关联，不足以证明双方持续共训练，也不能把相关性当作教学价值认证。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.30042","tldr":"背景与问题：约束规划失败常由具体违规决定，开放式修改却可能修错组件，或重复祖先的无效改动，持续消耗评估预算。\n\n方法：HGM-Dual把祖先修改、分数及错误变化整理成上下文，同时生成一般探索与针对主要违规的候选。错误定向路径只在预检信号稳定时启用；候选接受相同执行评估，最佳子代进入后续搜索。\n\n结果与结论：相同评估预算下，旅行规划案例准确率由最强表列基线的56.25%升至64.38%，购物任务也有收益。完整消融与划分说明缺失，无法把总体差异单独归给谱系记忆。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，规划改进可能更依赖编辑目标是否对应实际约束错误。祖先前后变化提供归因线索，但不隔离因果贡献；固定编辑与搜索流程也未证明改进者自身变强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.30017","tldr":"背景与问题：原始题目、回答与演化历史混入同一上下文，可能耗尽token并妨碍修改决策；Bedrock迁移还暴露格式和提前终止问题。\n\n方法：GuideEvolve让独立上下文中的模型专家分析任务表现，再由演化agent修改求解逻辑；保存最佳版本用于恢复，并在最低尝试要求后允许自主停止。反馈来自任务表现与模型建议，专家不是人工真值源。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称迭代数约减半、方差降低，但主表被截断。附录最佳求解器增加多次采样或切换模型，最终准确率因而混有推理资源变化，尚不能隔离各项控制的收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，这是上下文与运行控制的工程改进。专家上下文隔离不保证无偏，一阶优化只是类比；两类静态问答实验也不足以确立生产部署稳定性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.29784","tldr":"背景与问题：未来预测能获得事后真值，但反馈延迟、轨迹稀少，训练时重新搜索还可能接触已发生的答案，破坏时间边界。\n\n方法：DeepEvolve分离证据搜索与概率预测，用缓存证据和事件结果训练预测端；搜索轨迹经模型过程判断蒸馏为技能，弱点再改变任务生成指导。结果真值用于参数与环境更新，不提供给行为评审。\n\n结果与结论：材料称FutureX连续三周领先；自建表中各配置领先同组基线，但其中一个总体第九，与摘要四配置均居前三的说法不符。主要消融和完整成本缺失。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，值得保留的是各更新通道的证据时间边界。实时真值不保证自动提取与评分正确，系统排名也不能隔离权重、技能和课程贡献，更未证明开放世界是RSI的必要条件。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.29677","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人在固定流程下变强，不代表学习流程或修改流程的改进者变强；物理试验还受到观测不全、磨损与不可逆后果限制。\n\n方法：本文沿经验留下什么改变、谁在下一轮使用它组织研究，区分行为收益、后续学习收益、程序改进与递归关系。递归要求修补知识改善改进者，改善后的改进者再参与自身下一次改进，并提出两轮受控检验。\n\n结果与结论：综述认为现有物理研究支持前三类收益，部分系统改变了改进者知识或工具，但尚未隔离递归本身的增益。这是证据分类及实验原则，没有新机器人系统的收益实验。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，其价值是把组件名称转成跨轮可检验关系。比较新旧改进程序还须匹配起点、试验机会和物理条件；软件回滚无法恢复硬件损伤。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.29641","tldr":"背景与问题：语义通信的准确率、传输量与计算位置相互影响，固定架构内调权重覆盖不了程序结构变化；反复使用验证集又可能造成过拟合。\n\n方法：ComRSI用固定模型修改通信程序，受保护的信道、资源核算及公开评估筛选候选。获准代码与文字历史进入下一代，每个候选从头训练；隐藏图像及信道条件只在搜索后评价。\n\n结果与结论：十次重复搜索中，代码继承方案优于无记忆提案者，但相对带文字历史的非继承方案，差异统计上不确定。最终设计减少传输量并改善准确率，同时把更多计算移到发送端。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，代码继承与文字历史的拆分比单条涨分曲线更有价值。结果支持受约束的程序优化，未证明优化者增强；相同训练步数也不等于相同算力。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.29467","tldr":"背景与问题：长期对话记忆不断追加或按新近内容覆盖，容易把短暂噪声当成用户变化，也可能让过时事实持续牵引回答。\n\n方法：PreCoMem把用户信息存成带支持权重的信念，结合语义偏差、矛盾判断与检索集中度决定更新。模糊证据先写成假设，反复支持后晋级；可靠矛盾则降低旧事实权重，改变后续召回。\n\n结果与结论：材料称三个对话基准领先，并以自建漂移测试检验抗噪更新；主要结果及消融被截断，无法核对效果量与独立贡献。变化发生在记忆状态，门控和更新规则固定。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，延迟承诺适合处理不确定用户信息，但检索集中不等于证据正确，单条错误记忆也可能占据主导。支持权重不是校准概率，不能解释成事实真实性或管理器递归学习。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.29121","tldr":"背景与问题：编码agent子代尚未运行时，父代成绩无法区分同一父代提出的不同修改；逐个执行又会耗尽搜索预算。\n\n方法：本文用执行测试标注的编辑训练轻量预测器，结合父代成绩与代码差异排序新提案，只运行选中候选。预测器随后冻结，执行成绩决定档案和最终版本，校准支出计入测试预算。\n\n结果与结论：GPT-4o的HumanEval+留出成绩为87.0%，父代成绩消融为84.2%；相对HGM的配对区间却含零。Claude配置与HGM几乎持平，优势并不一致。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，预执行排序应按最终交付系统验收，不能只看预测相关性。理论给出的是Beta分布性质，未证明编辑预测有效；文内HGM计数存在单节点和谱系两种口径，复现前需澄清。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.28945","tldr":"背景与问题：只执行单一动作会遗漏替代方案，真实环境分支搜索又成本高；更准确地预测下一观察，也不保证选到更有用的动作。\n\n方法：系统预测少量候选动作的一步结果，由语言评估器判断进展与风险，按预测成本加权供控制器决策。真实转移分别写成规划和世界模型经验，改变后续提案、选择及预测；模型参数冻结。\n\n结果与结论：材料称在两个语言交互环境、三种骨干上整体领先，但主结果、消融和成本表缺失。理论拆分候选覆盖、预测成本与选择误差，不保证实际任务成功率单调提高。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，预测器与行动器需要分别验收：正确加权救不了缺失候选，控制器还可生成未经预测的新动作。经验基于真实转移，进展判断仍由模型完成，须隔离记忆收益和额外推理调用收益。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.28815","tldr":"背景与问题：harness演化加入更多任务后可能退化，重复或低价值轨迹会稀释修改方向；固定证据规模也难跟随当前失败分布。\n\n方法：SSR按可操作性和覆盖度排列经验，用不同长度的证据前缀分别修改同一父代。候选在共享批次上竞赛，逐步淘汰弱者并保护父代；接受新版本后重采轨迹，刷新下一轮排序。\n\n结果与结论：扩大任务池时，通过率从64.3%增至68.3%，所测基线下降。候选选择混合验证与训练任务，不能视为纯留出估计；理论仅给单轮有限池保证。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，证据规模值得成为每轮搜索变量。但嵌套前缀同时改变规模和内容，不能完全隔离规模效应；覆盖目标的近似保证不等于执行收益保证，长期选择偏差仍需单独测量。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.28577","tldr":"背景与问题：删除或总结早期文本会使后续KV缓存失效，重新预填充增加成本；为限制重算而大幅丢弃上下文，又可能损害任务表现。\n\n方法：Cache Engineering允许直接删除缓存并调整位置，保留其他已计算状态。服务系统同时记录token与操作历史，避免错误复用；这些操作也成为agent可搜索、评估和修改的推理资源策略。\n\n结果与结论：人工滚动删除策略比阈值总结平均省27.7%成本；演化策略在留出任务上比专家策略再省7.1%。演化反馈、预算与准确率约束段落缺失，不能把整体系统收益归于自改进。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，变化是开放内部缓存控制面。同样文本不再对应同样状态，复现必须保留操作历史；当前服务收益较明确，但策略演化的信用来源和递归机制仍待核查。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.28282","tldr":"背景与问题：图表总体成绩掩盖少数类型的严重短板，固定工具难覆盖异质结构；让模型逐步协调稳定操作链还增加调用开销。\n\n方法：ChartEvo用训练答案真值与执行轨迹诊断能力缺口，联合修订技能、工具，并把验证过的局部调用组合保存为工具链。获准组件进入下一轮，测试时冻结harness，在新实例上复用。\n\n结果与结论：ChartBench长尾准确率从48.0%升至93.6%，对应45.6个百分点，并非相对提高45.6%。两基准分别演化，支持同基准新实例适配，不能据此认定跨基准迁移。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，把稳定局部流程交给运行时执行，可能兼顾测量与调用效率。但案例中模型仍把不确定区间中点当答案，工具可执行和推断可信必须分开验收；完整消融与演化成本未见。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-21","critique":"今天这批材料有实质推进，但主要是把“为什么涨分”拆得更清楚，而非证明递归加速。HDA发现基准捷径可跨划分延续，留出集高分也不够；持续学习审计则把平均收益拆成新任务适应、旧知识遗忘和未见任务干扰[1][2]。Self-HPO让更新后的执行策略继续提出harness修改，但联合演化已有历史，真正增量是困难集刷新；尚不能把执行训练等同于改进能力训练[3]。具身技能编译更值得警惕宣传反转：多数成品首稿即合格，修补优势主要来自版本继承，反馈的额外贡献较弱[4]。安全共演化提供执行验证和同条件信用分配，但部分效率收益仍混有覆盖量变化[5]。优先精读HDA与技能编译，核对归因合同。以上基于截断全文；检索超时，本次只处理已有库，另有3篇待分析论文，并非当天全部候选总结。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.22466","arxiv:2610.25858","arxiv:2610.22791","arxiv:2610.25114","arxiv:2610.24896"],"backlog":3,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22791","tldr":"背景与问题：固定harness限制策略能获得的训练轨迹；策略更新后，旧harness针对的失败又可能过时。只改其中一侧，无法持续匹配执行能力与运行支持。\n\n方法：当前策略先分析失败并提出harness修订，按搜索集成绩保留候选；随后在新harness下用执行验证奖励训练策略。训练中始终未解的任务成为下一轮搜索集，更新后的策略继续担任提案者。\n\n结果与结论：三个编码基准平均解决率比仅训练策略高2.9个百分点。困难集刷新优于固定集的消融来自外部提案者配置，不能直接视为自提案条件下的独立验证；实验仅运行两轮。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键推进是让干预目标跟随失败分布，而非首次联合修改权重与harness。执行训练后的模型重新提案，不等于已证明它更会改进系统；应固定执行者，比较不同轮次提案者的单位预算编辑收益。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22740","tldr":"背景与问题：有技能提示时适中的任务，撤掉提示后可能全部失败，使组相对训练失去有效差异；直接按成功率撤技能，又混淆任务难度变化与技能实际贡献。\n\n方法：训练时随机向部分尝试隐藏一项技能，用同任务的有无技能对照判断它是否仍有帮助。课程选择偏向隐藏技能后仍有成功也有失败的任务，使学习持续发生在脱离指导后的能力边界。\n\n结果与结论：论文在十二项数据集报告领先，并称零技能测试保持表现；可见实验说明各方法共享执行Worker、任务和计算预算，但主要结果与消融数值被截断，无法核对各环节贡献。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，内化应由撤除指导后的表现验收，而非训练时高分推定。这里外层改变技能与课程，不是学习规则自主重写；仍需检查逐项撤除后的技能交互，以及撤除判据在任务漂移时是否可靠。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22599","tldr":"背景与问题：研究agent提出方案很快，真实训练却慢；选错实验会消耗后续搜索预算。只测能否二选一，不能判断模型是否知道收益大小。\n\n方法：收集机器学习改动及实际训练结果，让预测器读取任务、现有代码和改动差异，事前估计新分数，再分别检验方向、关联程度和幅度。分析排除失败运行或缺少可用预测的样本。\n\n结果与结论：最佳模型的拟合R²为0.49，各模型都压低大变化的预测幅度。正文把预测值对实际值回归，不能把该R²直接解释为原始预测准确解释一半实际收益；收益选择的理论换算还依赖高斯假设。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，有用排序与数值校准必须分开验收。这里包含有意改善和恶化的短实验，且主设置提供已实现代码差异，不能直接外推为尚未实现的新颖研究提案筛选能力。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22466","tldr":"背景与问题：harness搜索得分上涨，可能来自记住基准规律或增加调用；即使留出集也上涨，共享的数据构造捷径仍可能冒充泛化。\n\n方法：将原harness扩展到演化版本的推理预算，并从演化版本中最小化移除已检测捷径；两类干预由人工复核。剩余差额仅作为可泛化改进的上界，再独立检查留出表现。\n\n结果与结论：有显著搜索收益的设置中，过拟合与推理扩展的平均归因占比分别为54%和14%。部分编码配置虽无检测到的捷径、残差占全部收益，留出表现仍退化。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，最有价值的结果不是一个平均扣分比例，而是“没有检测到问题”仍不能认证迁移。归因依赖捷径识别、移除方式和预算匹配口径，报告比例还经过截断处理，不能当作普遍适用的精确因果份额。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25906","tldr":"背景与问题：动态图通常固定文本向量，让图编码器独自弥合通用语义与时序关系之间的差距；完全自由适配又可能破坏文本语义。\n\n方法：保持预训练语言模型不变，让轻量适配器接收图结构对比学习的梯度；另用原文本向量作语义锚点，使表征能够吸收时空信息而不必逐点复制原向量。\n\n结果与结论：材料称动态图边分类优于静态文本基线，并分析表征可分性与资源开销；主要结果表被截断，不能核对完整效果量，链接预测和节点分类仍属后续工作。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，这项工作的机制是受约束表征适配，不是agent改进自身。结构信息与语义保持之间的权衡值得图学习研究关注，但训练中的参数变化、动态图变化都不自动构成RSI，应排除在进展主视图之外。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25858","tldr":"背景与问题：单域平均分上升不能说明agent能持续学习。共享提示或工作区的一次改动会作用于所有后续任务，可能在学会新流程时破坏旧流程。\n\n方法：固定模型，在主题、流程、领域及组合漂移流中比较记忆检索、提示修改和工作区修改。任务组及边界不告知agent，各检查点冻结harness，在独立题集上区分当前适应、提前干扰和后续遗忘。\n\n结果与结论：多数流有总体收益，但没有方法同时兼顾高适应与高稳定。全局修改会干扰其他任务；检索能隔离遥远领域，却仍会在相似查询要求相反流程时发生碰撞。实验骨干固定为一种模型。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，外部记忆并未消除持续学习问题，只把参数干扰变成修改作用域与经验路由问题。下一步应在相同漂移流、预算和任务顺序下检验条件化检索与局部更新，而不是仅比较最终平均分。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25847","tldr":"背景与问题：盈利交易不代表批评正确，也不代表交易者据此作出的修订有益；历史经验在市场状态改变后还可能反向误导。\n\n方法：将原提案、批评、修订与事后市场结果关联保存，分开记录风险是否发生和修订是否改善收益。两个记忆选择器按当前情境选经验，用同账户起点下完整有无记忆流程的净收益差在线学习，交易LLM保持冻结。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称美股实验的收益和风险指标领先所列基线；正文给出同预算记忆消融设计，但主要数值结果被截断，无法核对优势幅度、跨时段稳定性与完整调用成本。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，区分预警命中与修订收益，比笼统复盘盈亏更有价值。但完整流程的共同标签不能识别每个角色或记忆的独立贡献；历史价格反事实也不等于真实成交与市场冲击下的部署验证。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25119","tldr":"背景与问题：记忆过去成功，不代表适合当前任务；一次成功与大量稳定成功也不该具有相同可信度。静态效用分数无法同时表达情境和证据量。\n\n方法：训练独立估值器，为任务—记忆组合输出效用分布并据此探索检索。执行后移除单条记忆重跑，用成绩差及保留它时的结果校准估值；新轨迹再凝练成经验，执行骨干不变。\n\n结果与结论：可见附录在两个推理设置中匹配三次采样及共同选择器，BEAM仍优于记忆基线，削弱纯推理扩展解释；主结果和完整训练成本被截断，不能推为已证明长程稳定学习。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，进步在于尝试测量经验的边际作用，而不只是记录共现成功。移除实验有额外执行成本，随机输出与多记忆交互也会影响信用；概率分布的形式本身不能证明不确定性已经校准。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25114","tldr":"背景与问题：每次机器人执行都调用强模型很贵；但离线修补得到高分技能，也可能只是首稿已足够好或多次选择，而非从反馈学会改进。\n\n方法：强模型离线写和修技能，经冻结后新抽布局考试，成品由纯代码或廉价异族模型调用。隐藏验证、重写及仅继承版本的对照，分离反馈、继承与选择；安全门控独立于作者。\n\n结果与结论：七个冻结技能中五个首稿已达标；修补相对重写的优势主要来自版本继承，开发反馈额外贡献证据较弱。部分技能纯代码复用达到148/150成功，但另有任务持续因安全中止未能编译。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，材料更支持“把已有能力编译成可复用工件”，而非作者递归变强。计入失败活动后成本明显变化；没有直接控制基线，不能计算部署盈亏平衡，有限零中止考试也不能认证真实安全。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25078","tldr":"背景与问题：新harness可能要求模型不会使用的接口，而最新检查点未必最适合它；只继承上一代配对，会丢掉更早但仍有用的结构与能力。\n\n方法：保留历代harness、权重和执行记录，分别选择结构起点与模型检查点，也允许合并历史权重。固定元agent结合任务分数与接口违例筛选组合，再用该运行时下的成功轨迹微调，将结果送回档案。\n\n结果与结论：论文在失败归因、权限SQL和家居控制上报告小模型达到或超过部分强模型；历史继承机制的主要消融被截断，跨模型排名不能独立证明继承优于继续训练。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可复用的单位可能不是单个“最好版本”，而是有条件的结构—能力配对。但接口违例率只覆盖可观察格式和调用错误；低违例不等于会完成任务，反复用验证集选择配对也可能积累选择偏差。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25012","tldr":"背景与问题：分别优化草稿模型与验证模型的内核，会忽略同GPU并行后的竞争和同步；孤立内核更快，整轮解码未必更快。\n\n方法：将两模型的执行纳入共同编译边界，LLM修改联合方案，经数值检查后测量完整共享执行时延。搜索树累计真实奖励，编译错误和内核诊断帮助后续提案，避免只追求局部速度。\n\n结果与结论：六种单GPU配置中，整轮几何平均加速为1.37倍，加入交错内核后为1.45倍。最终候选重新配对计时并检查噪声，但这些是每轮执行结果，不能直接等同完整服务吞吐收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可迁移认识是评价边界应覆盖组件相互作用。这里优化的是外部编译方案，未展示研究者权重、技能或搜索策略持续增强；搜索总成本及其相对传统优化器的独立贡献仍需核查。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24944","tldr":"背景与问题：长时研究跨越模型会话，代码和运行实验可保存，但过去为何放弃某方案、哪些经验仍适用容易丢失，导致重复探索。\n\n方法：将分支实现、证据和死路理由持久化，按层次记忆恢复上下文；异模型审查研究方向，隔离的固定验证器检查产物。经验影响下一次实验，而评价规则只在活动之间重新定义。\n\n结果与结论：论文列出带证书的数学构造和界；算法编码中，同底层模型与推理强度下，总分比Codex高5.4%，模型成本为其64%。相关对照细节被截断，纪录采用截至2026年9月16日的参考来源。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可核查数学证书增强的是产物可信度，不能自动证明记忆让研究者越来越会研究。应匹配总计算、初始参考和研究时长，移除跨活动经验，检验方法改进是否超出持续投入与分支搜索。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24896","tldr":"背景与问题：静态漏洞数据跟不上攻击者变化；只看训练奖励，还可能把对手停滞误判为防御进步。不同难度条件混在基线里，也会污染信用分配。\n\n方法：共同训练攻防适配器种群，攻击补丁须保持功能并在容器复现指定漏洞才有战略奖励。同角色策略在相同任务和冻结对手条件下比较，比赛保留多样性；另用历史及外部攻击者衡量进步。\n\n结果与结论：冻结攻击者时防御平衡准确率为60.8%，共同演化为64.8%，支持动态对手有贡献。但相对单策略组基线的效率优势混有训练条件覆盖量差异，关键匹配预算隔离臂未运行。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，比排名更重要的是把“对手变弱”和“自己变强”分开。代码奖励来自已知类别的可达漏洞探针，不是自主发现新漏洞；探针未触发也不等于代码完全安全，算法本身仍固定。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24630","tldr":"背景与问题：单轮技能修订可能覆盖以后仍有用的程序，坏技能却继续被检索。只有生成和编辑，没有保留与淘汰规则，经验库难以稳定积累。\n\n方法：按任务类别隔离轨迹分析，只修改相关技能；检索同时考虑相关性与历史使用成绩。候选库经选择集筛选，置信投票和效用控制生命周期，淘汰名称进入受限墓地，模型权重不变。\n\n结果与结论：论文在四个基准报告多数设置领先，但主要结果表未提供。附录明确只测试有限技能规模，跨基准迁移留待未来；不能把多域分别优化的结果当成持续跨域积累证据。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，库管理有工程价值，但使用某技能时的任务成绩不等于它的边际贡献。名称级禁返也挡不住换名重生，可能阻止情境变化后的合理恢复；长期维护应接受漂移流与语义去重的独立测试。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24464","tldr":"背景与问题：单个技能成功，不代表其结束状态满足下一技能的前提；工具正常返回也可能没有建立目标物理关系。任务级补丁难以修复这种共享接口问题。\n\n方法：从源任务轨迹定位最早失效要求，修改共享工具、完成合同、交接或验证逻辑。通用性检查与同初始状态的执行、回归比较决定继承版本；目标任务只提供声明式组合，不再修代码。\n\n结果与结论：论文报告仿真与三个实机组合任务收益，但主比较和经验扩展曲线的终点成绩不同。附录还披露部分推理比较复用评测行并曾接触目标场景，冻结执行不能直接证明完全未见目标。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，共享接口是可检验的迁移载体，但须将局部机制修复、完整任务成功与搜索流程变强分开。源诊断使用特权状态，基线并非全部匹配重跑，扩展曲线为单次运行，当前不足以确认稳定递归增长。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-20","critique":"今天这批材料有实质机制推进，但不足以支持“递归加速已经实现”。LM2LM把实验预测接入提案者训练，再用真实执行纠正策略放大的高估，比单纯累积研究记录更进一步[1]；SpecRSI学习编辑与验证的后续净收益，但目标成本下降不等于总成本下降[2]。评估器共演化值得关注，不过UCoE多数收益仍来自当前回答修补，不能全算作跨任务学习[3]。失败学习审计进一步表明，经验正确仍不保证迁移[4]；预植后门也能借记忆写回放大，静态检查不足[5]。相比之下，分层记忆与技能命名更像既有路线细化。优先精读LM2LM的校准对照和失败学习审计的迁移协议。本次均依据截断全文，部分结果仅见摘要；仍有18篇待分析论文，不是当天全部候选的总结。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.23344","arxiv:2610.16491","arxiv:2610.17609","arxiv:2610.22984","arxiv:2610.15244"],"backlog":18,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18083","tldr":"背景与问题：增加研究agent不一定增加有效进展：早期低分可能掩盖好想法，广播未确认诊断会使探索同质化，单次成功也不会自动变成下一次研究的方法。\n\n方法：AReaL-RSI让leader依据实验记录协调持续研究者，共享时保留发现的条件与不确定性，限制未解决问题的主动传播。活动结束后再把证据提炼成研究方向、知识和技能，供后续团队使用；骨干与leader策略不变。\n\n结果与结论：给定资源配置下，相对Codex-Goal，两种骨干的Terminal Bench成绩均增加2.2个百分点；内核实验中，分工加共享优于独立探索和仅共享。主要实验段落缺失，无法完整核对成本与跨活动继承收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键区别是共享有适用条件的证据，而非共享全部历史。正面标签的程序检查只确认来源，不认证结论；harness发布也不要求未来任务增益，因此配置可继承不能直接算作研究程序已变强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.17718","tldr":"背景与问题：心电模型的弱点会随训练变化，但定向生成波形可能同时改变其他特征，使问题、答案与实际信号不符；只追着反馈错误补数据也可能过拟合。\n\n方法：ECG-RSI先按目标特征编辑训练波形，再复测目标与受保护特征，合格后才生成监督。构造错误用于修补生成规则，学习者错误用于提出不同数据配方；同父模型训练出的分支在独立选择集比较，获选分支进入下一轮。\n\n结果与结论：三轮后，四项问答平均准确率由34.57%升至56.04%；保留路径的监督重心转向易混类别对比，但继续纠错的外部收益递减。可见附录另列一组三种子分数，口径未充分说明，不能与主结果混算。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，错误诊断只能提出干预，不能证明该干预有教学价值。独立选择与外部评测使这一区分可检验；波形复测仍依赖特征提取与问答审查，不能等同临床有效性认证。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.17609","tldr":"背景与问题：开放任务没有答案或可执行测试，错误verifier不仅会把当前回答改坏，还会把误导经验写入后续harness；固定评分标准又可能随任务变化失效。\n\n方法：UCoE构造只破坏一个属性的回答对，选择最弱属性族上辨别力最高的评分程序。该程序指导局部修补、选择交付回答并控制经验写入；完成任务的诊断再提出新程序，经对比测试后替换旧版，所有模型参数固定。\n\n结果与结论：六个开放基准上，两种骨干相对匹配直接生成的平均偏好率为59.00%和57.19%。可见引言明确称多数收益来自当前任务修补，不能把总体优势全部归于跨任务共演化。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，评分器应按能否辨别关键退化来选，而非只看平均准确率。但合成退化的偏好方向不等于自然修订的真实优劣；重复使用对比集也留下选择过拟合风险，理论不覆盖任意开放任务。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.17114","tldr":"背景与问题：隐式机器人世界模型预测出错时，难把偏差定位到可修正量；每次重建场景又很昂贵，过度谨慎还会阻止获得辨识模型所需的接触证据。\n\n方法：D-World让冻结LLM编写可执行数字孪生，用实机执行后的测量修订对象状态和物理参数。参数修改须在最新动作段回放中不显著恶化已测残差，下一段动作再经更新后的仿真检查；结构错误则触发重建。\n\n结果与结论：双臂机器人的毛巾与烤面包任务展示局部修订后继续执行，其中面包深度残差由22.4降至1.5毫米。材料没有提供完整成功率、重建成本和受控消融，案例不能证明普遍收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可编辑参数使误差成为行动依据，但本质仍含系统辨识。门控只约束最新可测证据，早期残差不否决更新，仿真通过也不认证实机安全；离线后训练用途尚不能算已验证闭环。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.16523","tldr":"背景与问题：多轮用户互动的坏训练信号未必来自策略：模拟用户可能泄露信息，工具或验证器可能出错。只做奖励塑形，无法修复产生这些轨迹的上游过程。\n\n方法：EAU让元agent读取训练轨迹与统计，诊断问题后修改用户规则、交互条件、奖励或训练配置；通过有限完整性检查的变更可在训练中热替换。策略继续按固定RL算法学习，已发现的干预经验跨运行保存。\n\n结果与结论：摘要在三个基准、两种骨干上给出相对最强基线14.7%—15.0%的总体增益。主要结果表被截断；附录说明不少基线来自既有报告，而PPO与EAU自行评测，因此并非全部统一重跑。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，把故障归因到训练系统而非一律归因策略，是有价值的改动。但运行内修补、奖励变化与超参数调整混合发生，需要核对各自增益和总预算；环境可编辑不等于元优化机制也在变强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.16491","tldr":"背景与问题：每改一版就完整评估，会把预算耗在尚未产生价值的中间状态；只预测当前候选质量，又忽略它还需多少编辑和检查才能成为可采用改进。\n\n方法：SpecRSI允许从未完成评估的版本继续起草，但采用前必须取得完整真实检查。搜索根据后续编辑与验证的预期净收益分配预算；外层用整次搜索的已验证收益减全部成本，训练下一轮改进者，真实评估合同不变。\n\n结果与结论：摘要给出编码验证成功率69.4%，对照HGM为64.3%，目标成本指标也下降；但可见图注另显示，相对MetaRSI-v1，目标成本更低时总成本指标略高，不能概括为全面省算力。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，改进者应学习哪些尚未成功的编辑值得继续验证，而非只模仿成功补丁。完整搜索信用回应了这一点；预测器仍可能浪费不可追回的预算，且固定外层算法不意味着改进过程无限自举。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.16078","tldr":"背景与问题：领域专家继续监督训练已达平台时，通用agent仍可能在部分实例上提供帮助；但专家变强后，旧agent策略与交互方式可能不再提供增量。\n\n方法：HACE用任务标签检验agent是否在当前实例上优于专家，探索结果决定专家重点训练哪些样本，专家仍学原始标签。候选专家与harness联合比较后，再收集相对保留专家有正贡献的新回答训练agent，改变下一轮可用贡献。\n\n结果与结论：材料称在推荐、蛋白功能和晶体稳定性预测中优于所比较自改进方法，起点为已收敛专家。主要结果表缺失；蛋白任务实际只更新预测头，不能统称所有领域基础模型权重均被改进。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，平均更弱的agent也可能凭局部互补性帮助专家，关键是验证哪些实例值得投入。这里监督来自原始标签而非纯自生知识；总体联合得分还需拆分专家、agent与harness各自的独立贡献。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15964","tldr":"背景与问题：agent重写harness后，端到端rollout昂贵，原仓库测试又漏掉大量行为变化；更大的生成测试集虽可能更强，却会增加每次准入成本。\n\n方法：TeSearch按测试集大小分区竞争，在每种规模内优化覆盖与变异检测，避免小而强的候选被大集合挤掉；实际生成数量反过来校准搜索。得到的测试集作为harness改写的可执行回归门控。\n\n结果与结论：在mini-swe-agent的470个核验改写上，行为变化拒绝率为59.9%，仓库测试为25.3%；代价是误拒部分等价改写。这里测的是构造改写的行为保持，不是多轮自改进后的任务成功率。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，回归检查是保住已有能力的护栏，不是改进价值本身。若目标本就需要改变行为，强制保持旧实现还可能阻止好更新；后续应把保持合同与允许变化的功能目标分开测试。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15772","tldr":"背景与问题：固定技能库或离线技能生成器会落后于训练中的策略；给教师增加技能也不保证它比学生可靠，统一蒸馏可能强化错误指导。\n\n方法：RSIPO让当前策略从自身轨迹写技能，在同起点回放中与随机留出的无技能轨迹比较执行收益。收益奖励技能生成，噪声校准后的收益则调节学生对技能教师的信任；更新策略再产生下一批轨迹，测试不提供技能。\n\n结果与结论：Qwen2.5-7B在ALFWorld成功率为98.6%，比次优基线高2.5个百分点。但附录显示3B模型在搜索任务只排第二，不能照摘要推广为所有配置均领先；完整成本和消融表未见。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，技能相关不等于具有教学价值，实际回放比教师自信更合适。收益来自同任务重放，还需防止答案泄漏与起点不一致；初始化也使用外部LLM技能监督，不能称全程无教师。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15708","tldr":"背景与问题：代码实体相互依赖，修好一个函数的规格可能改变整个模块生成，使其他函数退化；沿单条修订路径容易反复丢失已有成果。\n\n方法：SpecForge用从规格重建代码后的测试失败修改行为描述，而非直接积累代码补丁。搜索保留各实体上互有优势的规格状态，并优先修订被调用者，减少依赖错误造成的误导；新状态重新生成和测试整个模块。\n\n结果与结论：摘要给出五种骨干上平均比最强基线高5.7个百分点，并称规格可迁移到跨语言翻译和新功能实现。主要实验段落未提供，尚不能核对迁移效果量及完整预算。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，外部知识的质量可用其能否支持行为重建衡量，而非文档相似度。不过测试来自已有参考实现，验证的是捕捉现有行为；这不自动证明新需求正确性，也不证明搜索器自身越来越会优化。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15244","tldr":"背景与问题：只在初始记忆下扫描视觉触发器，可能漏掉依赖后续经验状态才激活的后门；部署时权重不变也不保证行为安全不变。\n\n方法：EvolvAttack通过部署前投毒训练预置联合条件：触发图像与载荷相关记忆同时存在才稳定输出恶意行为。早期罕见输出被正常记忆机制写回，后续检索再提高激活机会，形成放大；攻击者部署后不直接修改记忆或权重。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称攻击成功率从演化前0.5%升至百次交互内超过95%。但可见消融中，补充空记忆训练覆盖会降低攻击效果，说明静态隐蔽性与动态强度受具体训练覆盖影响。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，安全审计对象应是带写回的交互轨迹，而非单个权重快照。这是预植后门借记忆放大的证据，不能表述为普通经验学习自然生成恶意；真实部署风险还取决于触发暴露与记忆准入。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.23599","tldr":"背景与问题：一条轨迹可能同时暴露规划失误、工具误用和可自动化操作；把它们统一写进技能文档，不能决定该如何验证、维护或何时调用。\n\n方法：CDSE从成功与失败轨迹提取带证据的行为修改建议，按其作用分配维护方式：一般规则与局部经验保留适用条件，可执行程序须经过测试。协调冲突后重写调用描述，让更新后的技能影响后续执行，模型与协议保持固定。\n\n结果与结论：六个基准、三模型、两harness的测试表均领先，平均比各设置最强竞争方法高2.6个百分点。训练与测试分开，但完整消融及演化总成本未见，不能单靠总体排名确认功能拆分的独立贡献。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，有意义的是更新的功能决定验证合同，而非认知类比本身。多轮可重复整理固定轨迹，因此轮次增长不代表新增交互学习，更不说明技能更新器本身递归变强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.23574","tldr":"背景与问题：把用户交互原样塞进记忆或技能，会混淆环境限制与通用操作经验，也难判断哪些补丁应保留、哪些已过时。\n\n方法：Darwin-Claw把有学习信号的轨迹整理成带触发条件的经验单元，写入相关技能；后续轨迹提供效果与无效调用变化，控制试用、晋级和淘汰。LLM判断新轨迹是否相关及改善是否来自经验，底层模型参数不变。\n\n结果与结论：自主后训练场景中，相对只传递上下文报告，技能方案的六项平均分由28.42%升至31.91%。但具体模型—任务组合仍有退化，WildClawBench的完整数值表和消融未见，稳定性主张证据不足。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，限定经验容量与撤销低效补丁比持续追加更可控；但轨迹后的LLM归因不能替代同条件有无记忆对照。还需区分研究目标模型变强与负责优化的agent技能真正获得迁移。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.23344","tldr":"背景与问题：训练研究提案者若逐个运行模型实验，反馈成本过高；改用预测收益后，策略又会集中到预测器高估的方案，使代理奖励上涨而真实收益不涨。\n\n方法：LM2LM用读取真实实验记录的冻结LLM预测收益，训练提案者；定期真实执行当前策略中预测高分的提案，把测量结果补入预测器上下文。提案者权重改变、反馈记录刷新，校准专门针对优化偏爱的区域。\n\n结果与结论：留出任务采用真实执行评价，摘要称优于带实验记录的强模型，数据生成成本低33%。可见案例中，静态记录方案不断强化有害改动，加入真实负结果后该改动比例下降；但主结果表与完整成本口径被截断。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，预测器离线准确不足以支撑在线优化，最需要复测的恰是策略追逐的高分点。证据支持定向纠偏，不证明全空间校准；这里学到改进其他模型的能力，尚非研究者自主改造自身训练算法。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22984","tldr":"背景与问题：很多经验演化方法依赖成功轨迹或验证反馈；若agent空库起步、反复失败又不知道真实评分，能否仅靠反思获得可迁移能力仍不清楚。\n\n方法：论文由控制器只让失败轨迹触发外部记忆、技能或harness更新，隐藏评分且不告知失败筛选。分别测源任务重试恢复与固定未见任务表现，再筛出人工确认正确的经验，并放宽成功轨迹、反馈或额外交互条件。\n\n结果与结论：多个框架与环境中，源任务可部分修复，未见任务却少有持续改善。仅保留正确经验后，五种配置中四种的最终留出成绩仍不高于无经验基线，表明诊断错误不是唯一瓶颈。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，应把经验正确性、同题可用性和跨题可迁移性分开验收。成功轨迹带来更强迁移，但成功与失败任务流分别采样，包含难度和内容差异；结果不能推出失败经验普遍无用。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-19","critique":"今天这批材料有实质推进，但主要是改善自改进的证据组织与归因，而非证明递归加速。VideoHarness-SRSI 表明，更丰富的反馈也可能扩大验证集过拟合，搜索需要限制内容暴露并控制机制干扰[1]；SEAR 用预算匹配重启和空技能库对照，区分经验继承与多试几次[2]。STRATA 的反向经验混淆实验，比笼统宣称结构化记忆有效更有解释力[3]。相较之下，ABot-ER 的轮次并非连续继承链，最终语料单次训练即可匹敌迭代结果[4]；APT 去掉反馈循环后部分指标持平，其递归必要性证据弱于自动化主张[5]。优先精读[1][2]，核查预算、选择协议与迁移归因。本次不是当天全部候选的总结，仍有19篇待分析论文；来源多为截断全文，缺失对照不能当作已验证结论。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.19424","arxiv:2610.18792","arxiv:2610.19386","arxiv:2610.18355","arxiv:2610.18097"],"backlog":19,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19799","tldr":"背景与问题：让团队反复修改技能和角色，不保证合作会改善；弱主席可能压制强成员，增加角色也可能只增加等待。论文把团队组成与决策权限作为独立变量，而非默认有效的背景。\n\n方法：固定个体演化机制，改变成员能力配比及信息共享、修改提案和决策规则；执行轨迹与同伴备忘进入下一轮，团队修改经验证集阻止明显退化。权重不变，部分技能和记忆更新由固定强模型完成。\n\n结果与结论：网页搜索中，合适配置较独自演化的强代理最高多25分；但另一模型家族未稳定重现该优势，角色扩张还伴随超时。领导集中并非普遍有效的组织规律。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，值得检验的是强成员能否获得有效经验并减少协调损耗，而非多代理是否天然更强。竞争条件直接安排按分数轮换主席，不能把全部权力转移解释成演化涌现。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19725","tldr":"背景与问题：冻结时序模型不会自动利用节假日等任务知识，也不会自行修正重复误差；人工设计流水线昂贵，而平均最好的方案未必适合每个预测窗口。\n\n方法：编码代理在早期历史窗口执行候选代码，用预测误差和日志指导下一次修订，再用较晚窗口筛选部署方案。部署时根据相似且结果已完整揭晓的历史窗口选择流水线；此时代码固定，仅选择依据更新。\n\n结果与结论：198项任务中，同候选数的非迭代搜索弱于直接推理，反馈修订则改善结果；TIME 的平均绝对缩放误差相对降低1.52%。更换编码代理和预测骨干仍有收益，但候选数匹配未控制全部成本。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键不是多生成方案，而是让实际误差否定看似合理的领域改动。历史误差能指导部署工程，却不能保证分布突变后的收益，更未证明编码代理自身越来越会优化。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19591","tldr":"背景与问题：长期代理若每次等待、协调和恢复都依赖模型推理与人工审批，计算扩张会受人的注意力限制；允许代理写新工具，又可能扩大其操作权限。\n\n方法：L3M 把状态和轨迹持久化，并允许代理将重复程序封装为新工具。程序类型声明所需权限，运行时限制其不超过既有授权；可恢复或权限已限定的操作减少审批，部分检查由 Lean 内核验证。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称仅用无需人工审查的工具，可达到带不安全 shell 配置约三分之二的通过率；可见片段缺少完整实验表，不能据此判断自扩展的独立收益。定理也依赖编译、提供者和操作系统等可信部分。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，贡献是让能力增长与权限增长脱钩，而非认证代理会正确自改进。回滚本地文件不能撤回已经发出的外部请求，安全主张必须逐项对应可恢复范围和可信假设。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19581","tldr":"背景与问题：别的代理学到的经验可能有用，却未必适配接收者的工具和执行历史；只共享语义相似条目，容易合并不兼容经验或重复注入无效指导。\n\n方法：系统分别维护本地与共享经验图，保留来源并避免有歧义的合并。新任务结合相关性、其他代理的使用结果与本地结果选择经验；任务评分随后更新使用统计，并将新轨迹提炼成下一轮经验。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称跨任务和异构框架迁移优于记忆基线，但主要结果表未包含在片段中。跨框架实验增加贡献者时，也同步增加源任务总暴露量，不能将收益全部归于代理多样性。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，迁移价值必须由接收者校准，不能直接照搬贡献者的成功率。不过给所有已注入经验记同一个任务结果，仍无法区分谁真正有用；重复任务的累计成功也不等于未见任务泛化。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19424","tldr":"背景与问题：有限验证集同时决定保留哪个 harness、下一步探索什么；视频和题目细节会诱导样本特化，早期噪声还可能让提案者过早放弃有效机制。\n\n方法：固定视觉语言模型，只向提案者开放汇总分数和不含验证内容的执行统计。先做受控预实验，再让机制在独立分支积累证据，最后测试组合及相互作用，减少一次联合修改导致的归因混淆。\n\n结果与结论：四个视频基准上，相对基础演化流程，平均留出得分相对提高6.2%，验证—测试差距缩小37.9%。内容暴露对照支持过拟合诊断，但片段不足以核对完整消融和总成本。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，更多反馈并非总是更好：能解释已见题目的信息，也能帮助记住验证集。真正应优化的是证据对未见任务的预测力；屏蔽内容仍不能自动消除反复查询汇总分数带来的选择偏差。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19422","tldr":"背景与问题：固定攻击集不会随防御者变强而暴露新弱点；工具代理还会从请求、工具说明和环境观察受到攻击，仅训练安全措辞不足以保证安全行动。\n\n方法：攻击者学习构造完整对抗任务，防御者学习在其中完成合法要求。固定模型分别判断轨迹安全性和效用，反馈更新双方；对同任务多次执行中结果差异较大的任务加权，避免只追求让防御者全败。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称安全鲁棒性改善且保持一般能力；片段提供四类安全基准与通用能力协议，但主要结果和加权消融被省略，无法核对幅度及独立贡献。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可学习攻击应产生可区分的行为后果，而非单纯最难。不过奖励变化也可能来自评判噪声；训练依赖模型判断，尚需独立检查安全评分、合法任务完成与过度拒绝之间的关系。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19386","tldr":"背景与问题：把具体操作、任务流程和一般原则混在相似度记忆池里，会随规模增长稀释检索；更危险的是，表面相似但方向相反的程序可能被直接执行。\n\n方法：冻结模型，将经验组织成技能、流程和抽象原则，并按任务结果写回：成功产生可复用程序，失败只添加避坑提示。检索同时关注操作与目标，召回相反经验时明确警告，定期压缩和删除冗余流程。\n\n结果与结论：四个互动基准、两个骨干上，摘要称平均表现及效率优于记忆基线；ScienceWorld 同系统加入对比关系后，得分从78.7升至96.7。完整消融表缺失，尚不能核对各机制贡献。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，经验被执行时，错误召回的代价高于一般检索问答。方向识别因此可能比继续扩库更关键；但当前对比关系依赖固定反义操作词表，开放语义下能否覆盖混淆尚未验证。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18868","tldr":"背景与问题：长程任务里，同组轨迹经常全部失败，终局二元奖励无法区分接近完成和毫无进展，导致组相对强化学习缺少梯度。\n\n方法：先构造已知正确的潜在世界，再从同一世界生成受损输入、目标和阶段检查，按工作区正确程度计进度。训练奖励额外保留最终进度，使未完成轨迹也能产生差异；它不是保证原最优策略不变的传统塑形。\n\n结果与结论：训练所得27B模型在指定长程计算与数学任务上，Pass@5 相对基座提高65%；还报告终端子集迁移。可见材料未给出主要训练消融，不能将全部收益归于稠密奖励。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，共同真值来源有助于避免分别生成任务和检查器造成的工件失配。但代理目标仍被改变，部分进度奖励可能影响策略取舍；这属于训练基础，而非已展示的递归自改进。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18845","tldr":"背景与问题：新遥感任务往往需要专家重选模型和训练配方，少标签设置尤其依赖工程经验；论文试图把设计工作交给能运行实验的编码代理。\n\n方法：人固定可用数据、模型与预算，用封闭验证器只返回分数；代理自行写训练代码，并将已训练模型的预测或检查点用于后继模型，按分数选择保留。最终模型另在隐藏测试集评估。\n\n结果与结论：材料称六个遥感基准均超过所列已有方法，部分任务只需少量训练标签；每次运行上限为四张GB200、12小时。实验验证器仍使用基准标签，不能据此证明所有遥感任务都有可靠验证方式。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，减少训练标注不等于消除监督需求，部分成本转移到了验证标签与任务接口。递归发生在目标模型的自训练谱系，尚无证据表明编码代理或产生改进的规则也持续变强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18842","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人能自主执行，不代表能自主改进；即使技能越积越多，也可能只是固定更新流程不断运行，而非学习过程本身变得更有效。\n\n方法：论文将执行系统与改进程序分开，用L0—L5区分能力更新、元级更新及跨任务收益。最高等级要求从相同起点和经验出发，在匹配预算下由独立评估比较新旧改进程序；物理反馈可来自真实交互或物理仿真。\n\n结果与结论：这是一项框架与综述工作，不提供达到最高等级的新系统。其判断是所审阅文献尚未满足该定义的物理 RSI 证据要求，不能扩展成对全部机器人研究的否定。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，递归主张最关键的对照是“更新后的改进程序能否产生更好的后续改进”，而非机器人最终更强。独立评测还须防止标准随轮次改变，否则所谓递归增益可能只是目标漂移。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18813","tldr":"背景与问题：提示、记忆、工具实现和运行时控制都可能被称为 harness 演化，但修改边界及风险不同；仅有修订过程，也不代表产生了可保留的性能收益。\n\n方法：论文按被继承的状态分类，分开描述修改对象、候选生成和准入。模型固定，执行反馈驱动候选，获准版本跨运行加载；摘要再提出依赖明确假设的泛化、回归保留及独立验证准入界。\n\n结果与结论：可见正文主要是定义、分类和引用案例，并非新的匹配实验。所给文本虽未标截断，却未包含摘要承诺的理论正文，因此不能核验定理条件；插件成本案例还明确存在两套统计不一致。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，最有用的区分是“发生演化”和“经比较证明改进”。修改解释态、可执行代码与更新算法应分别记账；独立验证数据的理论要求，也不能直接套到反复复用同一验证集的搜索。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18792","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人成功率随时间上升，可能只是多次重试、熟悉初始状态或更大预算，不能直接证明保留了可迁移能力。\n\n方法：SEAR 将写控制程序、在线行动和自主微调纳入同一框架；用空技能库、同总预算短重启和隐藏初始状态评分分离继承与重采样。跨任务只保留代码技能和文字记忆，自动研究产生的权重不延续。\n\n结果与结论：RoboLab 中，一个模型无库成功率46.9%，继承自身库反而退化，改用其他模型的库则达60.6%。经验质量而非有无经验决定收益；硬件上练习成功也高于新场景表现。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，是否值得持续修改，取决于首次成功时间能否落在短尝试预算内，不能只按任务难度决定。封闭评分仍发现资产文件泄露等漏洞，且模型与工具绑定，跨模型排名并非纯模型能力比较。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18484","tldr":"背景与问题：终端代理执行错误后会改变文件和环境，重新从干净状态训练未必教会它恢复；人工注入的错误又可能偏离当前策略真正会犯的错。\n\n方法：先保存学生失败后的环境快照，让强教师生成经验证的恢复示范。在线训练再从当前策略产生的失败状态分叉多次续做，用最终任务验证结果比较恢复行为；近期失败进入队列，随策略变化刷新训练起点。\n\n结果与结论：Terminal-Bench 2.0 的Pass@1 达34.8%，较基座多14.6个百分点；材料称各错误类别恢复率优于普通GRPO。该总增益同时包含教师示范与强化学习，片段缺少完整消融和成本对照。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，失败不只是负样本，也是可复用的训练初始状态。其价值取决于能否准确恢复环境；这训练的是纠错策略，不代表更新算法自身进化，也不能由恢复旧任务直接推断未见故障泛化。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18355","tldr":"背景与问题：具身感知、规划与交互定位进步速度不同，固定数据比例会偏离当前短板；语义和动作空间输出共享参数，还可能互相干扰。\n\n方法：评估结果触发能力诊断，修订监督内容与混合比例，经固定规则筛选后训练并再评估；任务条件残差分担异构输出需求。改变的是语料和权重，数据准入规则及学习算法本身不随轮次学习。\n\n结果与结论：材料称十二个基准的各能力汇总领先；更关键的是，最终语料单次训练能匹敌六轮模型，累计后训练量仅五分之一。历史包含重启、跳过检查点和污染修复，不是一条连续增强链。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，证据更支持发现了可复用的数据配方，而非每轮继承权重不可替代。应分开计算数据清洗、预算扩大和反馈适配的贡献；交互定位得分也不能等同真实机器人运动控制能力。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18097","tldr":"背景与问题：不同图像模型的计数、文字和空间关系短板不同，统一人工训练集未必适配；模型变强后，训练优先级也应重新判断。\n\n方法：预先生成固定的提示—评分准则诊断集，用同一视觉语言评估器诊断与给训练奖励。数据代理据当前失败生成下一轮提示，主要针对弱项，也保留其他能力；强化学习更新图像模型后再次诊断。\n\n结果与结论：Lens 上，保留反馈循环的GenEval 为0.859，去掉后为0.844，但OneIG均值持平；只练难项在后者甚至更高。实验支持部分收益，不能据此宣称反馈循环或混合采样在所有指标上必要。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，自适应训练价值应由跨指标权衡检验，而非自动化程度代替证据。诊断与奖励共用评估器，可能共同放大其盲点；这里更新的是生成器和课程，不是诊断者或教学策略本身。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-18","critique":"今天这批材料有实质推进，但不是“递归加速”已获证明。变化集中在改进信号的校准：RRI 用攻击样本修补奖励，却仍接纳未彻底修好的任务[1]；AdaRSI 以同状态重试区分调用问题与动作缺口，比笼统联合训练更有解释力[2]。MetaExp 将经验学习能力与携带已有经验分开测量[3]，技能漂移审计则揭示原配高分可能掩盖部署脆弱性[4]。Athanor 展示真实算力上的自主后训练，但没有让研究者自身递归变强[5]。单纯交替训练再冠以 RSI，更像增量组织而非新范式。最值得精读 AdaRSI 的干预对照和技能漂移审计的理论前提。本次仅覆盖关键词候选与截断全文，部分比较仍属摘要级判断；尚有26篇待分析论文，并非当天全部候选的总结，也未验证代码或复现实验。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.21040","arxiv:2610.20474","arxiv:2610.21492","arxiv:2610.20845","arxiv:2610.21055"],"backlog":26,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22362","tldr":"背景与问题：物理上有效的仿真场景未必值得训练；只按成功率生成难题，分不清当前短板究竟可学，还是继续投入也无收益。\n\n方法：CoDA 用轨迹诊断提出困难因素，再比较定向扰动与其他因素扰动，验证诊断后存入共享记忆。同一困难生成针对性场景和密集势函数；机器可检查的任务成功条件保持独立，训练后的实际进步指导下一轮生成。\n\n结果与结论：四类操作任务中，同接受环境预算下，分布外成功率为27.6%，高于成功率引导生成的18.1%。这支持超越标量难度的反馈有价值，但不代表总计算成本相等，实机迁移仍未建立。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键不只是找失败，而是验证失败原因并测量能否学会。生成引擎靠记忆适配、策略靠梯度学习，两者共演化不等于生成算法自身变强；势函数保留最优策略也依赖标准塑形假设。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22344","tldr":"背景与问题：机器学习实验返回结果前，agent 已作出多轮分析和代码修改；等整段研究结束才训练，既浪费中间反馈，也难把结果归给相关决策。\n\n方法：MLExpert 先从按结果筛选的轨迹学习，再把相邻实验结果之间的决策视为一个窗口，用实验结果及局部进步共同奖励窗口内行为。实验完成即可异步更新，不必等待整个任务结束，并修正采样策略与训练策略的差异。\n\n结果与结论：MLE-Bench Lite 平均获牌率从基座的37.9%升至72.7%；算法优化迁移中也有收益，但部分任务持平或退化。窗口共享奖励并未实现窗口内部的精细归因。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，贡献是让研究者从真实实验节奏学习，而非证明研究流程递归自造。脚手架优化实验中，进一步强化学习同时增加调用量，准确率收益不能全解释为调用效率提高。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22192","tldr":"背景与问题：终端任务的冗长日志会让按 token 衰减的信用偏离实际决策距离；监督重写改变策略后，旧价值估计也可能失准。通过局部检查更不等于完成整个任务。\n\n方法：Terminal-RSI 交替学习经验证的重写轨迹与强化学习精炼，保留价值网络但在新阶段重新校准；信用按交互轮衰减，并限制失败轨迹的部分奖励，避免局部进展压过严格完成。\n\n结果与结论：长程终端测试的严格完成从0/46增至5/46，说明收益不只体现在过程奖励；但绝对完成率仍低。阶段还同时改变数据、奖励和学习率，现有曲线不能单独归因于价值继承。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，值得借鉴的是把检查覆盖、塑形奖励和终局成功分开报告。这里递归的是训练数据与策略继承，并无证据说明信用分配算法自身学会了如何改进；被丢弃分支也反对单调变强的叙事。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21791","tldr":"背景与问题：改权重、改 harness 或修任务产物各自有效，却未必对应当前瓶颈；固定的干预选择方式也不会自动从过去的改进尝试中受益。\n\n方法：RSIFlow 根据轨迹和环境反馈选择一个组件更新，固定其余组件比较候选。之后把成功、失败及回归提炼为带适用条件的技能和跨组件原则，修改元 agent 的接口与指令，让下一轮诊断和选择使用这些经验。\n\n结果与结论：六个基准、两种骨干的12种设置中，11种领先所比较基线。材料称消融支持自适应编排和元 harness 演化，但消融表被截断，无法核对独立贡献及完整成本。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，比最终任务分数更关键的是元经验能否在相同预算下改善下一次干预。方法确实改变了改进者的外部状态，但五轮结果尚不能证明持续加速；还应区分任务产物修补与可迁移能力增长。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21646","tldr":"背景与问题：自修改系统希望自动门控既不放过坏更新，也不阻止好更新；但门控必须停机，真正的行为改进却可能依赖无界运行，二者要求并不相容。\n\n方法：论文把 agent 与候选更新表示为程序，分别研究判断单次更新和从提案中寻找改进。利用自指构造证明普遍可靠且完备的停机程序不存在，再限制评估时域与提案数量，恢复相对于有界分数的可判定保证。\n\n结果与结论：可见证明支持认证器的不可能性；材料还给出搜索及随机门控的对应结果，并构造代理每轮上升、真实目标反而下降的更新链。这不是现实系统失败率的测量。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，工程意义是声明保证究竟针对哪个有限目标，而非宣布自改进不可行。经典不可判定性不能替代统计审计；有限测试恢复的正确性也不能自动覆盖未测输入和长期目标。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21492","tldr":"背景与问题：会解任务不等于会从任务中积累经验；独立任务训练难以告诉模型哪些知识应跨回合保留，部署时加记忆甚至可能使表现下降。\n\n方法：MetaExp 构造共享工具或潜在流程、但具体答案不能直接复用的任务族，用连续求解和反馈后修订技能的轨迹训练模型。测试时参数冻结、经验库清空，从新分布逐步积累技能，再在不参与更新的固定目标集测量收益。训练反馈以执行检查为主，模型复核失败项。\n\n结果与结论：SpreadsheetBench 中经验积累带来8.5分增长，匹配基座在同协议下反降2.2分；排除相关训练领域后仍有收益，支持经验学习不只是携带目标领域知识。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，较有力的变化是把初始解题水平与经验带来的增量拆开。训练过滤仍主要确认当前任务成功，尚未直接验证每次技能修改能改善后续任务；经验积累也不等于更新算法持续递归增强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21055","tldr":"背景与问题：自主后训练不仅要提出配方，还要完成耗时且易失败的 GPU 实验，同时防止开发集搜索和数据污染冒充通用能力增长。\n\n方法：Athanor 将作业、数据去污染和固定评估做成服务，把研究记录与模型谱系持久化；四个固定前沿 agent 自选数据、算法和模型组合，训练另一个基础模型。最终隐藏套件不向研究者开放，也不允许调用外部教师模型。\n\n结果与结论：104小时活动后，隐藏套件均分为48.2，官方指令版为47.9，支持接近其平均水平，而非可靠超越。论文区分活动期间协议与事后统一重测，结果不能混为同一条曲线。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，这说明低摩擦执行设施能支撑已知方法的自主重组，但尚无基础设施消融证明它是决定性瓶颈。单次活动也未显示研究者自身变强，运营者仍承担节点恢复等基础设施职责。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21040","tldr":"背景与问题：开放式专家任务缺少答案键，模型自写评分准则容易奖励关键词覆盖而非实质内容；求解器会把这些漏洞放大成训练方向。\n\n方法：RRI 从检索资料生成任务与准则，先写故意钻评分漏洞的答案，再与同一模型不看准则写出的诚实答案比较，由模型 judge 评分并指导修补。漏洞还改写未来任务和准则的生成指令，求解器用修补后的奖励学习。\n\n结果与结论：9B 设置相对只生成任务的基线提高10.9分，但相对已共演化任务与奖励的基线，攻击修补额外贡献为2.7分。修补次数受限，仍能被攻破的任务也进入训练，不能称为可靠奖励认证。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，主张应落在减少已发现的可利用性，而非无参考地建立真值。诚实答案和 judge 仍可能共享错误；专业基准收益不代表临床有效性，后续应独立测量修补后的排序可靠性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20845","tldr":"背景与问题：技能—策略共演化通常只测最终配对；部署后技能库比权重更新更频繁，原配高分可能掩盖对特定措辞和内容的依赖。\n\n方法：论文固定任务和策略，在固定检索下分别改写技能措辞、删除必要步骤或注入误导，并另测增删技能与撤库。沿训练检查点追踪敏感性，再以任务成功、语义一致性和抗损坏性审计交付系统；语义保持改写另经模型及部分人工检查。\n\n结果与结论：四种方法、六种设置中，所测最差成功率比原配低5—13个百分点；五种设置的内容漂移敏感性随训练增加。理论依赖理想选择与候选覆盖，不意味着任意共演化必然退化。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，共演化应优化技能变化下的可靠使用，而非只优化原配峰值。意义保持改写也会造成损失，说明问题不全是技能变坏；但所测最差值不是所有部署变化的全局最坏保证。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20809","tldr":"背景与问题：固定小型领域语言只能回答已有算子可组合的问题；让 agent 自写新算子又会引入计算错误，运行成功或模型自信不足以决定保留。\n\n方法：冻结模型先用独立表达式的一致结果扩展问题覆盖，再针对反复出现的能力缺口生成算子。新算子需通过第二实现的差分测试和基于可信原语的守恒关系检查，获准后进入后续组合；解释器与准入规则保持固定。\n\n结果与结论：独立参考条件下，门控拒绝全部138个错误变体；人为让两实现共享错误时仍会漏放。团队盲评中仅89%的问题表达式忠实于问题，说明算得一致不代表理解正确。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可信扩展需要同时检查执行关系与问题语义。无 oracle 指在线准入不看答案键，不代表实验没有外部金标准；有限输入上的一致性也不是所有输入正确的形式证明。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20474","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人子步骤失败可能是调用姿态或指令不当，也可能是执行器不会所需动作；直接微调所有失败既浪费数据，也可能损坏原本可用的能力。\n\n方法：AdaRSI 先修 harness，再从保存状态重试不同调用方式，只为仍不可靠的子步骤自采示范并微调。示范来自成功 rollout 或读取特权状态的脚本；训练起点取自实际到达状态，新策略经比较后仅在受益位置推荐使用。\n\n结果与结论：未见组合任务中，相对 harness-only 的9.9%，完整系统达到13.8%。同预算下只挑最低成功率步骤训练没有额外收益，支持训练状态与归因的重要性；结果限于仿真及单一执行器。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，harness 不只是廉价替代品，还决定训练数据来自哪些状态。保存状态重试提供受控干预，但有限重试找不到有效调用，并不严格证明动作不可实现；跨任务经验也尚未独立证明调度能力递归增强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20431","tldr":"背景与问题：科学实验失败不说明假设错还是实现错；按整体得分淘汰程序，还会丢掉对其他研究分支有用的局部组件。\n\n方法：SwarmRSI 将假设、程序、执行证据与未解决需求写入共享图，用其他分支反馈决定改研究方向还是修实现。保留假设可迁到另一程序上验证，互补组件也可重组；每次执行及评分结果进入下一轮继承状态。\n\n结果与结论：NatureBench 上删除程序修订后，匹配既有最佳结果的比例从44.4%降至31.1%，支持实现修复有贡献。跨任务经验结果仍受源任务数量混淆，生物学家复用程序不等于复现整套方法。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，负结果应保留可复用结构，而非只有一个失败标签。但重组后得分上升不能证明原科学假设成立；固定搜索规则下状态越来越丰富，也不能直接当作改进算法自身递归变强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20312","tldr":"背景与问题：空间任务只能看到部分环境，答错可能来自看错、探索不够或规划失误；不区分原因就总结经验，容易固化错误策略。\n\n方法：HiMeco 在执行结束后利用轨迹、答案真值与特权仿真信息诊断三类问题，比较多次尝试并提炼适用策略。程序片段抽象成参数化技能后，经证据合同和实际调用验证再保留；模型冻结，记忆只在轮间更新。\n\n结果与结论：材料称其在 ESI-Bench 领先，但结果表和关键消融未提供。EmbSpatial-Bench 的3.94个百分点收益发生在没有演化时，不能据此证明记忆更新有效。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，应优先核查去掉分类诊断后是否仍能取得同样收益，而非接受脑机制类比。诊断分数不是校准概率，离线特权信息也是重要监督来源；推广到无真值或真实机器人反馈时，归因可靠性尚未确定。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20294","tldr":"背景与问题：改变策略状态或写入记忆，只能说明发生适配；要证明递归改进，还须显示当前适配规则参与产生更好的继任规则，并由后者继续承担同一角色。\n\n方法：MMLA-RSI 分别规定数值更新器和记忆管理器的继任流程：前者训练提出后继的策略，后者选择该过程能读取的记录。候选锁定后由独立评估器准入，固定解释器和可信提交器限制可改范围，并记录更新先于新尝试的证据。\n\n结果与结论：现有组件研究有正有负：程序选择受益，连续集成回放保留状态却增加损失，SQL 未证实额外在线收益。论文明确表示，有益递归链及发现效率尚未评估。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，其价值在于把功能参与、任务收益和搜索效率分开。固定随机带下输出改变也不必然证明动作分布改变；这些证据要求比组件增益更接近真正递归主张，但目前仍是待验证方案。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20665","tldr":"背景与问题：游戏在推理期间继续运行时，正确动作也可能来得太晚；暂停评测会掩盖这一点，在线调用更强教师反而可能破坏控制。\n\n方法：TORSI 让快学生独立行动，慢教师在回合之间读取失败，从保存状态练习替代动作，再让学生按真实延迟检验指导。只有在独立验证任务上改善的指导才替换旧版，下一轮处理更新后的残余失败，双方权重和行动接口不变。\n\n结果与结论：两轮后按游戏分别选出的指导，使测试平均进度分从13.51升至24.19；这不是统一采用第二轮候选的结果。消融显示仅写指导或缺少任一侧练习均不足以取得完整收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，慢推理适合用于控制间隙的学习，而非每次动作决策。证据限于文本状态接口、六类游戏和两轮，进度分不等于通关率；这里变强的是指导，不是教师或教学算法自身。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-17","critique":"本次巡检没有待分析的新材料，因此没有新增已核实的研究进展。此前的判断保留在论文库中。","source_ids":[],"backlog":0,"papers":[]},{"date":"2026-10-16","critique":"今天这批材料有实质变化，但主要是改进机制与证据标准的细化，尚不足以确立新范式。LoopOPD 把额外循环计算变成中间循环的密集监督，并用共享参数让更新后的终端循环继续提供反馈；关键证据是数学推理对照，但结论仍限于 Ouro-Thinking 及作者实验。[1] 理论论文严格区分搜索效率、支持接口与验证边界的变化，说明分数上涨不等于正确任务范围扩大；它提供的是有条件的形式化框架，不是现实系统验证。[2] RSI-Forge 扩大研究环境供给并测试固定权重下的工件迭代，但专家对捷径抵抗、论文忠实度和任务饱和度更谨慎；这支持其作为评测基础设施，而非改进器递归变强的证据。[3] 今日最值得精读的是赢家诅咒研究：预注册对照量化了复用小型评测集造成的收益高估，也发现所测接受规则未稳定胜过贪心策略；这直接影响如何解释 RSI 实验结果。[4] 当前判断基于四篇所给全文片段，没有独立复现，不能外推为领域整体结论。本次 arXiv 检索未能连接，因此这是已有论文库的巡检点评，并非当天全部候选论文的总结；目前没有待分析论文积压。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.10623","arxiv:2610.10611","arxiv:2610.09426","arxiv:2610.09239"],"backlog":0,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10623","tldr":"背景与问题：LoopLM 用共享参数反复计算，却难以把稀疏的终局奖励直接分配给中间循环；外部教师可能不可得，带特权信息的自蒸馏又会造成师生上下文不匹配。\n\n方法：LoopOPD 让中间循环在自身生成的轨迹上匹配终端循环的 token 分布，将额外循环计算变成密集监督。D-LoopOPD 每步改用当前终端循环作教师；学生更新共享参数后，终端教师也随之改变，并在后续步骤继续提供监督。\n\n结果与结论：在 Ouro-Thinking 上，作者报告 LoopOPD 改善数学推理，动态教师进一步优于冻结教师；全文片段给出 Ouro-2.6B-Thinking 的 AIME 2024 Avg@16 从 62.08 升至 71.67，并称跨循环深度均有改善。跨任务收益限于数学训练后的指定推理和代码基准。\n\nInsights：这里值得检验的不是“自蒸馏是否有效”，而是共享参数是否能把中间循环的学习稳定传回终端策略；论文的局部改进定理也要求梯度对齐等条件。因此，机制成立依赖特定更新几何，不能推成共享参数更新普遍有益。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10611","tldr":"背景与问题：成功率上升可能来自搜索更久、获得更多支持或改变检查器；单看分数无法判断系统只是更容易找到已有解，还是扩展了可接受的正确任务范围。\n\n方法：论文将系统阶段表示为有界交互、支持接口、验证协议与终端检查器，分别定义默认支持下的可达范围和接口许可支持下的范围。它证明独立多数放大保留这两种范围，而随机带上任一次通过可能错误接纳输出；另为自修改和候选选择规定错误预算。\n\n结果与结论：在共同可靠解释器和固定验证协议等条件下，有界递归自修改仍处于同一验证类；有限 XOR 合成例区分搜索成功率提高与接受语言改变。这是条件性理论结果，不是现实 agent 的经验检验。\n\nInsights：该框架把“性能更好”拆成搜索、接口和验证语义三种可分别核查的变化；但其保证依赖明确的可靠性合同，不能直接认证只有经验准确率的学习型评估器。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.09426","tldr":"背景与问题：研究型 RSI 需要有挑战的任务、可靠评估和可比较基线，但逐领域依赖专家设计限制了规模；自动生成又可能带来捷径、失真或不可解任务。\n\n方法：RSI-Forge 将任务构建、论文方法复现和环境审查分配给不同角色，分别产出可执行任务与评估器、独立基线，并检查说明和评分是否对应。随后固定模型权重，让 agent 继承先前代码和笔记，检验环境是否支持连续修改。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告构建 210 个、覆盖 18 个领域的环境，其中 90 个经领域专家审阅；在 120 个环境的三次尝试中，至少一个模型在首轮后有所改善的环境占 84%，68 个环境超过复现方法基线。专家对捷径抵抗、来源忠实度及单一想法能否耗尽任务更为审慎。\n\nInsights：环境生成的价值不只是扩充题量，还在于提供可复现基线和分工审查；但专家指出的质量缺口与已观察到的评估材料访问风险，说明环境数量及分数不能单独证明测量可靠。固定权重结果也不代表改进器本身变强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.09239","tldr":"背景与问题：自改进系统常在小评测集上提出多个修改，再保留分数最高者；被选分数会受选择噪声抬高，重复使用同一集合还会改变后续比较的基线。\n\n方法：论文把保留候选视为相关误差下的噪声选择，并用独立留出集估计真实收益。作者比较多种接受门槛与确认程序，再以预注册实验检验这些规则是否改善完整运行，而非只看单次决策。\n\n结果与结论：预注册研究中，16 项选择集上的贪心循环最终选择分数比留出准确率高 13–20 个百分点；256 项时差距缩至 1–5 点。测试的接受规则在完整运行中没有稳定胜过贪心策略；另用未参与选择的 64 项评分可校正平均偏差，但单次估计仍约有 6 点误差。证据覆盖特定指令改写任务及 GEPA、MIPROv2 验证分数检查。\n\nInsights：结果把研究重点从设计更复杂的接受规则，转向独立报告留出收益和不确定性；依据是接受规则未稳定改善整轮结果，而扩大选择集可缩小高估。它不说明自改进普遍无效，只说明复用评测集上的分数不足以独立证明收益。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-15","critique":"今天这批材料有实质变化，但主要是把 RSI 闭环做得更可选择、更可控，尚未证明自我改进能力本身递归增强。SGUID 按蒸馏期间实际产生的有效信号筛技能，而非把检索相关性当训练价值；研究世界模型则显示，历史实验记录可帮助排序未执行干预，跨环境复用尤其值得关注 [1][2]。ReSI 把红队发现、训练配方搜索和能力保留门控接成多轮安全更新，但论文说明搜索程序本身固定，支持的是目标模型迭代，不是改进机制递归进化 [3]。反向证据也直接：DataSense-Bench 中数据选择与排序仍不稳定，说明会分析数据不等于能预测训练收益 [4]；EvoAlloc 的预算收益来自特定程序搜索基准，不能外推为普遍优势 [5]。本次只处理已有论文库，仍有待分析论文；虽有部分全文片段，判断仍主要受摘要及截断材料限制，作者实验均非独立复现。最值得精读 [2]：其大规模实验记录和跨环境选择设置，为检验经验能否减少昂贵试错提供了具体证据，也值得审视环境覆盖、预测不确定性与多轮稳健性。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.12367","arxiv:2610.12235","arxiv:2610.12233","arxiv:2610.12190","arxiv:2610.12086"],"backlog":4,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12367","tldr":"背景与问题：推理时检索到的技能未必能教会当前模型；论文报告，不到四分之一的检索技能提供有用蒸馏信号，因此语义相关性不足以代表训练价值。\n\n方法：SGUID 观察技能条件教师在学生 rollout 上产生的、与验证器一致的学习信号，只保留训练早晚阶段都持续有效的技能。精简技能蒸馏更新模型后，再从新模型 rollout 整理候选技能并筛选下一轮，形成模型与技能库的反馈闭环。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告，仅蒸馏 6 个技能在四个模型中的多数模型上可匹敌或超过全库；第二轮选出 3 个新技能，Qwen3-8B 的均值由 64.3% 升至 66.3%。结果限于数学推理基准，是作者实验而非独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示蒸馏瓶颈可能在监督信号筛选而非技能数量；依据是少量持续有效技能的结果，以及无筛选更新出现退化的报告。该结论仍受任务与验证器范围约束，不能外推到开放任务或缺少可靠验证器的场景。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12235","tldr":"背景与问题：研究 agent 能提出实验，却难以在预算有限时判断哪些干预值得执行；仅凭先验推理预测效果，也容易忽略模型、配方和环境差异。\n\n方法：研究世界模型接收环境、候选干预和既往实验记录，预测潜在收益并排序。被选实验执行后形成新记录，可供后续预测复用；因此闭环改善的是实验选择质量，不是本文已证明的模型参数递归训练。\n\n结果与结论：作者汇集九个环境的 2,653 条实验记录。同环境经验提高未见干预的排序相关性，跨环境经验也改善选择；在固定多轮选择预算下，作者报告经验增强的预测器取得更高最佳收益。这些是作者实验，覆盖范围受现有环境与记录限制。\n\nInsights：这提示稀缺实验预算下，积累可迁移的结果记录可能比单纯更换更强模型或增加推理量更关键；依据是跨环境预测和消融结果。边界在于迁移仍依赖目标环境描述与来源覆盖，预测排序也不能替代实际执行和不确定性估计。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12233","tldr":"背景与问题：模型持续更新会使旧安全对齐失效，新红队方法又不断揭示未见漏洞；只针对已知攻击训练，可能修补漏洞却损害能力或无法泛化。\n\n方法：ReSI 每轮攻击当前模型、生成训练配方候选并通过试验筛选，再以安全增益和能力保留门控晋级模型。新模型进入下一轮红队评估，反馈重新驱动配方搜索，形成有明确保留条件的安全更新循环。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告四种稠密及 MoE 模型在多项安全评估上改善，并称 X-Teaming 平均攻击成功率由 86.01% 降至 31.45%，同时大体保留一般能力。结果来自作者实验，外推范围受攻击集、训练预算和轮数限制。\n\nInsights：这提示保留门控不应只看目标安全指标，也需限制能力回归；未见攻击评估则是检验安全泛化的依据。由于搜索流程本身固定，现有证据支持迭代安全改进，不足以证明改进机制也在递归变强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12190","tldr":"背景与问题：模型能看数据、写分析代码，不代表能判断哪些样本真正有利于训练；数据表面质量、损失或轨迹成功与特定模型的学习收益并非一一对应。\n\n方法：DataSense-Bench 让 agent 在不能训练模型或查看测试题的条件下选择并排序数据子集，随后用固定流程训练同一基座并测量结果，将事前判断与事后训练结果对照。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告相对随机选择的收益有限，代理对所选数据组的排序也不可靠，且跨终端任务与工具使用任务不稳定。材料支持这是一项能力审计，不支持模型已具备可靠数据科学家能力；范围限于两类轨迹任务和小模型微调。\n\nInsights：这提示 RSI 的数据选择环节可能是瓶颈，必须用训练后的真实结果验证预测，而不能把合理分析过程当作有效信号。依据是排序及跨任务稳定性不足；这不证明所有数据选择方法都无效，也不涵盖在线训练并持续校准选择器的闭环。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12086","tldr":"背景与问题：程序演化的完整评估成本高，固定分配规则可能把预算花在低价值候选上；更深一层的问题是，被跳过的候选没有结果，分配器会因自己的选择而看不到错误。\n\n方法：EvoAlloc 把评估资源分配策略本身设为可修订对象，从搜索与分配结果提炼经验；偶尔完整评估被拒候选，补上反事实反馈，再据共同验证结果决定是否采用新策略。\n\n结果与结论：作者在编码及 agent-harness 优化基准报告，达到基线表现所需完整评估减少 59–82%，同预算下最终表现高 8.7–12.0%。消融支持策略演化和反事实探索的贡献，但结论限于所测搜索任务与预算。\n\nInsights：这提示自适应资源管理的关键不只是更聪明地筛选，还要主动测量被筛选机制隐藏的失败；依据是反事实反馈设计及消融。其收益是否转移到昂贵实验、非程序搜索或不同预算制度，现有材料尚不能确认。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11959","tldr":"背景与问题：复杂 agent 任务的强化学习受限于探索环境、长程奖励信号及大规模 rollout 基础设施；扩大算力也带来稳定训练与奖励投机风险。\n\n方法：报告扩大 RL 批量与吞吐、丰富环境和 harness，并增加 grader 计算以提供组间细粒度反馈；同时采用稳定性措施应对大规模训练中的路由变化与奖励投机。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称模型在多个领域基准随训练推进而持续提升，并计划开放训练动态、环境和框架。摘要没有提供足以判断相对基线、总成本或关键消融的完整证据，也未展示改进方法自身递归更新。\n\nInsights：这提示规模化 RL 的有效性取决于环境与奖励信号质量，不是算力单变量问题；依据是论文对 grader、环境多样性及稳定性的共同强调。就 RSI 范围而言，这更像推动模型能力的训练报告，而非已证实的自我改进闭环。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12536","tldr":"背景与问题：可执行控制策略可以用回报自动评估，但搜索集上保留高分程序并不保证新候选变好，也不保证收益迁移到新 episode。\n\n方法：EliteTable 将高分解保存在固定容量表中，用它们指导新程序生成、编辑和重组；候选经执行评估后再与精英竞争，留出回报不参与搜索决策。\n\n结果与结论：作者在六个 Gymnasium 任务上报告候选分数中位数均随代数上升，但留出端点仅四个任务的十次搜索全部改善；Acrobot 有六次下降且配对中位变化为负。作者承认仍需基线比较与消融，不能据此判断相对性能。\n\nInsights：这提示 RSI 证据应区分精英保留带来的搜索分数单调性与真正可迁移的能力变化；依据是 Acrobot 的搜索与留出结果分化。现有材料仅支持特定程序搜索的初步观察，不足以主张算法优势。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11803","tldr":"背景与问题：当数据生成分布和符号辅助信号也随学习过程变化时，训练目标不再固定；传统稳定性分析可能无法覆盖这种共同演变。\n\n方法：PRAXIS 将生成器、学习器及符号档案建模为耦合动态过程，并以受约束更新控制分布漂移、按效用调整档案权重，再分析学习器在变化目标下的稳定性。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称给出目标漂移界、档案相对固定比较对象的抑制性质及随机梯度平均驻点保证，并报告三类任务实验与理论机制相符。具体实验幅度和理论条件在实际任务中的适用范围，材料不足以确认。\n\nInsights：这提示 RSI 理论不能只分析模型参数更新，还应把数据分布和外部符号信号的漂移纳入稳定性条件；这是由其联合建模提出的启发，不等于已证明这些保证覆盖大语言模型或开放式自我改进。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11655","tldr":"背景与问题：长程 agent 失败可能来自工具阻塞、循环或步数耗尽，也可能是已交付方案本身质量差；笼统加权或改 harness，难以知道该动运行时还是模型权重。\n\n方法：论文按失败轨迹的首个触发信号区分过程故障与内容故障，先演化 harness 修复执行问题，再用演化轨迹训练 LoRA，测试哪些收益能脱离运行时内化到权重。作者还用 shuffled-answer placebo 和 fresh anchor 控制轨迹价值与选择噪声。\n\n结果与结论：作者在 DeepPlanning 报告 harness 与 adapter 对不同模型规模存在互补或替代关系，并在 WebArena-Lite 观察到迁移；该场景的增益来自运行时所见信息，adapter 未再增加收益。材料也揭示评分噪声、转换器偏差与任务范围等局限；非独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示选择干预对象前应先分解失败原因，并进一步判断 harness 改变的是模型写出的内容还是可见信息；依据是两任务的 adapter 结果差异。该诊断规则来自有限基准，失败标签阈值与评估器也会影响归因，尚非普遍定律。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11345","tldr":"背景与问题：静态任务集会随学习者变强而变得过易，远超能力的题目又难以提供有效反馈；只定期刷新数据，仍可能让合成器与推理器各自优化、反馈脱节。\n\n方法：SynCo 让合成器根据推理器能力与任务覆盖生成可验证问题，推理器多次作答；正确性更新推理器，任务质量、可靠性及由实际作答结果估计的可教性更新合成器，之后两者共同影响下一轮课程。\n\n结果与结论：作者在八个数学基准报告优于多类合成数据基线，且多数收益来自先前未解问题；全文片段还报告，相较冻结合成器，联合训练仅略增有效训练任务比例，计算量相近。结果来自作者实验，任务范围主要为数学推理。\n\nInsights：这提示任务价值不应仅靠预估难度，而应由当前学习者的实际交互结果校准；依据是任务可教性信号及合成器对照。反馈依赖题目检查器和学习者自身行为，能否扩展到开放任务与更长训练仍未证实。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10498","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人微调需要昂贵交互数据；仅反复试错修改代码和技能，可能重复探索相近方向，也难判断两者组合是否真的互补。\n\n方法：EmbodiedRSI 将竞争性代码、技能假设与证据存入图中，按预期信息价值选择能区分假设的物理试验；结果驱动代码—技能联合更新，慢速记忆模块再根据后续改进价值学习保留哪些经验。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告 RoboCasa365、LIBERO-Pro 上的成功率高于所列基线，并称从模拟到真实机器人零样本迁移。摘要给出若干比例，但未提供完整任务覆盖、预算和实地重复次数；这是作者报告而非独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示昂贵交互应被视为辨别竞争解释的实验，而非单纯收集更多轨迹；依据是信息价值选试验的机制。结论边界在于假设质量、模拟到现实差异及试验预算，尚不能推断长期自主部署会持续改进。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10426","tldr":"背景与问题：模型和 harness 交替变化时，轨迹的训练价值取决于其生成时的运行时；把不同 harness 的成功轨迹混在回放池里，可能让模型学到部署时不适用的操作程序。\n\n方法：CoTrace 将失败证据用于 harness 合成，只把已验证且与当前采用 harness 匹配的轨迹用于 SFT，或在同一运行时下生成新 RL 交互；分别固定另一组件评估候选，以避免把增益归错对象。\n\n结果与结论：作者在 Tmax promotion split 报告 Qwen3.5-9B 从 78 个解题任务升至 88（SFT）或 90（在线 RL）；紧凑匹配语料在较低计算下比跨 sibling harness 混合的大语料更稳定。外部基准结果也显示运行时兼容性影响迁移。均为作者实验。\n\nInsights：这提示数据规模不是联合演化的唯一瓶颈，轨迹来源与部署 runtime 的一致性可能决定数据是否可学；依据是匹配与混合语料的对照。结论受任务集、晋级划分和所测 harness 限制，长期运行时变化及独立复现仍待验证。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10310","tldr":"背景与问题：研究 agent 若每次都需重建训练、推理和评测基础设施，预算会耗在工程准备；只开放单一组件的基准又难检验数据、权重与 harness 的交互。\n\n方法：RSIGym 将训练、推理、rollout、评测和沙箱封装为服务，并统一预算与权限；设置分轨与联合轨道，让 agent 在约束下提出、评估并选择系统修改。\n\n结果与结论：作者比较六个研究模型，报告 Opus 5 在五个基准的 RSI-Index 最高，并给出 SWE-bench Verified、AIME 的提升。关键限制是论文明确承认，所得系统是否改善后续研究循环尚未评估；因此分数表示预算内目标系统改进，不等同递归能力增强。\n\nInsights：这提示 RSI 基准应把基础设施复用、预算审计与跨轮继承作为实验条件，同时区分“改进目标系统”和“改进产生改进的过程”。该区分来自论文的范围声明；平台可支持后续研究，但当前结果不能证明递归进展。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10120","tldr":"背景与问题：长程互动只有稀疏终局奖励，过程奖励虽更密集，却可能在策略变化后继续优化已不再是瓶颈的行为；频繁缺陷也不必然是失败原因。\n\n方法：RewardWeaver 从低结果轨迹中回溯归因，聚合反复出现且由策略控制的能力瓶颈，动态选择下一阶段过程奖励；已纳入能力的 Rubric 语义保持固定，新能力只有通过独立验证程序才可加入。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告在社交互动、议价与销售任务上优于所比较方法，并以消融支持动态分配、失败归因和语义稳定的重要性。摘要未给效果量、预算或跨模型细节，不能据此判断实际优势幅度。\n\nInsights：这提示过程奖励的关键不是不断改写评分标准，而是稳定定义能力后，随失败瓶颈变化重新分配训练信用；依据是方法对语义与当前相关性的区分。失败归因和 Rubric 评估仍可能有偏，跨领域及独立验证尚不足。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.09856","tldr":"背景与问题：依赖当前策略自一致性的训练，在采样答案完全一致时相对优势消失；课程生成若只追求分歧，也无法知道题目是否真的有学习价值。\n\n方法：AnchorLoop 保留上一轮 Executor 作为冻结参考，在求解训练中比较当前答案与当前、历史多数答案；在课程训练中以两组采样一致率差异塑造任务奖励。后者只是选择代理，因为该阶段两模型参数相同，不能当作版本进步或正确性证据。\n\n结果与结论：作者在 13 个推理基准报告较 Agent0 有数学和一般推理增益，并称后续迭代仍改善，而未锚定基线趋于停滞。结果为作者实验；摘要未详列预算和各任务方差。\n\nInsights：这提示历史参照可补充当前自一致性反馈，但参照的解释必须依阶段区分；依据是作者对课程信号局限的明确界定。锚点并不自动提供真值，也不能解决完全共识时优势仍为零的问题，故泛化和抗共同错误能力仍待验证。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-14","critique":"本批更有价值的推进，是把“如何改进”拆成可检验的信号与闭环。Marvo 用工具的边际收益构造学习信号，但长轮次退化提醒我们：自生成信号未必越迭代越可靠。[1] Harness² 连接任务内行为对比与跨任务经验积累，AutoEnvScaling 把环境生成纳入训练，值得看的是反馈如何塑造下一轮改进。[3][4] EvoBelief 强调可证伪世界模型，Genesis Accounting 尝试审计新机制生成；后者仍有人工触发、盲测零计数，不能当作自主发明的证据。[5][2] 建议优先精读 Harness²，再看 Marvo 的信号失效分析。这些是作者基于所给摘要或全文片段报告的结果，历史基线有限，仍有待分析论文；不同任务和预算下的收益不能直接横比，也不等于独立复现。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.15084","arxiv:2610.14843","arxiv:2610.14224","arxiv:2610.14163","arxiv:2610.12789"],"backlog":19,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15084","tldr":"背景与问题：视觉工具调用训练常依赖昂贵的标注问答或专家演示；仅按不确定性出题，也不能保证工具确实有用。方法：challenger 从无标注图像造题，solver 通过强化学习作答；solver 有无工具时的表现差作为出题反馈，使课程追踪工具的实际边际收益。结果与结论：作者报告覆盖 11,691 题的多基准评估中，Qwen2.5-VL-7B 平均准确率提高 7.1%；所给全文片段还报告八轮扩展中题目质量与表现后期下降。Insights：这提示课程信号应对准待学能力的边际贡献，而不是难度本身；依据是工具增益奖励及后期标签质量同步下滑。结论限于所测视觉任务，作者实验未经独立复现。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14843","tldr":"背景与问题：性能提升可能来自复用设计者提供的机制，也可能来自系统写出新机制；若不区分来源，RSI 声称难以证伪。方法：预注册区分机制实例与新算子，要求候选通过留出数据证书后才登记，并进入可复用注册表。结果与结论：作者报告氢谱与开普勒两次算子生成；氢谱协议修复循环性漏洞后，未见能级外推相对误差约为 10⁻⁶。盲选考试至今为零，事件触发仍需人工。Insights：这提示 RSI 应分别记录机制来源、验证与复用；依据是协议审计和诚实报告的零 tally。边界明确：结果支持受限语法下的机制生成能力，不证明系统能自主启动或持续进化。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14828","tldr":"背景与问题：办公工作流要求文档、表格和演示文件既正确、可编辑又彼此一致；单一文件类型上的修补成功，不代表形成可复用流程。方法：构建四类办公任务基准，对产物内容、原生结构、公式和跨文件一致性评分，并将反馈集、选择集与最终测试分离，控制初始 harness 与预算。结果与结论：在 GLM 5.3 与共同初始 harness 下，ACE/AHE 域内分别提高 4.90/2.64 分，跨办公任务却只变化 +0.03/-1.72 分。作者据此指出，域内收益不保证协调工作流迁移。Insights：这提示迁移目标应直接进入 RSI 测试，而不能用总体分数替代；依据是单模态与跨文件结果分化。边界是离线办公产物、有限配置及有限方法运行。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14730","tldr":"背景与问题：检索嵌入需要训练数据符合具体领域和相关性标准；人工设计查询、标签与合成指令难以随任务扩展。方法：系统从少量相关查询—文档示例推断任务要求，在小样本试产出上获取诊断反馈并修订共享合成指令，再用改进后的指令大规模生成数据。结果与结论：作者报告覆盖 24 个检索集、15 个领域；六项任务的自改进均提升训练数据效果，其中四项超过人工校准，MS MARCO 数据扩至初始规模 32 倍时性能仍提升。Insights：这提示递归改进对象也可以是产生训练经验的规则，而不只是模型参数；依据是指令修订与下游检索结果相联系。材料未提供独立复现，少量示例依赖、标签质量与长程闭环稳定性仍待验证。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14625","tldr":"背景与问题：RSI 工作涉及不同更新对象、反馈与保留机制，宽泛分类难以揭示设计差异及其交互。方法：论文提出九维设计空间，并从优化、正则化、数据增强、持续学习与进化计算等机制中归纳可能的研究方向，同时梳理在线与离线评测。结果与结论：材料支持其分类框架和研究议程；没有本文系统的递归改进实验或性能结果。Insights：这提示比较 RSI 时可分别追问改什么、谁提出、依据何种反馈保留；这是框架可能提供的分析工具，材料未证明它本身改善系统或研究产出。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14495","tldr":"背景与问题：解释视频既要视觉呈现，也要事实、推导和动画正确；只看像素难定位程序缺陷，偏好评审还可能把展示偏差当成改进。方法：把作品作为可读、可测试的程序记录；复盘将检查发现与修复差异配对，可静态检测的经验编译成带正反例的规则，并回查旧作品；playbook 更新需盲评且经人批准。结果与结论：作者报告一条规则在旧作品中发现四处潜在缺陷；研究也揭示盲评有明显顺序偏差。经验缩短修订循环，但没有形成累积改进或改变 judge。Insights：这提示可执行产物有助于把经验变成可审计检查，但偏好评分不能单独决定记忆保留；依据是回溯发现与位置偏差。证据限于单系统、有限作品和人工门控。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14224","tldr":"背景与问题：开放世界任务往往没有真值 verifier，按单一任务改出的 harness 又未必适用于后续新任务；直接继承任务专用修改还可能放大噪声。方法：先提出编辑并在相同任务和条件下探测行为变化，再据对比证据组合修改；随后从编辑过程提取适用条件与经验，更新未来任务的改进 harness。结果与结论：作者报告单步在多个专业基准和配置上有增益，增加任务级递归预算也带来提升。行为差异可帮助选择编辑，但不等于验证任务正确性。Insights：这提示应分别衡量“当前任务改得怎样”与“下一次是否更会改”；依据是双层循环及跨任务经验设计。证据限于特定基准、模型和预算，尚非独立复现。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14163","tldr":"背景与问题：终端 agent 的强化学习依赖多样且可验证的环境；人工设计限制供给，固定任务池也会随 solver 进步而失去训练价值。方法：proposer 阅读 solver 轨迹，在沙箱终端中编写、运行和修复环境；环境通过有效性与难度校准后入池，solver 的新表现再指导下一轮生成，形成数据飞轮。结果与结论：作者报告相较纯提示生成，有效环境率最高提升 25 倍、单个有效环境成本最高降低 75%；同一模型兼任 proposer 与 solver 时，Terminal-Bench 2.1 提升 12.2 分。Insights：这提示训练经验生成本身可成为 agent 能力的一部分；依据是环境构建与 solver 学习相互反馈。边界是生成者也参与构造测试，仍需审查测试漏洞、长期稳定性与外部分布迁移。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13829","tldr":"背景与问题：保存记忆或在一次任务中成功，不足以证明获得可迁移能力；后续表现可能受携带资源、源任务暴露量和早期执行失败影响。方法：用任务状态图和阶段验证器记录进度，重置目标世界与库存，只让声明的 agent 工件跨任务；在匹配预算下比较相关、不相关、打乱经验与无经验条件。结果与结论：作者报告控制器的直接能力优于规划器变体，但相关经验未显示稳定迁移，微小收益受单个种子影响且区间含零；早期采集、制作瓶颈还会使后续能力未被观察。Insights：这提示具身 RSI 的首要难点是把能力变化与环境状态、执行机会分开归因；依据是严格重置后仍无稳定迁移。结论限于 Minecraft 探针和所测代理，不能外推到所有具身环境。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13285","tldr":"背景与问题：固定蒸馏集会随学生能力变化而变得过易或过难；学生很弱时，单看错误也难判断哪些例子能提供有效监督。方法：先直接蒸馏少量教师推理轨迹建立基础能力，再持续选取学生尚未掌握、专家能可靠解决且题目质量合格的样本；学生更新后重新估计边界并刷新训练数据。结果与结论：作者报告只用 1,000 个训练样本，在 11 个基准上优于静态和动态选择基线；Qwen3.5-4B 在 IMO-AnswerBench 从 62.9 升至 75.3，在 AMO-Bench 从 26.8 升至 46.0。Insights：这提示有效课程信号需同时满足学习者有缺口、监督可学且目标可靠；依据是边界筛选机制和多基准结果。专家与分析器仍提供外部判断，不能称为完全自监督。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14118","tldr":"背景与问题：Harness agent 的任务空间宽，既有训练常依赖外部强模型造任务或收集轨迹，训练后评估结果又交由人分析，难以持续闭环。方法：系统合成并校验任务，用成功轨迹或强化学习更新模型，再从留出任务 rollout 诊断反复出现的短板，把分析反馈给下一轮任务生成。结果与结论：作者报告 Qwen3.6-27B 在三个基准持续提升；迭代任务转用于 Qwen3.5-4B 与 9B 时，各基准也有增益。摘要未提供具体提升幅度。Insights：这提示闭环的关键不只是生成更多任务，而是把诊断转成合格且针对当前能力的练习；依据是任务合成与能力报告相连。具体泛化范围、预算和长程稳定性仍需更多证据。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13098","tldr":"背景与问题：程序化图形 agent 主要根据最终渲染修订，图像差异难以说明符号编辑是否生效、被覆盖或互相干扰。方法：保留程序、渲染与运行时状态记录，从实际写入构造受限替代程序；重新执行检查指定端点和保持条件，再由常规视觉反馈判断目标相关性。结果与结论：作者报告在 BlenderGym 280 题与 BlenderBench 27 题上优于所比较的 refinement 方法；消融支持执行修订与证据组织的作用，但修复需额外执行。Insights：这提示改进信号的价值取决于能否观察编辑如何影响执行，而非单纯增加迭代；依据是执行修订消融。结论限于程序化 3D 场景，固定生成交互数也不代表总执行成本相同。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13021","tldr":"背景与问题：持续学习研究多限于非具身环境，而常见具身基准也不直接检验既有经验能否迁移到未见任务组合。方法：构造从原子动作、基础家务到未见组合任务的评测，并比较零样本、保留交互轨迹与压缩技能总结。结果与结论：作者报告复杂任务零样本成功率约为 10%，有基础任务经验后可超过 30%；但增加学习样本没有相称的持续收益，ICL 与技能学习也无稳定胜者。Insights：这提示积累经验可能先带来明显收益，之后瓶颈转为提取有效信息，而不是继续增加样本；依据是样本扩张未产生一致增益。任务采用离线状态图，不能直接代表真实在线具身交互。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12855","tldr":"背景与问题：on-policy 自蒸馏可提升总体能力，但训练推进时，先前答对的问题可能变为答错，单看总体分数会掩盖这种退化。方法：作者观察到能力退化伴随隐藏表征簇结构变模糊，提出在自蒸馏中约束簇内紧致与簇间分离，尽量保留已有表征结构。结果与结论：作者报告在多种自蒸馏方法和基准上，RGR 通常减轻能力退化，同时保留能力提升；摘要没有给出具体效果量。Insights：这提示 RSI 评估应同时追踪新能力与旧题回归，而不能只看平均表现。表征几何是作者提出并分析的关联机制，现有材料不足以断言它是各类自改进的普遍因果瓶颈。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12789","tldr":"背景与问题：Agent 即使会执行步骤，也可能因环境动态信念不完整或过时而失败；错误规则还可能传播到其他任务。方法：冻结语言模型，把环境知识存成带证据、适用范围和检验方式的假设。新观察触发验证，独立证据支持后规则才影响规划；反例会缩窄、降级或撤销规则。结果与结论：作者报告在 ALFWorld 中优于匹配的冻结世界模型，在 MiniGrid 中修订过时规则并适应动态变化；在 DiscoveryWorld Reactor Lab 也报告高于所测基线的完成率。Insights：这提示跨任务记忆要有可检验性、范围约束和撤销机制；依据是规则生命周期与漂移实验。证据来自有限模拟环境的作者实验，不能证明真实环境迁移或独立复现。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-13","critique":"这批论文的推进集中在“改进过程如何产生下一轮训练信号”：Evo² 联合优化权重与 harness，MASS 将多智能体轨迹用于递归微调。[2][3] RSI-Anything 与 Memento 3 把世界模型纳入闭环，但后者主要更新外部规则记忆，不能把两者都视为权重自进化。[1][4] 最值得精读的是评估器共演化：退化 grader 仍能带来相近任务表现，说明下游分数不足以认证反馈信号可靠。[5] 真正的瓶颈正在从“会不会更新”转向“更新依据是否可信”。这些是机制推进，尚无完整历史基线、统一预算比较或长期稳定性证据；判断限于所给摘要与全文片段，作者实验不等于独立复现。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.13912","arxiv:2610.13025","arxiv:2610.12176","arxiv:2610.11794","arxiv:2610.11464"],"backlog":0,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13912","tldr":"背景与问题：RSI 需要把交互经验转成后续能力，但外部评估昂贵；策略更新还可能改变经验分布，使既有世界模型失准。因此，单独改策略或预测器都不能保证下一轮系统仍可靠。\n\n方法：RSI-Anything 用预测模型预判候选行动结果，帮助选择行动和学习数据；真实反馈再驱动策略或工作流更新，并在可靠性、数据和预算条件满足时调整世界模型。组件检查与策略—模型兼容检查决定哪些更新被保留，获准组合进入下一轮。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告，在固定 coder 的代码修复任务中，成功率从静态 verifier 的 26.3% 经预测筛选升至 29.2%，再经世界模型适配升至 31.2%，测试使用量相近；还报告 GUI、实验规划和反应优化结果。这些是作者实验，不是独立复现；材料不足以确认长期稳定性和广泛泛化。\n\nInsights：这提示瓶颈不只是预测准确度，还包括策略变化后模型是否仍适用，以及如何筛选更新组合；依据是论文提出的耦合更新问题和兼容性保留设计。该机制能否延伸至更广任务，仍需长期及统一预算评估。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13025","tldr":"背景与问题：自进化 agent 常分别更新模型权重或修改 harness，忽略了二者的反馈关系：权重影响编辑质量，而编辑执行结果也能提供训练经验。分开优化可能无法让系统学会如何持续改进自身。\n\n方法：Evo² 让同一策略担任 harness 修改者和反思者；修改结果及执行反馈用于训练这两个角色。EvoTIDE 从编辑和反思轨迹中恢复可用训练数据，经监督微调与交错策略优化更新共享权重，再由更新后的策略继续搜索 harness。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告三个编码基准上的表现优于所比较的自进化方法，并称演化出的 harness 可迁移到其他任务；摘要给出 Polyglot 与 SWE-bench Verified 的对照分数。论文指出相关工作机制比较不是匹配性能基准，结果也不是独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示 harness 搜索不只是改善执行脚手架，也可能成为训练“改进者”的数据来源；依据是编辑反馈用于角色训练，更新权重又回到后续搜索。是否优于分别优化或其他联合方案，仍需统一预算、消融和多轮稳定性比较。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12176","tldr":"背景与问题：开放式研究等任务缺少可靠自动评分，结果可能超出人类专家稳定判断的范围；但让单一模型同时求解、评价和改进自身推理，也容易受同一偏见牵制。\n\n方法：MASS 先让模型搜索多智能体工作流，调整角色分工与信息传递，再把这些工作流生成的求解轨迹用于监督微调。更新后的模型重新担任求解者、工作流优化者和评估者，从而把工作流改进产生的数据带入下一轮能力更新。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告在 Qwen3.6-27B 上经过两轮 MASS，四个开放式基准的每输出 token 表现达到基线的 1.2–1.6 倍；多智能体轨迹训练的学生也优于使用更多 token 的单智能体轨迹学生。模型、任务和轮次有限，结果尚非独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示监督瓶颈可能部分来自组织方式：分工和信息路由可产生比单体长轨迹更有效的训练信号。依据是作者报告的轨迹效率结果；由于优化与评估存在同源性，且只展示有限递归轮次，不能据此断言能在开放任务中持续自我纠错。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11794","tldr":"背景与问题：在陌生环境中，少量观察可能同时支持多个世界模型；它们都能解释已发生的转移，却对未见状态作出不同预测。仅靠回放已观察数据，无法判定哪套规则能正确泛化。\n\n方法：Memento 3 让冻结 LLM 把环境假设写成可修订的自然语言规则手册，再编译为用于预测和规划的代码。新观察造成的预测误差促使规则或实现修订；候选代码需符合规则手册，并精确重现已观察转移，才会被接受并用于后续交互。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告其单模型系统在 ARC-AGI-3 的 25 个公开游戏中通过所有关卡，平均 RHAE 为 100，并在 Pong 的三个不同开局案例中以 21:0 获胜。后者是有限案例；回放验证只覆盖已有转移，不能证明对未见状态的模型正确性。\n\nInsights：这提示递归改进可以发生在外部记忆与可执行模型，而不必更新权重；依据是固定 LLM 下规则—代码闭环仍能改变后续规划。关键边界是观测覆盖：通过历史回放不等于掌握环境规律，需检查探索能否区分相互竞争的假设。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11464","tldr":"背景与问题：自改进循环每轮都要判断 agent 是否变好，但开放任务往往没有现成 verifier；手写 rubric 或由相似模型担任 judge，可能共享盲点并诱发奖励投机。更关键的是，训练后的任务分数也未必能证明评分器本身可靠。\n\n方法：论文把 verifier 作为演化对象，由失败聚类生成可检查的细粒度缺陷检测器，再以少量锚点参考和未标注输出共识筛选组合，不按 agent 得分选 grader。之后将演化出的 grader 接入技能改进循环，并用外部锁定评估监测结果。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告 MBPP+ 留出一致性较手写初始组合提高约 0.21；消融移除锚点防护后，grader 退化为始终放行，但技能训练表现仍相近。因此，下游任务得分不足以认证自进化 verifier。结果限于指定任务、锚点和实验设置，报告生成场景也没有金标准。\n\nInsights：这提示验证器需要独立于被优化任务表现的有效性检验；依据是退化 grader 仍能支撑相近技能表现的消融。该发现针对特定任务和锚点规模，不能直接证明锚点方案普遍可靠；应将 verifier 的留出一致性与下游收益分别报告。"}]}],"progress":[{"title":"将预测模型与规则记忆纳入改进闭环","topic":"世界模型与递归改进","description":"RSI-Anything 将预测筛选、反馈更新和策略—模型保留串联；Memento 3 以规则手册和可执行模型构成误差驱动闭环。两篇作者报告了各自特定任务实验，但彼此未比较，不能据此确立共同增益。","kind":"watch","limitations":"实验限于特定代码、GUI、科学规划或公开游戏场景；长期稳定性、未见环境泛化、预算敏感性和统一对照仍待检验。Memento 3 的回放只核验已观察转移；给定材料不足以确认领域级优先性。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.13912","arxiv:2610.11794"]},{"title":"权重与 agent harness 共演化","topic":"权重—harness 联合演化","description":"Evo² 将 harness 编辑及执行反馈用于更新进化策略权重，再以更新权重指导后续搜索；作者报告编码基准与跨任务迁移结果。这是权重与 harness 相互反馈的具体机制，但相关工作比较并非匹配性能基准。","kind":"advance","limitations":"需核对训练与评估预算、组件消融、不同模型和任务上的迁移及多轮稳定性；作者报告不能替代独立复现或统一基准比较。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.13025"]},{"title":"把多智能体协调轨迹转为递归自监督","topic":"多智能体工作流演化","description":"MASS 交替优化多智能体工作流并微调共享模型，使执行轨迹成为自监督信号；更新权重再用于求解、优化和评估。作者报告有限轮次实验与外部评估，但机制差异不等于相对既有方法的匹配性能优势。","kind":"advance","limitations":"证据限于特定基座模型、有限训练轮次和任务集；工作流筛选依赖同源模型反馈，需检验自评偏差、外部评估稳健性、训练预算和更广泛泛化。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.12176"]},{"title":"演化评估器并检验锚点防护","topic":"评估器递归改进","description":"论文以锚点一致性而非 agent 得分选择演化 grader；消融显示退化 grader 也可能支撑相近的技能训练表现，提示下游任务分数不能单独证明 verifier 有效。","kind":"advance","limitations":"实验覆盖指定任务、十项锚点和三种子；报告生成缺少金标准，技能侧结果也可能受评估与回滚设置影响。需检验更多任务、锚点规模、预算及长期 grader 漂移。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.11464"]},{"title":"训练经验随当前能力调整","topic":"自适应课程与数据合成","description":"Marvo 以工具有无的表现差生成适配当前能力的视觉问题；BoundaryEvo 先启动弱学生，再按学生—专家能力边界更新蒸馏数据；SYNTRA 迭代合成指令以改善检索训练数据；ClawLoop 将诊断反馈用于后续任务合成。共同变化是让训练经验随学习者状态调整，但各自反馈、任务与更新对象不同，不能视为统一机制已验证。","kind":"advance","limitations":"均为作者报告实验，缺少独立复现和匹配比较；任务分别限于视觉工具调用、推理蒸馏、检索和 harness 训练。长程闭环中的标签质量、错误累积、预算与跨域迁移仍待验证。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.15084","arxiv:2610.14730","arxiv:2610.13285","arxiv:2610.14118"]},{"title":"把改进过程纳入后续学习","topic":"Harness 递归演化","description":"Harness² 将任务内编辑的行为对比与跨任务改进经验积累连接；AutoEnvScaling 与 ClawLoop 则把任务或环境生成纳入训练循环。变化在于改进过程本身成为下一轮学习信号，但三者的验证器、角色来源和权重更新方式不同。","kind":"advance","limitations":"基准、预算和任务分布不同，报告增益不可横向比较；开放任务的行为对比不等于真值验证，环境生成还可能受到自建测试与目标偏差影响。多轮稳定性及外部分布迁移证据有限。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.14224","arxiv:2610.14163","arxiv:2610.14118"]},{"title":"把迁移与可归因能力变化单独测量","topic":"RSI 评测与迁移","description":"EvoCowork 显示单模态 harness 增益未必迁移到跨文件工作流；MC-EvoBench 未发现相关经验的稳定具身迁移；EmbodiedCLBench 则以组合任务检验经验收益。它们把迁移和能力归因从附加分析提升为 RSI 评测的核心问题。","kind":"watch","limitations":"评测分别限于离线办公产物、Minecraft 和离线具身状态图；模型、任务与方法有限，缺少独立复现。后续需共同控制源任务暴露、训练预算、样本量和目标任务难度。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.14828","arxiv:2610.13829","arxiv:2610.13021"]},{"title":"让改进建立在可核查的环境证据上","topic":"世界模型与递归改进","description":"EvoBelief 用可检验、带范围且可撤销的环境规则改变后续预测；VETR 从执行轨迹提取受约束的程序备选。两者将改进依据从最终分数或偏好判断，推进到更具体的环境状态与执行证据。","kind":"advance","limitations":"任务类型差异大且未直接比较；EvoBelief 限于若干模拟环境，VETR 的保持检查只覆盖已观测运行时性质并增加执行成本。规则泛化和长时稳定性仍待评估。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.12789","arxiv:2610.13098"]},{"title":"从任务得分转向机制与反馈审计","topic":"RSI 可证伪性与治理","description":"Genesis Accounting 预注册区分机制复用与新机制生成；Reels-RSI 把可检查经验编译成可回溯规则，并报告偏好 judge 的位置偏差。共同指向 RSI 需要独立于任务得分的审计证据，但现有材料没有证明稳定的自主递归。","kind":"watch","limitations":"Genesis 依赖人工触发和观察者注入语法，盲选 tally 为零；Reels-RSI 有人工审批且为单系统小规模研究。治理指标可能受到 Goodhart 影响，需扩大盲测与独立评估。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.14843","arxiv:2610.14495"]},{"title":"训练信号筛选与任务分布共演化","topic":"自适应训练经验","description":"SGUID 按训练期间持续有效的技能信号压缩蒸馏库；SynCo 联合更新任务合成器与推理器，让实际解题结果改变后续训练分布。两者共同体现训练经验随学习者状态适配，但反馈机制和任务不同，作者实验不构成彼此复现。","kind":"advance","limitations":"SGUID 限于带验证器的数学蒸馏及四个模型；SynCo 限于数学推理任务且依赖任务检查器。均为作者实验，无独立复现或匹配比较；长期训练稳定性、数据质量与跨域迁移仍待检验。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.12367","arxiv:2610.11345"]},{"title":"让实验经验改进后续预算决策","topic":"预算受限研究搜索","description":"研究世界模型将历史实验记录用于预测未执行干预并辅助固定预算选择；EvoAlloc 将程序搜索中的评估分配策略纳入经验更新，并用反事实评估补足选择性反馈。两者都把昂贵实验决策作为改进对象，但一个预测干预效果、一个调整评估投入，证据不可直接横比。","kind":"advance","limitations":"均为作者报告，分别依赖有限实验环境与程序搜索基准。跨环境迁移、预测不确定性、不同成本结构下的预算优势及长期稳定性仍待验证；没有独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.12235","arxiv:2610.12086"]},{"title":"从失败反馈调整下一轮安全与训练目标","topic":"失败驱动的递归更新","description":"ReSI 将模型更新纳入多轮红队—配方搜索，并以能力保留门控晋级；RewardWeaver 从低结果轨迹归因当前能力瓶颈，调整下一阶段过程奖励。共同变化是让训练配方或目标随失败证据改变，但两者任务和更新对象不同，尚无直接比较。","kind":"advance","limitations":"ReSI 受红队池、模型和安全基准约束；RewardWeaver 摘要未提供完整效果量及成本。失败归因、评估器偏差、长期能力保持和独立复现均是证据缺口。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.12233","arxiv:2610.10120"]},{"title":"将循环计算转化为跨深度监督","topic":"循环语言模型与跨循环蒸馏","description":"LoopOPD 将循环模型的额外计算转化为中间循环在自身轨迹上的密集分布监督；D-LoopOPD 再让共享参数更新后的终端循环继续充当教师。作者报告 Ouro-Thinking 数学推理与跨深度结果改善，并给出局部同时改进的条件分析。这推进了循环深度内部的反馈机制，但不是改进器自身递归进化的证据。","kind":"advance","limitations":"证据限于 Ouro-Thinking 作者实验及指定数据、循环结构和基准；理论结果依赖梯度对齐等条件。缺少独立复现、不同循环架构和统一预算比较；代码与检查点尚待发布。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.10623"]},{"title":"从论文自动构建可执行 RSI 环境","topic":"RSI 研究环境与评测","description":"RSI-Forge 从论文构建可执行研究环境，并用独立复现建立基线；作者在 120 个环境上测试固定权重 agent 继承代码和笔记的多轮改进。它扩展研究环境供给和工件迭代评测，未检验权重或改进器递归进化。","kind":"watch","limitations":"专家对捷径抵抗、论文忠实度和任务饱和度更为审慎；部分环境存在评估材料访问风险。结果限于作者构建的数据集、三次尝试和固定权重；仍需独立审计、预算匹配、长期稳定性与泛化测试。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.09426"]},{"title":"用受控失败诊断决定改哪里、练什么","topic":"失败驱动的递归更新","description":"AdaRSI 将已有诊断后选择 harness 或权重的思路落实到具身子步骤：同状态改变调用方式，确定训练对象及起点，再验证新策略的调用范围。CoDA 则用定向场景与控制扰动验证困难诊断，将其编译为生成程序与训练势函数，并按实际学习进步分配后续生成。二者分别推进干预对象与训练经验的选择，是对既有失败驱动更新主题的补充，不是同一机制的相互复现。","kind":"advance","limitations":"AdaRSI 限于单一执行器和 RoboCasa365 仿真，有限重试不能证明执行器绝对缺能；CoDA 的同环境预算不等于同总算力，真实机器人迁移未建立。诊断、训练和验证都有额外成本，长期稳定性与改进调度自身增强尚无独立证据。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.20474","arxiv:2610.22362","arxiv:2610.11655"]},{"title":"从设计经验库转向训练跨任务经验学习能力","topic":"RSI 评测与迁移","description":"MetaExp 用保留共享因素、变化具体实现的任务族训练经验获取和更新行为；在新分布空库起步、冻结权重，并将适配任务与固定目标评测分开。相对已有记忆结构设计和经验迁移评测，变化是训练产生经验的能力，而非预装目标经验；同协议下基座退化而训练模型获益，为这种区分提供直接对照。","kind":"advance","limitations":"证据限于指定大模型、三个下游基准和有限任务流；训练过滤尚未直接按技能更新的未来效用选择，反馈还含模型对失败检查的复核。需核对全部消融、训练预算、顺序敏感性和更长任务流稳定性，无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.21492"]},{"title":"将共演化交付后的技能漂移纳入审计","topic":"RSI 评测与迁移","description":"技能漂移审计固定策略与检索，改变被使用的技能内容，将共演化原配峰值拆成措辞一致性、抗损坏性和所测最差成功率。它补充既有跨任务迁移审计及 CoTrace 的运行时兼容性问题：不仅任务会变，系统内部被依赖的技能也会变。四种方法六设置的结果显示，原配能力增长可伴随漂移敏感性增加。","kind":"advance","limitations":"理论依赖理想化候选最优选择和覆盖，只保证覆盖改写族内不能改善，并不普遍证明大幅退化。实验证据来自有限内容扰动和训练轨迹，最差值不是全空间保证；更多技能规模、真实版本更新、审计成本和长期鲁棒训练仍需验证。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.20845","arxiv:2610.10426"]},{"title":"用已确认攻击修补逐任务奖励及其生成规则","topic":"评估器递归改进","description":"RRI 在已有评估器演化路线之外，加入逐任务评分准则的攻击—修补循环，并让已发现漏洞修改未来生成规则。相对只生成任务的总体增益，和已共演化任务与奖励相比的额外收益，更能检验攻击修补本身。该工作将奖励可利用性作为训练前应测量的对象，但没有把修补视为彻底认证。","kind":"advance","limitations":"判断仍依赖模型生成的诚实答案和 judge，修补两次后仍可被攻击的任务也进入训练。专业基准不能代表真实临床结果，部分跨域样本少；计算预算、长期奖励漂移及独立评估器一致性仍待核验，无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.21040","arxiv:2610.11464","arxiv:2610.17609"]},{"title":"在封存评估下展示长时自主通用模型后训练","topic":"RSI 研究环境与评测","description":"Athanor 将已有研究服务平台推进到真实 GPU 上的长时自主后训练活动：固定研究者自选数据、修改算法并组合检查点，隐藏套件检验所得通用模型。相对 RSIGym 的多轨目标系统搜索，本篇给出单个原始基座被自主后训练至接近官方指令版平均水平的具体案例；没有展示研究者自身递归升级。","kind":"advance","limitations":"主要证据为一次104小时、四研究者各一台八卡节点的活动；隐藏集仅覆盖既定能力，略高均分不能证明统计优势。活动中与事后重测协议不同，基础设施和人工运营职责仍存在，缺少服务消融、跨模型重复与预算匹配研究者对照。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.21055","arxiv:2610.10310"]},{"title":"限制反馈暴露并组织可归因的 harness 搜索","topic":"Harness 递归演化","description":"VideoHarness-SRSI 对既有完整轨迹驱动搜索作出具体修正：内容暴露对照显示反馈越丰富，验证—测试差距可能越大；继而限制内容反馈、隔离机制搜索并测试组合，四基准平均留出得分相对基础流程提高6.2%。这补充既有迁移审计，推进点是改变搜索使用证据的方式，而非新增一次验证门控。","kind":"advance","limitations":"作者实验集中于视频理解和固定骨干；主要结果及消融部分被截断，无法完整核对预算、重复次数与分阶段成本。屏蔽内容不消除汇总分数的适应性复用偏差；没有独立复现或改进器持续增强证据。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.19424","arxiv:2603.28052"]},{"title":"将经验继承与重复尝试分开审计","topic":"RSI 评测与迁移","description":"SEAR 将既有具身迁移审计扩展至机器人控制代码、多模拟器和真实硬件，以同开发时间的短重启、空技能库及隐藏状态评分，分离持续努力和经验继承。观察到自身技能库可能伤害表现、他人技能库反而有益；Physical RSI 框架进一步要求匹配起点与预算比较新旧改进程序，避免把任务收益当成元级收益。","kind":"advance","limitations":"SEAR 模型与工具配置绑定，部分自动研究设置只有一次运行，真实任务和场景数量有限，封闭评判仍存在信息旁路。Physical RSI 是规范框架，非递归收益实验；没有统一跨论文预算或独立复现，完整共演化仍未实现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.18792","arxiv:2610.18842","arxiv:2610.13829"]},{"title":"把经验混淆和接收者适配纳入记忆维护","topic":"经验迁移","description":"在已有经验学习与迁移主题内，STRATA 提供同系统方向混淆修复的具体证据：分层维护并显式警告相反程序，ScienceWorld 得分由78.7升至96.7。XferAgent 则保留跨代理来源，结合其他代理与本地使用结果校准经验选择。两者分别处理库内负迁移与异构共享，不构成彼此复现，也不替代 MetaExp 对经验学习行为的训练。","kind":"advance","limitations":"STRATA 对比边依赖固定反向操作词表，关键消融表不全；XferAgent 贡献者数量与源任务总暴露同步增加，经验使用结果尚非因果贡献。总预算、长期记忆漂移、任务顺序和开放语义泛化仍需评估，无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.19386","arxiv:2610.19581","arxiv:2610.21492"]},{"title":"以固定权限边界支持代理自扩展","topic":"RSI 可证伪性与治理","description":"L3M 将自扩展约束落实到运行时代码：代理可生成后续工具，但类型和能力令牌限制权限，部分核心检查有内核核验的定理；可恢复性及预先限定的影响范围决定审查层级。相对 harness 分类与准入原则，它提供具体实现，尚不能按已验证的多轮自改进收益入账。","kind":"watch","limitations":"关键评测表未提供，约三分之二通过率来自摘要，缺少自扩展独立消融、成本和长期部署证据。保证依赖可信编译、提供者、操作系统等，并非全系统语义安全；局部回滚不能撤回外部影响，无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.19591","arxiv:2610.18813"]},{"title":"用当前失败状态与对抗任务刷新训练经验","topic":"失败驱动的递归更新","description":"在已有失败驱动更新主题内，ReTerm 把当前策略的自然失败保留为可恢复训练状态，从同一快照分叉并用任务验证器训练纠错；AgentSafeEvo 则直接更新对抗任务生成者和防御策略，以安全、效用反馈及任务内奖励变化调整训练。两者都让后续训练经验适配当前弱点，但只有后者明确训练经验生成策略，反馈可靠性也不同。","kind":"advance","limitations":"ReTerm 总体收益混合强教师冷启动与在线 RL，完整预算及机制消融未见；快照恢复增加工程成本。AgentSafeEvo 依赖模型安全与效用判断，主结果表缺失，奖励方差可能含评判噪声。均无独立复现、长期稳定性或训练算法自我改写证据。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.18484","arxiv:2610.19422","arxiv:2610.12233"]},{"title":"训练研究提案与验证调度，并用真实结果纠偏","topic":"预算受限研究搜索","description":"在已有研究世界模型与预算决策主题内，LM2LM进一步用预测收益训练提案者，并执行当前策略偏爱的高分方案来纠正反馈高估；SpecRSI则学习后续编辑与检查的净验证收益，用整次搜索结果训练改进者。两者分别改变提案生成与验证调度，不是同一机制的相互复现，也不是仅增加并行尝试。","kind":"advance","limitations":"两篇均为截断全文下的作者实验，主结果及完整预算表未见。LM2LM的33%降低针对数据生成成本，不能当作全流程成本；定向校准的覆盖和长期稳定性未确定。SpecRSI目标成本下降时总成本可略升，跨任务预算优势与改进者迁移仍需独立验证。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.23344","arxiv:2610.16491","arxiv:2610.12235","arxiv:2610.13025"]},{"title":"将反馈质量与回归保持拆成可测试对象","topic":"评估器递归改进","description":"补充已有评估器改进主题：UCoE在固定模型下演化评分程序，以最弱属性对比族筛候选，再控制回答修补与经验准入；TeSearch优化小型可执行回归测试，对核验过的harness改写提升行为变化检出率。前者测试开放任务反馈的辨别力，后者检验行为保持，不能将两类检查统称为真实改进认证。","kind":"advance","limitations":"UCoE多数收益来自当前任务修补，合成属性对比向自然修订的泛化、重复校准集选择偏差及总成本仍待核验。TeSearch限于Python模块及构造的改写池，测试生成成本需摊销，仍有漏检和误拒；没有展示长期自演化收益或稳定性，也没有独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.17609","arxiv:2610.15964","arxiv:2606.09498"]},{"title":"经验正确仍可能不迁移，维护机制需接受独立验收","topic":"RSI 评测与迁移","description":"CFOE将既有迁移审计推进到无成功轨迹、无显式验证反馈的冷启动条件：局部修复不带来稳定留出收益，人工筛出正确经验也不足以消除缺口。CDSE、SpecForge与Darwin-Claw分别提出功能化维护、依赖约束和情境补丁；这些可作为应对缺口的候选机制，但没有在CFOE同协议下比较，不能当作已解决。","kind":"advance","limitations":"CFOE采用骨干特定的失败密集流，成功条件比较又分别采样任务，限制因果解释和普遍化。技能维护工作的完整消融、统一总预算、顺序敏感性与长期稳定性不足；SpecForge依赖参考实现测试，Darwin-Claw的LLM归因不等于因果识别。没有独立复现或跨方法统一迁移对照。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.22984","arxiv:2610.23599","arxiv:2610.15708","arxiv:2610.23574","arxiv:2610.21492","arxiv:2610.13829"]},{"title":"以执行反馈和学习者状态调整训练经验","topic":"自适应训练经验","description":"在自适应训练经验主题内，RSIPO用技能回放相对控制组的收益训练技能生成并校准蒸馏；ECG-RSI把信号有效性、弱点诊断与干预选择分离；HACE用标签验证局部贡献并双向选择训练经验；EAU进一步修改产生互动反馈的用户与环境配置。变化是让经验适配当前学习者，而非仅积累更多数据；各自监督来源和可变组件不同，不能合并为同一共演化机制。","kind":"advance","limitations":"均依赖有限任务和作者实验，未统一控制总算力、验证开销或干预次数。RSIPO的同题回放不直接证明跨任务技能价值；ECG-RSI完整消融与部分结果口径未能核对；HACE蛋白任务只更新预测头；EAU部分基线引用既有成绩。长程稳定性、开放反馈泛化和元更新机制自身增强均未建立。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.15772","arxiv:2610.17718","arxiv:2610.16078","arxiv:2610.16523","arxiv:2610.12367","arxiv:2610.11345"]},{"title":"将记忆写回后的延迟后门纳入轨迹级安全审计","topic":"RSI 可证伪性与治理","description":"EvolvAttack为已有自改进治理主题增加动态威胁证据：预植于权重的后门可在初始记忆检查中休眠，再由普通记忆写回与检索放大。其贡献不是提高自改进能力，而是说明安全状态取决于交互历史；静态权重或空记忆扫描不足以覆盖这种联合激活。","kind":"advance","limitations":"结论受部署前投毒能力、触发器暴露、检索与写回规则限制，不代表良性系统自然形成后门。空记忆训练覆盖改变攻击效果，完整跨设置结果被截断；现实流中的触发频率、审计预算、长期攻击稳定性及防御泛化未充分建立，无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.15244"]},{"title":"将搜索涨分拆成归因收益与跨流保留","topic":"RSI 评测与迁移","description":"在既有迁移与稳定性审计上增加两个不同维度：HDA以等推理预算和捷径移除分解搜索收益，显示同基准留出集仍可能共享捷径；持续学习审计在共享harness的漂移流中区分当前适应、未见任务干扰及遗忘。它们分别补充VideoHarness-SRSI的反馈暴露诊断和CODA的内部技能漂移审计，不是同协议复现。","kind":"advance","limitations":"HDA依赖人工复核的捷径检测、最小移除及任务特定预算匹配，残差只是上界；持续学习实验限于一个骨干、四类分块流和三种方法。完整重复、顺序敏感性、审计总成本及真实部署泛化仍不足，均无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.22466","arxiv:2610.25858","arxiv:2610.19424","arxiv:2610.20845"]},{"title":"联合演化细化到失败目标与历史配对","topic":"权重—harness 联合演化","description":"补充已有联合演化路线：Self-HPO让经过执行RL更新的策略重新提出harness编辑，并用未解任务刷新搜索目标；CoEvo-RSI允许harness结构与模型权重分别从历史档案继承或合并。相对Co-Harness沿当前配对修补和训练、CoTrace约束轨迹运行时匹配，两篇分别细化动态失败目标和历史初始化选择；Evo²则直接训练编辑及反思角色，不能与执行策略训练混同。","kind":"advance","limitations":"Self-HPO只有两轮、单一训练骨干，困难集消融主要来自外部提案者配置；CoEvo-RSI主要机制消融与完整预算被截断，接口违例率不覆盖全部能力失配。未统一比较搜索与训练总成本、长期稳定性或改进者能力迁移，无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.22791","arxiv:2610.25078","arxiv:2607.22688","arxiv:2610.10426","arxiv:2610.13025"]},{"title":"区分可部署技能、版本继承与反馈学习","topic":"具身 RSI","description":"在已有具身迁移审计中，Skill-RSI将冻结技能交给纯代码及廉价异族调用者执行，并以仅继承对照发现修补优势主要来自版本延续，而非开发反馈。Recursia把持久改进对象扩展为共享执行接口，尝试支持新组合，但评测暴露和成绩口径仍待核对。前者推进部署与归因合同，后者保留为迁移机制候选，不视为彼此验证。","kind":"advance","limitations":"技能编译仅覆盖七项仿真任务，成功成品多来自首稿，反馈增量对照样本少，失败成本及安全尾部风险突出，无直接控制基线。Recursia真实目标仅三项，部分比较存在历史目标暴露，经验扩展曲线单次运行。总预算、跨环境迁移和改进程序递归增强均未确证。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.25114","arxiv:2610.24464","arxiv:2610.18792","arxiv:2610.10498"]},{"title":"记忆估值从共现成功走向条件化干预","topic":"经验迁移","description":"在既有记忆维护主题内，BEAM尝试用逐条移除的执行差异训练情境化效用分布，ACE-Trader用完整有无记忆流水线收益差训练角色选择器，SELM则以使用成绩与置信投票管理库。相对STRATA及Darwin-Claw的结构和生命周期设计，本批更值得关注的是反馈信用的粒度；三类效用信号不具备相同因果含义，也尚未在持续学习审计的同一漂移流中比较。","kind":"advance","limitations":"BEAM反事实重跑与多轨迹采样增加成本，概率形式不认证校准；ACE-Trader共享标签无法隔离角色贡献，交易模拟不等于真实执行；SELM主表缺失且跨基准迁移未测。长期漂移、检索冲突、总预算及独立复现均不足。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.25119","arxiv:2610.25847","arxiv:2610.24630","arxiv:2610.19386","arxiv:2610.23574"]},{"title":"以执行验证和同条件比较训练攻防种群","topic":"递归安全改进","description":"Peer Pressure补充既有红队反馈路线：攻防适配器种群共同训练，代码分支通过构建、任务测试和指定漏洞利用确定奖励；同角色策略在相同条件下互作优势基线，冻结对手的对照支持适应性对手有贡献。相对ReSI逐轮搜索安全训练配方，本篇改变对手分布及信用分配；相对RRI的模型判分，代码反馈更直接依赖执行。","kind":"advance","limitations":"训练漏洞为已知类别和经预先认证的可达位置，不能表述为开放漏洞发现。相对单策略组基线的效率比较混有条件覆盖变化，关键隔离臂未运行；理论只分析优势方差而非梯度收敛。验证器成本、长期攻防稳定性及更广安全泛化仍需独立验证。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.24896","arxiv:2610.12233","arxiv:2610.21040"]},{"title":"让协调器与研究者在同一任务内共同学习","topic":"多智能体工作流演化","description":"MELD补充已有工作流训练与团队协调路线：协调器和私有研究策略接受任务内参数更新，分配改变学习经验，研究者结果再反馈协调器。两项任务中联合更新比单层更新产生更多高分候选，比最终系统排名更直接地支持互补性。","kind":"advance","limitations":"适配器逐任务重置，未测跨任务继承；按评估候选数而非总算力匹配。实际采用单轮信用，适配消融仅两项任务；长期稳定性、协调能力迁移和独立复现未建立。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.24454"]},{"title":"将编辑目标与证据规模纳入搜索决策","topic":"Harness 递归演化","description":"HGM-Dual用祖先编辑结果与约束违规指导候选生成，SSR每轮搜索证据规模并竞赛候选，分别补充已有可观测性和反馈治理。运行前编辑评分则提供固定代理筛选路线，但相对HGM的优势并不稳定。","kind":"advance","limitations":"SSR选择混用训练和验证任务，理论不覆盖跨轮泛化；HGM-Dual完整消融与划分未见。编辑评分部分配对区间含零，HGM计数叙述不一致。总调用成本、跨任务迁移、长期稳定性均待核对，无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.30042","arxiv:2610.28815","arxiv:2610.29121"]},{"title":"以同题比较和暂存假设减少错误记忆写回","topic":"经验迁移","description":"Hippo在已有结构化维护之外，连接同题尝试比较与适用条件修订，处理侥幸成功产生的错误经验；PreCoMem把模糊用户信息暂存为假设，避免立即覆盖。两者分别维护操作经验和用户状态，不构成相互复现。","kind":"advance","limitations":"主要结果及消融不全，Hippo多次尝试的预算对照未能核实，同源判断可能固化盲点。PreCoMem集中度和支持权重是代理。更长任务流、顺序敏感性、真实漂移和独立复现不足，维护规则自身学习未展示。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.24453","arxiv:2610.29467"]},{"title":"用配对提示实验测量学习者特定的课程价值","topic":"自适应课程与数据合成","description":"Environment Duels为环境生成路线增加同实例有无提示的配对评价，作者再根据求解轨迹修订一次；提示收益与后续训练收益的关联，为区分任务难度和教学匹配提供线索。DeepEvolve将失败分布反馈到实时预测题生成，但排名叙述冲突，保留关注。","kind":"advance","limitations":"Duels只有一次作者修订，训练关联限单一学习模型，提示可能伤害求解，模型调用预算不统一。DeepEvolve消融与成本不全，真值提取仍依赖自动检索评分。均未证明长期共演化稳定性或课程生成器递归增强。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.30116","arxiv:2610.29784"]},{"title":"由视频计划引导自采数据并自举动作映射","topic":"具身 RSI","description":"Mirror用实际执行观察和自身动作训练，即使未完成计划也能产生有效监督；视频规划器将采集引向能力边界，改进后的动作模型再访问后续阶段。相对代码—技能演化，本篇直接自举参数化动作映射。","kind":"advance","limitations":"依赖专家级视频规划器和外部视频训练，不能称无示范。部分未见目标不及随机采集对照，Minecraft基线设置不完全一致；主要为游戏与仿真证据，硬件泛化、总训练成本及学习程序递归增强未确证，无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.24177"]},{"title":"将覆盖范围与改进者收益分开验收","topic":"RSI 评测与迁移","description":"补充已有收益归因主题：Elicitation or Expansion 用尝试预算和难度拆分发现平均成功与覆盖可能分离；文献审计则量化最终产物评估、完整循环重跑及同起点改进者比较之间的证据落差。前者测系统行为，后者测报告实践，均进一步限制从涨分推断递归增强。","kind":"advance","limitations":"覆盖审计限于所测模型、任务和少量搜索运行，pass@k 不认证无限预算可达性；文献比例受检索框架、版本及编码一致性影响，不代表系统复现结果。总预算、长期稳定性和领域外泛化仍未建立。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.27889","arxiv:2610.27610","arxiv:2610.22466"]},{"title":"用异构模型证据优化共享 harness，并显式选择部署成本","topic":"Harness 递归演化","description":"MaD-RSI 将跨模型成功与失败前置为共享 harness 的诊断证据，六模型评价中共同成功改善；HarnessPro 在既有 RHO 路线上用固定生成测试和费用筛选多预算版本。两者分别改变证据来源与优化目标，不能把节省独立开发费用和降低部署费用混为一项收益。","kind":"advance","limitations":"MaD-RSI 成本参照为多次独立优化总和，安全任务更贵，关键消融不足；HarnessPro 主结果及测试质量对照缺失，生成测试可能遗漏缺陷。跨分布迁移、总搜索成本、多轮稳定性及独立复现尚不足，均未证明改进器增强。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.28201","arxiv:2610.26770","arxiv:2606.05922"]},{"title":"把训练破坏、验证失效与部署期影响分别审计","topic":"RSI 可证伪性与治理","description":"RSI Control 在后继训练中加入显式隐蔽副目标，显示主任务合格仍可伴随非预期属性；可恢复性研究则在普通错误场景中测出检查器静默失效，并区分保存版本恢复与已交付影响。它们将既有准入治理细化为对抗审计和恢复实验。","kind":"advance","limitations":"攻击实验使用明确副目标、小型后继和多数无害代理，未测完整多代累积或自发恶意；恢复实验主要为有限提示修改，弱验证器造成更差选择的趋势未显著，权重未测试。监控泛化、长期部署影响与审计预算仍不确定，无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.27735","arxiv:2610.27465"]},{"title":"以事后信息差补充自生成训练监督","topic":"自适应训练经验","description":"RSD 将完成轨迹的后续观察和跨任务经验用于同模型教师重评分，再蒸馏入权重；相对 RSIPO 的技能回放收益校准、LoopOPD 的额外计算教师，本篇采用事后信息优势。外部强模型还能调整上下文构造，但这部分另需环境验证，不应合并为全程无外部监督。","kind":"advance","limitations":"主结果表、消融及完整训练预算未提供，SearchQA 多轮收益有限；上下文拒绝后只回退规则、不回退权重，难隔离规则改进贡献。教师错误、长期训练稳定性、跨域泛化和独立复现仍需检验。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.27495","arxiv:2610.15772","arxiv:2610.10623"]},{"title":"把经验复用的效用、时效与物理成本分开测量","topic":"经验迁移","description":"TokenWorth 用执行反馈学习预算内检索及保留评分；BetaMem 将时间范围、原始来源和写入训练结合，但规则演化收益尚不能核验；PhysRSI-eval 以清空和冻结工作区验证保留经验的作用，并区分成绩与增益时机。三者补充已有经验维护主题，未在共同协议下证明相互优势。","kind":"watch","limitations":"TokenWorth 标签不是记忆因果贡献，扩展任务优势不一致；BetaMem 规则修补实验被截断；物理评测主要为有限布局、种子及模型配置，关联分析不能识别能力因果。总成本、漂移流稳定性、更广泛迁移与独立复现均不足。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.26453","arxiv:2610.26554","arxiv:2610.26848"]},{"title":"以跨分析视角的执行收益筛选可内化知识","topic":"自适应训练经验","description":"SPLICE补充已有技能回放与事后蒸馏路线：主动改变同一经验的解释方式，用重放收益的一致性选择更新证据，再验证知识并训练模型。两种规模的平均准确率优于所列共演化基线，支持进一步检查效用稳定性，而非仅凭指导文字合理性选择知识。","kind":"advance","limitations":"四类任务、两种规模；完整消融、训练方差和总重放成本缺失。跨视角一致性不保证跨任务或合并后效用，外部知识优化器未被训练；长期稳定性及独立复现尚无证据。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.30790","arxiv:2610.15772","arxiv:2610.27495"]},{"title":"将协作结构的训练信用定位到单次编辑","topic":"多智能体工作流演化","description":"RoleFlow在已有工作流搜索与训练之外，用相同链状态下修改和不修改的执行差训练路由器，将结构编辑从终局共享奖励中拆出。七项任务平均收益及可见问答消融支持该方向；与MASS的搜索后轨迹微调属于不同训练机制。","kind":"advance","limitations":"配对执行增加训练成本，完整预算和消融不全；即时编辑收益不覆盖长期结构交互，验证器误判仍会污染信用。测试不继承训练角色库，跨域与跨执行者泛化幅度需完整核验，无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.30429","arxiv:2610.12176"]},{"title":"将科学起点选择与有限时限优化程序共同演化","topic":"预算受限研究搜索","description":"ADAPT把已有搜索策略演化落实到物理约束下的历史设计迁移、渐进预算分配和局部优化程序。八个留出拓扑的相同运行预算比较显示损失下降；推进点是联合适配搜索环节，留出执行使用冻结程序。","kind":"advance","limitations":"限于可微引力波探测器模拟及既有设计库；主表、完整消融与开发总成本缺失。拓扑间标准差不能代表重复搜索稳定性，真实实验噪声、远分布迁移及外层演化器增强未验证，无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.30851","arxiv:2602.23413","arxiv:2610.12086"]},{"title":"用逐项后续任务审计检验复盘修改是否有用","topic":"RSI 评测与迁移","description":"arxiv:2610.34938 为已有修补—泛化缺口增加行为层证据：逐项迁移修改，区分问题出现、覆盖范围、读取和动作变化。七个信息充分事件中仅两项消除目标动作，任务成功未一致改善；相较 arxiv:2610.22984 的总体迁移结果，本篇更具体地定位经验适用范围。","kind":"advance","limitations":"单一 agent 和复盘版本，每条件五次运行；人工选择修改与能复现问题的同仓库任务，不能估计自然任务流的收益频率。修改可能捆绑额外检查，行为减少不等于质量或成本改善；长期失效、跨仓库迁移及独立复现未建立。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.34938","arxiv:2610.22984"]},{"title":"自主后训练开始显式检验跨域退化和用户偏好分离","topic":"RSI 研究环境与评测","description":"在 Athanor 的自主通用后训练案例上，ParetoRSI-Gym 用五域反馈与隐藏评价暴露平均收益背后的退化，且多数配置末轮并非最佳；RSI Arena 增加用户比较反馈，第二阶段多数模型偏好评分改善，却未伴随相应基准增长。推进点是分别验收不同改进目标，尚非研究者递归增强。","kind":"advance","limitations":"前者限五轮、指定模型及受限训练流程，部分领域采用同基准划分，种子覆盖不统一；后者固定单一基座、实际资源使用不等，且缺少第二阶段无用户反馈的继续训练对照。长程稳定性、偏好群体泛化和独立复现均不足。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.34386","arxiv:2610.33624","arxiv:2610.21055"]},{"title":"自适应课程扩展到多模态证据与自生成特权监督","topic":"自适应训练经验","description":"MTA-Zero 延续 SynCo 的混合成败课程信号，将生成策略训练扩展到有图像起点和外部证据检查的多跳搜索；OPST 则把自生成答案及推理用作教师特权信息，沿学生轨迹提供密集监督。两篇改变的是题目有效性约束与监督接口，不能当成首次提出模型—数据共演化。","kind":"watch","limitations":"关键消融或主结果被截断，无法统一比较总训练、造题和验证预算。MTA-Zero 依赖有答案的视觉种子、外部服务与模型裁判；OPST 的自一致性不排除共同错误。更长课程稳定性、跨域纠错与独立复现仍待验证。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.33799","arxiv:2610.32770","arxiv:2610.11345"]},{"title":"把可复用图像修补经验与裁判更新分开验收","topic":"评估器递归改进","description":"ImageRSI 在既有经验维护及 UCoE 评分程序演化之外，以同请求同种子的配对试验筛选图像修补策略，并离线训练裁判参数。留出任务上的经验库对照支持复用收益；正文明确重复裁判收集—训练循环仍为提案，进展应记在经验准入和裁判阶段比较。","kind":"advance","limitations":"限定图像生成请求、生成器和模型评价，经验库规模实验使用单一固定随机顺序；裁判监督来自模型标注。完整预算、顺序敏感性、跨生成器经验迁移、多轮裁判漂移与独立复现均未充分建立。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.32120","arxiv:2610.17609"]},{"title":"推理节省细分为学会少想与省去重复调用","topic":"预算受限研究搜索","description":"HarnessMM 将已经确定的动作与等待执行条件分开，以真实回执触发原动作并记录被省略的推理调用；MORE 则训练模式选择和长度分配。相对 HarnessPro 在搜索中权衡性能与费用，两篇进一步改变运行时成本来源，但其总收益仍需与外围配置和训练先验分离。","kind":"advance","limitations":"HarnessMM 部分配置存在质量回退，集成结果包含上下文与收尾设置；MORE 首阶段使用策展数据，关键消融不完整。开发成本摊销、实际延迟、复杂交互泛化和长期稳定性尚不清楚；均未证明优化规则自身增强，也无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.32813","arxiv:2610.33684","arxiv:2610.26770"]},{"title":"以任务技能优化增益评价可自改写的元技能","topic":"Harness 递归演化","description":"Skill∞ 将优化程序封装为可原生发现的技能，以固定候选预算下改善任务技能的幅度评价元技能，再把修订后的程序用于后续优化。相对 Hyperagents 的元程序可编辑与 RSIFlow 的编排经验维护，本篇给出了更直接的元级评分和去除自改进对照：总体通过率由55.9%升至60.7%。","kind":"advance","limitations":"截断材料未给出完整元任务划分、重复方差和费用；候选数相同不代表调用与执行成本相同。分领域存在退化，跨任务复用不等于长期稳定加速，尚无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.35434","arxiv:2603.19461","arxiv:2610.21791"]},{"title":"将反馈治理推进到修改前的经验筛选与动态诊断","topic":"Harness 递归演化","description":"补充既有反馈暴露和失败迁移主题：GEPA-Curator 在修改前选择可学习任务，并提供同题可靠成功参照；RuHarness 则随当前行为重新发现和排序诊断准则，最终仍用固定任务成绩选择修改。前者改变反思输入，后者改变干预重点，均比单纯增加事后门控更具体。","kind":"advance","limitations":"主要为指定交互基准和骨干的作者实验。关键消融被截断，无法完整分离经验选择、成功参照、准则排序及额外预算；模型诊断不认证因果，长期漂移、反复验证集选择偏差与独立复现仍未解决。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.37651","arxiv:2610.36826","arxiv:2610.19424","arxiv:2610.22984"]},{"title":"区分优化知识跨运行积累与训练中的持续适应","topic":"预算受限研究搜索","description":"RSI-Opt 将优化器 agent 的程序知识与操作政策作为跨运行继承对象，补充 ADAPT 的离线搜索程序演化。控制比较区分初始配方和后续决策：前者解释已见任务多数收益，后者对未见任务更有价值；部分模型继续演化后留出汇总表现下降。","kind":"advance","limitations":"九项小规模训练任务、有限代数与种子；固定决策机会不等于相同费用或训练时间。缺少等预算独立提案对照，留出描述暴露后的档案间接传播未查清；元 agent 程序固定，无长期稳定性或独立复现证据。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.32026","arxiv:2610.30851"]},{"title":"用图查询真值约束能力边界上的自出题训练","topic":"自适应课程与数据合成","description":"EoG 延续 SynCo 的求解结果驱动课程路线，把答案来源改为知识图谱上的逻辑查询执行，并让共享参数模型同时学习出题与探索。相对模型生成参考答案，完整答案集合具有更明确的执行来源；求解分数方差用于调整后续题目，而非只靠模型自估难度。","kind":"advance","limitations":"限于指定图谱、六类查询结构及基准，主要结果和课程消融不全。自然语言与符号查询的一致性仍需核验，相似度过滤不保证无泄漏；训练与验证总成本、长期课程稳定性及独立复现未建立。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.35598","arxiv:2610.11345","arxiv:2610.13285"]},{"title":"按共享能力生成简化世界并保留多分支 harness","topic":"跨任务迁移","description":"The Trinity 尝试把异构任务按共同能力组织，在简化可验证世界中演化模块，再回到原任务测迁移；与 Recursia 的共享执行接口路线相比，它保留多套能力分支并按任务路由，造环境者的 harness 也跨轮更新。当前属于迁移机制候选，不能由宽覆盖和总体均分确认能力抽象有效。","kind":"watch","limitations":"主要结果、分组与路由消融和总预算被截断；局部模块准入不要求性能提高，固定树拓扑限制适应范围。实机仅两个场景，生成世界的失真、长期分支稳定性及远分布迁移仍待检验，无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.36077","arxiv:2610.24464"]},{"title":"把当前安全与防护失效后的剩余保护分开验收","topic":"RSI 可证伪性与治理","description":"Masked Erosion补充已有验证失效与恢复审计：受控删除表明，真实任务收益和低观测危害可以同时伴随防护冗余流失；更大批次提高统计辨别力，也可能更可靠地选中有收益的防护删除。相对arxiv:2610.27465检查验收器是否有效，本篇增加单层失效与模型替换的检查维度，少量GEPA运行进一步显示保留规则原文不足以确保迁移后的安全。","kind":"advance","limitations":"两个环境、每个四层防护，主要为人为指定删除的压力测试，自由改写与GEPA样本少；模型替换实验假设部署时未重新审计。单层消融增加评估成本，长期多层交互及开放任务泛化未建立；部分预测后置冻结，独立复现缺失。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.38392","arxiv:2610.27465"]},{"title":"将题池刷新时机与题目生成策略分开研究","topic":"自适应课程与数据合成","description":"A-RSI在已有SynCo、MTA-Zero的在线课程路线旁，固定程序模板与题型份额，仅由训练日志决定何时启用新池；程序配置计算答案，避免以模型多数票直接充当标签。匹配训练进度的新池与旧池比较支持替换价值，但尚未隔离自适应时机的增量，不应登记为生成策略共同进化。","kind":"incremental","limitations":"各训练臂仅一次运行，缺少匹配周期的随机刷新对照，首次刷新点依据已有日志设定；旧池臂未完成预定终点。任务限固定视觉题型，模板设计受评测启发，生成、审计及训练总成本尚不能统一核算；长期稳定性与跨模型泛化证据有限。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.38568","arxiv:2610.11345","arxiv:2610.33799"]},{"title":"用后续可比改进的工作效率刻画递归收益","topic":"RSI 可证伪性与治理","description":"From Grind to Grasp为已有产物—过程区分增加效率表述：固定信息额度与系统边界，比较后继系统产生可比进一步改进所需的工作，并纳入知识构建、维护和协调。相对arxiv:2610.27610的同起点、同预算改进者比较，它提供概念上的成本解释，目前适合作为评测设计候选。","kind":"watch","limitations":"没有现实自改进系统实验；可比改进、信息额度及跨硬件工作量尚需操作化。固定解释器可以表示变化程序，却不保证效率排序不变；全生命周期预算、跨任务泛化与连续递归收益均未经验验证，不能把形式定义计作能力进展。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.38728","arxiv:2610.27610"]}]};
